},\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"yeah it\'s up speed and down so you can\",\r\n        \"start\": 21.16,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.76\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"see instead of landing on the front edge\",\r\n        \"start\": 24.439,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.801\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"I\'m landing on the back Edge and I\'m\",\r\n        \"start\": 26.92,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.599\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"landing one foot so I can drop straight\",\r\n        \"start\": 29.24,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.12\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"in the reason it\'s a speed step is\",\r\n        \"start\": 31.519,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.2\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"because your leg needs to take the\",\r\n        \"start\": 34.36,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.48\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"impact before your hand you don\'t want\",\r\n        \"start\": 36.719,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.32\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"to be jumping straight in with your\",\r\n        \"start\": 38.84,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.08\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"hands you want to jump in with your foot\",\r\n        \"start\": 41.039,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.721\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"land and drop straight into that speed\",\r\n        \"start\": 43.92,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.799\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"step um you can practice smaller drops\",\r\n        \"start\": 46.76,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.52\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"start off nice and close and sort of\",\r\n        \"start\": 51.719,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.441\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"like one foot into it up and drop and\",\r\n        \"start\": 54.28,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.599\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"then build up with bigger jumps bigger\",\r\n        \"start\": 59.16,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.12\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"drops um as you feel comfortable\",\r\n        \"start\": 62.879,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.6\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"so and down and yeah yeah is a nice good\",\r\n        \"start\": 67.28,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.4\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"feeling of uh that dual movement of a\",\r\n        \"start\": 71.479,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"running jump and uh speed step\",\r\n        \"start\": 74.68,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.479\r\n    }\r\n]'),(20220,55158,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(20221,55158,'video_transcript_srt','1\r\n00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:11,000\r\nokay so one dual movement that is quite\r\n\r\n2\r\n00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000\r\npopular is a broad jump into a speed\r\n\r\n3\r\n00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:17,000\r\nVault um because you land one foot and\r\n\r\n4\r\n00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000\r\ngo straight into the speed Vault so you\r\n\r\n5\r\n00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000\r\ncan do this running or standing uh but\r\n\r\n6\r\n00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000\r\nyeah it\'s up speed and down so you can\r\n\r\n7\r\n00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000\r\nsee instead of landing on the front edge\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000\r\nI\'m landing on the back Edge and I\'m\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000\r\nlanding one foot so I can drop straight\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000\r\nin the reason it\'s a speed step is\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000\r\nbecause your leg needs to take the\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000\r\nimpact before your hand you don\'t want\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000\r\nto be jumping straight in with your\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,000\r\nhands you want to jump in with your foot\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,000\r\nland and drop straight into that speed\r\n\r\n16\r\n00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:53,000\r\nstep um you can practice smaller drops\r\n\r\n17\r\n00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:58,000\r\nstart off nice and close and sort of\r\n\r\n18\r\n00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:02,000\r\nlike one foot into it up and drop and\r\n\r\n19\r\n00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,000\r\nthen build up with bigger jumps bigger\r\n\r\n20\r\n00:00:62,000 --> 00:01:10,000\r\ndrops um as you feel comfortable\r\n\r\n21\r\n00:00:67,000 --> 00:01:14,000\r\nso and down and yeah yeah is a nice good\r\n\r\n22\r\n00:00:71,000 --> 00:01:19,000\r\nfeeling of uh that dual movement of a\r\n\r\n23\r\n00:00:74,000 --> 00:01:19,000\r\nrunning jump and uh speed step\r\n\r\n'),(20222,55158,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(20223,55158,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJNFkL5tGXsbYKp4psVtc8EhACjv\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735839253,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"A popular dual movement in parkour involves executing a broad jump followed immediately by a speed vault. This technique can be performed from either a running or a standing position. The key aspect of this movement is to land on one foot, which allows for a seamless transition into the speed vault.nnWhen performing the jump, it\'s crucial to land on the correct edge of the surface. Instead of landing on the front edge, which can be unstable, the technique emphasizes landing on the back edge to better absorb impact. This strategy involves using the leg to take the initial impact before transitioning into the speed vault, ensuring that the hands do not bear the brunt of the landing.nnFor those new to this movement, it\'s advisable to start with smaller jumps to build confidence and technique. Practicing from a closer distance allows for easier landings, which can progressively increase in height and distance as proficiency improves. This method not only promotes safety but also helps in mastering the combination of the running jump and speed step effectively.nnKey Points:n1. The dual movement combines a broad jump with a speed vault, focusing on landing on one foot.n2. Proper landing technique involves using the back edge to minimize impact on the hands.n3. Beginners should practice with smaller jumps before advancing to larger ones.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 873,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 254,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1127,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"SkYHKK67qkpe9dba6QoEDKUh6jHoyuzXROSLRs6rSKk-1735839259-1.0.1.1-qWb0JWy6Aj1ipupEoN99Ow7Y_HSNPP4pReVADZptK2GwqiUHZDJJYM6S4Iql4PJF8OqzIlqjKYtehlhCTgKq4g\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735841059,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"JrLhqOcTc1qMa1syG1S3XkG.HjRV1x4epMnYgY.uSlI-1735839259505-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(20224,55158,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(20225,55158,'video_transcript_chatgpt','A popular dual movement in parkour involves executing a broad jump followed immediately by a speed vault. This technique can be performed from either a running or a standing position. The key aspect of this movement is to land on one foot, which allows for a seamless transition into the speed vault.\r\n\r\nWhen performing the jump, it\'s crucial to land on the correct edge of the surface. Instead of landing on the front edge, which can be unstable, the technique emphasizes landing on the back edge to better absorb impact. This strategy involves using the leg to take the initial impact before transitioning into the speed vault, ensuring that the hands do not bear the brunt of the landing.\r\n\r\nFor those new to this movement, it\'s advisable to start with smaller jumps to build confidence and technique. Practicing from a closer distance allows for easier landings, which can progressively increase in height and distance as proficiency improves. This method not only promotes safety but also helps in mastering the combination of the running jump and speed step effectively.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The dual movement combines a broad jump with a speed vault, focusing on landing on one foot.\r\n2. Proper landing technique involves using the back edge to minimize impact on the hands.\r\n3. Beginners should practice with smaller jumps before advancing to larger ones.'),(20226,55158,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(20227,55158,'svg_id',''),(20228,55158,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(20229,5