      \"duration\": 6.8\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"from here foot hand step down and drop\",\r\n        \"start\": 34.6,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.24\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"so it\'s a little bit quicker means that\",\r\n        \"start\": 38.8,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.4\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"the speed step is the first thing coming\",\r\n        \"start\": 40.84,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.28\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"in and then the second step Vault can\",\r\n        \"start\": 43.2,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.76\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"easily slow you down on that second drop\",\r\n        \"start\": 48.12,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.959\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"um but yeah practice that speed step\",\r\n        \"start\": 51.96,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.279\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"foot coming first taking the impact and\",\r\n        \"start\": 55.079,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.561\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"then hand\",\r\n        \"start\": 58.239,\r\n        \"duration\": 3.401\r\n    }\r\n]'),(20446,55160,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(20447,55160,'video_transcript_srt','1\r\n00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000\r\nso so when we\'re doing a speed Vault\r\n\r\n2\r\n00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,000\r\nwe\'re essentially going foot first so\r\n\r\n3\r\n00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:21,000\r\nfrom here um I\'m coming in my foot L\r\n\r\n4\r\n00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:25,000\r\nfirst and then hand drop and then I can\r\n\r\n5\r\n00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000\r\ndo whatever I\'m going to do so with the\r\n\r\n6\r\n00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,000\r\nspeed step we can do uh a double speed\r\n\r\n7\r\n00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000\r\nstep so similar to the step Vault but\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000\r\nnow just the foot is landing first so\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000\r\nfrom here foot hand step down and drop\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000\r\nso it\'s a little bit quicker means that\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000\r\nthe speed step is the first thing coming\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:51,000\r\nin and then the second step Vault can\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000\r\neasily slow you down on that second drop\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000\r\num but yeah practice that speed step\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000\r\nfoot coming first taking the impact and\r\n\r\n16\r\n00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000\r\nthen hand\r\n\r\n'),(20448,55160,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(20449,55160,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJN9lddBj0cZYZyXU87XTOCwj2v7\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735839247,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The technique of executing a speed vault involves a sequence where the foot makes the initial contact with the surface, followed by the drop of the hands. This two-step process is crucial for maintaining momentum and ensuring a smooth transition during the movement. By placing the foot first, practitioners can effectively manage their impact when landing, helping to prepare for the subsequent actions.nnIn addition to the basic speed vault, there is an advanced method known as the double speed step. This variation parallels the standard step vault but emphasizes the quickness of the execution by prioritizing the foot\'s landing. The sequence remains consistent, as the foot lands first, followed closely by the hands, enabling a swift progression to the next move.nnPracticing the speed step is essential to mastering this skill. The initial landing with the foot takes the brunt of the impact, allowing for a smoother transition into the following movement. As the practitioner becomes more comfortable with the motions, it is essential to avoid excessive slowing down during the second drop to maintain overall speed and fluidity.nnKey Points:n1. A speed vault begins with the foot landing first to effectively handle impact followed by the hands.n2. The double speed step is a faster variation that maintains the same initial foot-first landing technique.n3. Regular practice of the speed step helps in maintaining speed and smooth transitions during the vaulting process.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 617,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 270,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 887,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"9TowVZT8YcmrXPGX7npKxsDgNWwmPb8EkrX5OSfN0cY-1735839251-1.0.1.1-mMSej6lUYUfiYyz_r3ksikM0toDbnZdvghWBzf4oGm8QuhQ1lPlLjZlIxaLwR15kbuP4RDYmtGAkyATCn3Pl7Q\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735841051,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"jn0Yy5N81_4nbbz1cPmBIjHFfhUinnFPGyBqdUczs1s-1735839251954-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(20450,55160,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(20451,55160,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The technique of executing a speed vault involves a sequence where the foot makes the initial contact with the surface, followed by the drop of the hands. This two-step process is crucial for maintaining momentum and ensuring a smooth transition during the movement. By placing the foot first, practitioners can effectively manage their impact when landing, helping to prepare for the subsequent actions.\r\n\r\nIn addition to the basic speed vault, there is an advanced method known as the double speed step. This variation parallels the standard step vault but emphasizes the quickness of the execution by prioritizing the foot\'s landing. The sequence remains consistent, as the foot lands first, followed closely by the hands, enabling a swift progression to the next move.\r\n\r\nPracticing the speed step is essential to mastering this skill. The initial landing with the foot takes the brunt of the impact, allowing for a smoother transition into the following movement. As the practitioner becomes more comfortable with the motions, it is essential to avoid excessive slowing down during the second drop to maintain overall speed and fluidity.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. A speed vault begins with the foot landing first to effectively handle impact followed by the hands.\r\n2. The double speed step is a faster variation that maintains the same initial foot-first landing technique.\r\n3. Regular practice of the speed step helps in maintaining speed and smooth transitions during the vaulting process.'),(20452,55160,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(20453,55160,'svg_id',''),(20454,55160,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(20455,55160,'svg_colour',''),(20456,55160,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(20457,55160,'extra_variables',''),(20458,55160,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(20459,55160,'notes',''),(20460,55160,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(20461,55160,'enable_youtube_api',''),(20462,55160,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(20463,55160,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(20464,55160,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(20465,55160,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(20466,55160,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(20467,55160,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(20468,55160,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(20469,55160,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(20470,55160,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(20471,55160,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(20472,55160,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(20473,55160,'enable_transcript',''),(20474,55160,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(20475,55160,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(20476,55160,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(20477,55160,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I want this to sound like I wrote the result.'),(20478,55160,'_transcript_chatgpt_prompt','field_672214208bf31'),(20479,55160,'rank_math_primary_tutorial_category','0'),(20480,55160,'video_filename','Vaulting-SpeedStep/Tutorial-vaulting-speed_step-7-jump-step.mp4'),(20481,55160,'_video_filename','field_677cead91f698'),(20482,55160,'portrait_thumbnail_image','Vaulting-SpeedStep/screenshots/Tutorial-vaulting-speed_step-7-jump-step_3_4.png'),(20483,55160,'_po