ging various grips to facilitate climbing, particularly the overgrip.\r\n2. Elevating one forearm first allows for better body positioning and easier transitions while climbing.\r\n3. Mastering these foundational skills is essential for developing increased confidence and effectiveness in climbing overall.'),(22542,55182,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(22543,55182,'svg_id',''),(22544,55182,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(22545,55182,'svg_colour',''),(22546,55182,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(22547,55182,'extra_variables',''),(22548,55182,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(22549,55182,'notes',''),(22550,55182,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(22551,55182,'enable_youtube_api',''),(22552,55182,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(22553,55182,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(22554,55182,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(22555,55182,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(22556,55182,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(22557,55182,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(22558,55182,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(22559,55182,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(22560,55182,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(22561,55182,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(22562,55182,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(22563,55182,'enable_transcript',''),(22564,55182,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(22565,55182,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(22566,55182,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(22567,55182,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I want this to sound like I wrote the result.'),(22568,55182,'_transcript_chatgpt_prompt','field_672214208bf31'),(22569,55182,'rank_math_primary_tutorial_category','0'),(22570,55182,'video_filename','Climbing-ClimbUps/Tutorial-Climbing-Climbup-1