n generating upward momentum, so engaging them during the jump is essential.nnIn addition to standard jumps, the standing box jump is a valuable skill where no running momentum is used. This type of jump requires more strength and precision since the body must overcome the height of the obstacle without the assistance of a running start. Incorporating both types of jumps into training regimens not only provides variety but also enhances overall athletic performance and control. Safety should always be a priority, focusing on proper landing techniques to prevent injuries.nn**Key Points:**n1. Focus on form by emphasizing knee elevation and an upright torso during box jumps to enhance height and reduce injury risk.n2. Practice both standard and standing box jumps, gradually increasing difficulty to build strength and confidence.n3. Utilize arm movement for better momentum and incorporate jumps into a broader training routine for improved athletic performance.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 3438,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 328,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 3766,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"r1AEMzxh.g1Jh.aO.eHP8E7AAzQ.poGhBdF6QBX3onw-1735744632-1.0.1.1-hbnS8IznMM0QfyWLO6ZWGh.zFmBIFitAJoJWYLes3_64DtszPZMRhQK2rj4QjKWHrViBkqKqnmdDR8AvEia0cQ\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746432,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"attF4xjmMTpU3T2TAcMUvurStLOIahxaQf4TuVxh.WQ-1735744632689-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(24891,55202,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(24892,55202,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The box jump is a versatile exercise that involves jumping onto or over obstacles such as benches, walls, or other barriers. When performing a strict box jump, the technique often encourages a jump that does not involve running, promoting a cleaner jump where the focus is on bringing the knee up towards the chest and keeping the torso upright. This reduces the risk of injury and enhances the athlete\'s ability to gain height, with a preference for vertical movement rather than horizontal speed.\r\n\r\nTo effectively execute a box jump, emphasis should be placed on the leg movement. Practicing a knee-up motion while maintaining an upright torso is crucial for creating the necessary height to clear the obstacle. Beginners can start by jumping over lower heights and gradually work their way up as they build strength and mobility. Arms play a significant role in generating upward momentum, so engaging them during the jump is essential.\r\n\r\nIn addition to standard jumps, the standing box jump is a valuable skill where no running momentum is used. This type of jump requires more strength and precision since the body must overcome the height of the obstacle without the assistance of a running start. Incorporating both types of jumps into training regimens not only provides variety but also enhances overall athletic performance and control. Safety should always be a priority, focusing on proper landing techniques to prevent injuries.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. Focus on form by emphasizing knee elevation and an upright torso during box jumps to enhance height and reduce injury risk.\r\n2. Practice both standard and standing box jumps, gradually increasing difficulty to build strength and confidence.\r\n3. Utilize arm movement for better momentum and incorporate jumps into a broader training routine for improved athletic performance.'),(24893,55202,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(24894,55202,'svg_id',''),(24895,55202,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(24896,55202,'svg_colour',''),(24897,55202,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(24898,55202,'extra_variables',''),(24899,55202,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(24900,55202,'notes',''),(24901,55202,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(24902,55202,'enable_youtube_api',''),(24903,55202,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(24904,55202,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(24905,55202,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(24906,55202,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(24907,55202,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(24908,55202,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(24909,55202,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(24910,55202,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(24911,55202,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(24912,55202,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(24913,55202,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(24914,55202,'enable_transcript',''),(24915,55202,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(24916,55202,'enable_transcript_chatg