ipt_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AkurwFLGD0mzT60f37Z31EmMUjEnq\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735745056,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"As proficiency in jumping increases, it becomes crucial to incorporate impact and drop training into your routine. These exercises serve as an essential method for adapting to various heights and enhancing muscular strength through targeted stimuli. To begin with, one should start from a lower height and progressively increase the intensity and challenge, both in terms of height and distance with drops. This gradual build-up helps in developing resilience against impacts while ensuring safety throughout the process.nnWhile practicing drop techniques, maintaining good form and technique is vital. It is essential to avoid collapsing into a full squat when landing; rather, the goal should be to engage the quadriceps effectively. Proper body mechanics play a critical role in managing downward forces upon landing. Engaging the right muscles helps to dissipate impact efficiently, reducing the risk of injury while improving performance during high-impact movements.nnUltimately, emphasizing strength and proper technique during drop training will enhance overall jumping ability and athletic performance. Recognizing the importance of building strength through various stimuli is crucial in training. By consistently integrating these principles, one progresses not only in skill but also in the resilience required for high-impact activities.nnKey points:n1. Gradually incorporate impact and drop training to strengthen muscles and adapt to varying heights.n2. Focus on maintaining proper technique to efficiently manage forces during landings and reduce injury risks.n3. Consistent practice with attention to strength and form enhances jumping ability and overall athletic performance.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1311,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 280,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1591,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"9jajYX7JzHX8FjLUNBRZjQxxXYvwC9NgC2bpqSaEaLE-1735745060-1.0.1.1-yDvUns7k9asAKbrVlk_XT2daVOJ4H1I2QFvIog0pber_Vxcu_4XNp2PPMEyvK9vX4B2Ai7LfFo3x6xhXB9t_Ww\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746860,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"hDFglUkmjl3gNU9brUZFSe.owl6HtLOQ1HexLgKRHdw-1735745060481-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(27476,55229,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(27477,55229,'video_transcript_chatgpt','As proficiency in jumping increases, it becomes crucial to incorporate impact and drop training into your routine. These exercises serve as an essential method for adapting to various heights and enhancing muscular strength through targeted stimuli. To begin with, one should start from a lower height and progressively increase the intensity and challenge, both in terms of height and distance with drops. This gradual build-up helps in developing resilience against impacts while ensuring safety throughout the process.\r\n\r\nWhile practicing drop techniques, maintaining good form and technique is vital. It is essential to avoid collapsing into a full squat when landing; rather, the goal should be to engage the quadriceps effectively. Proper body mechanics play a critical role in managing downward forces upon landing. Engaging the right muscles helps to dissipate impact efficiently, reducing the risk of injury while improving performance during high-impact movements.\r\n\r\nUltimately, emphasizing strength and proper technique during drop training will enhance overall jumping ability and athletic performance. Recognizing the importance of building strength through various stimuli is crucial in training. By consistently integrating these principles, one progresses not only in skill but also in the resilience required for high-impact activities.\r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. Gradually incorporate impact and drop training to strengthen muscles and adapt to varying heights.\r\n2. Focus on maintaining proper technique to efficiently manage forces during landings and reduce injury risks.\r\n3. Consistent practice with attention to strength and form enhances jumping ability and overall athletic performance.'),(27478,55229,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(27479,55229,'svg_id',''),(27480,55229,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(27481,55229,'svg