ssistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"In performing a pole cat maneuver, the main goal is to execute a cat leap or arm jump towards a vertical pole such as a drain pipe or scaffolding. Proper landing technique is critical; one should focus on landing feet first to absorb impact through the legs. This technique encourages safety by ensuring that the arms are not the primary source of impact response as they serve mainly to grab the pole after landing.nnA successful landing requires a specific body posture for optimal momentum and stability. As one lands, it’s crucial that the hips do not lean back excessively, and the arms remain in a bent position to maintain balance. A rounded back or straight arms during landing can lead to improper posture, potentially increasing the risk of falling backward. Therefore, focus on keeping the arms drawn close to the body while bending the legs to cushion the landing.nnSafety is a major aspect of performing this technique, particularly concerning the type of pole one chooses to land on. It\'s advisable to check the integrity and material of the pole; metal poles are typically strong enough to handle weight, while plastic poles could be risky due to structural weaknesses. Ensuring the chosen surface is safe and stable is essential prior to attempting the pole cat to avoid accidents.nn**Key Points:**n1. Ensure a feet-first landing to distribute impact through the legs instead of the arms.n2. Maintain bent arms and avoid falling back to reduce risk of injury during the landing phase.n3. Always assess the strength and safety of the pole or surface prior to execution.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1989,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 300,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 2289,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"61lZbkkZ_pi0LMte2WyNdZwZCkmHh7IjFtgEixvGJuE-1735744441-1.0.1.1-afVQY158Hnx2AT_Gyiy04qkRYXEuXR57bnzb_nkkK2oiSWthJFVrXulhIic5XndFi6PJgjA3MX8snau5CPPcnQ\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746241,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"xAjbsRDEcc4iBb4usbYVUwrnM86AXvIeYHDPNXaAKws-1735744441040-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(30097,55255,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(30098,55255,'video_transcript_chatgpt','In performing a pole cat maneuver, the main goal is to execute a cat leap or arm jump towards a vertical pole such as a drain pipe or scaffolding. Proper landing technique is critical; one should focus on landing feet first to absorb impact through the legs. This technique encourages safety by ensuring that the arms are not the primary source of impact response as they serve mainly to grab the pole after landing.\r\n\r\nA successful landing requires a specific body posture for optimal momentum and stability. As one lands, it’s crucial that the hips do not lean back excessively, and the arms remain in a bent position to maintain balance. A rounded back or straight arms during landing can lead to improper posture, potentially increasing the risk of falling backward. Therefore, focus on keeping the arms drawn close to the body while bending the legs to cushion the landing.\r\n\r\nSafety is a major aspect of performing this technique, particularly concerning the type of pole one chooses to land on. It\'s advisable to check the integrity and material of the pole; metal poles are typically strong enough to handle weight, while plastic poles could be risky due to structural weaknesses. Ensuring the chosen surface is safe and stable is essential prior to attempting the pole cat to avoid accidents.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. Ensure a feet-first landing to distribute impact through the legs instead of the arms.\r\n2. Maintain bent arms and avoid falling back to reduce risk of injury during the landing phase.\r\n3. Always assess the strength and safety of the pole or surface prior to execution.'),(30099,55255,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(30100,55255,'svg_id',''),(30101,55255,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(30102,55255,'svg_colour',''),(30103,55255,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(30104,55255,'extra_variables',''),(30105,55255,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(30106,55255,'notes',''),(30107,55255,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(30108,55255,'enable_youtube_api',''),(30109,55255,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(30110,55255,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(30111,55255,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(30112,55255,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(30113,55255,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(30114,55255,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(30115,55255,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','f