oints:n1. The waste cat technique is best performed on lower walls to improve distance and accuracy in landing.n2. Key to successful execution are straight arms, legs, and proper alignment to prevent injuries during landing.n3. This technique provides a practical fallback for navigating gaps safely and effectively, increasing confidence in climbing and jumping transitions.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 2121,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 289,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 2410,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"tQXxAJY9yL9w5al42sEtUC9oq_VcEmRvaQFyCapXt1A-1735744389-1.0.1.1-Xx8YuY54yemn_lE.D7etqOvOEX5YZGRiE3xeugTmYJUtAa1k6hCfeEEhYxzEPVMEduvCjqiFQOUPmMKZxdP3xQ\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746189,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"LHGHuUPckcURREYyd_0qgpVREzClXFjNW3Ih1eKDqhk-1735744389450-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(30260,55256,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(30261,55256,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The waste cat technique is characterized by its execution on lower walls, improving the ability to cover distances efficiently. This maneuver emphasizes landing accurately, ideally with straight arms and feet first. Proper timing and trajectory are crucial to minimize jarring impacts on the arms, shoulders, and elbows. A successful landing feels smooth and comfortable, enabling practitioners to transition seamlessly into a vault or climb.\r\n\r\nWhen approaching the wall, focus on keeping the legs straight and toes pointed upwards. This posture helps prevent knees from striking the wall during landing, which can result in injury. Essential to mastering this technique is the proper alignment of the body; flat hands, straight arms, and a controlled descent foster safety and effectiveness. Repeating practice in diverse environments will aid in developing this essential skill.\r\n\r\nFinally, the waste cat technique serves as a valuable fallback for traversing gaps where distance is a concern, boosting confidence in the transition between climbing and jumping. Lower walls are generally more challenging due to the increased drop, but successfully mastering this skill allows for safer navigation in varied situations. Practicing this technique helps build proficiency in movement and adaptability in different environments.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The waste cat technique is best performed on lower walls to improve distance and accuracy in landing.\r\n2. Key to successful execution are straight arms, legs, and proper alignment to prevent injuries during landing.\r\n3. This technique provides a practical fallback for navigating gaps safely and effectively, increasing confidence in climbing and jumping transitions.'),(30262,55256,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(30263,55256,'svg_id',''),(30264,55256,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(30265,55256,'svg_colour',''),(30266,55256,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(30267,55256,'extra_variables',''),(30268,55256,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(30269,55256,'notes',''),(30270,55256,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(30271,55256,'enable_youtube_api',''),(30272,55256,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(30273,55256,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(30274,55256,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(30275,55256,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(30276,55256,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(30277,55256,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(30278,55256,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(30279,55256,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(30280,55256,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(30281,55256,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(30282,55256,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(30283,55256,'enable_transcript',''),(30284,55256,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(30285,55256,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(30286,55256,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(30287,55256,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I want this to sound like I wrote the result.'),(30288,55256,'_transcript_chatgpt_prompt','field_672214208bf31'),(30289,55256,'rank_math_primary_tutorial_category','0'),(30290,55256,'video_filename','Climbing-ArmJump/Tutorial-Climbing-Arm_Jump_5-Waist-cat.mp4'),(30291,55256,'_video_filename','field_677cead91f698'),(30292,55256,'portrait_thumbnail_image','Climbing-ArmJump/screenshots/Tutorial-Climbing-Arm_Jump_5-Waist-cat_3_4.png'),(30293,55256,'_portrait_thumbnail