r to enhance one\'s skills in performing higher jumps, regular practice is emphasized, particularly focusing on arm jumps. Practitioners are advised to develop comfort with the movements by repeatedly performing them and ensuring proper landing techniques, especially for larger jumps. The importance of a solid foundation in these basic drills before progressing to greater heights cannot be overstated, as mastering these fundamentals will contribute to improved performance.nnThe session suggests that even if the jumps aren\'t particularly high initially, they serve as critical steps in gaining the confidence necessary to tackle more challenging heights. Engaging in consistent practice not only aids in perfecting the technique but also helps athletes build the mental fortitude required to confront the fear associated with jumping from greater elevations. This gradual increase in difficulty allows for a smoother transition when approaching higher jumps.nnUltimately, the path to mastering higher jumps hinges on accumulating experience and overcoming fear through practice. Athletes are encouraged to focus on their prior successful performances as a reminder of their capabilities, which helps in reassessing the challenges presented by increased heights. Regular drills, confidence building, and familiarization with jump dynamics are key to achieving success in higher jump performances.nnKey Points:n1. Repeated practice and comfort with basic arm jumps are crucial for performing higher jumps.n2. Building confidence through gradual exposure to greater heights helps in overcoming fear.n3. Experience and mastering fundamentals are essential for successful performance in jumping.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 975,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 277,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1252,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"3MXooIWj7vAdxGLXo6Xdfd1x7bZiH0y017tcXd_Lx4s-1735744268-1.0.1.1-.LpcszMMc7_i7A_iDSfnIEh8XRtENb7qroRwpAC43PfX6xZUjwWSqkdIuoWAQ_fJLSKUjfIwDVBiSAhVEwnNkA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746068,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"oB4u0SVwXWXWHqQj7.weBDW8FgrlRpG2.YBJzk_ftvI-1735744268040-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(30931,55261,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(30932,55261,'video_transcript_chatgpt','In order to enhance one\'s skills in performing higher jumps, regular practice is emphasized, particularly focusing on arm jumps. Practitioners are advised to develop comfort with the movements by repeatedly performing them and ensuring proper landing techniques, especially for larger jumps. The importance of a solid foundation in these basic drills before progressing to greater heights cannot be overstated, as mastering these fundamentals will contribute to improved performance.\r\n\r\nThe session suggests that even if the jumps aren\'t particularly high initially, they serve as critical steps in gaining the confidence necessary to tackle more challenging heights. Engaging in consistent practice not only aids in perfecting the technique but also helps athletes build the mental fortitude required to confront the fear associated with jumping from greater elevations. This gradual increase in difficulty allows for a smoother transition when approaching higher jumps.\r\n\r\nUltimately, the path to mastering higher jumps hinges on accumulating experience and overcoming fear through practice. Athletes are encouraged to focus on their prior successful performances as a reminder of their capabilities, which helps in reassessing the challenges presented by increased heights. Regular drills, confidence building, and familiarization with jump dynamics are key to achieving success in higher jump performances.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. Repeated practice and comfort with basic arm jumps are crucial for performing higher jumps.\r\n2. Building confidence through gradual exposure to greater heights helps in overcoming fear.\r\n3. Experience and mastering fundamentals are essential for successful performance in jumping.'),(30933,55261,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(30934,55261,'svg_id',''),(30935,55261,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(30936,55261,'svg_colour',''),(30937,55261,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(30938,55261,'extra_variables',''),(30939,55261,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(30940,55261,'notes',''),(30941,55261,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(30942,55261,'enable_youtube_api',''),(30943,55261,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(30944,55261,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(30945,55261,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(30946,55261,'wordpres