the legs, where the knees may come in to assist with propulsion as they transition to a fully extended position after the pull.nnFor optimal practice, it is suggested to start with smaller gaps, such as those available at local playgrounds or along scaffolding structures. Building strength through variations of the double tap can significantly enhance one’s capabilities in more complex movements, like climb-ups and muscle-ups. With consistent practice, climbers can develop the upper body strength needed to execute this explosive movement more effectively.nn**Key Points:**n1. The double tap is a crucial movement technique for climbing, involving a transition between a lower and a higher bar.n2. Practicing with one hand leads to the eventual mastery of using both hands for a more explosive and coordinated motion.n3. Starting on smaller gaps and progressively working up can effectively enhance one\'s upper body strength and climbing skills.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 2676,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 339,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 3015,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0705bf87c0\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"0J_lNcnbX3COZkHgtgdVXKSwN5jV1srMHytq4i.aKKs-1733419430-1.0.1.1-hwT4hR6NMBzCeruFB3pr.YTgH8FR8EgSsma2huMp.hleWo.uJCCTQlbz7YzNTEsdHMVecE1SiOwIeMGrDQ.3bw\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1733421230,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"yV1xtAsozQCFST9DS6wyKGjaJu4MEQfruTtctiZiJEQ-1733419430064-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(31508,55267,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(31509,55267,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The concept of the \"double tap\" is introduced as a unique movement technique primarily used in climbing or navigating high bars. This movement involves transitioning from a lower bar to a higher bar in a fluid motion. Practicing this technique is crucial, as it requires a combination of strength, explosive power, and precise timing. The double tap is not something most people encounter often, making it even more essential for those looking to improve their climbing skills and overall upper body strength.\r\n\r\nTo perform the double tap, one typically begins by practicing the movement with one hand, using both arms to pull upwards while alternating the handhold. As proficiency increases, climbers are encouraged to execute the movement with both hands, requiring quick pulls and the ability to manage one’s body weight effectively. The initial phase of the double tap involves dynamic coordination of arms and the legs, where the knees may come in to assist with propulsion as they transition to a fully extended position after the pull.\r\n\r\nFor optimal practice, it is suggested to start with smaller gaps, such as those available at local playgrounds or along scaffolding structures. Building strength through variations of the double tap can significantly enhance one’s capabilities in more complex movements, like climb-ups and muscle-ups. With consistent practice, climbers can develop the upper body strength needed to execute this explosive movement more effectively.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. The double tap is a crucial movement technique for climbing, involving a transition between a lower and a higher bar.\r\n2. Practicing with one hand leads to the eventual mastery of using both hands for a more explosive and coordinated motion.\r\n3. Starting on smaller gaps and progressively working up can effectively enhance one\'s upper body strength and climbing skills.'),(31510,55267,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(31511,55267,'svg_id',''),(31512,55267,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(31513,55267,'svg_colour',''),(31514,55267,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(31515,55267,'extra_variables',''),(31516,55267,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(31517,55267,'notes',''),(31518,55267,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(31519,55267,'enable_youtube_api',''),(31520,55267,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(31521,55267,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(31522,55267,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(31523,55267,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(31524,55267,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(31525,55267,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(31526,55267,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(31527,55267,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs specifically focusing on the one-arm first:'),(31528,55267,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(31529,55267,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(31530,55267,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(31531,55267,'enable_transcript',''),(31532,55267,'_enable_transcript','fie