xed\" >🔸 <a class=\"underline hover:bg-green-500 hover:bg-green-800 text-green-500 hover:text-white\"  href=\"https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour\">https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour</a><br />\n🔸 <a class=\"underline hover:bg-green-500 hover:bg-green-800 text-green-500 hover:text-white\"  href=\"https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour\">https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour</a><br />\n🔸 contact@localhost:8443</p>'),(31639,55268,'_video_youtube_data_description_filtered','field_672253e91cdc8'),(31640,55268,'video_chatgpt_response','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": \"{n  \"id\": \"chatcmpl-Ab9u6sZKRZhmOdTIkNvJiJvFNxjce\",n  \"object\": \"chat.completion\",n  \"created\": 1733419570,n  \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",n  \"choices\": [n    {n      \"index\": 0,n      \"message\": {n        \"role\": \"assistant\",n        \"content\": \"The double-hand double-tap is an advanced parkour technique that requires precision and timing. It involves using both hands to tap or grip a surface as part of a fluid movement, allowing for greater upward momentum and control during tricks and jumps. Parkour enthusiasts often practice this technique to enhance their overall agility and capability when navigating urban environments, making it an essential skill for anyone serious about mastering parkour.nnTo execute the double-hand double-tap effectively, individuals need to focus on their hand placement and the timing of their movements. This technique typically starts with a jump or a vault towards a wall or a high surface. As the body is propelled upwards, both hands should make contact with the target area simultaneously, ensuring a strong grip that aids in maintaining balance and stability while transitioning to subsequent movements.nnPracticing the double-hand double-tap can lead to improved performance in various parkour maneuvers, such as wall runs, climbs, or flips. This technique not only improves physical strength but also boosts mental confidence in one\