nds to tap or grip a surface as part of a fluid movement, allowing for greater upward momentum and control during tricks and jumps. Parkour enthusiasts often practice this technique to enhance their overall agility and capability when navigating urban environments, making it an essential skill for anyone serious about mastering parkour.\n\nTo execute the double-hand double-tap effectively, individuals need to focus on their hand placement and the timing of their movements. This technique typically starts with a jump or a vault towards a wall or a high surface. As the body is propelled upwards, both hands should make contact with the target area simultaneously, ensuring a strong grip that aids in maintaining balance and stability while transitioning to subsequent movements.\n\nPracticing the double-hand double-tap can lead to improved performance in various parkour maneuvers, such as wall runs, climbs, or flips. This technique not only improves physical strength but also boosts mental confidence in one\'s ability to navigate complex environments efficiently. By incorporating the double-hand double-tap into their training routines, parkour practitioners can elevate their skills and expand their range of movements in exciting ways.'),(31643,55268,'_video_chatgpt_response_text','field_6722334bac798'),(31644,55268,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"let\'s take a look at what we call the\",\n        \"start\": 5.48,\n        \"duration\": 6.52\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"double tap now this is quite a unique\",\n        \"start\": 8.679,\n        \"duration\": 6.16\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"situation A Unique position here uh most\",\n        \"start\": 12,\n        \"duration\": 5.72\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"people wouldn\'t come across this uh the\",\n        \"start\": 14.839,\n        \"duration\": 6.001\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"rail to the rail but I wanted to use\",\n        \"start\": 17.72,\n        \"dur