script_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(32417,55275,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-Ab9p07EDycMy3xfqjRIITwVoSyOwZ\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1733419254,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"This transcript outlines an alternative method for climbing a parallel wall, which differs from the traditional back-to-the-wall approach. The climber employs a \"starfish\" position, utilizing one hand and one foot at a time to navigate the wall. This method requires finding a suitable gap where leverage is needed for the shoulders and arms, allowing for easier ascent despite the potential tightness of the wall configuration.nnThe technique involves a systematic shift of the climber\'s hands and feet, emphasizing the importance of tension in the hands while coordinating movements. By pushing off with the feet and repositioning the hands effectively, the climber can ascend without overwhelming difficulty. A focus is placed on creating a rhythm of pushing with the feet and hands alternately, ensuring balance and efficiency in motion.nnUltimately, by adopting this unique climbing style, climbers can effectively manage the challenges posed by narrow walls. This approach not only showcases versatility in climbing techniques but also highlights how proper body positioning and movement sequences can facilitate climbing, even in restrictive spaces. nnKey Points:n1. The climbing technique employs a \"starfish\" positioning with one hand and one foot on the wall at any time, instead of a traditional back-to-the-wall climb.n2. Leveraging body tension and rhythmically alternating hand and foot movements are crucial for maintaining balance and efficiency while ascending.n3. This method allows climbers to navigate narrow walls effectively, demonstrating adaptability in climbing approaches.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 876,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 285,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1161,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0705bf87c0\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"BrjhnfD9x8kPwLzT2lJ534QMxmFRTbUvgXBQbFVURes-1733419261-1.0.1.1-9U06dp3fb0rAvwt3S6hJhxItm2Uvba8iqBKaUhQ8IpSiQvG8DnksTJycqKgmZeUltjMW6WTtbr3usLw6NCr7pA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1733421061,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"5UYcUkKmSK7VnjJfB040kOijROPmbExOwwW9BhZ41Wg-1733419261637-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(32418,55275,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(32419,55275,'video_transcript_chatgpt','This transcript outlines an alternative method for climbing a parallel wall, which differs from the traditional back-to-the-wall approach. The climber employs a \"starfish\" position, utilizing one hand and one foot at a time to navigate the wall. This method requires finding a suitable gap where leverage is needed for the shoulders and arms, allowing for easier ascent despite the potential tightness of the wall configuration.\r\n\r\nThe technique involves a systematic shift of the climber\'s hands and feet, emphasizing the importance of tension in the hands while coordinating movements. By pushing off with the feet and repositioning the hands effectively, the climber can ascend without overwhelming difficulty. A focus is placed on creating a rhythm of pushing with the feet and hands alternately, ensuring balance and efficiency in motion.\r\n\r\nUltimately, by adopting this unique climbing style, climbers can effectively manage the challenges posed by narrow walls. This approach not only showcases versatility in climbing techniques but also highlights how proper body positioning and movement sequences can facilitate climbing, even in restrictive spaces. \r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The climbing technique employs a \"starfish\" positioning with one hand and one foot on the wall at any time, instead of a traditional back-to-the-wall climb.\r\n2. Leveraging body tension and rhythmically alternating hand and foot movements are crucial for maintaining balance and efficiency while ascending.\r\n3. This method allows climbers to navigate narrow walls effectively, demonstrating adaptability in climbing approaches.'),(32420,55275,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(32421,55275,'svg_id',''),(32422,55275,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(32423,55275,'svg_colour',''),(32424,55275,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(32425,55275,'extra_variables',''),(32426,55275,'_extra_va