-> 00:01:58,000\r\nlower abs and it means I can catch that\r\n\r\n37\r\n00:00:115,000 --> 00:01:59,000\r\nbar nice and solid\r\n\r\n'),(34109,55289,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(34110,55289,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-Akuwz8LCRVZgNCJn6WC6CGtjdQez4\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735745369,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The hip catch is an essential movement used in various athletic contexts, primarily focused on catching the body just below the hip bone while engaging the hands. This technique involves descending slowly onto the hip, allowing for a controlled transfer of weight. The placement is critical; it should be just above the groin and below the hip, ensuring the body can transition safely into subsequent movements, such as swings or vaults.nnWhen executed correctly, the hip catch serves as a way to manage momentum from larger jumps. By absorbing the impact through controlled descent, one can land safely on the bar, which minimizes the risk of injury. Essentially, this technique functions as a gradual reduction of force, allowing an athlete to maintain balance and momentum, facilitating a smooth transition into other aerial maneuvers.nnThe technique can also be applied at higher elevations, emphasizing its versatility in various scenarios. By positioning the body effectively, one can execute a hip catch even in more dynamic situations. This adaptability confirms the hip catch as a fundamental skill during athletic training, particularly for activities that involve rail access and aerial tricks.nnKey points:n1. The hip catch technique involves catching below the hip bone to allow for controlled momentum reduction during jumps.n2. Proper execution minimizes risk and ensures safe transitions into other movements like swings and vaults.n3. The hip catch can be adapted for higher jumps, highlighting its importance in various dynamic athletic scenarios.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1379,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 279,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1658,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"oD5gzpucgk2dbULkSaxBDx0DZGmdAV1xWT6Um99qYFU-1735745374-1.0.1.1-InIC_fVUw1Is08K7i1HULXh.YpjUAVmENszvgCAHGT1hnyMv5LVX9prAx1_a2DbzbxHHGNBEwR2QUENwYtw9rA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735747174,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"www9eJgXEBVZ7I7ZLT_wy206i7WrjZ8uF.kYsRYQvCo-1735745374977-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(34111,55289,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(34112,55289,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The hip catch is an essential movement used in various athletic contexts, primarily focused on catching the body just below the hip bone while engaging the hands. This technique involves descending slowly onto the hip, allowing for a controlled transfer of weight. The placement is critical; it should be just above the groin and below the hip, ensuring the body can transition safely into subsequent movements, such as swings or vaults.\r\n\r\nWhen executed correctly, the hip catch serves as a way to manage momentum from larger jumps. By absorbing the impact through controlled descent, one can land safely on the bar, which minimizes the risk of injury. Essentially, this technique functions as a gradual reduction of force, allowing an athlete to maintain balance and momentum, facilitating a smooth transition into other aerial maneuvers.\r\n\r\nThe technique can also be applied at higher elevations, emphasizing its versatility in various scenarios. By positioning the body effectively, one can execute a hip catch even in more dynamic situations. This adaptability confirms the hip catch as a fundamental skill during athletic training, particularly for activities that involve rail access and aerial tricks.\r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. The hip catch technique involves catching below the hip bone to allow for controlled momentum reduction during jumps.\r\n2. Proper execution minimizes risk and ensures safe transitions into other movements like swings and vaults.\r\n3. The hip catch can be adapted for higher jumps, highlighting its importance in various dynamic athletic scenarios.'),(34113,55289,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(34114,55289,'svg_id',''),(34115,55289,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(34116,55289,'svg_colour',''),(34117,55289,'_svg_colo