═════════════╝<br />\r\nSubscribe to channel: <a class=\"underline hover:bg-green-500 hover:bg-green-800 text-green-500 hover:text-white\"  href=\"https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_confirmation=1\">https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_confirmation=1</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"text-base leading-relaxed\" >╔══════════════════╗<br />\r\n║    🔗C O M P A N Y     ║<br />\r\n╚══════════════════╝</p>\r\n<p class=\"text-base leading-relaxed\" >🔹  <a class=\"underline hover:bg-green-500 hover:bg-green-800 text-green-500 hover:text-white\"  href=\"https://LONDONPARKOUR.COM\">https://LONDONPARKOUR.COM</a><br />\r\n🔹 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.</p>\r\n<p class=\"text-base leading-relaxed\" >🔸 <a class=\"underline hover:bg-green-500 hover:bg-green-800 text-green-500 hover:text-white\"  href=\"https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour\">https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour</a><br />\r\n🔸 <a class=\"underline hover:bg-green-500 hover:bg-green-800 text-green-500 hover:text-white\"  href=\"https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour\">https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour</a><br />\r\n🔸 contact@localhost:8443</p>'),(34955,55300,'_video_youtube_data_description_filtered','field_672253e91cdc8'),(34956,55300,'video_chatgpt_response','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": \"{n  \"id\": \"chatcmpl-Ab4qa26sHm9v7gfkcI7UTVSRGsq1b\",n  \"object\": \"chat.completion\",n  \"created\": 1733400132,n  \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",n  \"choices\": [n    {n      \"index\": 0,n      \"message\": {n        \"role\": \"assistant\",n        \"content\": \"London Parkour is an initiative focused on practical movement, aiming to change the way individuals think, move, and feel. The program provides various resources, including tutorials and guides, to help practitioners learn and develop their parkour skills effectively. By subscribing to their YouTube channel, followers can access a wealth of content designed to enhance their understanding and execution of parkour techniques.nnThe organization\'s website, LondonParkour.com, serves as a hub for all things related to parkour in London, offering visitors essential information and insights. By engaging with their content, including videos and social media posts, users can immerse themselves in the parkour community and discover new ways to improve their movement capabilities. They also offer opportunities for personal growth through physical activity and the development of new skills.nnAdditionally, London Parkour maintains a presence on social media platforms such as Instagram and YouTube, enhancing their reach and connection with followers. Users are encouraged to join the community by subscribing and following their accounts for the latest tutorials, updates, and parkour-related content. For inquiries, people can contact them via their email address, fostering a supportive and engaging environment for parkour enthusiasts.\",n        \"refusal\": nulln      },n      \"logprobs\": null,n      \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"n    }n  ],n  \"usage\": {n    \"prompt_tokens\": 232,n    \"completion_tokens\": 230,n    \"total_tokens\": 462,n    \"prompt_tokens_details\": {n      \"cached_tokens\": 0,n      \"audio_tokens\": 0n    },n    \"completion_tokens_details\": {n      \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,n      \"audio_tokens\": 0,n      \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,n      \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0n    }n  },n  \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0705bf87c0\"n}n\",\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"nSSL.6pO_ztlMUAzoxyImXI8Pe1dAmQBLhYNPcPkDww-1733400135-1.0.1.1-pF0ah_5OHoUKJvLXgMFnn5_HFJnc.Kg0c4rF4aQm9AG8bu1Op_4gX5uHVtGUxfc5My4ZPXjlObiBsCbLJ1Bddg\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1733401935,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"FRa3HlHVzB1vhf5m_Ti0wmePHP9q4LVviTOMh2CJbH8-1733400135802-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(34957,55300,'_video_chatgpt_response','field_67221dc82655d'),(34958,55300,'video_chatgpt_response_text','London Parkour is an initiative focused on practical movement, aiming to change the way individuals think, move, and feel. The program provides various resources, including tutorials and guides, to help practitioners learn and develop their parkour skills effectively. By subscribing to their YouTube channel, followers can access a wealth of content designed to enhance their understanding and execution of parkour techniques.\r\n\r\nThe organization\'s website, LondonParkour.com, serves as a hub for all things related to parkour in London, offering visitors essential information and insights. By engaging with their content, including videos and social media posts, users can immerse themselves in the parkour community and discover new ways to improve their movement capabilities. They also offer opportunities for personal growth through physical activity and the development of new skills.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, London Parkour maintains a presence on social media platforms such as Instagram and YouTube, enhancing their reach and connection with followers. Users are encouraged to join the community by subscribing and following their accounts for the latest tutorials, updates, and parkour-related content. For inquiries, people can contact them via their email address, fostering a supportive and engaging environment for parkour enthusiasts.'),(34959,55300,'_video_chatgpt_response_text','field_6722334bac798'),(34960,55300,'video_transcript_json','[\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"let\'s examine the quadraped movement\",\r\n        \"start\": 5.759,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.361\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"so sometimes abbreviated to qm\",\r\n        \"start\": 10.599,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.561\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"quadrupedal movement is moving on all\",\r\n        \"start\": 14.12,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.44\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"fours and there are many many ways of\",\r\n        \"start\": 17.16,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.279\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"doing this the basic\",\r\n        \"start\": 20.56,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.799\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"qm movement what we sometimes call\",\r\n        \"start\": 23.439,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.721\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"monkey walking is to alternate the hands\",\r\n        \"start\": 26.359,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.281\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"and feet so to start with you\'re going\",\r\n        \"start\": 31.16,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.399\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"to go into a press up\",\r\n        \"start\": 33.64,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"position so let\'s do this sideways press\",\r\n        \"start\": 35.559,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.761\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"up position the right hand is going to\",\r\n        \"start\": 38.32,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.36\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"go forwards and then the left foot is\",\r\n        \"start\": 40.32,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.88\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"going to go forwards something that\",\r\n        \"start\": 42.68,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.76\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"happens a lot is people put this foot\",\r\n        \"start\": 45.2,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.64\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"far too forward and it causes issues\",\r\n        \"start\": 47.44,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.439\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"because as I then step I\'m then going to\",\r\n        \"start\": 50.84,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.44\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"end up with my butt in the air so don\'t\",\r\n        \"start\": 52.879,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.041\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"go too forward with the foot just take a\",\r\n        \"start\": 55.28,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.72\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"small 20 cm step forwards now it\'s the\",\r\n        \"start\": 58.92,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.44\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"alternate hand and foot then move\",\r\n        \"start\": 63,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.24\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"forward so my right foot left\",\r\n        \"start\": 65.36,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.079\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"hand\",\r\n        \"start\": 70.24,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.559\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"and\",\r\n        \"start\": 72.439,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.121\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"alternating backwards and forwards this\",\r\n        \"start\": 74.799,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"is qm it\'s just the basic movement of\",\r\n        \"start\": 78.56,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.04\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"opposite hand and foot going forward\",\r\n        \"start\": 82.479,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.521\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"going back and keeping at a low level\",\r\n        \"start\": 85.6,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.519\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"it\'s called Low gate work um where yeah\",\r\n        \"start\": 89,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.6\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"you\'re under control and you can move\",\r\n        \"start\": 92.119,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.441\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"forwards and backwards just on all fours\",\r\n        \"start\": 95.6,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.839\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"practice that it can actually be quite\",\r\n        \"start\": 98.56,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.36\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"taxing especially over long distances\",\r\n        \"start\": 100.439,\r\n        \"duration\": 5\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"it\'s a good warmup because it\'s very low\",\r\n        \"start\": 102.92,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.64\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"impact um but you know on long distances\",\r\n        \"start\": 105.439,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.64\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"it\'s a great warm-up uh technique to use\",\r\n        \"start\": 108.56,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.519\r\n    }\r\n]'),(34961,55300,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(34962,55300,'video_transcript_srt','1\r\n00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:13,000\r\nlet\'s examine the quadraped movement\r\n\r\n2\r\n00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000\r\nso sometimes abbreviated to qm\r\n\r\n3\r\n00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000\r\nquadrupedal movement is moving on all\r\n\r\n4\r\n00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000\r\nfours and there are many many ways of\r\n\r\n5\r\n00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000\r\ndoing this the basic\r\n\r\n6\r\n00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000\r\nqm movement what we sometimes call\r\n\r\n7\r\n00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000\r\nmonkey walking is to alternate the hands\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000\r\nand feet so to start with you\'re going\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,000\r\nto go into a press up\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000\r\nposition so let\'s do this sideways press\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,000\r\nup position the right hand is going to\r