ed\": 1735745200,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The gorilla run is an exercise variant that differs from a standard monkey walk by introducing a 45-degree turn. This technique involves a crouched position while pulling forward, allowing for a faster and more dynamic movement compared to traditional movements. Participants are guided to position their hands and feet in a specific pattern that promotes agility and coordination, setting the stage for an intense physical workout.nnTo perform the gorilla run, individuals need to start by crouching down and facing 45 degrees to one side, using their hands and feet in a coordinated sequence. The essential movement consists of a rhythm of hand and foot placements that ensures balance and momentum. As participants become familiar with the movement, they are encouraged to increase their speed, significantly elevating the workout intensity compared to the monkey walk.nnAn important aspect of this exercise is the emphasis on practicing the movement from both sides, ensuring balanced development and strength. By exploring the acceleration potential of the gorilla run, individuals can achieve a more vigorous workout that enhances their overall fitness levels. This dynamic activity offers an engaging way to break a sweat and challenge body mechanics effectively.nnKey Points:n1. The gorilla run involves a 45-degree turn and is faster than the traditional monkey walk, incorporating a dynamic crouched movement.n2. Proper technique includes a sequence involving hands and feet to promote agility and coordination, allowing for increased intensity as participants gain familiarity.n3. Practicing the movement from both sides is crucial for balanced strength development and maximizing workout effectiveness.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1014,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 298,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1312,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"EZ6BhoCvW2SKUQHrISk7aiGtUb8kQhQkr2cBhv93Ofw-1735745205-1.0.1.1-vtkA8HJ6fpektDrTjBlghFEy6s5ipAj3OOMcDL20dH.aI.R3VrJ12p_QxRLQ0eRExpxf6XBcd5DjvS2g4peMlA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735747005,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"egmTUxGVPBHJkwzu7kyEeTi1OFePhFnGjKaZQTppGwc-1735745205988-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(35883,55307,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(35884,55307,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The gorilla run is an exercise variant that differs from a standard monkey walk by introducing a 45-degree turn. This technique involves a crouched position while pulling forward, allowing for a faster and more dynamic movement compared to traditional movements. Participants are guided to position their hands and feet in a specific pattern that promotes agility and coordination, setting the stage for an intense physical workout.\r\n\r\nTo perform the gorilla run, individuals need to start by crouching down and facing 45 degrees to one side, using their hands and feet in a coordinated sequence. The essential movement consists of a rhythm of hand and foot placements that ensures balance and momentum. As participants become familiar with the movement, they are encouraged to increase their speed, significantly elevating the workout intensity compared to the monkey walk.\r\n\r\nAn important aspect of this exercise is the emphasis on practicing the movement from both sides, ensuring balanced development and strength. By exploring the acceleration potential of the gorilla run, individuals can achieve a more vigorous workout that enhances their overall fitness levels. This dynamic activity offers an engaging way to break a sweat and challenge body mechanics effectively.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The gorilla run involves a 45-degree turn and is faster than the traditional monkey walk, incorporating a dynamic crouched movement.\r\n2. Proper technique includes a sequence involving hands and feet to promote agility and coordination, allowing for increased intensity as participants gain familiarity.\r\n3. Practicing the movement from both sides is crucial for balanced strength development and maximizing workout effectiveness.'),(35885,55307,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(35886,55307,'svg_id',''),(35887,55307,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(35888,55307,'svg_colour',''),(35889,55307,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(35890,55307,'extra_variables',''),(35891,55307,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e54