th the legs opened wider, enabling a bouncier motion and allowing the head to move up and down. Both methods are effective in targeting leg muscles while providing different challenges and benefits.nnIncorporating the duck walk into warm-up routines is also suggested, especially before engaging in jumping exercises, as it works the quadriceps and helps prepare the body for more vigorous activities. Experimenting with both styles of the duck walk can enhance muscle engagement and stability while minimizing injury risk.nnKey Points:n1. The duck walk is an effective exercise for strengthening the quadriceps and should be performed with proper form to avoid knee strain.n2. There are two key variations of the duck walk: one that maintains a stable head position with closed legs, and another that allows for more freedom with wider leg positioning.n3. Incorporating the duck walk into warm-up routines can help prepare the muscles for more intensive physical activities.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1449,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 306,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1755,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \".ycjTxjalC2oxhBcaH2WgRvIEE7CGjy047VUlu0eiMU-1735745215-1.0.1.1-49Bfq9rGTYZtwKYiT0pcTil1NsqzMMJVpPg0BoN3kXb6YFWavdoZOrXzdM6twHEdrti6nSCCfNE.8mR6DZy5vg\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735747015,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"i4tZ_yD2neDZf6xigPq54o4fKFXIL6ZyRQRQvi6jwXA-1735745215048-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(36014,55308,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(36015,55308,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The technique of the duck walk is highlighted as a beneficial exercise, particularly for targeting the quadriceps. As one engages in this exercise, it is crucial to maintain a proper form, including keeping the head at a consistent level while walking. The focus is on the position of the feet and knees, emphasizing the importance of care to avoid putting too much strain on the knees and tendons. \r\n\r\nTwo variations of the duck walk are described. The first emphasizes a compact stance where the knees are bent, and the individual walks forward or sideways while maintaining the head\'s height. In contrast, the second variation allows for more freedom of movement with the legs opened wider, enabling a bouncier motion and allowing the head to move up and down. Both methods are effective in targeting leg muscles while providing different challenges and benefits.\r\n\r\nIncorporating the duck walk into warm-up routines is also suggested, especially before engaging in jumping exercises, as it works the quadriceps and helps prepare the body for more vigorous activities. Experimenting with both styles of the duck walk can enhance muscle engagement and stability while minimizing injury risk.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The duck walk is an effective exercise for strengthening the quadriceps and should be performed with proper form to avoid knee strain.\r\n2. There are two key variations of the duck walk: one that maintains a stable head position with closed legs, and another that allows for more freedom with wider leg positioning.\r\n3. Incorporating the duck walk into warm-up routines can help prepare the muscles for more intensive physical activities.'),(36016,55308,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(36017,55308,'svg_id',''),(36018,55308,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(36019,55308,'svg_colour',''),(36020,55308,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(36021,55308,'extra_variables',''),(36022,55308,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(36023,55308,'notes',''),(36024,55308,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(36025,55308,'enable_youtube_api',''),(36026,55308,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(36027,55308,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(36028,55308,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(36029,55308,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(36030,55308,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(36031,55308,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(36032,55308,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(36033,55308,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(36034,55308,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(36035,55308,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(36036,55308,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(36037,55308,'enable_transcript',''),(36038,55308,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(36039,55308,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(36040,55308,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(36041,55308,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise 