\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000\r\nground at the same time so as you go\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,000\r\nunder you can hop through and drive with\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000\r\nboth feet and it means that uh yeah you\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000\r\ncan spin and turn quite quickly and\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000\r\nyou\'ve got speed as you do this um you\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000\r\nhave to have confidence to get your knee\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000\r\nthrough but to have that confidence\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000\r\nyou\'ve really got to drive it um up and\r\n\r\n16\r\n00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000\r\ntowards the direction so if you go under\r\n\r\n17\r\n00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000\r\nand you\'re quite lazy and you sort of\r\n\r\n18\r\n00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000\r\nlike bring the knee up and you\'re not\r\n\r\n19\r\n00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000\r\nlike twisting then yeah it\'s going to be\r\n\r\n20\r\n00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,000\r\nmore likely you\'ll whack your knee knee\r\n\r\n21\r\n00:00:60,000 --> 00:01:05,000\r\non the bar really twist direct that knee\r\n\r\n22\r\n00:00:63,000 --> 00:01:08,000\r\nand you\'ll get speed so let\'s go again\r\n\r\n23\r\n00:00:65,000 --> 00:01:11,000\r\nso from here under there there and\r\n\r\n24\r\n00:00:69,000 --> 00:01:12,000\r\nthat\'s the underbar\r\n\r\n'),(36610,55312,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(36611,55312,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AkuqfHDFkuEHGXFOAmldTZTjbw389\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735744977,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The transcript outlines a progression on a physical movement often described as an underbar technique, focusing on the coordination of knees and feet during execution. Initially, it discusses the importance of speed as it pertains to lifting both knees simultaneously off the ground while moving through the bar. This combination not only aids in fluidity but also enhances the ability to spin and make quick turns, essential for agility in this movement.nnConfidence plays a crucial role in successfully performing this technique. It emphasizes the need to drive the knees upward and toward the direction of the movement; a lack of proper technique — such as laziness or not twisting the body adequately — can lead to potential injuries, specifically knee impacts with the bar. Proper alignment and motion are critical to maintaining speed and preventing mishaps during the maneuver.nnThe session appears to culminate in a practical demonstration of the described technique, encouraging individuals to attempt the underbar movement as outlined. The overall takeaway highlights the need for intentional movements, precise positioning of the body parts involved, and a commitment to practice in order to embed these skills effectively.nnKey Points:n1. Speed and coordination are vital for executing the underbar technique effectively, particularly the simultaneous lift of both knees.n2. Confidence and correct body alignment greatly influence the success of the movement, reducing the risk of injury.n3. Practicing the technique with focus on proper form and intent can enhance agility and fluidity during execution.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 911,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 282,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1193,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_to