 on the bar.nnThe next phase involves executing a rotation while maintaining one hand connected to the bar. This process includes letting go with one hand, swinging around, and then re-grabbing the bar in a different direction. This technique may feel intimidating at first, as the body turns and the view changes during the motion. A pronated grip is emphasized for better control and efficiency during subsequent movements like cat leaps and arm jumps, which utilize this grip frequently.nnAfter practicing the one-handed technique, moving onto the two-handed turn introduces more power and height. This variation requires letting go with both hands while simultaneously turning and then regrabbing the bar upon descent. Although this step is more complex, frequent practice will enhance proficiency and reduce apprehension. Establishing a solid routine in these movements forms a strong basis for executing more advanced maneuvers in the future.nn**Key Points:**n1. Begin with the one-arm dead hang to build strength before progressing to turn movements.n2. Execute the turn by swinging and rotating around one arm while maintaining a firm grip.n3. Transition to the two-handed turn for increased power, practice regularly to build confidence and skill in these techniques.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 2547,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 332,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 2879,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"EJ2dH3AZAgJmFXEcVAgJF3LjqTrmi1IIXxo90ZIxWFE-1735744760-1.0.1.1-VNPFNWiPypdOatcevz9Or1mLnwQz1WA1HgbReMNhuG5sE9QrkEGmwB9_ge.S584oV6bcber.l5g7oxvnOrHl6w\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746560,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"JcQnyFq.V7ApZK18e8Eh.M1tUhBGx2Jzn3EhxZQ7RO0-1735744760002-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(38207,55326,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(38208,55326,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Practicing the \"turn\" movement can be approached in several ways, with an emphasis on starting slowly to build confidence. The one-arm dead hang is recommended as an initial exercise to improve strength and familiarity with the technique. It involves hanging on one arm for a short period, which helps set the foundation for more advanced movements. Additionally, transitioning into a \"turn\" requires a solid understanding of the dead hang, where you will need to turn and swing your body while maintaining a grip on the bar.\r\n\r\nThe next phase involves executing a rotation while maintaining one hand connected to the bar. This process includes letting go with one hand, swinging around, and then re-grabbing the bar in a different direction. This technique may feel intimidating at first, as the body turns and the view changes during the motion. A pronated grip is emphasized for better control and efficiency during subsequent movements like cat leaps and arm jumps, which utilize this grip frequently.\r\n\r\nAfter practicing the one-handed technique, moving onto the two-handed turn introduces more power and height. This variation requires letting go with both hands while simultaneously turning and then regrabbing the bar upon descent. Although this step is more complex, frequent practice will enhance proficiency and reduce apprehension. Establishing a solid routine in these movements forms a strong basis for executing more advanced maneuvers in the future.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. Begin with the one-arm dead hang to build strength before progressing to turn movements.\r\n2. Execute the turn by swinging and rotating around one arm while maintaining a firm grip.\r\n3. Transition to the two-handed turn for increased power, practice regularly to build confidence and skill in these techniques.'),(38209,55326,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(38210,55326,'svg_id',''),(38211,55326,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(38212,55326,'svg_colour',''),(38213,55326,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(38214,55326,'extra_variables',''),(38215,55326,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(38216,55326,'notes',''),(38217,55326,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(38218,55326,'enable_youtube_api',''),(38219,55326,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(38220,55326,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(38221,55326,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(38222,55326,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(38223,55326,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(38224,55326,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(38225,55326,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(38226,55326,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(38227,55326,'_youtube_chatgp