n performing a rotational swing around a perpendicular bar, an apparatus commonly used in gymnastics and calisthenics. The process starts with the individual grabbing as high as possible on the bar. Depending on the direction (to the right or left), one hand is positioned higher while the other supports balance. The person must keep their knees bent and aim for a compact position while executing the movement.nnAs the swing progresses, the practitioner is encouraged to build confidence gradually by starting with a smaller angle and increasing it as they feel more secure. A critical aspect of the swing is maintaining bent arms, which helps sustain elevation. This position allows for more rotation around the bar while keeping the upper body tight, primarily focusing on controlling the knees and maintaining an optimal grip throughout the maneuver.nnOverall, practice is advised to master the swing, with particular emphasis on safety, such as keeping an eye on overhead obstacles. As the technique improves, the swing can become more expansive, allowing the individual to navigate through the motion effectively. Understanding the nuances of grip, body positioning, and angle adjustments is essential for success in this skill.nnKey Points:n1. Mastery of the rotational swing around a perpendicular bar begins with a secure grip and proper body positioning, especially keeping the arms bent.n2. Gradual progression in swing angle is advised to build confidence and ensure safety during the maneuver.n3. Maintaining a compact posture, with knees bent and a tight upper body, is crucial for achieving the best rotation and control around the bar.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1399,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 304,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1703,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"u3w3aU725gmgv9pJI1Ah0hjGGOhNLHaeVyihrxnNXz0-1735745384-1.0.1.1-g3RefYISEsI3pWlWy3NCdhp2VbbjJyd_SzISXOLOxSAQLA6M_i729NzVywczCD0T9saikZX87KdSksE8arHj5Q\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735747184,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"3HDL13c35wrruNp_u9ScAoLLeIgT.rACvnuJu_gFTaw-1735745384701-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(38992,55335,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(38993,55335,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The technique discussed centers on performing a rotational swing around a perpendicular bar, an apparatus commonly used in gymnastics and calisthenics. The process starts with the individual grabbing as high as possible on the bar. Depending on the direction (to the right or left), one hand is positioned higher while the other supports balance. The person must keep their knees bent and aim for a compact position while executing the movement.\r\n\r\nAs the swing progresses, the practitioner is encouraged to build confidence gradually by starting with a smaller angle and increasing it as they feel more secure. A critical aspect of the swing is maintaining bent arms, which helps sustain elevation. This position allows for more rotation around the bar while keeping the upper body tight, primarily focusing on controlling the knees and maintaining an optimal grip throughout the maneuver.\r\n\r\nOverall, practice is advised to master the swing, with particular emphasis on safety, such as keeping an eye on overhead obstacles. As the technique improves, the swing can become more expansive, allowing the individual to navigate through the motion effectively. Understanding the nuances of grip, body positioning, and angle adjustments is essential for success in this skill.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. Mastery of the rotational swing around a perpendicular bar begins with a secure grip and proper body positioning, especially keeping the arms bent.\r\n2. Gradual progression in swing angle is advised to build confidence and ensure safety during the maneuver.\r\n3. Maintaining a compact posture, with knees bent and a tight upper body, is crucial for achieving the best rotation and control around the bar.'),(38994,55335,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(38995,55335,'svg_id',''),(38996,55335,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(38997,55335,'svg_colour',''),(38998,55335,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(38999,55335,'extra_variables',''),(39000,55335,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(39001,55335,'notes',''),(39002,55335,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(39003,55335,'enable_youtube_api',''),(39004,55335,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(39005,55335,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(39006,55335,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(39007,55335,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(39008,55335,'_wordpress_fi