w pushing with one hand make sure\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,000\r\nyou do both hands you\'re practicing with\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000\r\nboth uh nice and quick nice and short\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000\r\nbut it\'s good to get that pressure on\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000\r\none hand\r\n\r\n'),(39346,55339,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(39347,55339,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-Akuu3q6pxPnrItdCywulWHfSkP9Qi\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735745187,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The discussion revolves around a one-handed frog technique, which is related to standard frog movements but focuses on using only one hand. This method is particularly beneficial for practicing transitions over obstacles such as barriers or blocks. By adopting this approach, individuals can enhance their ability to maneuver and adapt their techniques while maintaining balance and control.nnA significant aspect of this practice is the emphasis on pushing with one hand while also ensuring to incorporate both hands in training. This balancing act is crucial for developing strength and proficiency in executing moves efficiently and effectively. Practicing both aspects helps to reinforce muscle memory and improve overall performance in a variety of physical activities.nnThe exercise is described as being quick and short in duration but has substantial benefits. By focusing on pressure and control with one hand, practitioners can build up their skills in a structured way that complements traditional techniques. Overall, this one-handed frog technique provides an opportunity for individuals to challenge themselves and refine their abilities.nn**Key Points:**n1. The one-handed frog technique enhances maneuverability over obstacles by focusing on using one hand.n2. It is important to practice with both hands to develop overall strength and muscle memory.n3. This exercise is quick and straightforward, offering significant benefits in control and technique refinement.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 499,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 246,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 745,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"8PmK4ix09Gy0C_ykUk8RumZSkzgtqeuJOev6MnICKcs-1735745193-1.0.1.1-gSdmhoXjmjDwg8ziA.94me6cWrV1yZMmK3ru3L1.gDrc5E62V_skiMOeUlIrN3R5Di1gkvfZNntkC9.7JBmlvQ\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746993,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"MDeRzpgQcppzEJ.albq89i0LSPw.eKW3xml.AlIdBMc-1735745193061-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(39348,55339,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(39349,55339,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The discussion revolves around a one-handed frog technique, which is related to standard frog movements but focuses on using only one hand. This method is particularly beneficial for practicing transitions over obstacles such as barriers or blocks. By adopting this approach, individuals can enhance their ability to maneuver and adapt their techniques while maintaining balance and control.\r\n\r\nA significant aspect of this practice is the emphasis on pushing with one hand while also ensuring to incorporate both hands in training. This balancing act is crucial for developing strength and proficiency in executing moves efficiently and effectively. Practicing both aspects helps to reinforce muscle memory and improve overall performance in a variety of physical activities.\r\n\r\nThe exercise is described as being quick and short in duration but has substantial benefits. By focusing on pressure and control with one hand, practitioners can build up their skills in a structured way that complements traditional techniques. Overall, this one-handed frog technique provides an opportunity for individuals to challenge themselves and refine their abilities.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. The one-handed frog technique enhances maneuverability over obstacles by focusing on using one hand.\r\n2. It is important to practice with both hands to develop overall strength and muscle memory.\r\n3. This exercise is quick and straightforward, offering significant benefits in control and technique refinement.'),(39350,55339,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(39351,55339,'svg_id',''),(39352,55339,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(3