oices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The Vault roll begins with a cat pass, which seamlessly transitions into a roll. To master this movement, practitioners can break down the skills into separate components, training each individually before integrating them. This gradual approach allows one to develop a fluid motion between the two techniques. When setting up for practice, finding a wall next to a grassy area is advised to minimize injury risk when training rolls.nnOnce a comfort level is established with performing individual movements, practitioners can increase their speed in transitioning from the cat pass to the roll. The goal is to execute the cat pass without a pause, culminating in an efficient and smooth transition into the roll. In this advanced version, both movements should be fluid, with an emphasis placed on the execution. Practicing this technique will develop a stronger foundation for more advanced vaulting skills and maneuvers.nnDuring the roll, the hands and arms play a crucial role in absorbing the impact. Proper technique involves rolling from the shoulder across to the hip, ensuring a safe landing. The approach encourages fun and experimentation while honing skills. Moreover, reinforcing practice in a safe environment, such as on grass, is vital for successful training.nn**Key Points:**n1. The Vault roll involves a cat pass followed by a roll, and practitioners should train these movements separately before combining them for fluidity.n2. Increasing speed and executing both movements seamlessly is crucial for proficiency in advanced vaulting techniques.n3. Proper technique during the roll involves using the hands and arms to absorb impact, with emphasis on practicing in a safe environment.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1860,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 308,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 2168,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"CtOYiZ582LFN0WlJ5j59Wxk7SQ5rYIG91EUqhHIXBMI-1735744902-1.0.1.1-DeQEj_dTgF06HfnHu8YZU_d6GSUHsRXWlaPrF94PQM4aXpEDdQPafA_CCszO8UTxrKMxscrMe.wFKEmU5ClRMg\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746702,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"Dq1IxAF6dH4rbz.M7lTwMlTHdtQSE_4iiZTsBDkkQTI-1735744902624-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(41528,55363,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(41529,55363,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The Vault roll begins with a cat pass, which seamlessly transitions into a roll. To master this movement, practitioners can break down the skills into separate components, training each individually before integrating them. This gradual approach allows one to develop a fluid motion between the two techniques. When setting up for practice, finding a wall next to a grassy area is advised to minimize injury risk when training rolls.\r\n\r\nOnce a comfort level is established with performing individual movements, practitioners can increase their speed in transitioning from the cat pass to the roll. The goal is to execute the cat pass without a pause, culminating in an efficient and smooth transition into the roll. In this advanced version, both movements should be fluid, with an emphasis placed on the execution. Practicing this technique will develop a stronger foundation for more advanced vaulting skills and maneuvers.\r\n\r\nDuring the roll, the hands and arms play a crucial role in absorbing the impact. Proper technique involves rolling from the shoulder across to the hip, ensuring a safe landing. The approach encourages fun and experimentation while honing skills. Moreover, reinforcing practice in a safe environment, such as on grass, is vital for successful training.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. The Vault roll involves a cat pass followed by a roll, and practitioners should train these movements separately before combining them for fluidity.\r\n2. Increasing speed and executing both movements seamlessly is crucial for proficiency in advanced vaulting techniques.\r\n3. Proper technique during the roll involves using the hands and arms to absorb impact, with emphasis on practicing in a safe environment.'),(41530,55363,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(41531,55363,'svg_id',''),(41532,55363,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(41533,55363,'svg_colour',''),(41534,55363,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(41535,55363,'extra_variables',''),(41536,55363,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(41537,55363,'notes',''),(41538,55363,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(41539,55363,'enable_youtube_