message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The discussion focuses on performing the Palm spin, which is a rotational movement that aids in overcoming obstacles, particularly those with angles of 90 degrees or more. The initial stage of learning involves positioning one hand on a oblique surface and hopping onto a block, using the hands to gain momentum and control while jumping around the corner. As comfort increases, the practitioner should aim for less jumping and more lateral distance, landing further away each time to develop confidence in the movement.nnKey techniques for mastering the Palm spin include maintaining a downward gaze to enhance stability and balance. It is essential to keep the head down and focus on a spot directly below the obstacle rather than looking up. This practice minimizes the tendency to arch the back excessively, resulting in tighter, quicker turns. With consistent practice, ensuring that the body remains close to the obstacle allows for a more efficient and smoother rotation.nnThe final stage involves transitioning fully into the Palm spin, where the individual must rely on their arms significantly while navigating the turn. Aiming to achieve a full 270-degree rotation while leaning on the arm ensures that weight is appropriately distributed, allowing for an effective spin. Progress can be tracked with chalk marks to visualize improvement and set goals, encouraging a gradual enhancement of the technique.nnKey points:n1. The Palm spin is initiated by incorporating hand placements and controlled jumping to navigate around corners.n2. Maintaining focus on a point below the obstacle helps improve stability and tighter turns.n3. Assessing progress with visual markers can aid in goal setting and enhancing overall performance of the Palm spin.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 3074,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 310,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 3384,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"QTFpKHxPhegLH3VCIF3bF0PK_BkI91NK1SPBZ7eNbMA-1735744854-1.0.1.1-mpcvgt0IGA7D0Af3dcflQNDZvN22NFPpKUFH0Qt1vmt6D9LmEO7EHV3Q1sUD7xPX.DRD3wB0tdnOYQWS0v8_3g\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746654,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"TKh3C6xVhG1YQUhl7Iu7g6aZIuJmELeRlgoeohzrVXw-1735744854291-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(42530,55370,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(42531,55370,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The discussion focuses on performing the Palm spin, which is a rotational movement that aids in overcoming obstacles, particularly those with angles of 90 degrees or more. The initial stage of learning involves positioning one hand on a oblique surface and hopping onto a block, using the hands to gain momentum and control while jumping around the corner. As comfort increases, the practitioner should aim for less jumping and more lateral distance, landing further away each time to develop confidence in the movement.\r\n\r\nKey techniques for mastering the Palm spin include maintaining a downward gaze to enhance stability and balance. It is essential to keep the head down and focus on a spot directly below the obstacle rather than looking up. This practice minimizes the tendency to arch the back excessively, resulting in tighter, quicker turns. With consistent practice, ensuring that the body remains close to the obstacle allows for a more efficient and smoother rotation.\r\n\r\nThe final stage involves transitioning fully into the Palm spin, where the individual must rely on their arms significantly while navigating the turn. Aiming to achieve a full 270-degree rotation while leaning on the arm ensures that weight is appropriately distributed, allowing for an effective spin. Progress can be tracked with chalk marks to visualize improvement and set goals, encouraging a gradual enhancement of the technique.\r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. The Palm spin is initiated by incorporating hand placements and controlled jumping to navigate around corners.\r\n2. Maintaining focus on a point below the obstacle helps improve stability and tighter turns.\r\n3. Assessing progress with visual markers can aid in goal setting and enhancing overall performance of the Palm spin.'),(42532,55370,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(42533,55370,'svg_id',''),(42534,55370,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(42535,55370,'svg_colour',''),(42536,55370,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(42537,55370,'extra_variables',''),(42538,55370,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(42539,55370,'notes',''),(42540,55370,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(42541,5537