arding experience, encouraging individuals to push their limits while mastering the techniques involved.nnKey Points:n1. The combination of a Tic Tac to a 360-degree step Vault promotes fluid movement and spatial awareness.n2. Practicing the techniques slowly facilitates better form and comfort before increasing speed.n3. Balanced practice on both sides is crucial for skill development and agility in executing the movements.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1197,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 276,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1473,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"Cw50.i64eVFEB_ypsPbmTOtwljwcB36WZa39H7IbH3c-1735744570-1.0.1.1-is_dZ_aRLiHpHZs6ahHyR273j7EA6dc1iffyREGq_kTKJCymMwC5E4pmMXypsI3S2UISGzRQtl5ziBdNsLDMwQ\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746370,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \".3tSdThEh5KyYSOlJWSbq0BSDWpC_AQ07aGLuf0b6sM-1735744570629-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(43601,55380,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(43602,55380,'video_transcript_chatgpt','A fun and engaging movement combination is introduced, focusing on a sequence that begins with a Tic Tac maneuver leading into a 360-degree step Vault. This combination can also be adapted into a slide Vault. Key aspects include maintaining contact with a wall for balance and spatial awareness while performing the steps. The exploration of this exercise promotes a fluid motion that feels natural and is easy for practitioners to grasp.\r\n\r\nThe sequence begins with placing one hand on the wall while executing the Tic Tac, guiding the foot placement before advancing to the step Vault. The initial approach should be slow, allowing for careful form, which integrates the left hand, followed by a pivot and step to reassess body positioning. Practicing the movement gradually helps develop speed naturally while ensuring the correct technique is upheld throughout.\r\n\r\nThe importance of practice on both sides is emphasized, as it allows for balanced skill development. Rotating in different directions will enhance the overall agility and control needed for the combination. Having fun while practicing these motions can foster a more enjoyable and rewarding experience, encouraging individuals to push their limits while mastering the techniques involved.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The combination of a Tic Tac to a 360-degree step Vault promotes fluid movement and spatial awareness.\r\n2. Practicing the techniques slowly facilitates better form and comfort before increasing speed.\r\n3. Balanced practice on both sides is crucial for skill development and agility in executing the movements.'),(43603,55380,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(43604,55380,'svg_id',''),(43605,55380,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(43606,55380,'svg_colour',''),(43607,55380,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(43608,55380,'extra_variables',''),(43609,55380,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(43610,55380,'notes',''),(43611,55380,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(43612,55380,'enable_youtube_api',''),(43613,55380,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(43614,55380,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(43615,55380,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(43616,55380,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(43617,55380,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(43618,55380,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(43619,55380,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(43620,55380,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(43621,55380,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(43622,55380,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(43623,55380,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(43624,55380,'enable_transcript',''),(43625,55380,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(43626,55380,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(43627,55380,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(43628,55380,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I want this to sound like I wrote the result.'),(43629,55380,'_transcript_chatgpt_prompt','field_672214208bf31'),(43630,55380,'rank_math_primary_tutorial_category','0'),(43631,55380,'video_filename','Flowing-Chaining/Tutorial-Chaining-2-Tictac-360-step-vault.mp4'),(43632,55380,'_video_filename','field_677cead91f698'),(43633,55380,'portrait_thumbnail_image','Flowing-Chaining/screenshots/Tutorial-Chaining-2-Tictac-360-step-vault_3_4.png'),(43634,55380,'_portrait_thumbnail_image',''),(43635,55380,'landscape_thumbnail_image','Flowing-Chaining