es to facilitate a proper roll.nnOne key component of this technique is the necessity to perform a 90 or 180-degree turn before descending. Depending on the direction of the drop, the ability to orient the body appropriately will determine how well the impact is dispersed into the roll. Timing this movement correctly can significantly minimize stress on the legs, allowing a more graceful and effective landing.nnPracticing this dual movement regularly helps in developing muscle memory and confidence. It\'s essential to focus on spotting the landing area during the descent and to push away from the wall before executing the roll. While fluidity in execution isn\'t always required, understanding the sequence will enhance mastery of this fundamental parkour skill.nn**Key Points:**n1. The drop and roll technique is vital for safely landing from heights in parkour.n2. Proper orientation through turns before landing is crucial for dispersing impact.n3. Regular practice of this movement develops muscle memory and increases confidence.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1488,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 253,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1741,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_