age\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"A new training drill involves performing exercises at height, particularly focusing on a static one-hand, one-foot step-up technique. This drill engages key muscle groups such as the abs, obliques, and hip flexors while emphasizing balance and control. The objective is to master the step vault motion with enhanced stability, allowing practitioners to develop confidence in their physical capabilities during dynamic movements.nnCompleting this drill is not only physically demanding but also serves as an excellent conditioning exercise. Participants are encouraged to find elevated fixtures like scaffolding or goalposts to practice, which may vary in height and thickness. Engaging in this drill can help individuals refine their skills, targeting both physical strength and mental composure while overcoming fear when working at greater heights.nnAdditionally, the exercises focus on building body control and mastering the fear associated with performing high-impact moves. The push for precision and safety at height reinforces crucial psychological and physical elements that can be transferred to other activities. Integrating this drill into regular training can greatly enhance overall performance and readiness for more challenging tasks. nn**Key Points:**n1. The drill targets core stability and control through height-based exercises, specifically a one-hand, one-foot step-up technique.n2. Practicing at height aids physical conditioning and builds mental resilience by confronting fears related to performing elevated movements.n3. Participants are encouraged to utilize various elevated structures to enhance their skills, with an emphasis on balance and the proper execution of the step vault.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1320,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 290,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1610,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"ihE2tphoKjECTyxZ3NH0iVcYVAE.QRMtcRUO77Aehzs-1735840116-1.0.1.1-7IBfKREykQ_cvE7J2rhDRCkwIHqR5mbVGGw25mCWAIf_MEE5IEUcXNwm396kT1_hZ4YyfwqwflSRNXb4AD8bhg\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735841916,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"i8Epd3sRvFQ5i3XypCMsewWLlZEq8q5zPrO.sXp224Y-1735840116949-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(46735,55407,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(46736,55407,'video_transcript_chatgpt','A new training drill involves performing exercises at height, particularly focusing on a static one-hand, one-foot step-up technique. This drill engages key muscle groups such as the abs, obliques, and hip flexors while emphasizing balance and control. The objective is to master the step vault motion with enhanced stability, allowing practitioners to develop confidence in their physical capabilities during dynamic movements.\r\n\r\nCompleting this drill is not only physically demanding but also serves as an excellent conditioning exercise. Participants are encouraged to find elevated fixtures like scaffolding or goalposts to practice, which may vary in height and thickness. Engaging in this drill can help individuals refine their skills, targeting both physical strength and mental composure while overcoming fear when working at greater heights.\r\n\r\nAdditionally, the exercises focus on building body control and mastering the fear associated with performing high-impact moves. The push for precision and safety at height reinforces crucial psychological and physical elements that can be transferred to other activities. Integrating this drill into regular training can greatly enhance overall performance and readiness for more challenging tasks. \r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. The drill targets core stability and control through height-based exercises, specifically a one-hand, one-foot step-up technique.\r\n2. Practicing at height aids physical conditioning and builds mental resilience by confronting fears related to performing elevated movements.\r\n3. Participants are encouraged to utilize various elevated structures to enhance their skills, with an emphasis on balance and the proper execution of the step vault.'),(46737,55407,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(46738,55407,'svg_id',''),(46739,55407,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(46740,55407,'svg_colour',''),(46741,55407,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(46742,55407,'extra_variables',''),(46743,55407,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(46744,55407,'notes',''),(46745,55407,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(46746,55407,'enable_youtube_api',''),(46747,55407,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(4674