7414,55412,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJ71lJ3vAbpva3hjhmV6tQiyw4RJ\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735838247,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The drill focuses on mastering the reverse step vault by incorporating both the forward step vault and the reverse motion in an alternating pattern. Participants are encouraged to practice the movements repetitively, which helps develop rhythm and muscle memory. Starting with the right hand and left foot, the drill encourages transitioning from a forward step vault into a reverse step vault as a way to reinforce the skills required for both techniques.nnAs individuals practice the drill, they are guided to perform numerous rounds of the movements to build proficiency. While executing the forward and reverse vaults, participants are reminded to maintain a fluid motion, first vaulting forward, landing, and then smoothly transitioning back. This back-and-forth pattern not only helps participants understand the movements better but also enhances their ability to perform them with ease and confidence.nnThe drill emphasizes that the reverse step vault begins to feel more natural as practitioners reinforce their understanding through the forward vault. By repeatedly practicing both movements, participants are able to replicate the techniques and enjoy the exercise. Overall, this method of training is both effective and enjoyable, providing an engaging way to master vaulting skills.nnKey points:n1. The drill incorporates both forward and reverse step vaults to help develop rhythm and muscle memory.n2. Repetitive practice of alternating vaults enables smoother transitions and builds proficiency in both techniques.n3. Mastering the forward vault enhances the natural feel of the reverse vault, making the training enjoyable and effective.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 894,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 287,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1181,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"B8_7CiqDP18j4l4Uw4v6A9k4q1XvM03BvYf8UObnhpc-1735838251-1.0.1.1-qZaAUYAYNHCWE5XlbVzaI5oZY789B6g72Ki5WbqlsYieubg6hPC0h0imFDdft88BXJZ3tvEmykvLBSC4TYHxaw\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840051,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"GrADr3Z7IuLhK63b1Axvjm6mq3Kj750rS76SwR2Q9kI-1735838251286-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(47415,55412,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(47416,55412,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The drill focuses on mastering the reverse step vault by incorporating both the forward step vault and the reverse motion in an alternating pattern. Participants are encouraged to practice the movements repetitively, which helps develop rhythm and muscle memory. Starting with the right hand and left foot, the drill encourages transitioning from a forward step vault into a reverse step vault as a way to reinforce the skills required for both techniques.\r\n\r\nAs individuals practice the drill, they are guided to perform numerous rounds of the movements to build proficiency. While executing the forward and reverse vaults, participants are reminded to maintain a fluid motion, first vaulting forward, landing, and then smoothly transitioning back. This back-and-forth pattern not only helps participants understand the movements better but also enhances their ability to perform them with ease and confidence.\r\n\r\nThe drill emphasizes that the reverse step vault begins to feel more natural as practitioners reinforce their understanding through the forward vault. By repeatedly practicing both movements, participants are able to replicate the techniques and enjoy the exercise. Overall, this method of training is both effective and enjoyable, providing an engaging way to master vaulting skills.\r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. The drill incorporates both forward and reverse step vaults to help develop rhythm and muscle memory.\r\n2. Repetitive practice of alternating vaults enables smoother transitions and builds proficiency in both techniques.\r\n3. Mastering the forward vault enhances the natural feel of the reverse vault, making the training enjoyable and effective.'),(47417,55412,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(47418,55412,'svg_id',''),(47419,55412,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(47420,55412,'svg_colour',''),(47421,55412,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e