                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"Incorporating the reverse step vault into training can enhance strength and improve techniques. This drill focuses on the most challenging aspect of the movement, specifically the middle section, allowing practitioners to become accustomed to maintaining proper form. By performing the exercise slowly and with control, individuals can strengthen their core and improve their overall performance in this skill set.nnThe process involves transitioning one foot across while hopping up and maintaining the reverse step vault position. This method is particularly effective in engaging the obliques and abdominal muscles, which are crucial for core stability. It emphasizes the importance of holding the position, which not only fortifies the core but also boosts overall balance and control in executing the movement.nnConsistently integrating this drill into training routines can lead to substantial improvements in technique and execution of the reverse step vault. Practicing this maneuver systematically will cultivate better conditioning and awareness of body mechanics. Therefore, regular application of these steps will contribute to greater mastery of the skill over time.nnKey Points:n1. Strength and technique can be improved through the reverse step vault drill, focusing on the middle section of the movement.n2. Engaging the core muscles, particularly the obliques and abs, is essential for better performance and control.n3. Consistent practice, performed slowly and with intent, enhances overall mastery of the reverse step vault.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 871,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 265,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1136,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"mcXT0w52I7SyXoh2Hj1moCz9J5Wl.r8YSBinJKVdAec-1735838243-1.0.1.1-5byQQ9aa7tnaeYZXKDe3FvEa4.wSf.8UOvCDGdk3V5gvLMIIeZ_CZzkcALjPGA5_DHWLW4F.y3SpAwmJaVqKEQ\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840043,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"FNQBPMVWQAsAenj5lEI90xMbVTMqwX4S0vvIEUDnxDk-1735838243748-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(47570,55413,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(47571,55413,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Incorporating the reverse step vault into training can enhance strength and improve techniques. This drill focuses on the most challenging aspect of the movement, specifically the middle section, allowing practitioners to become accustomed to maintaining proper form. By performing the exercise slowly and with control, individuals can strengthen their core and improve their overall performance in this skill set.\r\n\r\nThe process involves transitioning one foot across while hopping up and maintaining the reverse step vault position. This method is particularly effective in engaging the obliques and abdominal muscles, which are crucial for core stability. It emphasizes the importance of holding the position, which not only fortifies the core but also boosts overall balance and control in executing the movement.\r\n\r\nConsistently integrating this drill into training routines can lead to substantial improvements in technique and execution of the reverse step vault. Practicing this maneuver systematically will cultivate better conditioning and awareness of body mechanics. Therefore, regular application of these steps will contribute to greater mastery of the skill over time.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. Strength and technique can be improved through the reverse step vault drill, focusing on the middle section of the movement.\r\n2. Engaging the core muscles, particularly the obliques and abs, is essential for better performance and control.\r\n3. Consistent practice, performed slowly and with intent, enhances overall mastery of the reverse step vault.'),(47572,55413,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(47573,55413,'svg_id',''),(47574,55413,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(47575,55413,'svg_colour',''),(47576,55413,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(47577,55413,'extra_variables',''),(47578,55413,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(47579,55413,'notes',''),(47580,55413,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(47581,55413,'enable_youtube_api',''),(47582,55413,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(47583,55413,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(47584,55413,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(47585,55413,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(47586,55413,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(47587,55413,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(47588,55413,'_enable_yo