> 00:01:28,000\r\nlean onto your hand a bit more and\r\n\r\n27\r\n00:00:85,000 --> 00:01:31,000\r\nplacing your foot on top of the the wall\r\n\r\n28\r\n00:00:88,000 --> 00:01:34,000\r\nuh as you come down rather than go up to\r\n\r\n29\r\n00:00:92,000 --> 00:01:35,000\r\nit\r\n\r\n'),(47723,55414,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(47724,55414,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJ6eSsN136QUp7qeK98Jh5Ji7rvb\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735838224,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The next phase of mastering the reverse step vault involves learning to hop and land effectively on top of a wall. This technique requires precise foot trajectory to avoid potential hazards, such as clipping one\'s heel while approaching. Instead of heading straight towards the wall, it is essential to adopt a more angled approach that allows for a safer and more controlled landing.nnWhen executing the vault, the goal is to use a trajectory that carries the body upwards and over the top of the wall before descending. This method ensures that the individual feels more confident while landing on the wall, as it decreases the likelihood of falling backward. Practicing this movement routine emphasizes the importance of not just jumping upward but also focusing on landing with accuracy and control.nnAs a drill, it is suggested to practice jumping and landing without an upward trajectory directly to the wall. The emphasis should be on coming down and placing the foot properly on top of the wall. Additional practice includes leaning more onto the hands and ensuring the foot finds a stable position, facilitating a safer and more efficient approach to the reverse step vault.nn**Key Points:**n1. Use an angled trajectory when approaching the wall to prevent clipping the heel and falling backward.n2. Focus on jumping higher and coming down to ensure a controlled landing on the wall.n3. Integrate drills to practice proper hand placement and foot positioning for increased safety and confidence.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1069,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 273,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1342,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"oEa0thJHMtmnWh_snSwbRxXZXr4UwJ28Npie14jM62s-1735838229-1.0.1.1-2M1xsF8tSTZll.cclTyu31w_a4JTiJWPMgWBdSUB2rlrohVbWPAhLRvQwS4ilAxTcPxGateocVyVBJF3z4hn_w\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840029,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"3pWti5nP67Y42MywuZqFRbGielL2HTc276Zbh9axBl8-1735838229117-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(47725,55414,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(47726,55414,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The next phase of mastering the reverse step vault involves learning to hop and land effectively on top of a wall. This technique requires precise foot trajectory to avoid potential hazards, such as clipping one\'s heel while approaching. Instead of heading straight towards the wall, it is essential to adopt a more angled approach that allows for a safer and more controlled landing.\r\n\r\nWhen executing the vault, the goal is to use a trajectory that carries the body upwards and over the top of the wall before descending. This method ensures that the individual feels more confident while landing on the wall, as it decreases the likelihood of falling backward. Practicing this movement routine emphasizes the importance of not just jumping upward but also focusing on landing with accuracy and control.\r\n\r\nAs a drill, it is suggested to practice jumping and landing without an upward trajectory directly to the wall. The emphasis should be on coming down and placing the foot properly on top of the wall. Additional practice includes leaning more onto the hands and ensuring the foot finds a stable position, facilitating a safer and more efficient approach to the reverse step vault.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. Use an angled trajectory when approaching the wall to prevent clipping the heel and falling backward.\r\n2. Focus on jumping higher and coming down to ensure a controlled landing on the wall.\r\n3. Integrate drills to practice proper hand placement and foot positioning for increased safety and confidence.'),(47727,55414,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(47728,55414,'svg_id',''),(47729,55414,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(47730,55414,'svg_colo