,\r\n        \"start\": 39.92,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.28\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"time and jump and through and that is\",\r\n        \"start\": 46,\r\n        \"duration\": 12.12\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"close to the full reverse step vault\",\r\n        \"start\": 51.44,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.68\r\n    }\r\n]'),(47876,55415,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(47877,55415,'video_transcript_srt','1\r\n00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000\r\nthe next drill is to practice going over\r\n\r\n2\r\n00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000\r\nthe\r\n\r\n3\r\n00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000\r\nwall without starting with your hand on\r\n\r\n4\r\n00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:17,000\r\nthe wall so you don\'t want to start here\r\n\r\n5\r\n00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000\r\nand then go and do it I want you to\r\n\r\n6\r\n00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000\r\nstart a step away so you as you\'re ready\r\n\r\n7\r\n00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000\r\nto go you have to go and commit with the\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000\r\nhand and then the foot all in one so\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000\r\nyou\'re not sort of positioning yourself\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000\r\nso you just have to worry about the foot\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:39,000\r\nso take a step back and then step in\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:44,000\r\nhand and foot as you\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000\r\njump and down okay let\'s go one more\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:58,000\r\ntime and jump and through and that is\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000\r\nclose to the full reverse step vault\r\n\r\n'),(47878,55415,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(47879,55415,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJ6mBWMx8Cy57yVLTwWIj8sSIBSR\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735838232,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The focus of the drill is to practice the reverse step vault without initially placing a hand against the wall. Participants should begin by taking a step back, which helps eliminate dependency on positioning themselves too close to the wall. Instead of starting with their hands on the wall, they need to commit to the jump by synchronizing their hand and foot movement as they approach the wall, ensuring a more fluid and confident execution of the vault.nnAs they perform the drill, emphasis is placed on the importance of coordination between the hand and the foot during the jump. Practitioners are encouraged to focus solely on the footwork and the jump technique, rather than getting caught up in pre-jump positioning. The instruction is to step back further away from the wall before attempting the jump, as this promotes better momentum and control.nnBy the end of the session, participants are expected to demonstrate improvements in their reverse step vault technique, culminating in a smoother execution that closely resembles the full movement. Repeated practice until mastery of the jump is encouraged, underscoring the goal of achieving both speed and precision in their movements.nnKey Points:n1. The drill emphasizes initiating the jump from a step-back position rather than from the wall.n2. Coordination between hand and foot movements is crucial for executing the reverse step vault effectively.n3. Repeated practice is necessary to refine technique and achieve a fluid jump response.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 582,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 277,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 859,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"bQ_U3HhLKYqmjHEBK9_rSXdB0clYbu9FCiYfwv9BRas-1735838235-1.0.1.1-dYfY0sUDfPLMyTZmuQ_2AIhYAHHioHRLnDQlZTaAW7n_2LdCDKVMrGLdIQI3i.BAaDFZIX9S17pxjjZeA00gUA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840035,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"n.N3IRu7Ct4yoVxNlJJ2ysLGd.32VsKTdT5LgO4GOnE-1735838235539-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(47880,55415,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(47881,55415,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The focus of the drill is to practice the reverse step vault without initially placing a hand against the wall. Participants should begin by taking a step back, which helps eliminate dependency on positioning themselves too close to the wall. Instead of starting with their hands on the wall, they need to commit to the jump by synchronizing their hand and foot movement as they approach the wall, ensuring a more fluid and confident execution of the vault.\r\n\r\nAs they perform the drill, emphasis is placed on the importance of coordination between the hand and the foot during the jump. Practitioners are encouraged to focus solely on the footwork and the jump technique, rather than getting caught up in pre-jump positioning. The instruction is to step back further away from the wall before attempting the jump, as this promotes better momentum and control.\r\n\r\nBy the end of the session, participants are expected to demonstrate improvements in their reverse step vault technique, culminating in a smoother execution that closely resembles the full movement. Repeated practice until mastery of the jump is encouraged, underscoring the goal of achieving both speed and precision in their movements.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The drill emphasizes initiating the jump from a step-back position rather than from the wall.\r\n2. Coordination between hand and foot movements is crucial for executing the reverse step vault effectively.\r\n3. Repeated practice is necessary to refine technique and achieve a fluid jump response.'),(47882,55415,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(47883,55415,'svg_id',''),(47884,55415,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(47885,55415,'svg_colour',''),(47886,55415,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(47887,55415,'extra_variables',''),(47888,55415,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(47889,55415,'notes',''),(47890,55415,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(47891,55415,'enable_youtube_api',''),(47892,55415,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(47893,55415,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(47894,55415,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(47895,55415,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(47896,55415,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(47897,55415,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(47898,55415,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt',