        \"content\": \"The instructions focus on performing a reverse step vault, which begins with momentum starting away from the vault. The process involves running towards the vault while turning and placing a hand on the block. It’s emphasized that the foot should land downwards instead of rising vertically, creating a more fluid and dynamic motion.nnAs the movement progresses, the individual is encouraged to step through, allowing the natural momentum from the run to continue flowing through the maneuver. The technique includes taking advantage of this momentum to enhance the height and distance achieved in the vault while maintaining a rotational movement. The exit from the vault is a continuation of the same movement, ensuring a smooth transition back to the ground.nnFinally, it is highlighted that practicing the reverse step vault on both sides is crucial for building coordination and consistency. The overall aim is to combine all elements of the technique, infusing it with speed to generate higher and farther jumps with efficiency. Mastering this skill involves integrating both the physical aspects of vaulting and the mental understanding of momentum and movement.nn**Key Points:**n1. The reverse step vault begins with generating momentum and involves a specific hand placement and foot landing technique.n2. Maintaining fluid movement is essential as the sequence should harmonize with the natural momentum of the run, allowing for effective rotation and exit.n3. Practicing the technique on both sides while incorporating speed can improve height and distance in the vaulting performance.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 777,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 281,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1058,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"ZmJtzBPwQ8jz_91cdDOcHWOrFfo3rFz10xCCdxEx4QU-1735838224-1.0.1.1-2lh_5mKLVInDSadLNETABGx0cAcmYjest9k0_25GwKZig3CzFF4vIJqfV1vC6CZINhIzMc4GVcBuyfW.ndZ.HA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840024,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"H7ACFHPh8XM6EGFGQEgFBIrHjhAIaY4WOZR.aujsNXo-1735838224274-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(48041,55416,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(48042,55416,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The instructions focus on performing a reverse step vault, which begins with momentum starting away from the vault. The process involves running towards the vault while turning and placing a hand on the block. It’s emphasized that the foot should land downwards instead of rising vertically, creating a more fluid and dynamic motion.\r\n\r\nAs the movement progresses, the individual is encouraged to step through, allowing the natural momentum from the run to continue flowing through the maneuver. The technique includes taking advantage of this momentum to enhance the height and distance achieved in the vault while maintaining a rotational movement. The exit from the vault is a continuation of the same movement, ensuring a smooth transition back to the ground.\r\n\r\nFinally, it is highlighted that practicing the reverse step vault on both sides is crucial for building coordination and consistency. The overall aim is to combine all elements of the technique, infusing it with speed to generate higher and farther jumps with efficiency. Mastering this skill involves integrating both the physical aspects of vaulting and the mental understanding of momentum and movement.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. The reverse step vault begins with generating momentum and involves a specific hand placement and foot landing technique.\r\n2. Maintaining fluid movement is essential as the sequence should harmonize with the natural momentum of the run, allowing for effective rotation and exit.\r\n3. Practicing the technique on both sides while incorporating speed can improve height and distance in the vaulting performance.'),(48043,55416,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(48044,55416,'svg_id',''),(48045,55416,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(48046,55416,'svg_colour',''),(48047,55416,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(48048,55416,'extra_variables',''),(48049,55416,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(48050,55416,'notes',''),(48051,55416,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(48052,55416,'enable_youtube_api',''),(48053,55416,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(48054,55416,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(48055,55416,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(48056,55416,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(48057,55416,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(48058,55416,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(48059,55416,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6