r\n00:00:95,000 --> 00:01:38,000\r\nreverse step vault\r\n\r\n'),(48207,55417,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(48208,55417,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJ6RPA56qyKKCaM9oeBAkMapHX1v\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735838211,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The reverse step vault on a rail can be daunting due to its need for precise technique and control. Unlike typical vaults, the execution requires turning away from the rail, which complicates the approach as you lose visibility of the bar. Success hinges on landing correctly, particularly with the ball of the foot, to ensure stability and proper execution. nnTo master this skill, practice is essential. It is crucial to focus on jumping high enough so that the foot can come down onto the rail instead of moving upwards towards it. This approach reduces the risk of missing the rail altogether, making controlled and deliberate movements key to achieving the desired outcome. Repeated drills will help develop the muscle memory required for accurate foot placement and timing.nnA suggested technique involves a static start with the hands positioned away from the body for stability. The initial push should be upward, aiming for height and a controlled landing on the rail. Practicing this motion with a comfortable jump height can build confidence in performing the reverse step vault effectively. Each repetition reinforces the necessary skills to perform the vault safely and successfully.nnKey Points:n1. The reverse step vault requires precise foot placement and controlled jumping to ensure safety and accuracy.n2. Adequate practice is vital for developing the skills needed, including a focus on proper foot landing techniques.n3. Utilizing a static start with careful hand positioning can help build stability and confidence in executing the vault.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1126,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 281,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1407,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"1Yvcx5h2Mg61rZ2rMnFErcjCPIkxzvXFg8MCnacxaRM-1735838217-1.0.1.1-N.FXQ4u0Z_04Djyr1dYkcSHIAvYNJD8veDCSpoQDV_OGWUMQuIJcy5fTAus.YCygTFbx87.VnzFqODfRhgi15A\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840017,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"25gF4X0kVWhULpDANvDHlxXkdyLzPS5wZ6Ko2xugnbs-1735838217120-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(48209,55417,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(48210,55417,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The reverse step vault on a rail can be daunting due to its need for precise technique and control. Unlike typical vaults, the execution requires turning away from the rail, which complicates the approach as you lose visibility of the bar. Success hinges on landing correctly, particularly with the ball of the foot, to ensure stability and proper execution. \r\n\r\nTo master this skill, practice is essential. It is crucial to focus on jumping high enough so that the foot can come down onto the rail instead of moving upwards towards it. This approach reduces the risk of missing the rail altogether, making controlled and deliberate movements key to achieving the desired outcome. Repeated drills will help develop the muscle memory required for accurate foot placement and timing.\r\n\r\nA suggested technique involves a static start with the hands positioned away from the body for stability. The initial push should be upward, aiming for height and a controlled landing on the rail. Practicing this motion with a comfortable jump height can build confidence in performing the reverse step vault effectively. Each repetition reinforces the necessary skills to perform the vault safely and successfully.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The reverse step vault requires precise foot placement and controlled jumping to ensure safety and accuracy.\r\n2. Adequate practice is vital for developing the skills needed, including a focus on proper foot landing techniques.\r\n3. Utilizing a static start with careful hand positioning can help build stability and confidence in executing the vault.'),(48211,55417,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(48212,55417,'svg_id',''),(48213,55417,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(48214,55417,'svg_colour',''),(48215,55417,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(48216,55417,'extra_variables',''),(48217,55417,'_ext