ssage\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The discussion focuses on a mounting technique onto a rail or wall, emphasizing safety and proper technique. The initial step involves positioning both hands on the rail while preparing to execute a step vault mount. The goal is to elevate one foot onto the rail while managing body weight effectively, which requires a series of controlled movements and balance adjustments.nnThe process begins by placing one foot on the rail, pushing off from the ground, and transferring weight onto the elevated foot. As stability increases, the other foot is brought onto the rail, all while ensuring that the hands remain in place primarily for support rather than weight. This transitioning process involves shifting body weight smoothly and ensuring a proper grip and engagement of foot muscles for balance.nnFinally, emphasis is placed on ensuring that the ball of the foot is correctly positioned on the rail to enhance control during the mount. Careful contraction and release of the toes provide stability, and having a firm grip is crucial. This technique fosters both safety and efficiency when mounting onto a rail or wall, encouraging a blend of strength and coordination.nnKey points:n1. Proper technique involves a step vault mount, starting with hands on the rail and transitioning weight effectively.n2. Emphasis on balance and control, utilizing the feet for weight distribution rather than relying solely on the hands.n3. Safety measures include maintaining a secure grip and activating the toes for stability while on the rail.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1548,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 276,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1824,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0705bf87c0\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"2FpgEhLTYDpfxjn5R4Ttd3WxxQV6SGKUnv8E4vH27l8-1733399564-1.0.1.1-Eql36keVIuprubX9eO46faaTvs11URPl6vWl5Ezf7AGYYqkP6QsoAeW909BwNMMue8hkSGWUL1lVgYYHX0WZ3Q\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1733401364,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"dF5U0r96WwoNJHdUfoWHide5TDoW4Fm8tj2u.ud2acU-1733399564819-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(48509,55419,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(48510,55419,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The discussion focuses on a mounting technique onto a rail or wall, emphasizing safety and proper technique. The initial step involves positioning both hands on the rail while preparing to execute a step vault mount. The goal is to elevate one foot onto the rail while managing body weight effectively, which requires a series of controlled movements and balance adjustments.\r\n\r\nThe process begins by placing one foot on the rail, pushing off from the ground, and transferring weight onto the elevated foot. As stability increases, the other foot is brought onto the rail, all while ensuring that the hands remain in place primarily for support rather than weight. This transitioning process involves shifting body weight smoothly and ensuring a proper grip and engagement of foot muscles for balance.\r\n\r\nFinally, emphasis is placed on ensuring that the ball of the foot is correctly positioned on the rail to enhance control during the mount. Careful contraction and release of the toes provide stability, and having a firm grip is crucial. This technique fosters both safety and efficiency when mounting onto a rail or wall, encouraging a blend of strength and coordination.\r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. Proper technique involves a step vault mount, starting with hands on the rail and transitioning weight effectively.\r\n2. Emphasis on balance and control, utilizing the feet for weight distribution rather than relying solely on the hands.\r\n3. Safety measures include maintaining a secure grip and activating the toes for stability while on the rail.'),(48511,55419,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(48512,55419,'svg_id',''),(48513,55419,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(48514,55419,'svg_colour',''),(48515,55419,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(48516,55419,'extra_variables',''),(48517,55419,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(48518,55419,'notes',''),(48519,55419,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(48520,55419,'enable_youtube_api',''),(48521,55419,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(48522,55419,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(48523,55419,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(48524,55419,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(48525,55419,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(48526,55419,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(48527,55419,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(48528,55419,'youtube_chatgpt_prom