ltiple\",\r\n        \"start\": 9.28,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.44\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"steps and you you got to plan it because\",\r\n        \"start\": 12.92,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.16\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"the the normal Tic Tac would be in this\",\r\n        \"start\": 16.72,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.16\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"situation my left hand and my right foot\",\r\n        \"start\": 19.08,\r\n        \"duration\": 3.92\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"would be going up onto the wall which\",\r\n        \"start\": 20.88,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.6\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"means that if I need to get into that\",\r\n        \"start\": 23,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.279\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"position the step before would be my\",\r\n        \"start\": 26.48,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.76\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"left foot so I\'ve got to go up with my\",\r\n        \"start\": 29.279,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.28\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"opposite foot first so the inside foot\",\r\n        \"start\": 31.24,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.12\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"left and then I can step another step\",\r\n        \"start\": 34.559,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.52\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"and then do the Tic Tac so that would be\",\r\n        \"start\": 37.36,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.44\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"the two-step Tic Tac so from here I\",\r\n        \"start\": 40.079,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.121\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"would go up left foot\",\r\n        \"start\": 42.8,\r\n        \"duration\": 3.4\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"first one two and over that gives you\",\r\n        \"start\": 46.28,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.04\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"height and it also allows you to cover\",\r\n        \"start\": 50.68,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.16\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"distance um it\'s not one of those ones\",\r\n        \"start\": 53.32,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.399\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"that is used very\",\r\n        \"start\": 55.84,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.399\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"often but uh it looks kind of cool it\'s\",\r\n        \"start\": 57.719,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.921\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"fun you you know you get an Assassin\'s\",\r\n        \"start\": 61.239,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.041\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"Creed vibe to it and yeah it feels good\",\r\n        \"start\": 63.64,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.76\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"doing it but in reality functionally\",\r\n        \"start\": 67.28,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.04\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"it\'s not something we do that often uh\",\r\n        \"start\": 70.4,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.52\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"sometimes there are scenarios where we\",\r\n        \"start\": 73.32,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.56\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"will but um a lot of the time a single\",\r\n        \"start\": 74.92,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"Tic Tac will do um yeah give it a go\",\r\n        \"start\": 77.88,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.559\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"practice uh trying to get the steps in\",\r\n        \"start\": 81.6,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.6\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"the correct order and see how far you\",\r\n        \"start\": 84.439,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.921\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"can get around with that double foot Tic\",\r\n        \"start\": 87.2,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.72\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"Tac\",\r\n        \"start\": 89.36,\r\n        \"duration\": 2.56\r\n    }\r\n]'),(50678,55436,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(50679,55436,'video_transcript_srt','1\r\n00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,000\r\nokay one of the fun things about the Tic\r\n\r\n2\r\n00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,000\r\nTac is you can actually do multiple\r\n\r\n3\r\n00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000\r\nsteps and you you got to plan it because\r\n\r\n4\r\n00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000\r\nthe the normal Tic Tac would be in this\r\n\r\n5\r\n00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:22,000\r\nsituation my left hand and my right foot\r\n\r\n6\r\n00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000\r\nwould be going up onto the wall which\r\n\r\n7\r\n00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000\r\nmeans that if I need to get into that\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000\r\nposition the step before would be my\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000\r\nleft foot so I\'ve got to go up with my\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,000\r\nopposite foot first so the inside foot\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000\r\nleft and then I can step another step\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,000\r\nand then do the Tic Tac so that would be\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,000\r\nthe two-step Tic Tac so from here I\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000\r\nwould go up left foot\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:53,000\r\nfirst one two and over that gives you\r\n\r\n16\r\n00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000\r\nheight and it also allows you to cover\r\n\r\n17\r\n00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000\r\ndistance um it\'s not one of those ones\r\n\r\n18\r\n00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000\r\nthat is used very\r\n\r\n19\r\n00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000\r\noften but uh it looks kind of cool it\'s\r\n\r\n20\r\n00:00:61,000 --> 00:01:07,000\r\nfun you you know you get an Assassin\'s\r\n\r\n21\r\n00:00:63,000 --> 00:01:09,000\r\nCreed vibe to it and yeah it feels good\r\n\r\n22\r\n00:00:67,000 --> 00:01:13,000\r\ndoing it but in reality functionally\r\n\r\n23\r\n00:00:70,000 --> 00:01:14,000\r\nit\'s not something we do that often uh\r\n\r\n24\r\n00:00:73,000 --> 00:01:17,000\r\nsometimes there are scenarios where we\r\n\r\n25\r\n00:00:74,000 --> 00:01:20,000\r\nwill but um a lot of the time a single\r\n\r\n26\r\n00:00:77,000 --> 00:01:23,000\r\nTic Tac will do um yeah give it a go\r\n\r\n27\r\n00:00:81,000 --> 00:01:26,000\r\npractice uh trying to get the steps in\r\n\r\n28\r\n00:00:84,000 --> 00:01:28,000\r\nthe correct order and see how far you\r\n\r\n29\r\n00:00:87,000 --> 00:01:31,000\r\ncan get around with that double foot Tic\r\n\r\n30\r\n00:00:89,000 --> 00:01:31,000\r\nTac\r\n\r\n'),(50680,55436,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(50681,55436,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJegztCHqv6ekpK537r1mboehBKs\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735840334,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The transcript discusses the technique and planning involved in executing a two-step Tic Tac move, emphasizing the need to think ahead about foot placements. The speaker outlines how the sequence begins with the left foot, followed by a step with the opposite foot, allowing for a successful launch onto a wall. This planning is crucial to gain both height and distance and make the movement more fluid and effective.nnDespite the complexity involved in the two-step Tic Tac, it is noted that this move isn\'t frequently utilized in practice. The speaker acknowledges its aesthetic appeal and the sense of excitement it brings, akin to characters in video games like Assassin\'s Creed. However, the move is primarily for show, as simpler techniques are often sufficient for most scenarios.nnPracticing the sequence and mastering the order of steps is encouraged, as it can enhance overall agility and adaptability in various situations. The speaker suggests that, while the two-step version can be fun to learn, one should also be comfortable with the standard single Tic Tac, which is more commonly employed in practical applications.nnKey Points:n1. The two-step Tic Tac requires careful planning and sequencing of foot movements for effective execution.n2. The move is visually impressive but not often necessary in practical use, with simpler techniques being more common.n3. Practicing the two-step Tic Tac can improve agility, but proficiency in the single Tic Tac is also important for overall skill development.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1127,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 278,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1405,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"63E3wtLA9lJvtxJbQeHTHP3dVzNT0u.dAOOaP_oXyMM-1735840338-1.0.1.1-fzKeMt0aez8kqdSJXBjxR0R_x4QwpLKierGOMBNSebsi93KGIxV90VdklVbN497aLa7zOclr60C2DNNIeCdAng\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735842138,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"wrdl54Big1SoZn7G_trVYM7awQpnNUtFtDnQJwfapWI-1735840338122-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(50682,55436,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(50683,55436,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The transcript discusses the technique and planning involved in executing a two-step Tic Tac move, emphasizing the need to think ahead about foot placements. The speaker outlines how the sequence begins with the left foot, followed by a step with the opposite foot, allowing for a successful launch onto a wall. This planning is crucial to gain both height and distance and make the movement more fluid and effective.\r\n\r\nDespite the complexity involved in the two-step Tic Tac, it is noted that this move isn\'t frequently utilized in practice. The speaker acknowledges its aesthetic appeal and the sense of excitement it brings, akin to characters in video games like Assassin\'s Creed. However, the move is primarily for show, as simpler techniques are often sufficient for most scenarios.\r\n\r\nPracticing the sequence and mastering the order of steps is encouraged, as it can enhance overall agility and adaptability in various situations. The speaker suggests that, while the two-step version can be fun to learn, one should also be comfortable with the standard single Tic Tac, which is more commonly employed in practical applications.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The two-step Tic Tac requires careful planning and sequencing of foot movements for effective execution.\r\n2. The move is visually impressive but not often necessary in practical use, with simpler techniques being more common.\r\n3. Practicing the two-step Tic Tac can improve agility, but proficiency in the single Tic Tac is also important for overall skill development.'),(50684,55436,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(50685,55436,'svg_id',''),(50686,55436,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(50687,55436,'svg_colour',''),(50688,55436,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(50689,55436,'extra_variables',''),(50690,55436,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(50691,55436,'notes',''),(50692,55436,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(50693,55436,'enable_youtube_api',''),(50694,55436,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(50695,55436,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(50696,55436,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(50697,55436,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(50698,55436,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(50699,55436,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(50700,55436,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(50701,55436,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(50702,55436,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(50703,55436,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(50704,55436,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(50705,55436,'enable_transcript',''),(50706,55436,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(50707,55436,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(50708,55436,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(50709,55436,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I want this to sound like I wrote the result.'),(50710,55436,'_transcript_chatgpt_prompt','field_672214208bf31'),(50711,55436,'rank_math_primary_tutorial_category','0'),(50712,55436,'video_filename','Vaulting-TicTac/Tutorial-vaulting-tictac-9-two-steps.mp4'),(50713,55436,'_video_filename','field_677cead91f698'),(50714,55436,'portrait_thumbnail_image','Vaulting-TicTac/screenshot