al understandings. Ultimately, a combination of controlled speed and technical application will enhance the effectiveness of the cat pass.nnKey Points:n1. Speed should be controlled when practicing the cat pass to maintain technical proficiency.n2. The right positioning and momentum from controlled steps are crucial for successfully navigating obstacles.n3. Gradual practice with varying wall heights helps improve skills and technical understanding of the cat pass.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1340,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 278,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1618,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"h.TC1m5rpk6Z9IwSFaaqBVew17vpavYpNcGvpm.BeOY-1735837059-1.0.1.1-LE1ludQIuGb15SdWY5r6.f9mUXta92_ZAaKI0098dI.M68s6tfnN_RKDVl3wkVCQ5n0k1bfCOXAFUrPlb8o5Uw\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735838859,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"HRHljJIn.kslpE4cKZWL9kvOz7Yggm3oNEg8iQjWygw-1735837059167-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(51303,55441,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(51304,55441,'video_transcript_chatgpt','To master the cat pass movement in parkour, it\'s important to start by incorporating speed as a final variable. Speed can often lead to a decrease in technical proficiency, so it should be controlled effectively. Practicing the technique with precise movements allows a person to maintain better control over their skills while adding momentum. By beginning with two controlled steps, one can learn how to efficiently navigate obstacles without relying too much on speed.\r\n\r\nPositioning plays a significant role in the cat pass. By stepping back and then taking two steps forward, one can develop an understanding of how to use their body’s momentum to achieve the desired outcome. By limiting the amount of speed, practitioners can focus on the technical aspects of the movement. This technique is crucial for ensuring that they can get onto the wall confidently and successfully.\r\n\r\nProgressing with practice is essential, and one should vary the heights of the walls they are attempting to pass over. This incremental approach allows for a gradual improvement in skills, along with the development of better technical understandings. Ultimately, a combination of controlled speed and technical application will enhance the effectiveness of the cat pass.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. Speed should be controlled when practicing the cat pass to maintain technical proficiency.\r\n2. The right positioning and momentum from controlled steps are crucial for successfully navigating obstacles.\r\n3. Gradual practice with varying wall heights helps improve skills and technical understanding of the cat pass.'),(51305,55441,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(51306,55441,'svg_id',''),(51307,55441,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(51308,55441,'svg_colour',''),(51309,55441,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(51310,55441,'extra_variables',''),(51311,55441,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(51312,55441,'notes',''),(51313,55441,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(51314,55441,'enable_youtube_api',''),(51315,55441,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(51316,55441,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(51317,55441,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(51318,55441,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(51319,55441,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(51320,55441,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(51321,55441,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(51322,55441,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(51323,55441,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(51324,55441,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(51325,55441,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(51326,55441,'enable_transcript',''),(51327,55441,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(51328,55441,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(51329,55441,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(51330,55441,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I want this to sound like I wrote the result.'),(51331,55441,'_transcript_chatgpt_prompt','field_672214208bf31'),(51332,55441,'rank_math_primary_tutorial_category','0'),(51333,55441,'video_filename','Vaulting-CatPass/Tutorial-vaulting-cat_pass-4-momentum.mp4'),(51334,55441,'_video_filename','field_677cead91f698'),(51335,55441,'portrait_thumbnail_image','Vaulting-CatPass/screenshots/Tutorial-vaulting-cat_pass-4-momentum_3_4.png'),(51336,55441,'_portrait_thumbnail_image',''),(51337,55441,'landsc