kour\r\n\r\nHave questions or want to get in touch? Email us at contact@localhost:8443.\r\n\r\n📌 Hashtags:\r\n#ParkourTutorial #LearnParkour #LondonParkour #HowToParkour #ParkourForBeginners #ParkourPulse\r\n\r\n╔══════════════════╗\r\n║  ▶️ ＳＵＢＳＣＲＩＢＥ  ║\r\n╚══════════════════╝\r\nSubscribe to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_confirmation=1\r\n\r\n╔══════════════════╗\r\n║    🔗C O M P A N Y     ║\r\n╚══════════════════╝\r\n\r\n🔹 https://LONDONPARKOUR.COM\r\n🔹 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.\r\n\r\n🔸 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour\r\n🔸 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour\r\n🔸 contact@localhost:8443'),(52202,55448,'_video_youtube_data_description','field_67222e14397d2'),(52203,55448,'video_youtube_data_description_filtered',''),(52204,55448,'_video_youtube_data_description_filtered','field_672253e91cdc8'),(52205,55448,'video_chatgpt_response',''),(52206,55448,'_video_chatgpt_response','field_67221dc82655d'),(52207,55448,'video_chatgpt_response_text',''),(52208,55448,'_video_chatgpt_response_text','field_6722334bac798'),(52209,55448,'video_transcript_json','[\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"let\'s talk about the speed step the\",\r\n        \"start\": 5.44,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.04\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"speed step is a step Vault however the\",\r\n        \"start\": 8.44,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.759\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"slight change is you are leading with\",\r\n        \"start\": 13.48,\r\n        \"duration\": 7\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"your foot rather than your hand the\",\r\n        \"start\": 17.199,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.601\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"reason being you want your foot to take\",\r\n        \"start\": 20.48,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.16\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"the impact rather than your hands if you\",\r\n        \"start\": 23.8,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.28\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"go with your hands first it\'s Al also\",\r\n        \"start\": 26.64,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.4\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"head first and face first and sometimes\",\r\n        \"start\": 30.08,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.92\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"you don\'t want to do that if you\'re\",\r\n        \"start\": 33.04,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.92\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"going fast that\'s one condition where\",\r\n        \"start\": 35,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.2\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"you would usually use a speed step\",\r\n        \"start\": 37.96,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.759\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"instead of a step Vault the other one\",\r\n        \"start\": 40.2,\r\n        \"duration\": 5\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"the other one would be going downward so\",\r\n        \"start\": 42.719,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.84\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"if I was going down to a step Vault I\",\r\n        \"start\": 45.2,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.56\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"don\'t want to go down onto my hands\",\r\n        \"start\": 48.559,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.52\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"because again that\'s my face first and\",\r\n        \"start\": 50.76,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.959\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"I\'d have to take the impact with my arm\",\r\n        \"start\": 53.079,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.521\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"instead I go down with my foot first so\",\r\n        \"start\": 55.719,\r\n        \"duration\": 6\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"let\'s give this a go with the uh foot\",\r\n        \"start\": 58.6,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.959\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"first and I\'m going to just try and lead\",\r\n        \"start\": 61.719,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.08\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"with my foot and end up landing on top\",\r\n        \"start\": 64.559,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.161\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"so I\'m just going up on top I\'m not\",\r\n        \"start\": 68.799,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.481\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"going over yet but I\'m trying to lead\",\r\n        \"start\": 70.72,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.439\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"with my foot and then my hand is going\",\r\n        \"start\": 73.28,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"to drop to the side so from\",\r\n        \"start\": 76.159,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.6\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"here foot and then hand okay let\'s go\",\r\n        \"start\": 78.96,\r\n        \"duration\": 9.24\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"again foot hand so that timing is key\",\r\n        \"start\": 83.759,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"making sure that the leg lands first you\",\r\n        \"start\": 88.2,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.44\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"take that impact and then you drop to\",\r\n        \"start\": 90.439,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.401\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"the hand\",\r\n        \"start\": 92.64,\r\n        \"duration\": 3.2\r\n    }\r\n]'),(52210,55448,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(52211,55448,'video_transcript_srt','1\r\n00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:13,000\r\nlet\'s talk about the speed step the\r\n\r\n2\r\n00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000\r\nspeed step is a step Vault however the\r\n\r\n3\r\n00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000\r\nslight change is you are leading with\r\n\r\n4\r\n00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:23,000\r\nyour foot rather than your hand the\r\n\r\n5\r\n00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000\r\nreason being you want your foot to take\r\n\r\n6\r\n00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000\r\nthe impact rather than your hands if you\r\n\r\n7\r\n00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:32,000\r\ngo with your hands first it\'s Al also\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000\r\nhead first and face first and sometimes\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,000\r\nyou don\'t want to do that if you\'re\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000\r\ngoing fast that\'s one condition where\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,000\r\nyou would usually use a speed step\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000\r\ninstead of a step Vault the other one\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000\r\nthe other one would be going downward so\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000\r\nif I was going down to a step Vault I\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000\r\ndon\'t want to go down onto my hands\r\n\r\n16\r\n00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000\r\nbecause again that\'s my face first and\r\n\r\n17\r\n00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000\r\nI\'d have to take the impact with my arm\r\n\r\n18\r\n00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000\r\ninstead I go down with my foot first so\r\n\r\n19\r\n00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,000\r\nlet\'s give this a go with the uh foot\r\n\r\n20\r\n00:00:61,000 --> 00:01:08,000\r\nfirst and I\'m going to just try and lead\r\n\r\n21\r\n00:00:64,000 --> 00:01:10,000\r\nwith my foot and end up landing on top\r\n\r\n22\r\n00:00:68,000 --> 00:01:12,000\r\nso I\'m just going up on top I\'m not\r\n\r\n23\r\n00:00:70,000 --> 00:01:15,000\r\ngoing over yet but I\'m trying to lead\r\n\r\n24\r\n00:00:73,000 --> 00:01:18,000\r\nwith my foot and then my hand is going\r\n\r\n25\r\n00:00:76,000 --> 00:01:23,000\r\nto drop to the side so from\r\n\r\n26\r\n00:00:78,000 --> 00:01:27,000\r\nhere foot and then hand okay let\'s go\r\n\r\n27\r\n00:00:83,000 --> 00:01:29,000\r\nagain foot hand so that timing is key\r\n\r\n28\r\n00:00:88,000 --> 00:01:32,000\r\nmaking sure that the leg lands first you\r\n\r\n29\r\n00:00:90,000 --> 00:01:35,000\r\ntake that impact and then you drop to\r\n\r\n30\r\n00:00:92,000 --> 00:01:35,000\r\nthe hand\r\n\r\n'),(52212,55448,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(52213,55448,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJOHYBmsklPnf1t2KV7ibrUI9nrQ\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735839317,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The speed step is a variation of the step vault where the practitioner leads with their foot instead of their hands. This technique is designed to ensure that the foot absorbs the impact rather than the hands, which can help avoid injuries, particularly to the face and upper body. By approaching the vault with the foot first, the individual can also reduce the chance of a head-first fall, which can occur if the hands are used as the leading point during the movement.nnThere are specific scenarios where using a speed step is advantageous. One such situation is when moving quickly, as the momentum can lead to a more controlled descent if the foot is positioned first. Additionally, going downward to a lower surface benefits from this approach, as it helps mitigate the risk of injuries that might arise from falling onto the hands. Instead of leading with the hands and potentially taking the impact on the arms or head, opting for a foot-first landing creates a safer transition.nnPracticing the correct timing is crucial to executing the speed step effectively. The landing order should prioritize the foot\'s arrival before the hand, which requires coordination and focus. By refining this technique, individuals can improve their vaulting skills and ensure that their landings are less jarring, ultimately enhancing their overall agility and performance.nnKey points:n1. The speed step leads with the foot to avoid injuries and make landings safer.n2. It is particularly useful when moving quickly or descending to a lower surface.n3. Proper timing in foot and hand placement is essential for effective execution.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1118,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 303,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1421,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"vKgqLc869Z_4WrnHneHPzkvB19npI0rbeYETHtQmKeM-1735839322-1.0.1.1-_gH06VIrw.e0QnNSYl11qEhkIYlSm4y9RD5huz9oIXt.j1c0wqQFPVNivJnlsRZRMxGPV1lK_MUKD3ta5ljhIw\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735841122,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"yR._N4Vt1IIy46YscW9sv2HEcqwth8W6PELal8iFjZo-1735839322768-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(52214,55448,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(52215,55448,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The speed step is a variation of the step vault where the practitioner leads with their foot instead of their hands. This technique is designed to ensure that the foot absorbs the impact rather than the hands, which can help avoid injuries, particularly to the face and upper body. By approaching the vault with the foot first, the individual can also reduce the chance of a head-first fall, which can occur if the hands are used as the leading point during the movement.\r\n\r\nThere are specific scenarios where using a speed step is advantageous. One such situation is when moving quickly, as the momentum can lead to a more controlled descent if the foot is positioned first. Additionally, going downward to a lower surface benefits from this approach, as it helps mitigate the risk of injuries that might arise from falling onto the hands. Instead of leading with the hands and potentially taking the impact on the arms or head, opting for a foot-first landing creates a safer transition.\r\n\r\nPracticing the correct timing is crucial to executing the speed step effectively. The landing order should prioritize the foot\'s arrival before the hand, which requires coordination and focus. By refining this technique, individuals can improve their vaulting skills and ensure that their landings are less jarring, ultimately enhancing their overall agility and performance.\r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. The speed step leads with the foot to avoid injuries and make landings safer.\r\n2. It is particularly useful when moving quickly or descending to a lower surface.\r\n3. Proper timing in foot and hand placement is essential for effective execution.'),(52216,55448,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(52217,55448,'svg_id',''),(52218,55448,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(52219,55448,'svg_colour',''),(52220,55448,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(5