ng onto the wall with one foot after placing one hand on the outside and the other on the inside for support. The technique also emphasizes practicing bounce and foot placement to ensure that both feet land securely on the wall together. Proper positioning of the feet and hands is essential, as this forms the foundation for more complex movements.nnTo refine the side vault, it is advised to practice making initial jumps where one foot is placed onto the wall, followed by the other foot joining it. This drill helps build confidence and stability as participants learn to coordinate their movements effectively. Emphasis is placed on maintaining both feet together while jumping, as successful execution of the side vault requires synchronized movement to lift both feet off the ground simultaneously. nnFinally, variations can be introduced, such as using walls of different heights to establish skill levels and adaptability. Progressing from lower to higher walls allows for a gradual increase in difficulty, ultimately leading to successful execution of the full side vault. Consistent repetition of these techniques is crucial for mastering the movement and safely landing both feet on the wall during the final execution.nnKey Points:n1. Proper technique for side vaulting starts with foot and hand positioning to establish balance and control.n2. Practicing jumps to get both feet onto the wall is essential for achieving coordination and confidence.n3. Using walls of varying heights allows for progressive skill development in executing the side vault effectively.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1096,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 299,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1395,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"ZNYS44YPyJwsT4pktVqACt2H8G6JnNwBNGYOqX0PxZE-1735838529-1.0.1.1-bM5U52_P.ksQgx.IrTwHIWspbbmE9S4zNZLcnVo9n70sYiRH0_BGAmjRM2t1Y.QWAbHTVtG49w570cHnYaEMYQ\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840329,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"09zxdvl.540JFlbJlelsPZKH8s3TK2rRfiopFNsa9zQ-1735838529994-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(52990,55453,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(52991,55453,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The process of performing a side vault entails several critical steps designed to build skills progressively. The initial phase involves getting onto the wall with one foot after placing one hand on the outside and the other on the inside for support. The technique also emphasizes practicing bounce and foot placement to ensure that both feet land securely on the wall together. Proper positioning of the feet and hands is essential, as this forms the foundation for more complex movements.\r\n\r\nTo refine the side vault, it is advised to practice making initial jumps where one foot is placed onto the wall, followed by the other foot joining it. This drill helps build confidence and stability as participants learn to coordinate their movements effectively. Emphasis is placed on maintaining both feet together while jumping, as successful execution of the side vault requires synchronized movement to lift both feet off the ground simultaneously. \r\n\r\nFinally, variations can be introduced, such as using walls of different heights to establish skill levels and adaptability. Progressing from lower to higher walls allows for a gradual increase in difficulty, ultimately leading to successful execution of the full side vault. Consistent repetition of these techniques is crucial for mastering the movement and safely landing both feet on the wall during the final execution.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. Proper technique for side vaulting starts with foot and hand positioning to establish balance and control.\r\n2. Practicing jumps to get both feet onto the wall is essential for achieving coordination and confidence.\r\n3. Using walls of varying heights allows for progressive skill development in executing the side vault effectively.'),(52992,55453,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(52993,55453,'svg_id',''),(52994,55453,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(52995,55453,'svg_colour',''),(52996,55453,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(52997,55453,'extra_variables',''),(52998,55453,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(52999,55453,'notes',''),(53000,55453,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(53001,55453,'enable_youtube_api',''),(53002,55453,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(53003,55453,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(53004,55453,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(53005,55453,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(53006,55453,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(53007,