: 26.439,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.041\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"now going over and trying to clear the\",\r\n        \"start\": 29.24,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.639\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"whole thing so still one hand on the\",\r\n        \"start\": 33.48,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.919\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"outside one hand on the inside facing\",\r\n        \"start\": 36.879,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.2\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"parallel to the rail I\'m going to jump\",\r\n        \"start\": 40.399,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"up and\",\r\n        \"start\": 43.079,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.16\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"over you can build up to this as well by\",\r\n        \"start\": 45.079,\r\n        \"duration\": 8\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"just using the end of a rail so like\",\r\n        \"start\": 49.239,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.281\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"this where you are not making it over\",\r\n        \"start\": 53.079,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.081\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"but you can gradually build up so you\'re\",\r\n        \"start\": 57.52,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.879\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"relying on the hands getting your hips\",\r\n        \"start\": 60.16,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.24\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"up higher and higher and higher and you\",\r\n        \"start\": 62.399,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.641\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"can clear the rail so again face\",\r\n        \"start\": 65.4,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.399\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"parallel up over still parallel on the\",\r\n        \"start\": 69.04,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.399\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"other side this is the side Vault over a\",\r\n        \"start\": 72.799,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.64\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"rail\",\r\n        \"start\": 76.439,\r\n        \"duration\": 3\r\n    }\r\n]'),(53316,55455,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(53317,55455,'video_transcript_srt','1\r\n00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,000\r\nthe next part of a side Vault would be\r\n\r\n2\r\n00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000\r\nto practice on a rail and the reason to\r\n\r\n3\r\n00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000\r\npractice on a rail rather than a wall is\r\n\r\n4\r\n00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000\r\nthat it\'s much narrower and it means you\r\n\r\n5\r\n00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:25,000\r\ndon\'t have to travel as far as you go\r\n\r\n6\r\n00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000\r\nover it so it\'s instead of going on and\r\n\r\n7\r\n00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000\r\noff so jumping up on and off we\'re just\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:36,000\r\nnow going over and trying to clear the\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000\r\nwhole thing so still one hand on the\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000\r\noutside one hand on the inside facing\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000\r\nparallel to the rail I\'m going to jump\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000\r\nup and\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:53,000\r\nover you can build up to this as well by\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:57,000\r\njust using the end of a rail so like\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:53,000 --> 00:01:00,000\r\nthis where you are not making it over\r\n\r\n16\r\n00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000\r\nbut you can gradually build up so you\'re\r\n\r\n17\r\n00:00:60,000 --> 00:01:05,000\r\nrelying on the hands getting your hips\r\n\r\n18\r\n00:00:62,000 --> 00:01:08,000\r\nup higher and higher and higher and you\r\n\r\n19\r\n00:00:65,000 --> 00:01:12,000\r\ncan clear the rail so again face\r\n\r\n20\r\n00:00:69,000 --> 00:01:16,000\r\nparallel up over still parallel on the\r\n\r\n21\r\n00:00:72,000 --> 00:01:18,000\r\nother side this is the side Vault over a\r\n\r\n22\r\n00:00:76,000 --> 00:01:19,000\r\nrail\r\n\r\n'),(53318,55455,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(53319,55455,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJBHoJxjdWsG3dBvX7Z4IX2aqtzn\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735838511,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"Practicing a side vault on a rail is an effective way to improve technique and control. The rail\'s narrowness allows for a more focused movement pattern without the need for extensive travel distance, making it easier to approach the vault. Instead of simply jumping on and off, the goal is to learn to clear the rail, emphasizing a smoother motion over the obstacle.nnThe execution of the vault involves positioning one hand on the outside of the rail and the other on the inside, aligning the body parallel to the rail. This setup aids in building muscle memory before attempting to fully clear the rail. It’s also beneficial to start with smaller sections of the rail, gradually increasing the height as comfort and skill improve. Focusing on raising the hips while relying on the hands can facilitate getting over the rail effectively.nnWith consistent practice, the athlete will be able to clear the rail while maintaining parallel alignment throughout the movement, showcasing balance and control. Ultimately, mastering the side vault requires patience and progressive training, ensuring the fundamentals are solid before advancing to more complex maneuvers.nnKey Points:n1. Practicing on a rail is beneficial due to its narrowness, facilitating focus and reducing travel distance.n2. The side vault technique involves hand placement and body alignment for effective execution and control.n3. Gradual progression in height builds confidence and skill, aiding in the transition to more advanced vaulting techniques.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 831,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 278,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1109,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"KimAYXMjM7AaM.U25sVrLQmf.m3bsMnAfq0qTjzp3EU-1735838515-1.0.1.1-OCc7LkhdRJVtAb0F67mUONXU7R911BdURnHAWiTep9vIf3VzpNY_hbyW0TpPU6zQKcx3yyHVH7sueMH_9eBSJw\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840315,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"pylvV7nNJAe_b1ghn3JKfxGGveDxrjVGDDS268eaDW8-1735838515936-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(53320,55455,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(53321,55455,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Practicing a side vault on a rail is an effective way to improve technique and control. The rail\'s narrowness allows for a more focused movement pattern without the need for extensive travel distance, making it easier to approach the vault. Instead of simply jumping on and off, the goal is to learn to clear the rail, emphasizing a smoother motion over the obstacle.\r\n\r\nThe execution of the vault involves positioning one hand on the outside of the rail and the other on the inside, aligning the body parallel to the rail. This setup aids in building muscle memory before attempting to fully clear the rail. It’s also beneficial to start with smaller sections of the rail, gradually increasing the height as comfort and skill improve. Focusing on raising the hips while relying on the hands can facilitate getting over the rail effectively.\r\n\r\nWith consistent practice, the athlete will be able to clear the rail while maintaining parallel alignment throughout the movement, showcasing balance and control. Ultimately, mastering the side vault requires patience and progressive training, ensuring the fundamentals are solid before advancing to more complex maneuvers.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. Practicing on a rail is beneficial due to its narrowness, facilitating focus and reducing travel distance.\r\n2. The side vault technique involves hand placement and body alignment for effective execution and control.\r\n3. Gradual progression in height builds confidence and skill, aiding in the transition to more advanced vaulting techniques.'),(53322,55455,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(53323,55455,'svg_id',''),(53324,55455,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(53325,55455,'svg_colour',''),(53326,55455,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(53327,55455,'extra_variables',''),(53328,55455,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(53329,55455,'notes',''),(53330,55455,'_notes','field_6749f566