good challenge uh\r\n\r\n6\r\n00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000\r\na dual movement that is a good challenge\r\n\r\n7\r\n00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000\r\nso traveling\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000\r\nI\'m going to go left to right and\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,000\r\nlanding on that\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:44,000\r\nbar okay so that\'s the side Vault to pre\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:47,000\r\num and you will find this situation it\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000\r\nlooks a little bit unique but actually\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000\r\nyou\'ll find this more often than you\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000\r\nwould think this going over a w and\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:57,000\r\nlanding on something\r\n\r\n16\r\n00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000\r\nperpendicular uh yeah is uh the\r\n\r\n17\r\n00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,000\r\nsomething that happens in parkour\r\n\r\n18\r\n00:00:60,000 --> 00:01:05,000\r\nquite often and getting used to sort of\r\n\r\n19\r\n00:00:63,000 --> 00:01:08,000\r\ndoing that Precision sometimes it\'s\r\n\r\n20\r\n00:00:65,000 --> 00:01:11,000\r\nblind so you can\'t see the landing uh\r\n\r\n21\r\n00:00:69,000 --> 00:01:14,000\r\nyeah that\'s also an extra thing to get\r\n\r\n22\r\n00:00:72,000 --> 00:01:18,000\r\nused to so yeah practice that side Vault\r\n\r\n23\r\n00:00:74,000 --> 00:01:17,000\r\n2 pre\r\n\r\n'),(54154,55461,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(54155,55461,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJArmt5IkxMmUuUrRjpVPrqxHb5r\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735838485,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The discussion introduces a challenge in parkour that involves performing a side vault to pre, highlighting that this movement does not necessarily need to be a rail pre or precision landing. The task is described as going over an obstacle, such as a wall or bar, and then landing accurately on another surface. Completing this task can enhance proficiency in dual movement and improve landing accuracy.nnThe speaker emphasizes that maneuvers where a practitioner goes over an obstacle and lands on a perpendicular surface occur more frequently in parkour than one might expect. This kind of challenge requires adaptability, as often the landing is not clearly visible, making it essential for practitioners to develop the skill to execute moves confidently without direct sightlines to their landing space. Practice in these areas is vital for building trust in one\'s own abilities and spatial awareness.nnFurthermore, the session encourages continued practice of the side vault to pre. Engaging consistently with this movement prepares individuals for more complex parkour scenarios, ensuring they are well-equipped to handle various parkour environments. Ultimately, they are urged to actively refine their precision and adaptability through dedicated practice.nnKey points:n1. The side vault to pre is a useful parkour challenge that enhances landing accuracy and dual movement skills.n2. Practitioners often face landing on perpendicular surfaces, which may not always be visible, requiring significant spatial awareness.n3. Regular practice of challenging moves is essential for developing confidence and proficiency in various parkour scenarios.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 853,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 286,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1139,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"867V0kbrm.khqyisxgr1vzAXzi5ZKqDYAqz8aRWYmng-1735838489-1.0.1.1-HpHYiCZ6Q6jY1yaTnwwlTYx_oaEGSUHHSnyw4GayG0RXKN0cImtvur4FieCe3B57wnkX8fc.n1NwWORkPda.Qw\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840289,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"v2ba3mY1xUg7gi.oBC_sc1byexLXQsAKA9tJ1iDau2w-1735838489735-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(54156,55461,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(54157,55461,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The discussion introduces a challenge in parkour that involves performing a side vault to pre, highlighting that this movement does not necessarily need to be a rail pre or precision landing. The task is described as going over an obstacle, such as a wall or bar, and then landing accurately on another surface. Completing this task can enhance proficiency in dual movement and improve landing accuracy.\r\n\r\nThe speaker emphasizes that maneuvers where a practitioner goes over an obstacle and lands on a perpendicular surface occur more frequently in parkour than one might expect. This kind of challenge requires adaptability, as often the landing is not clearly visible, making it essential for practitioners to develop the skill to execute moves confidently without direct sightlines to their landing space. Practice in these areas is vital for building trust in one\'s own abilities and spatial awareness.\r\n\r\nFurthermore, the session encourages continued practice of the side vault to pre. Engaging consistently with this movement prepares individuals for more complex parkour scenarios, ensuring they are well-equipped to handle various parkour environments. Ultimately, they are urged to actively refine their precision and adaptability through dedicated practice.\r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. The side vault to pre is a useful parkour challenge that enhances landing accuracy and dual movement skills.\r\n2. Practitioners often face landing on perpendicular surfaces, which may not always be visible, requiring significant spatial awareness.\r\n3. Regular practice of challenging moves is essential for developing confidence and proficiency in various parkour scenarios.'),(54158,55461,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(54159,55461,'svg_id',''),(54160,55461,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(54161,55461,'svg_colour',''),(54162,55461,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(54163,55461,'extra_variables',''),(54164,55461,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(54165,55461,'notes',''),(54166,55461,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(54167,55461,'enable_youtube_api',''),(54168,55461,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(54169,55461,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(54170,55461,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(54171,55461,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(54172,55461,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(54173,55461,'ena