into an arm jump position or a similar stance to mitigate the risk of falling or losing their balance. By executing the turn vault, the performer can effectively drop and save themselves, displaying a combination of agility and control just before landing.nnThe procedure begins with the athlete jumping across the surface to initiate the turn vault. It resembles a conventional straight turn vault but modifies crucial aspects to adapt to the specific scenario of landing on a rail or wall. The technique involves a structured sequence where the performer transitions from the jump into the arm jump position, executing a half-turn and preparing for a stable landing.nnThrough careful timing and body positioning, the turn vault integrates a descending motion that enables the individual to navigate forward momentum effectively. By dropping to one hand and shifting to the arm jump position, a practitioner can land safely while maintaining control. This technique ultimately reinforces the importance of adapting movement strategies based on situational dynamics in parkour practice.nnKey Points:n1. The turn vault technique is used to manage excessive forward momentum when landing, allowing for a safe transition into an arm jump position.n2. The maneuver combines elements of a traditional turn vault and an arm jump to create a fluid movement upon landing.n3. Proper execution involves precise timing and body control to facilitate a secure landing while mitigating the risk of losing balance.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 995,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 289,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1284,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"DEOiPZYSE6i2._FK2mf5Wh4TTWUuC8dtSRQvp1IZ0Tw-1735840456-1.0.1.1-eOr1zNM2Sf51Em.k5OTp4cD8IcMg6iWSagnRJONEKgIq8EZPHff3UcQwPZ9sMYgGEjyX6SkVPI_AX2.TBLyDPQ\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735842256,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"2iq20i_DugSY62h_EsMWSDs.trjYPAdWrbuWaw2PCbQ-1735840456131-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(55717,55470,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(55718,55470,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The turn vault technique is crucial when a performer finds themselves with excessive forward momentum while landing on a wall. This maneuver allows the athlete to transition smoothly into an arm jump position or a similar stance to mitigate the risk of falling or losing their balance. By executing the turn vault, the performer can effectively drop and save themselves, displaying a combination of agility and control just before landing.\r\n\r\nThe procedure begins with the athlete jumping across the surface to initiate the turn vault. It resembles a conventional straight turn vault but modifies crucial aspects to adapt to the specific scenario of landing on a rail or wall. The technique involves a structured sequence where the performer transitions from the jump into the arm jump position, executing a half-turn and preparing for a stable landing.\r\n\r\nThrough careful timing and body positioning, the turn vault integrates a descending motion that enables the individual to navigate forward momentum effectively. By dropping to one hand and shifting to the arm jump position, a practitioner can land safely while maintaining control. This technique ultimately reinforces the importance of adapting movement strategies based on situational dynamics in parkour practice.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The turn vault technique is used to manage excessive forward momentum when landing, allowing for a safe transition into an arm jump position.\r\n2. The maneuver combines elements of a traditional turn vault and an arm jump to create a fluid movement upon landing.\r\n3. Proper execution involves precise timing and body control to facilitate a secure landing while mitigating the risk of losing balance.'),(55719,55470,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(55720,55470,'svg_id',''),(55721,55470,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(55722,55470,'svg_colour',''),(55723,55470,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(55724,55470,'extra_variables',''),(55725,55470,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(55726,55470,'notes',''),(55727,55470,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(55728,55470,'enable_youtube_api',''),(55729,55470,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(55730,55470,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(55731,55470,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(55732,55470,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(55733,55470,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(55734,55470,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(55735,55470,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(55736,55470,'you