00:01:77,000\r\ndoing the step first\r\n\r\n'),(56190,55473,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(56191,55473,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJJOLj0HImxh05CKOuvV0p0TGRZ6\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735839014,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"To successfully perform a vault, proper foot placement is essential. The inside foot, which is the one closest to the wall, should be positioned forward. This orientation allows the outside leg to swing upward effectively during the vault. Conversely, if the front leg is not positioned correctly, it could hinder the upward swing needed for a fluid motion into the vault.nnPracticing the kick-off and landing with the same foot is crucial for mastering the vault. Instead of a traditional step vault, one should hop down using the same leg that was used to initiate the jump. This method helps to develop the coordination necessary for a smooth transition from the vault\'s ascent to its descent, reinforcing muscle memory during training.nnAn additional focus should be on hand positioning to aid balance and support. It\'s beneficial to place the other hand behind oneself as the jump is executed. This technique allows for better stability and alignment, ultimately making the landing more controlled and balanced. Over time, this practice will lead to more advanced proficiency in vaulting techniques. nnKey points:n1. Correct foot placement is crucial, with the inside foot forward to facilitate a better swing of the outside leg.n2. Practice should involve using the same foot for both take-off and landing to enhance coordination.n3. Hand positioning can significantly impact balance, with the opposite hand placed behind to improve stability during the vault.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1523,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 269,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1792,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"LWxJFPao4.GgpaCUYXn9r6_rQKV91.HPm8jkWcYKQ9k-1735839018-1.0.1.1-z1QrDi2Bz34phPNHuF0e.HjA1oqP_rrGwpzEc37bVmSVI8_00FoCkeTyvgdZhE1CLO1LJ8orlwlUj7f3Ghm7rA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840818,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"wYoSYXB0rrCMMzqBNG6wnp.kSwlN3UvtQQqqtP0FPNw-1735839018950-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(56192,55473,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(56193,55473,'video_transcript_chatgpt','To successfully perform a vault, proper foot placement is essential. The inside foot, which is the one closest to the wall, should be positioned forward. This orientation allows the outside leg to swing upward effectively during the vault. Conversely, if the front leg is not positioned correctly, it could hinder the upward swing needed for a fluid motion into the vault.\r\n\r\nPracticing the kick-off and landing with the same foot is crucial for mastering the vault. Instead of a traditional step vault, one should hop down using the same leg that was used to initiate the jump. This method helps to develop the coordination necessary for a smooth transition from the vault\'s ascent to its descent, reinforcing muscle memory during training.\r\n\r\nAn additional focus should be on hand positioning to aid balance and support. It\'s beneficial to place the other hand behind oneself as the jump is executed. This technique allows for better stability and alignment, ultimately making the landing more controlled and balanced. Over time, this practice will lead to more advanced proficiency in vaulting techniques. \r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. Correct foot placement is crucial, with the inside foot forward to facilitate a better swing of the outside leg.\r\n2. Practice should involve using the same foot for both take-off and landing to enhance coordination.\r\n3. Hand positioning can significantly impact balance, with the opposite hand placed behind to improve stability during the vault.'),(56194,55473,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(56195,55473,'svg_id',''),(56196,55473,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(56197,55473,'svg_colour',''),(56198,55473,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(56199,55473,'extra_variables',''),(56200,55473,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(56201,55473,'notes',''),(56202,55473,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(56203,55473,'enable_youtube_api',''),(56204,55473,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf')