y the tricky part is getting the\",\r\n        \"start\": 12.36,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.36\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"leg the inside leg tucked underneath you\",\r\n        \"start\": 16.32,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"so you\'ll see when when you do it that\",\r\n        \"start\": 19.72,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.52\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"back leg is tucked underneath As you\",\r\n        \"start\": 23,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.08\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"move so one way to practice that is find\",\r\n        \"start\": 25.24,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.8\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"a wide wall that you can sit on so from\",\r\n        \"start\": 29.08,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.08\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"here sit on the wall and bring the other\",\r\n        \"start\": 32.04,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.72\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"hand back so your hips are facing along\",\r\n        \"start\": 35.16,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.64\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"the wall if you don\'t put this hand on\",\r\n        \"start\": 37.76,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.08\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"you\'ll tend to twist out of the Vault\",\r\n        \"start\": 39.8,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.52\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"and this isn\'t good you\'re not going to\",\r\n        \"start\": 42.84,\r\n        \"duration\": 4\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"be able to land properly but land in\",\r\n        \"start\": 44.32,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.44\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"this position to sit on the wall and\",\r\n        \"start\": 46.84,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"then focus on bringing that foot down\",\r\n        \"start\": 48.76,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.319\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"first the the leg that\'s tucked under\",\r\n        \"start\": 51.52,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.679\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"never goes on the floor first um yeah it\",\r\n        \"start\": 54.079,\r\n        \"duration\": 6.721\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"stays tucked so let\'s do that again so\",\r\n        \"start\": 58.199,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.801\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"up Tuck hand behind step off and down\",\r\n        \"start\": 60.8,\r\n        \"duration\": 7.679\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"get used to that foot tuck underneath\",\r\n        \"start\": 66,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.36\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"and then as you feel more comfortable\",\r\n        \"start\": 68.479,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.361\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"instead of sitting you just go\",\r\n        \"start\": 70.36,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"over it\'s the same thing your bum\",\r\n        \"start\": 72.84,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.24\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"doesn\'t touch and the slide Vault then\",\r\n        \"start\": 76.04,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.759\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"becomes the slide vault\",\r\n        \"start\": 78.08,\r\n        \"duration\": 3.719\r\n    }\r\n]'),(56360,55474,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(56361,55474,'video_transcript_srt','1\r\n00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,000\r\nso when we are talking about the slide\r\n\r\n2\r\n00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:16,000\r\nVault uh or slide\r\n\r\n3\r\n00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:19,000\r\nmonkey the tricky part is getting the\r\n\r\n4\r\n00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000\r\nleg the inside leg tucked underneath you\r\n\r\n5\r\n00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000\r\nso you\'ll see when when you do it that\r\n\r\n6\r\n00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,000\r\nback leg is tucked underneath As you\r\n\r\n7\r\n00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:31,000\r\nmove so one way to practice that is find\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000\r\na wide wall that you can sit on so from\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000\r\nhere sit on the wall and bring the other\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000\r\nhand back so your hips are facing along\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,000\r\nthe wall if you don\'t put this hand on\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000\r\nyou\'ll tend to twist out of the Vault\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,000\r\nand this isn\'t good you\'re not going to\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000\r\nbe able to land properly but land in\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000\r\nthis position to sit on the wall and\r\n\r\n16\r\n00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000\r\nthen focus on bringing that foot down\r\n\r\n17\r\n00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000\r\nfirst the the leg that\'s tucked under\r\n\r\n18\r\n00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:00,000\r\nnever goes on the floor first um yeah it\r\n\r\n19\r\n00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:05,000\r\nstays tucked so let\'s do that again so\r\n\r\n20\r\n00:00:60,000 --> 00:01:07,000\r\nup Tuck hand behind step off and down\r\n\r\n21\r\n00:00:66,000 --> 00:01:10,000\r\nget used to that foot tuck underneath\r\n\r\n22\r\n00:00:68,000 --> 00:01:12,000\r\nand then as you feel more comfortable\r\n\r\n23\r\n00:00:70,000 --> 00:01:15,000\r\ninstead of sitting you just go\r\n\r\n24\r\n00:00:72,000 --> 00:01:17,000\r\nover it\'s the same thing your bum\r\n\r\n25\r\n00:00:76,000 --> 00:01:21,000\r\ndoesn\'t touch and the slide Vault then\r\n\r\n26\r\n00:00:78,000 --> 00:01:21,000\r\nbecomes the slide vault\r\n\r\n'),(56362,55474,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(56363,55474,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJJGaMwx2F3bg1aPRhBmbb4bWqz0\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735839006,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"When learning the slide vault technique, one of the essential aspects is ensuring that the inside leg remains tucked underneath throughout the movement. Practicing this technique involves sitting against a wall to develop the habit of keeping this leg in the correct position while preparing to execute the vault. The placement of the hands is also crucial; it is recommended to place a hand behind to maintain proper alignment, preventing twisting out of the vault, which can lead to an improper landing.nnA suggested exercise for mastering this technique starts with sitting against a wall and then transitioning to bringing the tucked leg down. It’s important to practice this movement consistently and make sure that the tucked leg never touches the ground first. This step helps in building the necessary muscle memory, so the movement becomes more fluid and instinctive. As comfort increases, practitioners should gradually progress by eliminating the sitting position and moving directly into the vault.nnThe ultimate goal is to execute the slide vault smoothly by transitioning from a sitting position to executing the movement without any contact of the backside with the ground. With practice and attention to detail, this progression will help refine the technique and increase confidence when performing the slide vault. Following these steps can facilitate learning the slide vault effectively through repetition and gradual advancement.nnKey Points:n1. Keeping the inside leg tucked during the slide vault is essential for proper technique and landing.n2. Practicing by sitting against a wall and ensuring correct hand placement helps in developing muscle memory.n3. Progression from a sitting position to executing the vault directly promotes fluidity and confidence in the movement.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 973,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 308,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1281,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"frnphm8e0RtTpvZMiiQkwx0MFX7JqYi9uPFhfKyb0uU-1735839013-1.0.1.1-ML.DatH0KuD1kT8axWq2WXcJO6Pnn9QvRWMR0Lv_s.V7B97ts0bVaeo6FzMM5o6O1AnL_YY1flC9hmDlO60Atg\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735840813,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"9lMfkKd4MOJWeH7.yOwqDWwhelwZMbTMQxxXPNJv7CA-1735839013067-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(56364,55474,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(56365,55474,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When learning the slide vault technique, one of the essential aspects is ensuring that the inside leg remains tucked underneath throughout the movement. Practicing this technique involves sitting against a wall to develop the habit of keeping this leg in the correct position while preparing to execute the vault. The placement of the hands is also crucial; it is recommended to place a hand behind to maintain proper alignment, preventing twisting out of the vault, which can lead to an improper landing.\r\n\r\nA suggested exercise for mastering this technique starts with sitting against a wall and then transitioning to bringing the tucked leg down. It’s important to practice this movement consistently and make sure that the tucked leg never touches the ground first. This step helps in building the necessary muscle memory, so the movement becomes more fluid and instinctive. As comfort increases, practitioners should gradually progress by eliminating the sitting position and moving directly into the vault.\r\n\r\nThe ultimate goal is to execute the slide vault smoothly by transitioning from a sitting position to executing the movement without any contact of the backside with the ground. With practice and attention to detail, this progression will help refine the technique and increase confidence when performing the slide vault. Following these steps can facilitate learning the slide vault effectively through repetition and gradual advancement.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. Keeping the inside leg tucked during the slide vault is essential for proper technique and landing.\r\n2. Practicing by sitting against a wall and ensuring correct hand placement helps in developing muscle memory.\r\n3. Progression from a sitting position to executing the vault directly promotes fluidity and confidence in the movement.'),(56366,55474,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(56367,55474,'svg_id',''),(56368,55474,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(56369,55474,'svg_colour',''),(56370,55474,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(563