times you land in\r\n\r\n41\r\n00:00:117,000 --> 00:01:64,000\r\nthis position and you can only do one or\r\n\r\n42\r\n00:00:120,000 --> 00:01:65,000\r\nthe other in particular scenarios\r\n\r\n'),(58112,55485,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(58113,55485,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlIqodir4ylE24G4QVq9pVlouEbJ8\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735837242,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The lazy vault and slide vault are two fundamental techniques used in acrobatic movements, with the lazy vault being the reverse of the slide vault. In a slide vault, the outside leg is positioned to reach the wall, while in a lazy vault, the inside leg moves back. Practicing these techniques involves adjusting body positioning to effectively drive the leading knee and foot over the obstacle and landing appropriately on the other side.nnWhen executing the lazy vault, coordination is key. The practitioner must ensure that the inside leg goes over first, followed by the front leg. Maintaining a straight line towards the wall helps ensure proper form and a safe landing. It is also important to keep the upper body facing forward while avoiding twisting the hips. Practicing on a wall can help in mastering the movements until the correct technique becomes second nature.nnMastering both the lazy vault and slide vault adds versatility to an acrobat\'s skill set. Each technique has its advantages depending on the landing position or the obstacle\'s height. By being trained in both styles, practitioners can adapt to different scenarios when performing, enhancing their proficiency in movement and overall performance.nn**Key Points:**n1. The lazy vault is the opposite of the slide vault, with different leg positioning and body mechanics.n2. Proper body coordination and alignment are crucial for executing the lazy vault effectively.n3. Mastering both the lazy vault and slide vault gives practitioners greater adaptability in various acrobatic scenarios.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1540,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 288,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1828,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"0ketWfsxjrssMReRvtCgfPynvhpSuhmX.k81AOl0gDI-1735837248-1.0.1.1-Y1DY0Aq06VASEcE_meQ3IhB.ZwzyYzbYJf9ySBlIo0U485DYFUmIQTbvmnb5_rjzpo.K4d2ZBcjyBZvYqd0eLQ\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735839048,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"biyDlFzD57DOl286XTJ_.Py8wxfmJBuohQR6ztabzgw-1735837248361-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(58114,55485,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(58115,55485,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The lazy vault and slide vault are two fundamental techniques used in acrobatic movements, with the lazy vault being the reverse of the slide vault. In a slide vault, the outside leg is positioned to reach the wall, while in a lazy vault, the inside leg moves back. Practicing these techniques involves adjusting body positioning to effectively drive the leading knee and foot over the obstacle and landing appropriately on the other side.\r\n\r\nWhen executing the lazy vault, coordination is key. The practitioner must ensure that the inside leg goes over first, followed by the front leg. Maintaining a straight line towards the wall helps ensure proper form and a safe landing. It is also important to keep the upper body facing forward while avoiding twisting the hips. Practicing on a wall can help in mastering the movements until the correct technique becomes second nature.\r\n\r\nMastering both the lazy vault and slide vault adds versatility to an acrobat\'s skill set. Each technique has its advantages depending on the landing position or the obstacle\'s height. By being trained in both styles, practitioners can adapt to different scenarios when performing, enhancing their proficiency in movement and overall performance.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. The lazy vault is the opposite of the slide vault, with different leg positioning and body mechanics.\r\n2. Proper body coordination and alignment are crucial for executing the lazy vault effectively.\r\n3. Mastering both the lazy vault and slide vault gives practitioners greater adaptability in various acrobatic scenarios.'),(58116,55485,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(58117,55485,'svg_id',''),(58118,55485,'_svg_id','field_67160c9