"text\": \"up like this so again let\'s go again you\",\r\n        \"start\": 47.44,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.68\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"kick and both feet come underneath you\",\r\n        \"start\": 52.76,\r\n        \"duration\": 8.36\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"and land between your hands\",\r\n        \"start\": 56.12,\r\n        \"duration\": 5\r\n    }\r\n]'),(59271,55494,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(59272,55494,'video_transcript_srt','1\r\n00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000\r\nwe\'ve been working on the pop Vault so\r\n\r\n2\r\n00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000\r\nwe\'ve been able to get our foot on the\r\n\r\n3\r\n00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000\r\noutside we\'ve been able to get our foot\r\n\r\n4\r\n00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:19,000\r\nin the inside the next step which is a\r\n\r\n5\r\n00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,000\r\nbig progression is now getting both feet\r\n\r\n6\r\n00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000\r\non top at the same time so this is a cap\r\n\r\n7\r\n00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000\r\npass or the same movement as a cat pass\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000\r\nbut combined with the pop on the side of\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000\r\nthe wall so we\'re getting height we\'re\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000\r\ngetting our hips up high to then be able\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000\r\nto push and get our feet in in between\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,000\r\nour hands it\'s a bilateral movement both\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000\r\nhands are on both feet come\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:55,000\r\nup like this so again let\'s go again you\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:00,000\r\nkick and both feet come underneath you\r\n\r\n16\r\n00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000\r\nand land between your hands\r\n\r\n'),(59273,55494,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(59274,55494,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJ3KxpCCD3ArlatineKUmXwvtJdh\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735838018,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The discussion revolves around a new movement technique known as the \"pop Vault,\" which is designed to enhance performance in gymnastics or related disciplines. The technique begins with establishing a strong position, first utilizing one foot, then integrating both feet into the movement to create a significant progression. This evolution emphasizes the importance of balance and control while executing the vault, which requires practice for mastery.nnThe \"pop Vault\" combines elements of existing methods, particularly the \"cat pass,\" while adding a dynamic side movement against a wall. By focusing on getting the hips up high, practitioners can effectively push and position their feet correctly between their hands. This requires coordination and timing, ensuring both feet land in a controlled manner to facilitate a clean finish to the movement.nnTraining for the pop Vault incorporates several key components, including synchronized bilateral movements and the necessity of kicking both feet underneath the body as one ascends. Successful execution not only depends on strength but also on technique, prompting a need for repeated practice to enhance performance and achieve the desired landing position.nnKey Points:n1. The pop Vault enhances performance by integrating both feet into a dynamic movement after establishing a solid base.n2. The technique combines elements of the \"cat pass,\" focusing on height and controlled landing between the hands.n3. Mastery requires synchronized movements and repeated practice to improve timing and technique.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 624,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 266,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 890,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"ZJYrkrtJT5MnaALVvlaCdth2sRlzPnQMOib.2ZHJeFs-1735838021-1.0.1.1-B5d9GWqt0AJYrWRx1jA_WJeFiMPpG1twt5L8AI3L.2IKb2x8foSdlKt0MWdFhyfWrIIquQz2uwKYQXuyR1OARg\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735839821,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"_0YY2f.o2cOrZTUiBzWCmDeXrDqATSSlj.TiENY4mFA-1735838021601-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(59275,55494,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(59276,55494,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The discussion revolves around a new movement technique known as the \"pop Vault,\" which is designed to enhance performance in gymnastics or related disciplines. The technique begins with establishing a strong position, first utilizing one foot, then integrating both feet into the movement to create a significant progression. This evolution emphasizes the importance of balance and control while executing the vault, which requires practice for mastery.\r\n\r\nThe \"pop Vault\" combines elements of existing methods, particularly the \"cat pass,\" while adding a dynamic side movement against a wall. By focusing on getting the hips up high, practitioners can effectively push and position their feet correctly between their hands. This requires coordination and timing, ensuring both feet land in a controlled manner to facilitate a clean finish to the movement.\r\n\r\nTraining for the pop Vault incorporates several key components, including synchronized bilateral movements and the necessity of kicking both feet underneath the body as one ascends. Successful execution not only depends on strength but also on technique, prompting a need for repeated practice to enhance performance and achieve the desired landing position.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The pop Vault enhances performance by integrating both feet into a dynamic movement after establishing a solid base.\r\n2. The technique combines elements of the \"cat pass,\" focusing on height and controlled landing between the hands.\r\n3. Mastery requires synchronized movements and repeated practice to improve timing and technique.'),(59277,55494,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(59278,55494,'svg_id',''),(59279,55494,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(59280,55494,'svg_colour',''),(59281,55494,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(59282,55494,'extra_variables',''),(59283,55494,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(59284,55494,'notes',''),(59285,55494,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(59286,55494,'enable_youtube_api',''),(59287,55494,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5