\r\nusually on something that\'s a little bit\r\n\r\n8\r\n00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000\r\nhigher than normal than you would do on\r\n\r\n9\r\n00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000\r\na normal Vault um\r\n\r\n10\r\n00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000\r\nand I tend to see people try to do it\r\n\r\n11\r\n00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000\r\nand land on top so it would be sort of\r\n\r\n12\r\n00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,000\r\nlike a like that but this is sort of\r\n\r\n13\r\n00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:44,000\r\nlike a half pop\r\n\r\n14\r\n00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000\r\nVault when you\'re doing a a full proper\r\n\r\n15\r\n00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000\r\npop Vault the idea is to not land on top\r\n\r\n16\r\n00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000\r\nso if you\'re doing a cat pass Pop um you\r\n\r\n17\r\n00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000\r\nneed to go over it or if you\'re doing a\r\n\r\n18\r\n00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000\r\nstep volt it needs to be over it speed\r\n\r\n19\r\n00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000\r\nvolt whatever but the pop is supposed to\r\n\r\n20\r\n00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:02,000\r\ntry and get you over the wall not on top\r\n\r\n21\r\n00:00:62,000 --> 00:01:06,000\r\nso let\'s give that a go you need to put\r\n\r\n22\r\n00:00:63,000 --> 00:01:08,000\r\na lot more force in and when you kick it\r\n\r\n23\r\n00:00:66,000 --> 00:01:12,000\r\nyou\'re pushing upwards um you can\r\n\r\n24\r\n00:00:69,000 --> 00:01:14,000\r\npractice that so pushing up off of the\r\n\r\n25\r\n00:00:72,000 --> 00:01:20,000\r\nwall um but it should give you enough\r\n\r\n26\r\n00:00:75,000 --> 00:01:20,000\r\nmomentum to then land in the\r\n\r\n27\r\n00:00:88,000 --> 00:01:31,000\r\nvault and\r\n\r\n'),(59879,55498,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(59880,55498,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlJ2ZX2k8WotJ5I5Bb9uK7jJ0PKxh\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735837971,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The POP Vault is an advanced movement technique that combines elements of a cat pass and a normal vault. The key difference lies in how one uses their foot against the wall to generate upward momentum. This technique is typically executed on a surface that is higher than what one would use for a standard vault, allowing for a more dynamic performance. Instead of aiming to land on top of the obstacle, the objective is to clear it completely by propelling oneself over.nnWhen attempting the POP Vault, it is crucial to direct the body upwards while executing the movement. Many practitioners mistakenly land on or try to cling to the top of the obstacle, failing to fully utilize the vault\'s capabilities. A successful POP Vault requires confidence in pushing off the wall with greater force, ensuring that the focus remains on achieving height and distance over the barrier rather than just clearing the top edge.nnIn practice, the technique involves generating sufficient upward momentum through a strong kick off the wall, facilitating a successful landing beyond the obstacle. Emphasis is placed on maintaining speed and form throughout the execution to improve proficiency in the movement. By mastering the POP Vault, individuals can enhance their overall agility and performance in various parkour activities.nn**Key Points:**n1. The POP Vault combines elements of the cat pass and standard vault, emphasizing momentum to clear obstacles rather than landing on them.n2. Proper technique involves pushing upward off the wall with force, ensuring focus on height and distance.n3. Practicing this movement improves agility and overall performance in parkour activities.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1011,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 303,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1314,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"ydQRNOv4mSNxZM8B2QCcwerWyApe_x.FEDX2ljVI_oQ-1735837975-1.0.1.1-G9qZ9JnFHSmtvcxCCcvgO79kb6uXINtmlDKrNhwO0aaBd25qVrrFvj5kYjIYuHa_ZuPva0ZTw0eJO.6SBPzj5w\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735839775,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"WoVdEGeF8gqYRH2ajor4vdehL40_1_3CVhcFrvqpoq0-1735837975072-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(59881,55498,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(59882,55498,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The POP Vault is an advanced movement technique that combines elements of a cat pass and a normal vault. The key difference lies in how one uses their foot against the wall to generate upward momentum. This technique is typically executed on a surface that is higher than what one would use for a standard vault, allowing for a more dynamic performance. Instead of aiming to land on top of the obstacle, the objective is to clear it completely by propelling oneself over.\r\n\r\nWhen attempting the POP Vault, it is crucial to direct the body upwards while executing the movement. Many practitioners mistakenly land on or try to cling to the top of the obstacle, failing to fully utilize the vault\'s capabilities. A successful POP Vault requires confidence in pushing off the wall with greater force, ensuring that the focus remains on achieving height and distance over the barrier rather than just clearing the top edge.\r\n\r\nIn practice, the technique involves generating sufficient upward momentum through a strong kick off the wall, facilitating a successful landing beyond the obstacle. Emphasis is placed on maintaining speed and form throughout the execution to improve proficiency in the movement. By mastering the POP Vault, individuals can enhance their overall agility and performance in various parkour activities.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. The POP Vault combines elements of the cat pass and standard vault, emphasizing momentum to clear obstacles rather than landing on them.\r\n2. Proper technique involves pushing upward off the wall with force, ensuring focus on height and distance.\r\n3. Practicing this movement improves agility and overall performance in parkour activities.'),(59883,55498,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(59884,55498,'svg_id',''),(59885,55498,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(59886,55498,'svg_colour',''),(59887,55498,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(59888,55498,'extra_variables',''),(59889,55498,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(59890,55498,'enable_youtube_api',''),(59891,55498,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(59892,55498,'enable_