                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The lesson focuses on executing the full-speed vault, transitioning from using two hands to a single hand for support during the jump. The technique involves taking off similarly to a step vault, where the individual relies primarily on one hand for power and propulsion as they prepare to leap over the obstacle. Instead of two hands touching the wall, the athlete uses one flat hand to help with balance and height, marking a key difference from previous vaulting techniques.nnDuring the execution, it\'s essential to gather enough speed before taking off on the single leg. The technique relies heavily on the strength and positioning of the hand, which must support most of the body weight during the vault. Proper form is emphasized to ensure that the landing is stable, with one foot making contact with the ground first, allowing for a controlled descent that maintains momentum.nnThis full-speed approach represents a more advanced form of vaulting that builds on earlier foundational skills. It requires not only physical strength but also precision in timing and body control. As the athlete practices, the objective is to smoothly integrate these movements and achieve a successful vault with confidence and finesse.nn**Key Points:**n1. Transitioning to the full-speed vault involves using one hand to assist in the jump, differing from the traditional two-hand technique.n2. Athletes must gather adequate speed and focus on the strength of their hand to ensure a successful landing.n3. Mastery of this advanced technique relies on precision and body control developed from foundational skills.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 651,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 293,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 944,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"Bb.fkCsGF_W2iLDZkY6NbAwnUGvk8ZZwsWD4zvo9rgA-1735839954-1.0.1.1-P_M9rKA4I8P8oz2P5dmi7IUAJO.L84iSbuXRxaDfzoCv97Dxp5Mxbh0oMB.rYryTLFHzwI6oHVE9NqHb1UHztw\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735841754,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"9zWzCISYil7KXna7WCt1e5aIKPmp9S4QqtqrwnZuj_U-1735839954617-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(60978,55507,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(60979,55507,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The lesson focuses on executing the full-speed vault, transitioning from using two hands to a single hand for support during the jump. The technique involves taking off similarly to a step vault, where the individual relies primarily on one hand for power and propulsion as they prepare to leap over the obstacle. Instead of two hands touching the wall, the athlete uses one flat hand to help with balance and height, marking a key difference from previous vaulting techniques.\r\n\r\nDuring the execution, it\'s essential to gather enough speed before taking off on the single leg. The technique relies heavily on the strength and positioning of the hand, which must support most of the body weight during the vault. Proper form is emphasized to ensure that the landing is stable, with one foot making contact with the ground first, allowing for a controlled descent that maintains momentum.\r\n\r\nThis full-speed approach represents a more advanced form of vaulting that builds on earlier foundational skills. It requires not only physical strength but also precision in timing and body control. As the athlete practices, the objective is to smoothly integrate these movements and achieve a successful vault with confidence and finesse.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. Transitioning to the full-speed vault involves using one hand to assist in the jump, differing from the traditional two-hand technique.\r\n2. Athletes must gather adequate speed and focus on the strength of their hand to ensure a successful landing.\r\n3. Mastery of this advanced technique relies on precision and body control developed from foundational skills.'),(60980,55507,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(60981,55507,'svg_id',''),(60982,55507,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(60983,55507,'svg_colour',''),(60984,55507,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(60985,55507,'extra_variables',''),(60986,55507,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(60987,55507,'notes',''),(60988,55507,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(60989,55507,'enable_youtube_api',''),(60990,55507,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(60991,55507,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(60992,55507,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(60993,55507,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(60994,55507,'_wordpress_filter_name','