\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The scissor kick speed vault is a visually appealing movement in Parkour, often associated with the early practitioners like the Yamakasi. While it adds a flair to the speed vault by emphasizing the top leg leading forward, it is not a necessary technique for effective Parkour practice. Its primary purpose is to enhance the aesthetics of the movement, making it appear cooler and more dynamic than it otherwise might be.nnExecuting the scissor kick involves coordinating both legs – leading with the top leg while scissoring the back leg to land smoothly. This technique brings a degree of nostalgia and fun, reminiscent of its usage in the early days of Parkour. Although it does not serve a significant functional role in Parkour, its engaging nature allows practitioners to experiment with their skills and creativity.nnIn conclusion, the scissor kick speed vault is primarily a stylistic element rather than a fundamental part of Parkour. Those proficient with the standard speed vault can consider incorporating the scissor kick for added visual excitement while maintaining their technique. Overall, it\'s a playful addition to enhance one\'s repertoire in Parkour.nn**Key Points:**n1. The scissor kick speed vault enhances the aesthetics of Parkour but is not essential for effective practice.n2. It involves careful coordination of movement, highlighting the top leg while the back leg is scissored to land.n3. The technique is nostalgic and fun, allowing for creativity but serves no significant functional purpose in Parkour.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1247,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 290,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1537,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"ubDN_tXyXFOcB04d2AKqJ0McmXhjSiBFjKb8hrh8pRE-1735839948-1.0.1.1-kV1uUM.olwcwHE.q3n_LJGeufylQcUEhMg_1OTAbkQab1v2cmu6YE_C7_AaAMVQ6OJJFEgD.d9zNOMMJH_1siw\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735841748,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"M.TNSS33pBtnvy4aE3kEw6LepLRXMyeJfDyieX4aLbo-1735839948694-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(61379,55510,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(61380,55510,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The scissor kick speed vault is a visually appealing movement in Parkour, often associated with the early practitioners like the Yamakasi. While it adds a flair to the speed vault by emphasizing the top leg leading forward, it is not a necessary technique for effective Parkour practice. Its primary purpose is to enhance the aesthetics of the movement, making it appear cooler and more dynamic than it otherwise might be.\r\n\r\nExecuting the scissor kick involves coordinating both legs – leading with the top leg while scissoring the back leg to land smoothly. This technique brings a degree of nostalgia and fun, reminiscent of its usage in the early days of Parkour. Although it does not serve a significant functional role in Parkour, its engaging nature allows practitioners to experiment with their skills and creativity.\r\n\r\nIn conclusion, the scissor kick speed vault is primarily a stylistic element rather than a fundamental part of Parkour. Those proficient with the standard speed vault can consider incorporating the scissor kick for added visual excitement while maintaining their technique. Overall, it\'s a playful addition to enhance one\'s repertoire in Parkour.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. The scissor kick speed vault enhances the aesthetics of Parkour but is not essential for effective practice.\r\n2. It involves careful coordination of movement, highlighting the top leg while the back leg is scissored to land.\r\n3. The technique is nostalgic and fun, allowing for creativity but serves no significant functional purpose in Parkour.'),(61381,55510,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(61382,55510,'svg_id',''),(61383,55510,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(61384,55510,'svg_colour',''),(61385,55510,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(61386,55510,'extra_variables',''),(61387,55510,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(61388,55510,'notes',''),(61389,55510,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(61390,55510,'enable_youtube_api',''),(61391,55510,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(61392,55510,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(61393,55510,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(61394,55510,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(61395,55510,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(61396,55510,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(61397,55510,'_ena