0\r\nfirst step\r\n\r\n'),(61928,55514,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(61929,55514,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlIjeKEJa6NjrzosbkKib87pklHK8\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735836798,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"Learning to perform a dash vault is a progressive journey that begins with the fundamental movements necessary for success. Initially, one should focus on jumping onto a wall with the feet first, incorporating a box jump to build momentum. The technique involves landing with the feet and subsequently using the hands to push away from the wall, an essential part of mastering the dash vault skill.nnTo practice effectively, starting with a lower wall can help build confidence and control. As one gets comfortable with the initial motions, it is important to work on the jump using both feet and to bring the hands behind for a better push-off. This not only aids in the mechanics of the vault but also enhances the overall experience of executing the move, making it smoother and more reliable.nnUltimately, gaining confidence with each practice session is crucial. The better one can manage the jump and push away, the more successful they will become at performing the dash vault. Regularly practicing these drills will lead to significant improvements in technique and execution, paving the way for more advanced variations in the future.nnKey points:n1. The dash vault involves sequential movements: jumping with feet first, landing on the wall, and pushing off with hands.n2. Starting with a lower wall encourages skill development and confidence, allowing for gradual progression.n3. Consistent practice of the jump and push-off techniques enhances overall performance and confidence in executing the vault.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 938,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 277,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1215,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"OPH88nokE1yjgsCRPnXj6xyywFBXfJIKDwkshtpT1iE-1735836802-1.0.1.1-JxV_EK1KI3R_r2BY1mqmkv5.iFnTohOx5ALNFxL26FblrPCyA7YccgxO2SODP9cs1m96LE9DiKvq8xZ9.hGPrQ\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735838602,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"K20ysJ6h4NHVEiTeXLkuJsUpKdjoGYwtqLYuecYUWtk-1735836802445-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(61930,55514,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(61931,55514,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Learning to perform a dash vault is a progressive journey that begins with the fundamental movements necessary for success. Initially, one should focus on jumping onto a wall with the feet first, incorporating a box jump to build momentum. The technique involves landing with the feet and subsequently using the hands to push away from the wall, an essential part of mastering the dash vault skill.\r\n\r\nTo practice effectively, starting with a lower wall can help build confidence and control. As one gets comfortable with the initial motions, it is important to work on the jump using both feet and to bring the hands behind for a better push-off. This not only aids in the mechanics of the vault but also enhances the overall experience of executing the move, making it smoother and more reliable.\r\n\r\nUltimately, gaining confidence with each practice session is crucial. The better one can manage the jump and push away, the more successful they will become at performing the dash vault. Regularly practicing these drills will lead to significant improvements in technique and execution, paving the way for more advanced variations in the future.\r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. The dash vault involves sequential movements: jumping with feet first, landing on the wall, and pushing off with hands.\r\n2. Starting with a lower wall encourages skill development and confidence, allowing for gradual progression.\r\n3. Consistent practice of the jump and push-off techniques enhances overall performance and confidence in executing the vault.'),(61932,55514,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(61933,55514,'svg_id',''),(61934,55514,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(61935,55514,'svg_colour',''),(61936,55514,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(61937,55514,'extra_variables',''),(61938,55514,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(61939,55514,'notes',''),(61940,55514,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(61941,55514,'enable_yo