00:75,000 --> 00:01:20,000\r\nthe hands placing them on the wall\r\n\r\n25\r\n00:00:77,000 --> 00:01:23,000\r\nbehind me and getting used to dropping\r\n\r\n26\r\n00:00:80,000 --> 00:01:24,000\r\noff of that wall uh in the correct Dash\r\n\r\n27\r\n00:00:83,000 --> 00:01:28,000\r\nVault position this is the first thing\r\n\r\n28\r\n00:00:85,000 --> 00:01:28,000\r\nto start getting used to\r\n\r\n'),(62386,55517,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(62387,55517,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AlIjzIZIDeyFPizHzWkZUPfRAKxRq\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735836819,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The dash vault is an acrobatic move that contrasts with the cat pass. While the cat pass involves leading with the hands and executing a bilateral movement with both legs following, the dash vault begins with the legs leading and is followed by the hands coming into contact with the wall. This technique is crucial for parkour and similar fields, as it allows for smoother transitions over obstacles.nnTo properly perform the dash vault, one must focus on exiting the maneuver effectively. Initially, the practitioner should practice hopping down from a wall while simultaneously placing their hands behind them on the wall. This technique helps develop muscle memory and confidence, especially since one does not typically see where their hands are placed during the vault. The goal is to ensure that the legs clear the wall before the hands follow up, allowing for a safe and efficient landing.nnIt is important to get accustomed to the motions involved in the dash vault, particularly the act of dropping off the wall in the proper position. This foundational practice builds the necessary skills to execute more complex parkour maneuvers while maintaining safety and control during high-energy movements.nnKey Points:n1. The dash vault involves leading with the legs, unlike the cat pass which leads with the hands.n2. Practicing the exit technique is crucial for mastering the dash vault.n3. Developing muscle memory and comfort with hand placements during the movement enhances overall performance and safety.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1041,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 277,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1318,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"eKjUb9I96Wl6Ty7ZBYfTaaGi9g.bq8zMifFHhnFHMsY-1735836823-1.0.1.1-GAtSlwhP84v_hsZOzEmrTF0t_UHAPYqfKoR9IKiVEy2BzQ25tkmQMrcr4AtMPdNHFa9vupEm5AkAstnExOojhA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735838623,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"lps3CeLIicOkS0lGoPQiqCbARAnu3pVOxxNffB1X_TA-1735836823444-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(62388,55517,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(62389,55517,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The dash vault is an acrobatic move that contrasts with the cat pass. While the cat pass involves leading with the hands and executing a bilateral movement with both legs following, the dash vault begins with the legs leading and is followed by the hands coming into contact with the wall. This technique is crucial for parkour and similar fields, as it allows for smoother transitions over obstacles.\r\n\r\nTo properly perform the dash vault, one must focus on exiting the maneuver effectively. Initially, the practitioner should practice hopping down from a wall while simultaneously placing their hands behind them on the wall. This technique helps develop muscle memory and confidence, especially since one does not typically see where their hands are placed during the vault. The goal is to ensure that the legs clear the wall before the hands follow up, allowing for a safe and efficient landing.\r\n\r\nIt is important to get accustomed to the motions involved in the dash vault, particularly the act of dropping off the wall in the proper position. This foundational practice builds the necessary skills to execute more complex parkour maneuvers while maintaining safety and control during high-energy movements.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The dash vault involves leading with the legs, unlike the cat pass which leads with the hands.\r\n2. Practicing the exit technique is crucial for mastering the dash vault.\r\n3. Developing muscle memory and comfort with hand placements during the movement enhances overall performance and safety.'),(62390,55517,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(62391,55517,'svg_id',''),(62392,55517,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(62393,55517,'svg_colour',''),(62394,55517,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(62395,55517,'extra_variables',''),(62396,55517,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(62397,55517,'notes',''),(62398,55517,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(62399,55517,'enable_youtube_api',''),(62400,55517,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(62401,55517,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(62402,55517,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(62403,55517,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(62404,55517,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(62405,55517,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(62406,55517,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(62407,55517,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(62408,55517,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(62409,55517,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(62410,55517,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(62411,55517,'enable_transcript',''),(62412,55517,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(62413,55517,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(62414,55517,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(62415,55517,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I want this to sound like I wrote the result.'),(62416,55517,'_transcript_chatgpt_prompt','field_672214208bf31'),(62417,55517,'rank_math_primary_tutorial_category','0'),(62418,55517,'video_filename','Vaulting-Dash/Tutorial-vaulting-dash-6-full-dash.mp4'),(62419,55517,'_video_filename','field_677cead91f698'),(62420,55517,'portrait_thumbnail_image','Vaulting-Dash/screenshots/Tutorial-vaulting-dash-6-full-dash_3_4.png'),(62421,55517,'_portrait_thumbnail_image',''),(62422,55517,'landscape_thumbnail_image','Vaulting-Dash/screenshots/Tutorial-vaulting-dash-6-full-dash_16_9.p