aced at the right distance from the rail—about 20 to 30 cm away is ideal. This position allows enough momentum to carry over while avoiding awkward landings that may occur if the hands are too close or too far. During the movement, the legs should follow a coordinated kick over, ensuring one foot lands first, followed by the other. The landing should be gentle and on the side of the hips, rather than directly on the spine, to minimize impact.nnUltimately, practicing the walkover should be approached with caution and patience. Starting off slowly is advised, possibly with the help of a partner who can assist during the initial phases of the movement. As confidence and skill develop, the speed and complexity of the transfers can be increased. This skill, while challenging, adds an impressive visual element when incorporated into a flowy routine. nnKey Points:n1. The walkover involves transitioning from a handstand to landing on a rail or wall and is best practiced on a rail for safety and skill development.n2. Correct hand placement and body positioning are crucial for effective execution, allowing for controlled momentum and safe landings.n3. Practicing slowly with assistance is recommended before progressing to faster movements, improving skill and confidence in the technique.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 2138,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 347,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 2485,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"_2b__itN0BB3hIKkCFSdzxOJwT2WT3ATgCNF55TDYMc-1735837430-1.0.1.1-MM9sqUGwMfe1zxHYa2mcXJNuhGuijzsCUudrfGGUjt93xnnpMII3BsXcg8oQIIA4FFN1KBAZB_rWSrLOEvtWHw\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735839230,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"HbXOQH0_ZGVGm9CnuC.99M41311sgEUm2_lUuxv1jws-1735837430195-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(64107,55531,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(64108,55531,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The walkover is a movement that involves transitioning downward into a handstand and then kicking over to land onto a rail or a wall. This technique is typically used in more fluid and dynamic sequences rather than in more static or large movements. It is important for practitioners to begin with the rail, as its thin profile allows for a focused landing, providing a safer and easier way to develop the necessary skills for the exercise.\r\n\r\nTo successfully execute a walkover, one must ensure that their hands are placed at the right distance from the rail—about 20 to 30 cm away is ideal. This position allows enough momentum to carry over while avoiding awkward landings that may occur if the hands are too close or too far. During the movement, the legs should follow a coordinated kick over, ensuring one foot lands first, followed by the other. The landing should be gentle and on the side of the hips, rather than directly on the spine, to minimize impact.\r\n\r\nUltimately, practicing the walkover should be approached with caution and patience. Starting off slowly is advised, possibly with the help of a partner who can assist during the initial phases of the movement. As confidence and skill develop, the speed and complexity of the transfers can be increased. This skill, while challenging, adds an impressive visual element when incorporated into a flowy routine. \r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The walkover involves transitioning from a handstand to landing on a rail or wall and is best practiced on a rail for safety and skill development.\r\n2. Correct hand placement and body positioning are crucial for effective execution, allowing for controlled momentum and safe landings.\r\n3. Practicing slowly with assistance is recommended before progressing to faster movements, improving skill and confidence in the technique.'),(64109,55531,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(64110,55531,'svg_id',''),(64111,55531,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(64112,55531,'svg_colour',''),(64113,55531,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(64114,55531,'extra_variables',''),(64115,55531,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(64116,55531,'notes',''),(64117,55531,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(64118,55531,'enable_youtube_api',''),(64119,55531,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(64120,55531,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(64121,55531,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(64122,55531,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(64123,55531,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(64124,55531,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(64125,55531,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(64126,55531,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three pa