dy placement against the climbing surface. There are two primary methods for hanging off a wall: the straight arm position and the bent arm position. The straight arm is often initially preferred due to comfort, but it presents limitations as fatigue sets in, leaving climbers with no effective way to relieve the strain on their arms.nnIn contrast, the bent arm position is recommended as a more sustainable technique for climbing. When in this position, climbers can gradually transition between the bent and straight arm positions, allowing for better endurance as they ascend. Key aspects of the bent arm position include maintaining a firm grip with the whole hand on the edge and correctly positioning the legs—one high and one low—to maintain stability against the wall.nnThe essential takeaways emphasize the importance of practicing the bent arm technique for improved climbing efficiency. Proper hand placement and leg position are critical in creating a stable stance that counters backward forces. Ultimately, developing the strength to hold a bent arm position will facilitate longer and more effective climbs, allowing climbers to traverse more comfortably.nnKey points:n1. The bent arm position is preferable for climbing, as it allows for better endurance and transitioning between positions.n2. Proper hand and leg positioning are crucial for maintaining stability and controlling movements while climbing.n3. Developing strength in the bent arm position requires practice, ultimately leading to more effective climbing techniques.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 2581,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 288,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 2869,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 2560,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0705bf87c0\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"NJPtMG.dNm0U67wi5RYWTtk46c2pz0NxBPNbtH9y3z4-1733419840-1.0.1.1-9fhNUhvQzpBCEhfOtso8tBNJ1Xwcpo.JQvlseJy7H3yKGfR1rSQr8pNEHoEE5nDbhEFxwJzGo6kFV0KhLFLbjA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1733421640,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"tnunGwmfpjMscKI9MUUGoRuPPWPof9CYPg8WC4cOdy0-1733419840634-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(65431,55543,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(65432,55543,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The discussion centers around the techniques for traversing while climbing, focusing specifically on arm positioning and body placement against the climbing surface. There are two primary methods for hanging off a wall: the straight arm position and the bent arm position. The straight arm is often initially preferred due to comfort, but it presents limitations as fatigue sets in, leaving climbers with no effective way to relieve the strain on their arms.\r\n\r\nIn contrast, the bent arm position is recommended as a more sustainable technique for climbing. When in this position, climbers can gradually transition between the bent and straight arm positions, allowing for better endurance as they ascend. Key aspects of the bent arm position include maintaining a firm grip with the whole hand on the edge and correctly positioning the legs—one high and one low—to maintain stability against the wall.\r\n\r\nThe essential takeaways emphasize the importance of practicing the bent arm technique for improved climbing efficiency. Proper hand placement and leg position are critical in creating a stable stance that counters backward forces. Ultimately, developing the strength to hold a bent arm position will facilitate longer and more effective climbs, allowing climbers to traverse more comfortably.\r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. The bent arm position is preferable for climbing, as it allows for better endurance and transitioning between positions.\r\n2. Proper hand and leg positioning are crucial for maintaining stability and controlling movements while climbing.\r\n3. Developing strength in the bent arm position requires practice, ultimately leading to more effective climbing techniques.'),(65433,55543,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(65434,55543,'svg_id',''),(65435,55543,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(65436,55543,'svg_colour',''),(65437,55543,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(65438,55543,'extra_variables',''),(65439,55543,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(65440,55543,'notes',''),(65441,55543,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(65442,55543,'enable_youtube_api',''),(65443,55543,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(65444,55543,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(65445,55543,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(65446,55543,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(65447,55543,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(65448,55543,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(65449,55543,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt',