,000 --> 00:01:215,000\r\nit\'s just the friction of my shoe but\r\n\r\n94\r\n00:00:274,000 --> 00:01:218,000\r\nthat\'s where I want to be I want to try\r\n\r\n95\r\n00:00:276,000 --> 00:01:224,000\r\nto use that foot as much as I can keep\r\n\r\n96\r\n00:00:278,000 --> 00:01:223,000\r\nmy body weight on it to hold myself up\r\n\r\n'),(65562,55544,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(65563,55544,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AbA0dJuNtt7iFI0iHOUcDH6y3e1J6\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1733419975,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The straight-arm traverse technique begins by positioning oneself in a high stance, ideally close to the top edge, and starting the movement with a bent arm position for better control. The key is to shift weight from one arm to the other gradually, allowing the body to acclimate to holding one\'s weight on a single hand. Utilizing large, deliberate movements instead of smaller, ineffective shifts helps in maintaining momentum and balance, which is vital for successful traversing.nnAs practitioners become comfortable with the initial movements, they should progress to taking wider grips and moving their feet in conjunction with their hands. A focus should be maintained on the line of sight, with an emphasis on keeping the eyeline high. As fatigue sets in, it may be necessary to transition into a hang traverse, where less reliance on leg support increases the demand on arm strength, changing the way the body feels during the exercise.nnAn essential aspect of maintaining balance on the wall during the traverse is ensuring that the high foot—placed below hip height—firmly grips the wall. This foot placement is critical, as it prevents slipping and keeps the individual securely positioned. Ultimately, optimal body weight distribution between the hands and that critical foot will improve performance and control while executing various traversing movements.nnKey Points:n1. Begin with a bent arm position for better control before transitioning to a straight-arm traverse, focusing on weight shifts from one arm to the other.n2. Utilize wide grips and coordinated foot movements to enhance stability and momentum, adjusting eyeline focus as needed.n3. Ensure the high foot is correctly placed on the wall to prevent slipping and maintain balance, allowing for better overall control during traversing.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 3479,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 331,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 3810,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0705bf87c0\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"kpuq2tmk_LuqdcG2bQTGZQ8S2crDqWRhNtQsTuJcPv4-1733419980-1.0.1.1-Th6w_JlXzGVWk51FHSvm1wU3P8v1Wh3soAeJwje2J32h.8t5eNWdaQhyjyTd2t5i6fG08Y8ohG4lfpo9azicug\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1733421780,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"lUN6zQdp.YzjjFnRj4GGlxyx0pI.5yCLrlO.5trRfGs-1733419980697-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(65564,55544,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(65565,55544,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The straight-arm traverse technique begins by positioning oneself in a high stance, ideally close to the top edge, and starting the movement with a bent arm position for better control. The key is to shift weight from one arm to the other gradually, allowing the body to acclimate to holding one\'s weight on a single hand. Utilizing large, deliberate movements instead of smaller, ineffective shifts helps in maintaining momentum and balance, which is vital for successful traversing.\r\n\r\nAs practitioners become comfortable with the initial movements, they should progress to taking wider grips and moving their feet in conjunction with their hands. A focus should be maintained on the line of sight, with an emphasis on keeping the eyeline high. As fatigue sets in, it may be necessary to transition into a hang traverse, where less reliance on leg support increases the demand on arm strength, changing the way the body feels during the exercise.\r\n\r\nAn essential aspect of maintaining balance on the wall during the traverse is ensuring that the high foot—placed below hip height—firmly grips the wall. This foot placement is critical, as it prevents slipping and keeps the individual securely positioned. Ultimately, optimal body weight distribution between the hands and that critical foot will improve performance and control while executing various traversing movements.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. Begin with a bent arm position for better control before transitioning to a straight-arm traverse, focusing on weight shifts from one arm to the other.\r\n2. Utilize wide grips and coordinated foot movements to enhance stability and momentum, adjusting eyeline focus as needed.\r\n3. Ensure the high foot is correctly placed on the wall to prevent slipping and maintain balance, allowing for better overall control during traversing.'),(65566,55544,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(65567,55544,'svg_id',''),(65568,55544,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(65569,55544,'svg_colour',''),(65570,55544,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(65571,55544,'extra_variables',''),(65572,55544,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(65573,55544,'notes',''),(65574,55544,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(65575,55544,'enable_youtube_api',''),(65576,55544,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(65577,55544,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(65578,55544,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(65579,55544,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(65580,55544,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(65581,55544,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(65582,55544,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(65583,55544,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(65584,55544,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(65585,55544,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(65586,55544,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(65587,55544,'enable_transcript',''),(65588,55544,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(65589,55544,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(65590,55544,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(65591,55544,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Focus on the straight-arm traverse. Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I