ody weight on it to hold myself up\r\n\r\n'),(65695,55545,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(65696,55545,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-AbA0Hb5OA4Qxgp5F3g6EmpinN6SVI\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1733419953,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"In exploring the cat leap position, fundamental techniques for climbing and traversing are discussed. The focus starts with utilizing the bent arm position, allowing for better stability close to the top edge of a climbing surface. The initial movements require minor shifts of the hands while getting accustomed to balancing body weight on one arm, practicing the coordination required for effective traversal in both directions.nnAs proficiency increases, it’s emphasized that large movements and grips are more effective than small, controlled motions. The feet play a crucial role in maintaining balance while traversing, often moving synchronously with hand movements. The overall goal is to maximize grip and control, keeping the eye line high to enhance focus and balance during the climb. When fatigue sets in, transitioning into the hang traverse further tests grip strength by relying predominantly on hand strength without the assistance of feet.nnImportant considerations when traversing include ensuring that the high foot is placed properly on the wall to prevent sliding. The foot\'s position significantly aids in maintaining stability and support, which is more critical than just relying on upper body strength. Correct foot positioning allows climbers to leverage friction effectively, maintaining grip and balance throughout the climbing movement. This technique emphasizes gradual practice and movement awareness while ensuring both hands and feet are appropriately engaged.nn**Key Points:**n1. Emphasize using the bent arm position for stability and practice shifting body weight to enhance climbing proficiency.n2. Focus on large movements and concurrent foot and hand action to maintain balance and progress effectively while traversing.n3. Proper high foot placement is crucial for maintaining grip and preventing slipping, allowing for better support during climbing.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 3472,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 319,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 3791,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0705bf87c0\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"jRKT9ENY3O7PrLeWSqw59yhMJWsx8mEzotDAqb1ctTA-1733419958-1.0.1.1-GZodLLJ.gmD5NtI4ihItsS5ofYd_qeWPr2L0O11H2k043k7j1rVhMimlNJmN6oC2Nxco1bkGamhZVh6el.MjUA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1733421758,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"lAzoxNhZ9EAkBdtRb33GqppnUCJfpe6Nhd2iZQQMAw8-1733419958229-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(65697,55545,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(65698,55545,'video_transcript_chatgpt','In exploring the cat leap position, fundamental techniques for climbing and traversing are discussed. The focus starts with utilizing the bent arm position, allowing for better stability close to the top edge of a climbing surface. The initial movements require minor shifts of the hands while getting accustomed to balancing body weight on one arm, practicing the coordination required for effective traversal in both directions.\r\n\r\nAs proficiency increases, it’s emphasized that large movements and grips are more effective than small, controlled motions. The feet play a crucial role in maintaining balance while traversing, often moving synchronously with hand movements. The overall goal is to maximize grip and control, keeping the eye line high to enhance focus and balance during the climb. When fatigue sets in, transitioning into the hang traverse further tests grip strength by relying predominantly on hand strength without the assistance of feet.\r\n\r\nImportant considerations when traversing include ensuring that the high foot is placed properly on the wall to prevent sliding. The foot\'s position significantly aids in maintaining stability and support, which is more critical than just relying on upper body strength. Correct foot positioning allows climbers to leverage friction effectively, maintaining grip and balance throughout the climbing movement. This technique emphasizes gradual practice and movement awareness while ensuring both hands and feet are appropriately engaged.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. Emphasize using the bent arm position for stability and practice shifting body weight to enhance climbing proficiency.\r\n2. Focus on large movements and concurrent foot and hand action to maintain balance and progress effectively while traversing.\r\n3. Proper high foot placement is crucial for maintaining grip and preventing slipping, allowing for better support during climbing.'),(65699,55545,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(65700,55545,'svg_id',''),(65701,55545,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(65702,55545,'svg_colour',''),(65703,55545,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(65704,55545,'extra_variables',''),(65705,55545,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(65706,55545,'notes',''),(65707,55545,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(65708,55545,'enable_youtube_api',''),(65709,55545,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(65710,55545,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(65711,55545,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(65712,55545,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(65713,55545,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(65714,55545,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(65715,55545,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(65716,55545,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(65717,55545,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(65718,55545,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(65719,55545,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(65720,55545,'enable_transcript',''),(65721,55545,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(65722,55545,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(65723,55545,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(65724,55545,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I want this to sound like I wrote the result.'),(65725,55545,'_transcript_chatgpt_prompt','field_672214208bf31'),(65726,55545,'rank_math_seo_score','21'),(65727,55545,'video_file