 using your hands\r\n\r\n50\r\n00:00:167,000 --> 00:01:112,000\r\nuh give it a try start off small as I\r\n\r\n51\r\n00:00:169,000 --> 00:01:115,000\r\nsay and gradually build up and on height\r\n\r\n52\r\n00:00:173,000 --> 00:01:120,000\r\nand distance and that\'s what you need to\r\n\r\n53\r\n00:00:176,000 --> 00:01:120,000\r\ndo for the Hang Traverse\r\n\r\n'),(66261,55550,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(66262,55550,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\r\n    \"headers\": {},\r\n    \"body\": {\r\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-Akuj8s5E0QFKaxX4NXVPi2EklXEEC\",\r\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\r\n        \"created\": 1735744510,\r\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\r\n        \"choices\": [\r\n            {\r\n                \"index\": 0,\r\n                \"message\": {\r\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\r\n                    \"content\": \"The Hang Traverse is a challenging movement that requires careful technique and body positioning. It involves hanging with straight arms while swinging the body from side to side over a gap, relying solely on hand strength. Practicing this maneuver starts with small drops to build confidence and comfort while using one\'s feet to assist in balance and motion.nnKey to successfully navigating the Hang Traverse is the establishment of a rhythmic swinging pattern. This involves alternating hand grips as the body swings, allowing momentum to help move across the gap more smoothly. Building endurance and strength in the shoulders is crucial, as hands alone will bear all the weight during the traverse, making dead hang training beneficial for preparation.nnThe environment plays a significant role in the difficulty of the Hang Traverse, as uneven surfaces or lack of gripping points can increase the challenge. It\'s important to adapt and assess each situation while starting at manageable heights and distances, gradually pushing boundaries for skill enhancement. With persistence and practice, one can master this impressive parkour skill.nnKey Points:n1. The Hang Traverse requires a combination of strength, rhythm, and proper technique to cross a gap using only hand grips while hanging.n2. Establishing a rhythmic motion by swinging the body and alternating hand grips helps in smoothly traversing gaps and building shoulder strength.n3. Different environments present unique challenges; thus, starting small and gradually increasing height and distance will facilitate progression in mastering the Hang Traverse.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1945,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 278,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 2223,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"FbQabSuvrBQ8mE6x4pf1rTtewfTSMMVorRB2LiQvMBY-1735744515-1.0.1.1-mDq3YUgwr_GA6rUuWTkO20dmH4yo5nxs0p7EqyJxKtO90pJHgYAVIx1x0OSKFS_2vwStyRzhTZKdXp6euU6G3Q\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746315,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"DQh_Z9hyxWZRfGRCdbP7oNlHDYocfjZiYcTT_bpkAfw-1735744515606-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(66263,55550,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(66264,55550,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The Hang Traverse is a challenging movement that requires careful technique and body positioning. It involves hanging with straight arms while swinging the body from side to side over a gap, relying solely on hand strength. Practicing this maneuver starts with small drops to build confidence and comfort while using one\'s feet to assist in balance and motion.\r\n\r\nKey to successfully navigating the Hang Traverse is the establishment of a rhythmic swinging pattern. This involves alternating hand grips as the body swings, allowing momentum to help move across the gap more smoothly. Building endurance and strength in the shoulders is crucial, as hands alone will bear all the weight during the traverse, making dead hang training beneficial for preparation.\r\n\r\nThe environment plays a significant role in the difficulty of the Hang Traverse, as uneven surfaces or lack of gripping points can increase the challenge. It\'s important to adapt and assess each situation while starting at manageable heights and distances, gradually pushing boundaries for skill enhancement. With persistence and practice, one can master this impressive parkour skill.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. The Hang Traverse requires a combination of strength, rhythm, and proper technique to cross a gap using only hand grips while hanging.\r\n2. Establishing a rhythmic motion by swinging the body and alternating hand grips helps in smoothly traversing gaps and building shoulder strength.\r\n3. Different environments present unique challenges; thus, starting small and gradually increasing height and distance will facilitate progression in mastering the Hang Traverse.'),(66265,55550,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(66266,55550,'svg_id',''),(66267,55550,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(66268,55550,'svg_colour',''),(66269,55550,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(66270,55550,'extra_variables',''),(66271,55550,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(66272,55550,'notes',''),(66273,55550,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(66274,55550,'enable_youtube_api',''),(66275,55550,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(66276,55550,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(66277,55550,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(66278,55550,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(66279,55550,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(66280,55550,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(66281,55550,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(66282,55550,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(66283,55550,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(66284,55550,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(66285,55550,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(66286,55550,'enable_transcript',''),(66287,55550,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(66288,55550,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(66289,55550,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(66290,55550,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I want this to sound like I wrote the result.'),(66291,55550,'_transcript_chatgpt_prompt','field_672214208bf31'),(66292,55550,'rank_math_primary_tutorial_category','0'),(66293,55550,'video_filename','Climbing-Traversing/Tutorial-Climbing-Traversing-10-hang-traverse.mp4'),(66294,55550,'_video_filename','field_677cead91f698'),(66295,55550,'portrait_thumbnail_image','Climbing-Traversing/screensh