to keep their hips close, knees bent, and arms flexed to optimize grip and stability. The absence of a wall or side support means that the climber must rely solely on foot grip on the bar, making it similar to how monkeys ascend.nnTo successfully execute the koala climb, the climber should focus on keeping their feet low and avoiding spreading out their limbs, as this can lead to difficulties in maintaining grip. Practicing climbing by moving up and down a couple of steps can enhance skills and confidence in this technique. Proper body positioning throughout the climb is vital to avoid sliding down from the bar.nnUltimately, the key to mastering the koala climb lies in the climber\'s ability to maintain a compact form and practice the movement repeatedly, paying attention to their foot placement and grip strength. The drill of climbing up and back down serves as a practical way to refine the technique and ensure effective execution.nn**Key Points:**n1. Maintain a compact body position with hips close, knees bent, and arms flexed for the koala climb.n2. Foot placement and grip are critical for success, avoiding spreading limbs to ensure stability.n3. Regular practice of ascending and descending can improve technique and confidence in the koala climb.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1044,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 268,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1312,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_d02d531b47\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"7WmP6Y.svfBwGiNLk5hdUJRlw9YR9vrR1R2Tb2_SvLM-1735745244-1.0.1.1-Xha74xmmVK1d7bfm2i1c7mtn.2eD2SB6sAH4wsLZN8njcUD0uihA_IcIZ0E2m_hBROqDY.A1L_WArAm.ODu1BA\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735747044,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"rUn_8007IZ4Zj_szqjsbZPoaStZRPNuUaSL8l1g4j3M-1735745244346-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(67765,55567,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(67766,55567,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The koala climb technique emphasizes maintaining a proper body position while ascending. It requires the climber to keep their hips close, knees bent, and arms flexed to optimize grip and stability. The absence of a wall or side support means that the climber must rely solely on foot grip on the bar, making it similar to how monkeys ascend.\r\n\r\nTo successfully execute the koala climb, the climber should focus on keeping their feet low and avoiding spreading out their limbs, as this can lead to difficulties in maintaining grip. Practicing climbing by moving up and down a couple of steps can enhance skills and confidence in this technique. Proper body positioning throughout the climb is vital to avoid sliding down from the bar.\r\n\r\nUltimately, the key to mastering the koala climb lies in the climber\'s ability to maintain a compact form and practice the movement repeatedly, paying attention to their foot placement and grip strength. The drill of climbing up and back down serves as a practical way to refine the technique and ensure effective execution.\r\n\r\n**Key Points:**\r\n1. Maintain a compact body position with hips close, knees bent, and arms flexed for the koala climb.\r\n2. Foot placement and grip are critical for success, avoiding spreading limbs to ensure stability.\r\n3. Regular practice of ascending and descending can improve technique and confidence in the koala climb.'),(67767,55567,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(67768,55567,'svg_id',''),(67769,55567,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(67770,55567,'svg_colour',''),(67771,55567,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(67772,55567,'extra_variables',''),(67773,55567,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(67774,55567,'notes',''),(67775,55567,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(67776,55567,'enable_youtube_api',''),(67777,55567,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(67778,55567,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(67779,55567,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(67780,55567,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(67781,55567,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(67782,55567,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(67783,55567,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(67784,55567,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(67785,55567,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(67786,55567,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(67787,55567,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(67788,55567,'enable_transcript',''),(67789,55567,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(67790,55567,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(67791,55567,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(67792,55567,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript in