ng enhances landing techniques to reduce impact and improve safety.n2. Initiating movement from a height, like a wall, allows for better momentum management during descent.n3. Controlled landings and maintaining momentum are essential for executing the plyo technique effectively.\",\r\n                    \"refusal\": null\r\n                },\r\n                \"logprobs\": null,\r\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\r\n            }\r\n        ],\r\n        \"usage\": {\r\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 759,\r\n            \"completion_tokens\": 278,\r\n            \"total_tokens\": 1037,\r\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0\r\n            },\r\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\r\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"audio_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"accepted_prediction_tokens\": 0,\r\n                \"rejected_prediction_tokens\": 0\r\n            }\r\n        },\r\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0aa8d3e20b\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"response\": {\r\n        \"code\": 200,\r\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\r\n    },\r\n    \"cookies\": [\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\r\n            \"value\": \"9wNYGWMaVL8t61Yl208dLP84.pT8CnVye8CBsEJqrgU-1735744495-1.0.1.1-NuFtFtAJ2YyBz9SoykT5GvntK3pdQiAgEF.kQFM6P2lQk3vPBEEKeVlogTDcn5h9k6Do5VdG0a7.BjPeqEdafg\",\r\n            \"expires\": 1735746295,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        },\r\n        {\r\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\r\n            \"value\": \"yrmKjilBqXZ38J7EwwojZkwnwS.cghCKb4gpUED9oBM-1735744495047-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\r\n            \"expires\": null,\r\n            \"path\": \"/\",\r\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\r\n            \"port\": null,\r\n            \"host_only\": false\r\n        }\r\n    ],\r\n    \"filename\": null,\r\n    \"http_response\": {\r\n        \"data\": null,\r\n        \"headers\": null,\r\n        \"status\": null\r\n    }\r\n}'),(68667,55577,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(68668,55577,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The transcript discusses a technique called \"plyometric\" (plyo) jumping that is applied to a movement known as the \"Splat cat.\" This technique is designed for specific scenarios where an individual can enhance their landing technique by jumping into the landing area instead of descending directly. The concept centers around maintaining momentum while making a controlled landing, which can reduce impact and improve overall safety.\r\n\r\nTo effectively execute this technique, the individual is advised to start from a height, such as a wall. By jumping towards the wall upon landing, they can redirect their momentum safely downward rather than just falling straight down to the ground. This approach allows for a smoother transition and helps mitigate the risks associated with landing from a significant drop, thus improving the overall landing experience.\r\n\r\nIn practicing this plyo technique, the key is to ensure a controlled and safe landing by leveraging the wall\'s support. Maintaining momentum throughout the movement is crucial, as it enhances stability and safety, ultimately leading to more effective execution. This particular approach can be beneficial in various environments where height adjustments and controlled landings are necessary to minimize the risk of injury.\r\n\r\nKey Points:\r\n1. Plyometric jumping enhances landing techniques to reduce impact and improve safety.\r\n2. Initiating movement from a height, like a wall, allows for better momentum management during descent.\r\n3. Controlled landings and maintaining momentum are essential for executing the plyo technique effectively.'),(68669,55577,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(68670,55577,'svg_id',''),(68671,55577,'_svg_id','fi