 in weight. Keeping the arms straight and extending them to shoulder height also contributes to maintaining stability during the exercise.\r\n\r\nFinally, the importance of core engagement is highlighted, which helps in reducing unnecessary movement and maintaining control. By contracting the abdominals and glutes, the body can achieve a steadier state, minimizing large muscle fluctuations. It is recommended to practice balancing on both feet and switching positions to develop overall stability on the rail.\r\n\r\nKey points:\r\n1. Proper foot alignment and weight distribution are crucial for effective balancing on a rail.\r\n2. Using one foot while engaging the remaining limbs helps create better balance and stability.\r\n3. Engaging the core muscles is essential to reduce movement and improve control during balancing exercises.'),(69202,55582,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(69203,55582,'svg_id',''),(69204,55582,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(69205,55582,'svg_colour',''),(69206,55582,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(69207,55582,'extra_variables',''),(69208,55582,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(69209,55582,'notes',''),(69210,55582,'_notes','field_6749f56647b9e'),(69211,55582,'enable_youtube_api',''),(69212,55582,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(69213,55582,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(69214,55582,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(69215,55582,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(69216,55582,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(69217,55582,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(69218,55582,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(69219,55582,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(69220,55582,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(69221,55582,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(69222,55582,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(69223,55582,'enable_transcript',''),(69224,55582,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(6