orial on how to Cat Leap (Beginner) in Parkour - Introduction.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Cat Leap Series. Episode #01nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Climbing #Introduction #---nnCat leap foot position.nnFirst step is to get used to placing you foot on the wall first. Always the foot first because the leg muscles take any impact and absorb the force.nnThe arms u26d4 RARELY u26d4go first because that means your face is going ahead of your body too... Which can be bad. ud83dude26ud83dude35 Ball of the foot on the wall and start to see if you can take your body weight on the side of the wall without slipping down.nnHave fun!nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Climbing}}{{Series:Cat leaps Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lyMhhmFrvJU/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lyMhhmFrvJU/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lyMhhmFrvJU/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lyMhhmFrvJU/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lyMhhmFrvJU/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPc3OMC6iA2nmJsJ5ynObql\",\"position\":0,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"lyMhhmFrvJU\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":0}'),(74044,55813,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Arm Jumps'),(74045,55813,'authId','Auth1'),(74046,55813,'searchId','Tutorials - Arm Jumps'),(74047,55813,'filterId','none'),(74048,55813,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(74049,55813,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Arm Jumps'),(74050,55813,'_edit_last','1'),(74051,55813,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to practicing cat leaps, understanding the mechanics is essential for safety and efficiency. A cat leap is a movement often utilized in parkour or free running, where you jump towards a wall and land on it with your feet. This tutorial will guide you through the basic steps to master this technique, highlighting the importance of proper form to minimize the risk of injury and maximize your success.\n\nTo get started, focus on getting your feet up to the wall before you introduce any hand movement. Begin by running towards the wall, and as you approach, launch yourself upwards. The key is to place one foot on the wall first. This foot will absorb most of the impact during the leap, so choosing which one to use is crucial. After your foot or feet have landed securely, you can then position your hands onto the wall to stabilize and pull yourself up if needed. It’s essential to maintain a controlled motion; rather than relying solely on momentum, concentrate on precise placements of your feet and hands to build your confidence and technique gradually.\n\nIn summary, practicing cat leaps can be a rewarding experience when approached correctly. Remember to prioritize foot placement against the wall before adding in hand movements, and focus on the feel of landing safely. With patience and practice, you’ll find that feline-like agility is not just for cats—humans can harness it too!\n\n- Start with your feet hitting the wall first to control impact.\n- Focus on precise movements instead of relying on momentum.\n- Practice consistently for improved technique and confidence in your cat leaps.'),(74052,55813,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(74053,55813,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"