ull,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(74058,55813,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(74059,55813,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(74060,55813,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(74061,55813,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(74062,55813,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(74063,55814,'_thumbnail_id','14032'),(74064,55814,'video_id','kYI8bKc76_o'),(74065,55814,'video_type','tutorial'),(74066,55814,'order_position','1'),(74067,55814,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"txQaBrl_jlY-o1ueDLnUba_uekc\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUGMzT01DNmlBMm5tSnNKNXluT2JxbC45NDk1REZENzhEMzU5MDQz\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T08:44:53Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Cat Leap #02 - Foot Position 2 Parkour Tutorial. [016]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Cat Leap (Beginner) in Parkour - Foot Position 2.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Cat Leap Series. Episode #02nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Climbing #FootPosition2 #---nnCat Leap Foot position.nnSimple one today... Positioning of the feet ud83dudc63on the wall when landing.ud83dudeec. nn1. With the body pushing into the wall, the u2b06 higher foot will get a lot more grip and traction so that it will help prevent slipping downwards.nn2. The lower u2b07 foot will help you not slip backwards off the wall if your hands come off.nn3. If you had both feet high on the wall, the pressure from them would be greater backwards... Therefore you are more likely to have your hands rip off the wall and you go backwards onto the floor.nn4. If both feet were low, your hip flexors and abs would be on overdrive and it would be very difficult to use the feet to stay on the wall. Your arms would be doing all the work. Therefore it would be more likely that you would slip down the wall.nnThis all translates into bigger cat-leaps and will help you to stay on the wall.nnIf you feel like you are slipping down the wall, try to have the higher foot even higher on the wall. Your body should be pressing it into the wall to maintain traction and grip.nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25