_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to mastering cat loops, proper foot positioning can make a world of difference. This technique not only improves your control but also enhances your overall performance. Whether you\'re a beginner looking to refine your skills or an experienced practitioner wanting to add variety to your routine, paying attention to how you place your feet can help you maintain balance and stability during the movement.\n\nTo set yourself up for success, start by positioning one foot higher on the wall and the other lower. The higher foot will prevent you from slipping down, while the lower foot will provide support and help you avoid leaning back too much. It\'s essential to try this position on both sides to develop even strength and flexibility. Remember, as you practice, keep your movements fluid and enjoy the process—you\'ll find that being relaxed and having fun with it can lead to better results.\n\nIn conclusion, focusing on foot placement is a simple yet effective way to improve your cat loops. By strategically adjusting the height of each foot and practicing consistently, you\'ll gain better control and confidence in your movement. Don’t hesitate to experiment and find what feels comfortable for you; after all, the key to progression is practice and enjoyment.\n\n- Place one foot higher and one foot lower for better stability during cat loops.\n- Practice on both sides to develop balanced skills and strength.\n- Have fun with the technique—it helps you relax and enhances performance!'),(74076,55814,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(74077,55814,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"today of carrying on with cat loops and\",\n        \"start\": 0.19,\n        \"duration\": 5.129\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"I want you to have a look at how the\",\n        \"start\": 2.86,\n        \"duration\": 4.74\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"feet are positioned all right so it\'s\",\n        \"start\": 5.