l first will help you develop the right habits and coordination as you progress.nnIn summary, this jumping exercise is all about letting your legs do the heavy lifting. By focusing on a small jump with proper foot positioning, you’ll not only gain strength but also improve your jumping technique. Remember that practice makes perfect, so don’t rush the process. Enjoy honing your skills, and soon, you\'ll feel more comfortable and confident with your jump.nn- Position one foot on the wall for support while jumping with the other leg.n- Keep jumps small and controlled, relying on your legs for impact absorption.n- Use your arms for balance but avoid letting them lead the jump.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 337,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 335,\n            \"total_tokens\": 672,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"cKTaEipBspNpxmT40XIgkJYmXkJIVNi8YWX70z1dCJA-1730718649-1.0.1.1-AqqaZ5m_eWV21dwZoWFt.m2UWQIGZi.SoXOGK7_d12qxeneCm2FyKQQqUKrB3SI0it7sW.C2fwe4pILWxJFNaA\",\n            \"expires\": 1730720449,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"nbDy8FZDHxtp0Xj6f0u11uAFKrPUZk.3HMh0IXGdCr8-1730718649025-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n          