T performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Climbing}}{{Series:Cat Leaps Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/herLqEaMxnc/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/herLqEaMxnc/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/herLqEaMxnc/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/herLqEaMxnc/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/herLqEaMxnc/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPc3OMC6iA2nmJsJ5ynObql\",\"position\":4,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"herLqEaMxnc\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":4}'),(74140,55817,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Arm Jumps'),(74141,55817,'authId','Auth1'),(74142,55817,'searchId','Tutorials - Arm Jumps'),(74143,55817,'filterId','none'),(74144,55817,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(74145,55817,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Arm Jumps'),(74146,55817,'_edit_last','1'),(74147,55817,'video_transcript_chatgpt','To enhance your training routine, incorporating specific jumping techniques can make a significant difference. This tutorial focuses on mastering the cat leap—a dynamic movement that combines agility and strength. By adding a slight momentum into your practice, you\'ll not only improve your jumping skills but also develop better coordination and control.\n\nLet\'s break down the cat leap technique. Begin by stepping onto a sturdy platform or block. From there, you want to drive one leg forward, aiming straight through to an imaginary wall in front of you. It\'s essential to remember not to put both feet on the block at once; instead, focus on preparing yourself to leap efficiently with one leg. As you jump, try to direct your movement upward rather than moving straight ahead, which will help you maximize your height and ensure a safer landing. Your legs will absorb the impact as you come down, so stay mindful of maintaining good form to prevent injury.\n\nIn summary, the cat leap is an exciting and effective skill to incorporate into your fitness regimen. By emphasizing proper technique and building momentum, you\'ll not only elevate your performance but also enjoy the process of mastering new skills. Remember, practice consistently, and you\'ll see improvement over time, making your workouts both more engaging and rewarding.\n\nHighlights:\n- Focus on jumping with one leg while driving through towards the wall.\n- Aim for an upward trajectory rather than a straight path to enhance your leap.\n- Practice consistently for better coordination and control in your movements.'),(74148,55817,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(74149,55817,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"slight momentum today the idea is we\'re\",\n        \"start\": 0.39,\n        \"duration\": 6.55\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"going to step up onto the block and then\",\n        \"start\": 3.999,\n        \"duration\": 4.56\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"do the cat leap all right so they\'re\",\n        \"start\": 6.94,\n        \"duration\": 3.329\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"adding a very very slight amount of\",\n        \"start\": 8.559,\n        \"duration\": 5.361\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"momentum into the carry\",\n        \"start\": 10.269,\n        \"duration\": 6.84\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"[Music]\",\n        \"start\": 13.92,\n        \"duration\": 3.189\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay two things to note that number one\",\n        \"start\": 28.46,\n        \"durati