consistently, and you\'ll see improvement over time, making your workouts both more engaging and rewarding.nnHighlights:n- Focus on jumping with one leg while driving through towards the wall.n- Aim for an upward trajectory rather than a straight path to enhance your leap.n- Practice consistently for better coordination and control in your movements.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 311,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 285,\n            \"total_tokens\": 596,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"LyhQAS1F7ZyxXQ6uvrI53YY9LAK5_9hRIvt0zODwVuU-1730718189-1.0.1.1-ZlO4PDt8P4qdxW5UeF8nSX.OfgVy69KE.N4.hdAKOgRuFaQFMC68elmDn7IvkIXmBbKwgz2vht7XBQIbGTmVCA\",\n            \"expires\": 1730719989,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"cYpzsAFvod3fcixF.4R9IuCPjxmRhnUywU5ubmQBrCg-1730718189167-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(74154,55817,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(74155,55817,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(74156,55817,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(74157,55817,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(74158,55817,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(74159,55818,'_thumbnail_id','14040'),(74160,55818,'video_id','hZy97xtITR4'),(74161,55818,'video_type','tutorial'),(74162,55818,'order_position','5'),(74163,55818,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"j5vZx1YmTeBhVabbdq1vFZ-hZM0\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUGMzT01DNmlBMm5tSnNKNXluT2JxbC4yODlGNEE0NkRGMEEzMEQy\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T08:44:53Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Cat Leap #06 - Hand Position Parkour Tutorial. [020]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Cat Leap (Beginner) in Parkour - Hand Position.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Cat Leap Series. Episode #06nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Climbing #HandPosition #---nnCat-Leap hand position.nnA lot of people have asked me in the past how they should hold onto the wall... This should answer those questions! Some students only use the ends of the phalanges and therefore don\'t get as much grip... nn1. Whole length of fingers on the wall. You may feel a crease in your hand forming. Don\'t worry, this is good!nn2. Pain. So, unfortunately, the only way to make your hands tougher and more resilient is to take the pain, soreness and ripping of the skin. This way the skin grows back thicker and harder.nn3. Don\'t use gloves. A fundamental reason for Parkour is to be able to use it at any time, in any situation. Parkour is about making you a more functional human being. If you can\'t do a cat leap without the aid of gloves, now\'s the time to start... Otherwise, what happens when you NEED to do that cat leap and don\'t have your gloves? Also, they\'re unreliable and can slip/rip. Just put it out of your head to use aids of any kind... It just makes you less functional.nn4. Try staying on the wall for periods of time to get used to the hand soreness.nnEnjoy!n n--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Climbing}}{{Series:Cat Leaps Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/hZy97xtITR4/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/hZy97xtITR4/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/hZy97xtITR4/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/hZy97xtITR4/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/hZy97xtITR4/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPc3OMC6iA2nmJsJ5ynObql\",\"position\":5,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"hZy97xtITR4\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":5}'),(74164,55818,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Arm Jumps'),(74165,55818,'authId','Auth1'),(74166,55818,'searchId','Tutorials - Arm Jumps'),(74167,55818,'filterId','none'),(74168,55818,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(74169,55818,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Arm Jumps'),(74170,55818,'_edit_last','1'),(74171,55818,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to climbing, mastering your hand position is crucial for both performance and safety. A proper grip not only helps you ascend more effectively but also allows for better control and balance on the wall. One key element to focus on is how your fingers are positioned; this nuanced detail significantly impacts your ability to maintain a secure hold, especially when the route becomes challenging.\n\nThe most important takeaway is that your hand should be bent at the knuckles while gripping holds. This position allows for a stronger grip, ensuring that as you climb, you\'re not only hanging on but actively engaging with the surface. The goal is to get as much of your hand over the hold as possible, locking your fingers in place to create a secure connection. If you do happen to start slipping, rather than losing your grip completely, this technique helps to control descents, allowing you to gradually slide down your fingers instead of falling off the hold.\n\nIn summary, focusing on your hand positioning is a small yet pivotal adjustment that can enhance your climbing experience. By keeping your knuckles bent and gripping firmly, you not only improve your climbing efficiency but also increase your safety. So, next time you\'re on the wall, remember to check in with your grip—it\'s the details that often make the biggest difference! \n\n- Focus on bending your knuckles while gripping holds for increased control.\n- Engage fully with the surface by getting your hand over the hold.\n- Remember that a solid grip allows for safer descents in case of slips.'),(74172,55818,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(74173,55818,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we\'ve talked about our position but\",\n        \"start\": 0.1,\n        \"duration\": 5.73\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"today it\'s going to be a hand position\",\n        \"start\": 3.28,\n        \"duration\": 5.16\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"and we\'ve already kind of said about\",\n        \"start\": 5.83,\n        \"duration\": 5.129\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"this on the climb ups and that is that\",\n        \"start\": 8.44,\n        \"duration\": 4.859\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"essentially our hand wants to be bent at\",\n        \"start\": 10.959,\n        