g\":\"nC7ggVQIqfJ_k3tS-0jy206sqwU\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUGMzT01DNmlBMm5tSnNKNXluT2JxbC41MzJCQjBCNDIyRkJDN0VD\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T08:44:53Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Cat Leap #08 - Arm Reset Position Parkour Tutorial. [022]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Cat Leap (Beginner) in Parkour - Arm Reset Position.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Cat Leap Series. Episode #08nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Climbing #ArmResetPosition #---nnCat-Leap Arm Reset Position.nnNow it\'s time to practice reclaiming that arm extension and pull back up again. At the end of the day you want to be able to get back over the wall, so getting used to Cat-Leaping and the climbing up is a very useful skill.nn1. Always jump using both sides.nn2. Start with a smaller jump, with less impact, and build up.nn3. Always try to pull up to the highest point you can, with the maximum range of motion as you can.nn4. Make the pull as explosive as possible and utilise the legs and feet as much as possible. For a real climbup (another series), the legs are heavily used!nnGet outside and train!nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Climbing}}{{Series:Cat Leaps Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/mFzc_kmp8D8/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/mFzc_kmp8D8/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/mFzc_kmp8D8/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/mFzc_kmp8D8/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/mFzc_kmp8D8/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPc3OMC6iA2nmJsJ5ynObql\",\"position\":7,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"mFzc_kmp8D8\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":7}'),(74213,55820,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Arm Jumps'),(74214,55820,'authId','Auth1'),(74215,55820,'searchId','Tutorials - Arm Jumps'),(74216,55820,'filterId','none'),(74217,55820,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(74218,55820,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Arm Jumps'),(74219,55820,'_edit_last','1'),(74220,55820,'video_transcript_chatgpt','In this tutorial, we\'re going to explore a simple yet effective exercise that will help you build strength and improve your technique when navigating walls. Whether you\'re looking to enhance your climbing skills or just want to get more comfortable with wall movements, this exercise can serve as a great tool in your training routine. By focusing on how to reposition yourself using straight arms, you’ll develop the strength and awareness needed for various climbing scenarios.\n\nTo start, position yourself with your arms straight and in control. From here, practice pulling your body back up towards the wall, using your strength to engage your core as you transition into the desired posture. This movement mimics the action you\'ll need when climbing or pushing off a wall, making it practical and relevant. It may feel challenging at first, but with consistent repetition, you\'ll notice improvements in your grip, body control, and overall fitness, which are essential for climbing.\n\nIn conclusion, mastering this conditioning exercise can greatly enhance your climbing efficiency and confidence. By focusing on your form and control as you pull back into position, you’ll better prepare yourself for real climbing scenarios where returning to the wall is necessary. Consistency in practice will not only build your strength but also make the process of climbing feel more fluid and natural.\n\n- Engage your core while pulling yourself back up to improve body control.\n- Consistency is key; practice regularly for noticeable strength gains.\n- This exercise is practical for real-life climbing scenarios, making it highly beneficial.'),(74221,55820,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(74222,55820,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"this is starting to turn into a little\",\n        \"start\": 0.07,\n        \"duration\": 4.769\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"bit more of a conditioning exercise but\",\n        \"start\": 2.199,\n        \"duration\": 5.16\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"now the idea is once you\'re straight\",\n        \"start\": 4.839,\n        \"duration\": 4.021\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"armed we\'re now going to pull back up\",\n        \"start\": 7.359,\n        \"duration\": 3.811\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"again to try and get ourselves back into\",\n        \"start\": 8.86,\n        \"duration\": 4.61\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"position all right\",\n        \"start\": 11.17,\n        \"duration\": 5.439\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"[Music]\",\n        \"start\": 13.47,\n        \"duration\": 3.139\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay that\'s going to get us used to\",\n        \"start\": 30.17,\n        \"duration\": 6.15\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"pulling ourselves back up onto the wall\",\n        \"start\": 32.96,\n        \"duration\": 5.62\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"it\'s going to be very useful obviously\",\n        \"start\": 36.32,\n        \"duration\": 4.12\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"once you\'re on the side of a wall you\",\n        \"start\": 38.58,\n        \"duration\": 3.36\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"need to then get back up agai