not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Climbing}}{{Series:Cat Leaps Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4eCeYbYTVwc/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4eCeYbYTVwc/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4eCeYbYTVwc/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4eCeYbYTVwc/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4eCeYbYTVwc/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPc3OMC6iA2nmJsJ5ynObql\",\"position\":9,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"4eCeYbYTVwc\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":9}'),(74261,55822,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Arm Jumps'),(74262,55822,'authId','Auth1'),(74263,55822,'searchId','Tutorials - Arm Jumps'),(74264,55822,'filterId','none'),(74265,55822,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(74266,55822,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Arm Jumps'),(74267,55822,'_edit_last','1'),(74268,55822,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to mastering a skill like bail training, preparation is key. In this tutorial, we\'ll explore a technique that helps you get comfortable with falling safely, particularly when you\'re transitioning from a tricky position, such as when you\'re on the wall. Learning how to manage this movement can minimize the risk of injury and improve your overall confidence during dynamic activities.\n\nThe core of this training involves using a soft surface, often referred to as a \"splat cat.\" This setup helps you practice falling safely. To start, position yourself to face a wall. As you begin to fall, focus on hitting the wall with your legs first, followed by your hands. This sequential approach helps distribute the impact and keep your body aligned. Remember to maintain control throughout the fall, allowing your body to come down gently rather than crashing to the ground. Practicing this regularly will help you develop a feel for the movement and improve your technique over time.\n\nBy integrating bail training into your routine, you’ll not only enhance your safety skills but also build confidence in high-pressure situations. Remember, the goal is comfort and control when falling; the more you practice, the more instinctual these movements will become. So gather your splat cat, find a safe space, and start falling—safely!\n\n- Practice falling with control by hitting the wall with your legs first, then your hands.\n- Use a soft surface, like a splat cat, to cushion your landing and reduce injury risk.\n- Regular practice will build confidence and improve your falling technique over time.'),(74269,55822,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(74270,55822,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"ok today we\'re gonna have a look at a\",\n        \"start\": 2,\n        \"duration\": 4.439\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"little bit of bail training\",\n        \"start\": 4.46,\n        \"duration\": 5.64\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"this is still Kathleen and stuff but the\",\n        \"start\": 6.439,\n        \"duration\": 5.161\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"idea is to start feeling more\",\n        \"start\": 10.1,\n        \"duration\": 4.29\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"comfortable about if you don\'t make the\",\n        \"start\": 11.6,\n        \"duration\": 6.03\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"Kathleen getting used to being in the\",\n        \"start\": 14.39,\n        \"duration\": 4.709\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"position where you\'re going to slice\",\n        \"start\": 17.63,\n     