keep your body aligned. Remember to maintain control throughout the fall, allowing your body to come down gently rather than crashing to the ground. Practicing this regularly will help you develop a feel for the movement and improve your technique over time.nnBy integrating bail training into your routine, you’ll not only enhance your safety skills but also build confidence in high-pressure situations. Remember, the goal is comfort and control when falling; the more you practice, the more instinctual these movements will become. So gather your splat cat, find a safe space, and start falling—safely!nn- Practice falling with control by hitting the wall with your legs first, then your hands.n- Use a soft surface, like a splat cat, to cushion your landing and reduce injury risk.n- Regular practice will build confidence and improve your falling technique over time.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 335,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 308,\n            \"total_tokens\": 643,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"SMqG3_yb2C1tdGhk7WVdtPmr5Pk2dMWJwylnwL.pLvM-1730718656-1.0.1.1-0LjruTVHSk6xHdhcrZDiaLHti.oDGdkpskvK3tEr5vy_CB01pdfnkETaNBWl7wakdtPP3dC.kUKcFSFvKhS._w\",\n            \"expires\": 1730720456,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"Na0Q7Ys2lAgIlR11q7BUOcflzehAW2z25lUBmKdrTHY-1730718656061-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(74275,55822,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(74276,55822,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(74277,55822,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(74278,55822,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(74279,55822,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(74280,55823,'_thumbnail_id','20456'),(74281,55823,'video_id','_2g9XgPf5Bg'),(74282,55823,'video_type','tutorial'),(74283,55823,'order_position','0'),(74284,55823,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"n3joWNV0H5Bp7QlZkPSLlLaFSHM\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUGl1a0xaRXFZaUM2cFlkMUxSNWUxOC41NkI0NEY2RDEwNTU3Q0M2\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2021-09-27T13:40:15Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"Step Vault Basics - Parkour Tutorials - 001\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on Step Vaults for Beginnersnud83eudd77 The Parkour Vaulting Series. Episode 001nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnn#Vaulting #Step-Vault #Parkournn##u00a0Step Vault 1 - Basicsn---n### IntronnThis is called the **Step Vault** or also known as the Safety VaultnThe step vault\'s primary purpose is to allow maximum confidence overcoming an obstacle, nMoving both safely and securely.nn### The TL;DRnnIt is usually the vault that is taught first to beginners because of it\'s simplicity. nHowever this vault is hugely versatile and can have a huge range of variations.nn### The goalnnThe key is control and security, so the more confidence you feel with this vault, the better because it will always be your fall-back vault. nAdvanced practitioners will also use this vault, especially when they\'re feeling uncomfortable or want maximum reliability. So nailing this down to perfection is in your best interest.nnn### PrerequisitesnnYou do not need any previous experience and very little movement ability to complete this vault at its basic level.nHowever, having the mobility to be able to get a foot and hand on the obstacle will be nessesary.nn### Getting startednn1. General Joint Mobility should be encouraged. It\'ll loosen up the joints and help with being able to reach better ranges of motion under controln2. Thorough warmups should always be done. Unless you are a top-level athlete who monitors their performance, you should start slow but gradually move into going hard on the warmups.n3. Shoulders and arms with QM / Diving Monkeys / Pushupsn4. Hip mobility with squats / lunges / burpees / jumps.nnnnnn## Basicsnn### The setupnnYou need to find a wall roughly thigh to hip height. This is the general height for starting vaults.nnWe are going to do everything with as much control as possible, which means nice and slow.nnn### Both Hands & FootnnStart with both hands and a single foot to create space under you.nYou want them a good distance apart to create a large space.nn### Hand positionnnStart with placing both hands on the wall first. Hands facing forward, have a good grip, flat, with the whole palm on the wall.nThe pressure should be in the middle of the hand to ball of thumb.nn### FootnnPlace one of your feet onto the wall, with the ball of the foot. Facing forwards. nn### Foot trajectorynnTry to place the foot up and over the wall, not straight at it. This is to prevent clipping the foot on the corner. As your accuracy improves, this can be refined, but for the beginning, over exaggerate the movement.nn### HipsnnPush your hips up high behind you. nAgain, you are trying to create space, so less mobility means higher hips.nn### Inside legnnThis is the Tricky part - Remove the inside arm and push the back leg through the gap between the stabilising hand and foot. nn### LandingnnPlace the ball of that foot down on the ground, controlled and slow.nn### DirectionnnMove forward in a straight line, removing the hand/foot on the wall behind you.nn### Cue 1 - straightnnStraight line - For now, remember that you are travelling in a straight line, so pick a point in front of you and head towards it.nn### Cue 2 - spacennThe amount of space under you is key. Either you have good mobility, or you create more space to get the trailing leg through.nn### Cue 3 - weight distributionnnAt the beginning, try to move your weight so that it\'s more towards your arms.nn---n{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Vaulting}}{{Tax:Step Vault}}{{Tag:beginner}}\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_2g9XgPf5Bg/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_2g9XgPf5Bg/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_2g9XgPf5Bg/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_2g9XgPf5Bg/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/_2g9XgPf5Bg/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPiukLZEqYiC6pYd1LR5e18\",\"position\":0,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"_2g9XgPf5Bg\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":0}'),(74285,55823,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Step Vault New'),(74286,55823,'authId','Auth1'),(74287,55823,'searchId','Tutorials - Step Vaults New'),(74288,55823,'filterId','none'),(74289,55823,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(74290,55823,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Step Vaults New'),(74291,55823,'_edit_last','1'),(74292,55823,'video_transcript_chatgpt','The safety vault, also known as the step vault, is an essential skill for anyone looking to safely navigate obstacles, whether you\'re a beginner just starting out or an experienced practitioner needing a reliable fallback move. Its straightforward approach makes it a great starting point, while its versatility allows for a myriad of variations as you progress. Developing confidence and control with this vault can significantly enhance your overall parkour experience, ensuring you\'re equipped to tackle challenges both comfortably and efficiently.\n\nTo get started with the step vault, first ensure you\'re warmed up properly—this promotes safety and reduces the risk of injury. Incorporating exercises that develop shoulder and arm strength as well as hip mobility, such as push-ups, burpees, and lunges, will set a solid foundation. When you\'re ready to practice, find a wall that is about thigh to hip height. Begin by placing both hands firmly on the wall and positioning one foot on top. Focus on pushing your hips high to create space as you move your back leg through. Timing and control are crucial here; land on the ball of your foot and step down smoothly. Initially, aim to travel in a straight line, ensuring your weight is distributed correctly towards your arms as you vault.\n\nThe key takeaway with the step vault is to prioritize space and control. As you build confidence, you can refine your technique and explore various advanced forms of this fundamental vault. Remember, practice makes perfect, so keep working on your skills, and soon you\'ll be vaulting over obstacles with ease and style. Enjoy the journey of improvement, and remember that the more comfortable you become, the more dynamic your movements can get.\n\n- Always prioritize a thorough warm-up to prevent injury and improve mobility.\n- Start with a wall at a comfortable height, focusing on control and creating space as you practice.\n- Remember to distribute your weight towards your arms to facilitate the movement and improve your technique.'),