om/vi/wNCWjiHmSPY/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/wNCWjiHmSPY/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/wNCWjiHmSPY/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/wNCWjiHmSPY/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTN2l71qGTXgK3Qmo7jRLj-7\",\"position\":1,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"wNCWjiHmSPY\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":1}'),(74431,55829,'scrapeId','Tutorial - QM Basics'),(74432,55829,'authId','Auth1'),(74433,55829,'searchId','Tutorials - QM Basics'),(74434,55829,'filterId','none'),(74435,55829,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(74436,55829,'importId','Tutorial Videos  - QM Crawling'),(74437,55829,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to mastering hip movement, specifically reducing unnecessary hip swinging, it\'s important to understand the correct posture and movement mechanics. Many people tend to move their hips too much when they walk or run, which can lead to inefficiencies and potential discomfort. The key to a smooth motion is maintaining a stable core while keeping your hips aligned and facing forward.\n\nTo achieve this, start by positioning your hands and feet correctly. Place one hand forward and the opposite foot ahead of you, creating a natural stance. As you move, concentrate on stepping forward and backward without allowing your hips to sway side to side. This may require some practice, but focusing on tightening your abdominal muscles can help in minimizing that unwanted hip movement. Instead of letting your body lurch left and right, keep your movements straightforward and controlled.\n\nIncorporating these techniques into your routine can significantly enhance your movement efficiency. Keeping your core engaged while ensuring your hips remain stable will not only improve your mobility but also contribute to overall better performance in any physical activity. So, practice moving straight ahead and back, maintaining alignment and control throughout the process.\n\nHighlights:\n- Reduce hip swing by focusing on a stable core and correct posture.\n- Practice stepping forward and back with minimal side-to-side movement.\n- Tighten your abs to help keep your hips aligned and improve movement efficiency.'),(74438,55829,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(74439,55829,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"oh okay so we are back with the qm we\",\n        \"start\": 0.16,\n        \"duration\": 5.04\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"are going to have a quick look at hip\",\n        \"start\": 3.52,\n        \"duration\": 4.319\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"swing and so the problem that i\",\n        \"start\": 5.2,\n        \"duration\": 5.28\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"sometimes see is there\'s too much swing\",\n        \"start\": 7.839,\n        \"duration\": 4.321\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"at the hips the idea is you want to keep\",\n        \"start\": 10.48,\n        \"duration\": 4\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"them straight and facing forwards so we\",\n        \"start\": 12.16,\n        \"duration\": 3.76\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"went through the hand and foot position\",\n        \"start\": 14.48,\n        \"duration\": 3.44\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so i\'m going to face you this time so\",\n        \"start\": 15.92,\n        \"duration\": 4.64\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"one hand forwards other foot forward and\",\n        \"start\": 17.92,\n        \"duration\": 4.72\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we move forwards\",\n        \"start\": 20.56,\n        \"duration\": 4.24\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"there and back\",\n        \"start\": 