led steps instead of large strides. When you\'re in motion, imagine that you\'re carefully placing your feet rather than lunging forward. For instance, if you start in a standing position, gently step forward with shorter strides, ensuring that your hips remain aligned. This not only helps with balance but also keeps your movements smooth and allows for greater coordination throughout your routine. Remember, the goal is to keep your hips stable rather than elevated, as this will enhance your overall posture and execution.\n\nIn summary, mastering your footwork can greatly enhance your physical performance and prevent common pitfalls. By concentrating on smaller steps and maintaining proper hip alignment, you can achieve a more graceful and controlled movement. Whether you\'re dancing, exercising, or just trying to improve your coordination, these adjustments will make a significant difference in your technique.\n\n* Take small, controlled steps to enhance balance and stability.  \n* Keep your hips aligned to maintain proper posture.  \n* Focus on smooth and coordinated movement for better overall performance.'),(74484,55831,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(74485,55831,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"all right so one of the things that i\",\n        \"start\": 1.36,\n        \"duration\": 3.36\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"sometimes see\",\n        \"start\": 3.199,\n        \"duration\": 4.64\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"is uh one of the faults is the step with\",\n        \"start\": 4.72,\n        \"duration\": 5.36\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the qm is too big\",\n        \"start\": 7.839,\n        \"duration\": 5.041\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"and you want to kind of reduce how much\",\n        \"start\": 10.08,\n        \"duration\": 4.88\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you take with the foot take small little\",\n        \"start\": 12.88,\n        \"duration\": 3.92\n    },\n    {\n    