"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/36V18H975PA/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/36V18H975PA/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/36V18H975PA/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/36V18H975PA/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/36V18H975PA/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTN2l71qGTXgK3Qmo7jRLj-7\",\"position\":6,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"36V18H975PA\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":6}'),(74546,55834,'scrapeId','Tutorial - QM Basics'),(74547,55834,'authId','Auth1'),(74548,55834,'searchId','Tutorials - QM Basics'),(74549,55834,'filterId','none'),(74550,55834,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(74551,55834,'importId','Tutorial Videos  - QM Crawling'),(74552,55834,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you’re looking to improve your parkour skills, one essential aspect to focus on is your body’s adaptability to different surfaces, particularly when it comes to hand positioning and strength. Many people might instinctively want to wear gloves to protect their hands from the cold and rough textures of the ground, but this can impede your development. By allowing your hands to feel the surfaces directly, you’re training your body to adapt and strengthen, which is crucial for success in parkour.\n\nWhen practicing the QM (quadrupedal movement) position, keep your hands bare and pressed flat against the ground. The cold concrete or rough rocks can feel uncomfortable initially, but your hands will toughen up over time. Embrace the discomfort as a part of your training! You can even seek out various surfaces like stones, gravel, or other challenging textures to further enhance your adaptability. The goal here is to build resilience and take advantage of the natural feedback your hands receive from these surfaces.\n\nIn conclusion, stepping away from gloves during your training may feel counterintuitive, but it’s an important strategy for improving your parkour skills. By pushing through the initial discomfort and giving your hands the opportunity to connect with different surfaces, you’ll be building the strength and awareness you need. Remember, the journey of adapting to your environment is just as vital as mastering the movements themselves, so dive in and experiment with various terrains!\n\n- Embrace bare hands when practicing parkour for better adaptability.\n- Use flat-hand positioning to connect with the ground effectively.\n- Challenge yourself by training on different surfaces to build resilience.'),(74553,55834,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(74554,55834,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay so with this one\",\n        \"start\": 1.68,\n        \"duration\": 4.8\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"um again we\'re gonna talk about just the\",\n        \"start\": 3.84,\n        \"duration\": 5.92\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"qm position and moving but more to do\",\n        \"start\": 6.48,\n        \"duration\": 6.72\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"with um what you don\'t do and one of\",\n        \"start\": 9.76,\n        \"duration\": 6.079\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"those things is wear gloves you don\'t\",\n        \"start\": 13.2,\n        \"duration\": 4.56\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"want to be using gloves the whole point\",\n        \"start\": 15.839,\n        \"duration\": 4.881\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"of this is warming your body up but also\",\n        \"start\": 17.76,\n        \"duration\": 6.08\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"with parkour it\'s also adapting so yes\",\n        \"start\": 20.72,\n        \"duration\