0:01:138,000\ntoes ball of the foot heels high bent\n\n72\n00:00:197,000 --> 00:01:141,000\nknees because you\'re trying to protect\n\n73\n00:00:199,000 --> 00:01:145,000\nyourself so focus\n\n74\n00:00:201,000 --> 00:01:147,000\non nice active Landing uh grip the bar\n\n75\n00:00:205,000 --> 00:01:149,000\nlike you were a bird on a\n\n76\n00:00:207,000 --> 00:01:150,000\nbranch\n\n'),(74983,55851,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(74984,55851,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APp6BJPwPWyAnQNZZm5e6f7WHvKLR\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730717987,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"When it comes to landing techniques, understanding the difference between active and passive landings can significantly impact your performance and safety. Many people tend to land passively, simply placing their feet down without control, which can lead to injuries and inefficiencies. In contrast, focusing on active landings helps you engage more of your body, improving your stability and reducing the risk of injury. Ultimately, mastering this technique not only enhances your athleticism but also protects your joints.nnTo achieve an active landing, focus on gripping the ground with your toes as if you are trying to hold onto a branch. This sensation of \"gripping the wall\" generates stability and control, making your landings both softer and more effective. Make sure that when you land, you keep your heel raised and your knees bent. This posture indicates that your muscles are engaged, and it helps keep your ankle in a safe position, minimizing the risk of injury. Wearing shoes provides some protection, but be mindful that they can numb your feet and make it harder to feel the ground beneath you. Therefore, practicing landing techniques barefoot can help you develop better awareness and control over your foot placement.nnIn summary, actively landing on the ball of your foot while gripping the surface beneath you allows for a safer and more efficient landing technique. Keep your heel elevated and your body engaged, and don’t hesitate to practice barefoot to enhance your skills. By mastering the art of active landing, you’re not only prepping yourself for better performance but also taking steps to safeguard your body against potential injuries.nn- Focus on gripping the ground with your toes to achieve an active landing.n- Keep your heel elevated and knees bent to engage your muscles and protect your ankles.n- Practice barefoot to enhance your awareness and improve your landing technique.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 829,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 351,\n            \"total_tokens\": 1180,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"hcSgKNzP1iWlb_3CcCTzi8XKgeuR6BY34t6qSC.CV3Y-1730717991-1.0.1.1-LJvN_si7fGHVJVrf8GoZRa3fUSLAl83jzfuEtdxcO6CgS8IVbn40LGvzhCM4TOPbKpNSFgsXHX9G_DYd.e7mjw\",\n            \"expires\": 1730719791,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"ygRpj5lgzuT713lYMI7.Kr3HghmgM_8XoiUYy6RQubU-1730717991420-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(74985,55851,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(74986,55851,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to landing techniques, understanding the difference between active and passive landings can significantly impact your performance and safety. Many people tend to land passively, simply placing their feet down without control, which can lead to injuries and inefficiencies. In contrast, focusing on active landings helps you engage more of your body, improving your stability and reducing the risk of injury. Ultimately, mastering this technique not only enhances your athleticism but also protects your joints.\n\nTo achieve an active landing, focus on gripping the ground with your toes as if you are trying to hold onto a branch. This sensation of \"gripping the wall\" generates stability and control, making your landings both softer and more effective. Make sure that when you land, you keep your heel raised and your knees bent. This posture indicates that your muscles are engaged, and it helps keep your ankle in a safe position, minimizing the risk of injury. Wearing shoes provides some protection, but be mindful that they can numb your feet and make it harder to feel the ground beneath you. Therefore, practicing landing techniques barefoot can help you develop better awareness and control over your foot placement.\n\nIn summary, actively landing on the ball of your foot while gripping the surface beneath you allows for a safer and more efficient landing technique. Keep your heel elevated and your body engaged, and don’t hesitate to practice barefoot to enhance your skills. By mastering the art of active landing, you’re not only prepping yourself for better performance but also taking steps to safeguard your body against potential injuries.\n\n- Focus on gripping the ground with your toes to achieve an active landing.\n- Keep your heel elevated and knees bent to engage your muscles and protect your ankles.\n- Practice barefoot to enhance your awareness and improve your landing technique.'),(74987,55851,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(74988,55851,'svg_id',''),(74989,55851,'_svg_id','field_67160c975525b'),(74990,55851,'svg_colour',''),(74991,55851,'_svg_colour','field_67161465e3b58'),(74992,55851,'extra_variables',''),(74993,55851,'_extra_variables','field_671615de0e542'),(74994,55851,'_order_position','field_67160c294bfb8'),(74995,55851,'enable_youtube_api',''),(74996,55851,'_enable_youtube_api','field_6721ddb5e8fdf'),(74997,55851,'enable_youtube_filter',''),(74998,55851,'_enable_youtube_filter','field_67225378495f0'),(74999,55851,'wordpress_filter_name','tutorial_filter'),(75000,55851,'_wordpress_filter_name','field_6722538b495f1'),(75001,55851,'enable_youtube_chatgpt',''),(75002,55851,'_enable_youtube_chatgpt','field_6721f22d49ffe'),(75003,55851,'enable_use_as_excerpt',''),(75004,55851,'_enable_use_as_excerpt','field_67225a0b50411'),(75005,55851,'youtube_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following description into three paragraphs :'),(75006,55851,'_youtube_chatgpt_prompt','field_67222f1d7722b'),(75007,55851,'enable_transcript',''),(75008,55851,'_enable_transcript','field_6722088670e84'),(75009,55851,'enable_transcript_chatgpt',''),(75010,55851,'_enable_transcript_chatgpt','field_67223080dbaa5'),(75011,55851,'transcript_chatgpt_prompt','Summarise the following transcript into three paragraphs and summarise with three key points. Never mention the speaker or the transcript. I want this to sound like I wrote the result.'),(75012,55851,'_transcript_chatgpt_prompt','field_672214208bf31'),(75013,55851,'