act and\n\n10\n00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000\nyou\'re going to more often than not feel\n\n11\n00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,000\nthe shock through your body you want to\n\n12\n00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000\ncontract early and again you\'ll notice a\n\n13\n00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:39,000\nlot of the pros\n\n14\n00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000\nare absolutely solid before they\'ve even\n\n15\n00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000\nlanded and you you can see by their body\n\n16\n00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:51,000\nshape so try and get ready and prepare\n\n17\n00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:54,000\nfor the impact before you\'ve even landed\n\n18\n00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000\nso from\n\n19\n00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000\nhere so from here you can see that it\n\n20\n00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,000\nwas already raed before I\'d even landed\n\n21\n00:00:62,000 --> 00:01:07,000\nand yeah you you really want to get in\n\n22\n00:00:64,000 --> 00:01:08,000\nthe habit of doing that\n\n'),(75136,55856,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(75137,55856,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APp6WinZkbGz4y5merMgVHbivQ7QS\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730718008,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"When it comes to landing effectively, mastering the timing of your contraction can make all the difference. The challenge many face is that they often wait until after they land to contract their muscles. This approach can lead to discomfort, as the impact can travel through your body, leaving you feeling shaky or unsteady. By preparing your body to contract before you make contact with the ground, you\'ll establish a solid base that can absorb the landing more effectively, much like the professionals do.nnTo practice this technique, focus on tensing your muscles and adopting a strong body shape even before you hit the ground. As you approach landing, visualize sealing your core and lower body, creating a solid alignment. You\'ll notice that successful jumpers and athletes visibly prepare their bodies prior to impact, showcasing a readiness that mitigates shock. It might feel a bit awkward at first, but with practice, it will become second nature. Try to develop this habit; not only will it improve your stability, but it will also enhance your performance overall.nnIn summary, getting the timing right with contraction is essential for smoother landings and less discomfort. By preparing your body to be solid before you land, you can significantly reduce the shock from impacts that could otherwise hinder your performance. Remember, learning this method may take some time, but it’s worth the effort for better athletic execution.nnKey highlights:n- Contract your muscles before landing to ensure stability and reduce impact shock.n- Observe professional athletes as they prepare for landing; they visibly tense their bodies pre-impact.n- Practice this technique consistently to make it a natural part of your landing process.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 361,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 319,\n            \"total_tokens\": 680,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"zy5gGOEV4rH_cYoT3Qdrm1dBU6Reethyf9qJarhnlRU-1730718013-1.0.1.1-B8Pbkbq2_F6fr99axZo0zPFRGKWqb5KLFSWstGU73oHub8ZtAcgYTD5iRefW4iu6nkSU5nSSI52Xptnw1VjrDw\",\n            \"expires\": 1730719813,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"InXsSLO3NkEn3eeO3D7EIkDfJGhFmQQjGvviO.m8Kh4-1730718013890-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(75138,55856,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(75139,55856,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to landing effectively, mastering the timing of your contraction can make all the difference. The challenge many face is that they often wait until after they land to contract their muscles. This approach can lead to discomfort, as the impact can travel through your body, leaving you feeling shaky or unsteady. By preparing your body to contract before you make contact with the ground, you\'ll establish a solid base that can absorb the landing more effectively, much like the professionals do.\n\nTo practice this technique, focus on tensing your muscles and adopting a strong body shape even before you hit the ground. As you approach landing, visualize sealing your core and lower body, creating a solid alignment. You\'ll notice that successful jumpers and athletes visibly prepare their bodies prior to impact, showcasing a readiness that mitigates shock. It might feel a bit awkward at first, but with practice, it will become second nature. Try to develop this habit; not only will it improve your stability, but it will also enhance your performance overall.\n\nIn summary, getting the timing right with contraction is essential for smoother landings and less discomfort. By preparing your body to be solid before you land, you can significantly reduce the shock from impacts that could otherwise hinder your performance. Remember, learning this method may take some time, but it’s worth the effort for better athletic execution.\n\nKey highlights:\n- Contract your muscles before landing to ensure stability and reduce impact shock.\n- Observe professional athletes as they prepare for landing; they visibly tense their bodies pre-impact.\n- Practice this technique consistently to make it a natural part of your landing process.'),(75140,55856,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75141,55856,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(75142,55856,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(75143,55856,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(75144,55856,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(75145,55857,'_thumbnail_id','14461'),(75146,55857,'video_id','kLZ8ZmzMUHg'),(75147,55857,'video_type','tutorial'),(75148,55857,'order_position','21'),(75149,55857,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"_pXnTPA7bq_-NymHWW2ZoSduud8\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTmZLWU5EQ0xLeWN1THRyYnJPVTNUNi5GM0Q3M0MzMzY5NTJFNTdE\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2023-11-06T14:48:49Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"Landing Accuracy - Parkour Tutorials for Beginners\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on Precisions for Beginnersnud83eudd77 The Parkour Jumping Series.nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnn#Precisions #Jumping #Parkournnu2554u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2557nu2551u2007u2007ud83cudf93D E S C R I P T I O N u2007u200au200au2007u2551nu255au2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u255dnnDetailsnnu2554u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u2550u