),(75226,55860,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75227,55860,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Precisions'),(75228,55860,'_edit_last','1'),(75229,55860,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Overcoming fear can be a challenging yet rewarding journey, especially when it comes to mastering physical skills or new movements. Whether you\'re trying to conquer your fear of jumping, trying a new sport, or even learning a dance move, practicing is the first step to building your confidence and comfort. Regular practice helps transform fear into familiarity, making previously daunting challenges feel more manageable.\n\nTo get started, commit to practicing your skills whenever possible. This means dedicating time each day to repeat the specific jumps or movements you’re working on. The key is consistency; the more you repeat these motions, the more natural they will become. Focus on perfecting your technique during your practice sessions—this is what leads to true improvement. Remember, it\'s not just about doing it often, but doing it well. Aim for \"perfect practice,\" as mastering good habits will accelerate your progress.\n\nIn conclusion, the journey to overcoming fear is all about persistence and proper technique. By incorporating regular practice into your routine, you\'ll build the confidence needed to tackle challenges head-on. Embrace the repetitions, focus on your technique, and watch as your fear fades away, replaced by a newfound competence and self-assurance. \n\nPracticing consistently helps build comfort and confidence. \nPerfecting technique through regular sessions leads to true improvement. \nEmphasizing daily practice transforms fear into familiarity.'),(75230,55860,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75231,55860,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so how do you overcome\",\n        \"start\": 0.28,\n        \"duration\": 5.88\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"fear the first thing to do is practice\",\n       