verall, the four gauges can transform your training, offering insights that help you gradually build your confidence and skillset in a supportive way.nnTo recap the essential points: nn- Use four gauges to assess jumps: technical difficulty, physical exertion, fear level, and energy levels.n- Sum the gauge values to compare jumps and create a structured approach to progressive difficulty.n- Design prep jumps that focus on overcoming specific challenges while boosting confidence and readiness for main jumps.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 747,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 385,\n            \"total_tokens\": 1132,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"kon.FhVZkRR01Rpw8l5QcV0wn2izRnS8Bc8N3OZaSMQ-1730722978-1.0.1.1-G6d3rxB4Qzc1uFrK.4QCLBMhhxEsqFHy_rUuGtai3Xf94iNlWy3LvVm4r76qHSkeQBmUaLTw5zM.VkLzRVlxIQ\",\n            \"expires\": 1730724778,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"gdjr7.p5kezA36H67W54RAyp_qxd.bbbU7k5jFd9.TY-1730722978799-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(75332,55864,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(75333,55864,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(75334,55864,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(75335,55864,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(75336,55864,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(75337,55865,'_thumbnail_id','14296'),(75338,55865,'video_id','FXMj3tUcifs'),(75339,55865,'video_type','tutorial'),(75340,55865,'order_position','0'),(75341,55865,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"WBGO0lB2RcUifHv1rQS7paLYNFA\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUGR1VnNvOXBnZWN2VkJzWmVQaUFhUC4xOTEzQzhBQzU3MDNDNjcz\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2020-04-11T06:44:50Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Land #01 - Intro Parkour Tutorial. [058]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Land (Beginner) in Parkour - Intro.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Land Series. Episode #01nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Jumping #Intro #---nnThe Landings Tip SeriesnnSo I\'ve decided to hit the 20s with new Parkour Tutorials.nEvery Monday, Wednesday & Friday at 11am.nn1. First up, Landing Properly.nnUsing the balls of your feet. ( Or the largest \"metatarsaophalangeal joint\" ). This will enable you to engage your muscles and muscular system rather than the skeletal system and joints. nnUse your toes to grip the wall, curb or rail. This will help you to contract tighter.nnAs you contract your muscles, try to keep your heels up, above the toes. Dropping the heel (which will put your foot into a \'dorsiflexion\' position) can injure your ligaments in the ankle and cause issues with:n- Achilles Heel.n- Anterior Talofibular ligament (top of the foot, on top of the ankle)n- Calcaneofibular ligament (outside of the foot, behind the ankle)nn--- Tu