//youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Jumping}}{{Series:Landing Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Fuz6XKl3l84/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Fuz6XKl3l84/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Fuz6XKl3l84/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Fuz6XKl3l84/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Fuz6XKl3l84/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPduVso9pgecvVBsZePiAaP\",\"position\":2,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"Fuz6XKl3l84\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":2}'),(75390,55867,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Landings'),(75391,55867,'authId','Auth1'),(75392,55867,'searchId','Tutorials - Landings'),(75393,55867,'filterId','none'),(75394,55867,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75395,55867,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Landings'),(75396,55867,'_edit_last','1'),(75397,55867,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Landing correctly after a jump is essential for maintaining balance and preventing injuries. One of the best ways to achieve this is by utilizing the balls of your feet. This technique not only helps to absorb the impact but also engages your muscles effectively, allowing them to contract and stabilize your body as you land. Using the balls of your feet ensures that you’re using your muscular system to manage the forces acting on your body, which significantly reduces the stress on your joints compared to landing on your heels.\n\nTo practice this landing technique, focus on bending your knees slightly as you come down, bringing your weight forward onto the balls of your feet. This action allows your muscles to engage, providing better balance and absorbing the impact of landing. By doing so, you’ll be able to maintain control, preventing the jarring that can often happen when landing flat-footed or on your heels. Remember, the key here is to keep the energy within your muscles rather than letting it travel through your skeleton, which can lead to discomfort and potential injuries.\n\nIn summary, landing on the balls of your feet is a vital skill that helps protect your joints and enhances your stability. By incorporating this technique into your movements, you’ll not only improve your landing but also boost your overall performance, whether you\'re jumping for fun or engaging in more intense activities. Practicing this method will lead to a smoother, safer landing experience and empower you to move with more confidence.\n\n- Focus on landing on the balls of your feet to engage your muscles.\n- Bend your knees slightly to absorb impact and maintain balance.\n- Protect your joints and enhance stability by avoiding flat-footed landings.'),(75398,55867,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75399,55867,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay so why do we use the balls of the\",\n        \"start\": 2.659,\n        \"duration\": 6.641\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"feet when we land so the reason we use\",\n        \"start\": 5.879,\n        \"duration\": 6.061\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the balls of the feet is anatomically it\",\n        \"start\": 9.3,\n        \"duration\": 5.28\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"means that we will be using our muscular\",\n        \"start\": 11.94,\n        \"duration\": 5.91\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"system ie our muscles to contract and\",\n        \"start\": 14.58,\n        \"duration\": 6.75\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"keep our balance and absorb the impact\",\n        \"start\": 17.85,\n        \"duration\": 6.54\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so as we land what is going to happen is\",\n        \"start\": 21.33,\n        \"duration\": 5.82\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"our muscles will contract and they will\",\n        \"start\": 24.39,\n        \"duration\": 4.979\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"absorb the energy that is going down\",\n        \"start\": 27.15,\n        \"duration\": 5.219\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"into them secondly the balls of the feet\",\n        \"start\": 29.369,\n        \"duration\": 5.641\n    },