rd or standing upright, you can create a landing posture that either absorbs impact or provides balance. By practicing these adjustments, you can find your optimal landing technique, depending on the circumstances.nnIn summary, understanding how to manipulate your ankle, knee, and hip angles gives you greater control over your landing posture. By experimenting with these angles, you’ll enhance your stability and performance while minimizing the risk of injury. Remember, the key to effective landing is being flexible and responsive to your environment, so don’t hesitate to practice these variations regularly.nn- Manipulate your ankle angle by raising or lowering your heel.n- Adjust your knee position between being locked or fully bent for better shock absorption.n- Use your hip angle to either bend forward or stand upright, adapting based on your landing needs.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 384,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 308,\n            \"total_tokens\": 692,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"GHw2qHGuPS5lybkuWtwd7i3rqWN2.aIDIyOzofOtDOc-1730721435-1.0.1.1-WIF_Mm1dJRjmhLBxlJQDF3tKAPRp6XWJSvEeHr65jk4MF2WUeVx5i7Cj.DbZUHkTvJ1mxagzuzslYrTTEq1kKg\",\n            \"expires\": 1730723235,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \