g a high amount of force (from the jump/landing) through that extreme angle is then going to guarantee an injury. So negate that risk by keeping thee foot in a strong position.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Jumping}}{{Series:Landing Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/tpxCDs80-ZA/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/tpxCDs80-ZA/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/tpxCDs80-ZA/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/tpxCDs80-ZA/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/tpxCDs80-ZA/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPduVso9pgecvVBsZePiAaP\",\"position\":4,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"tpxCDs80-ZA\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":4}'),(75438,55869,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Landings'),(75439,55869,'authId','Auth1'),(75440,55869,'searchId','Tutorials - Landings'),(75441,55869,'filterId','none'),(75442,55869,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75443,55869,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Landings'),(75444,55869,'_edit_last','1'),(75445,55869,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When engaging in activities that strain the ankles, proper technique is crucial to prevent injuries. Often, individuals overlook the importance of maintaining correct ankle position while landing or transitioning, which can lead to unnecessary stress on tendons. This guide will help you understand how to position your ankles effectively to minimize risk and enhance performance.\n\nStart by focusing on the angle of your ankles while in the landing position, especially if you\'re using blocks, a wall, or a curb. Make sure the balls of your feet are engaged and your heels are lifted. Common mistakes include allowing the heels to drop, which can create a jarring impact upon landing that could potentially cause tendon injuries. To practice this, concentrate on keeping your heel elevated as you land, ensuring you maintain a stable posture. This will not only support your ankles but also improve your overall balance and control.\n\nUltimately, mastering the proper ankle position can significantly reduce your chances of injury and enhance your athletic performance. By keeping your heels elevated and engaging the balls of your feet, you create a stable foundation. Remember that small adjustments in your technique can lead to big improvements in your safety and effectiveness during physical activities.\n\n- Keep your heels elevated while landing to reduce impact stress on your ankles.\n- Engage the balls of your feet for better stability and control.\n- Practice proper ankle positioning to prevent injuries and enhance performance.'),(75446,55869,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75447,55869,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay so looking at these angles the\",\n        \"start\": 4.22,\n        \"duration\": 7.57\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"first one is the angle the ankle I think\",\n        \"start\": 7.049,\n        \"duration\": 8.161\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"that\'s going to be pushed in so we said\",\n        \"start\": 11.79,\n        \"duration\": 4.86\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"this at the beginning the balls of the\",\n        \"start\": 15.21,\n        \"duration\": 4.68\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"feet want to be engaged so this needs to\",\n        \"start\": 16.65,\n        \"duration\": 5.52\n    },\