OTE4QTREQUU4\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2020-04-11T06:44:50Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Land #08 - Contraction Parkour Tutorial. [065]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Land (Beginner) in Parkour - Contraction.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Land Series. Episode #08nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Jumping #Contraction #---nnContract HARD!nnWhen you land, you\'re trying to do two things. First, absorb all of the downward force into the muscles, without anything going into the joints or causing too much strain on the tendons.nnSecondly, you\'re trying to maintain control and balance on the landing. That means that you need to keep the contraction of your muscles to stop any loose flexing of any joints, which in turn moves the centre of gravity and makes you more unstable.nnBy contracting as hard as you can and NOT BOUNCING BACK UP FROM THE LANDING (which is a redirection of the downward force not being fully absorbed, but rather redirected back up again) you will minimise any movement of the spine and hips which control the balance.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Jumping}}{{Series:Landing Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NJX7W5_gCbI/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NJX7W5_gCbI/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NJX7W5_gCbI/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NJX7W5_gCbI/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NJX7W5_gCbI/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPduVso9pgecvVBsZePiAaP\",\"position\":7,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"NJX7W5_gCbI\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":7}'),(75510,55872,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Landings'),(75511,55872,'authId','Auth1'),(75512,55872,'searchId','Tutorials - Landings'),(75513,55872,'filterId','none'),(75514,55872,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75515,55872,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Landings'),(75516,55872,'_edit_last','1'),(75517,55872,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to landing techniques, especially in activities involving jumps or drops, mastering your landing posture is essential for efficiency and safety. A common issue many experience is allowing their bodies to bounce back up after landing, which not only wastes energy but can also lead to injury. This tutorial focuses on how to effectively contract your muscles upon landing, taking advantage of the downward energy to stabilize your position rather than allowing it to push you back up.\n\nTo begin, as you approach your landing, focus on preparing your body to absorb the impact. When you make contact with the ground, instead of flexing your legs and rising back up, think of going into a strong, controlled contraction. This means tightening your core and other muscles to hold the position at the bottom. By doing this, you\'re actively using your muscles to manage the energy from your landing instead of just letting it move you back up. Maintaining a solid posture at this moment allows you to harness that force and maintain control, which is crucial for efficiency and injury prevention.\n\nIn summary, the key takeaway here is to hold your position upon landing with a firm contraction of your muscles rather than bouncing back up. This method not only helps you better manage the impact forces but also enhances your overall performance in your activity. By practicing this technique, you\'ll create a strong foundation for more advanced movements and ensure your body is well-prepared to handle dynamic situations.\n\n- Focus on strong muscle contraction when landing to absorb energy effectively.\n- Avoid bouncing back up after landing; instead, hold your position firmly.\n- Practicing this technique improves control, efficiency, and reduces injury risk.'),(75518,55872,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75519,55872,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay so next up is when you land you\",\n        \"start\": 4.85,\n        \"duration\": 5.02\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"want to be contracting hard with\",\n        \"start\": 8.01,\n        \"duration\": 4.95\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"everything so what generally happens is\",\n        \"start\": 9.87,\n        \"duration\": 5.519\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"people land that as flex and come back\",\n        \"start\": 12.96,\n        \"duration\": 4.95\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"up again what you want to do is hold the\",\n        \"start\": 15.389,\n        \"duration\": 5.281\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"position at the bottom and use your\",\n        \"start\": 17.91,\n        \"duration\": 5.73\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"muscles to take the energy that is\",\n        \"start\": 20.67,\n        \"duration\": 5.22\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"coming downwards as you land it\'s here\",\n        \"start\": 23.64,\n        \"duration\": 6.479\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you stop nice and hard you don\'t want\",\n        \"start\": 25.89,\n        \"duration\": 6.54\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"that energy bouncing back up and coming\",\n        \"start\": 30.119,\n        \"duration\": 4.71\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"up towards you you don\'t land and push\",