vely using your muscles to manage the energy from your landing instead of just letting it move you back up. Maintaining a solid posture at this moment allows you to harness that force and maintain control, which is crucial for efficiency and injury prevention.nnIn summary, the key takeaway here is to hold your position upon landing with a firm contraction of your muscles rather than bouncing back up. This method not only helps you better manage the impact forces but also enhances your overall performance in your activity. By practicing this technique, you\'ll create a strong foundation for more advanced movements and ensure your body is well-prepared to handle dynamic situations.nn- Focus on strong muscle contraction when landing to absorb energy effectively.n- Avoid bouncing back up after landing; instead, hold your position firmly.n- Practicing this technique improves control, efficiency, and reduces injury risk.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 349,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 321,\n            \"total_tokens\": 670,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"8IcJx.Xk6stCGyUvbtevPa2d8WkWfzt96XgRX1v5tuc-1730721541-1.0.1.1-9QkDBA9.OsEyQa3hpxvnmFmE8jhZ2sr3uqrPTYU2W2e5MMOdioZOVfYkES.ruG2pApeUt8BmswggNEDfJ7c8Dg\",\n            \"expires\": 1730723341,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\