 of the other or twisted outwards. Both feet should face directly forwards.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Jumping}}{{Series:Landing Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Atq_dpNuThw/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Atq_dpNuThw/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Atq_dpNuThw/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Atq_dpNuThw/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Atq_dpNuThw/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPduVso9pgecvVBsZePiAaP\",\"position\":8,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"Atq_dpNuThw\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":8}'),(75534,55873,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Landings'),(75535,55873,'authId','Auth1'),(75536,55873,'searchId','Tutorials - Landings'),(75537,55873,'filterId','none'),(75538,55873,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75539,55873,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Landings'),(75540,55873,'_edit_last','1'),(75541,55873,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to improving your landing technique, attention to foot placement is key. By making sure your feet are correctly positioned, you can enhance your stability and reduce the risk of injury. This tutorial will guide you through proper foot alignment and landing mechanics, making it easier to enjoy your activities and perform at your best.\n\nTo get started, focus on landing with your feet in line and parallel. Imagine creating a straight line from one foot to the other, ensuring that they are close together and neither foot is positioned forward or backward. You’ll also want to check that your feet aren\'t twisted either inwards or outwards. The main goal is to have your knees and toes aligned; both should be facing the same direction. When you look down at your feet, the toes should point straight ahead while the knees track in line with them. It can be helpful to practice holding this position before making any landing attempts, ensuring you get comfortable with the alignment.\n\nBy dedicating time to mastering your foot placement and landing position, you\'ll not only improve your performance but also safeguard yourself against potential injuries. Remember, consistency is vital, so practice regularly until the correct positioning feels second nature. The more you hone these skills, the more confident you’ll become in your movements, whether you\'re jumping, running, or simply trying to stay agile on your feet.\n\n- Focus on aligning your feet so they are in line and parallel when landing.\n- Ensure that your knees and toes are pointing in the same direction to maintain proper tracking.\n- Practice holding the landing position before attempting to jump, making the alignment instinctive.'),(75542,55873,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75543,55873,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay so we\'re gonna look at the details\",\n        \"start\": 3.049,\n        \"duration\": 4.691\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"of the foot placement and the landing so\",\n        \"start\": 5.37,\n        \"duration\": 4.08\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"today I want you to have a look at\",\n        \"start\": 7.74,\n        \"duration\": 4.5\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"trying to get your feet in line and\",\n        \"start\": 9.45,\n        \"duration\": 5.91\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"parallel so the idea being that whe