onse\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(75548,55873,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(75549,55873,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(75550,55873,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(75551,55873,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(75552,55873,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(75553,55874,'_thumbnail_id','14314'),(75554,55874,'video_id','u8vBtkE3hoU'),(75555,55874,'video_type','tutorial'),(75556,55874,'order_position','9'),(75557,55874,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"qVt9Rtx2ltSWiQIRXUva-YV2ALw\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUGR1VnNvOXBnZWN2VkJzWmVQaUFhUC44Mjc5REFBRUE2MTdFRDU0\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2020-04-11T06:44:50Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Land #10 - Silently Parkour Tutorial. [067]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Land (Beginner) in Parkour - Silently.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Land Series. Episode #10nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Jumping #Silently #---nnSilencennThe use of sound as a learning technique is a favourite of mine. By landing quietly, softly and silently you have to practice, practice, practice.nIt requires good timing too. You need to start contracting BEFORE you land, and prepare to take the landing by contracting as hard as possible.nnThe coaching cue I tend to give is that you should try to imagine you are creeping about the house at night like a ninja. Every movement is slow and controlled, with maximum amount of contraction the whole time.nnTry change the surface material to make this harder and harder. Try doing it on wood, concrete, metal or one of the hardest is onto a wet curb or low rock with a puddle of water... Try being quiet without slapping the water on landing.nnBarefoot is a great way of doing this. Having no foot protection will make you use the correct position every time because you\'ve got nothing protecting you.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Jumping}}{{Series:Landing Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/u8vBtkE3hoU/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/u8vBtkE3hoU/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/u8vBtkE3hoU/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/u8vBtkE3hoU/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/u8vBtkE3hoU/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPduVso9pgecvVBsZePiAaP\",\"position\":9,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"u8vBtkE3hoU\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":9}'),(75558,55874,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Landings'),(75559,55874,'authId','Auth1'),(75560,55874,'searchId','Tutorials - Landings'),(75561,55874,'filterId','none'),(75562,55874,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75563,55874,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Landings'),(75564,55874,'_edit_last','1'),(75565,55874,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to enhancing your landing technique in any athletic activity, mastering the art of softness and control can significantly improve your performance. It’s common to hear a loud thump when landing, which usually indicates a lack of muscle engagement and control. This tutorial focuses on the vital skill of landing softly while engaging your muscles properly—a technique that can make a noticeable difference in your movements.\n\nTo practice landing softly, one effective drill is to train barefoot. This will heighten your awareness of your feet and the ground, allowing you to feel more in control. Start by jumping gently and focusing on landing quietly. The goal is to contract your muscles firmly right before you touch the ground, which will help you absorb the impact without making much noise. Think of it like sneaking around your home; you want to make as little sound as possible while still executing your movements with precision. The more you practice this soft landing, the more instinctual it will become.\n\nIn conclusion, developing the ability to land softly while effectively engaging your muscles can significantly enhance your athletic performance. It takes practice, but the drill of jumping barefoot and focusing on quiet landings is a fun and practical way to build this skill. Remember, the key is to concentrate on muscle contraction just before you land, allowing for better control and reduced impact. With consistency in your practice, you’ll find that your landings become much more refined and efficient.\n\n- Practice jumping barefoot to improve awareness and control.\n- Focus on contracting your muscles just before landing for better impact absorption.\n- Aim for a silent landing, similar to sneaking around, to refine your technique.'),(75566,55874,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75567,55874,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay so another great drill to practice\",\n        \"start\": 6.02,\n        \"duration\": 5.92\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"is being as soft as you camp and as\",\n        \"start\": 8.73,\n        \"duration\": 7.05\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"quiet as you can so when you land if you\",\n        \"start\": 11.94,\n        \"duration\": 6.72\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"hear a thump when you land it means that\",\n        \"start\": 1