playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTPduVso9pgecvVBsZePiAaP\",\"position\":10,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"Mwh-XrIqtFI\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":10}'),(75582,55875,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Landings'),(75583,55875,'authId','Auth1'),(75584,55875,'searchId','Tutorials - Landings'),(75585,55875,'filterId','none'),(75586,55875,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75587,55875,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Landings'),(75588,55875,'_edit_last','1'),(75589,55875,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Landing safely while engaging in physical activities is crucial for preventing injuries and ensuring better performance. One effective way to improve your landing technique is to practice barefoot. Going shoeless encourages your body to adopt the natural mechanics of landing, ensuring proper contact with the ground and reducing the likelihood of improper foot strikes. By allowing your feet to feel the surface beneath you, you\'ll develop a better sense of how to land effectively.\n\nWhen you train barefoot, you’ll notice that your body instinctively wants to land on the balls of your feet instead of on your heels or the middle of your foot. This natural adjustment helps to build solid muscle memory, making your landings more efficient over time. Additionally, training without shoes promotes the development of calluses on the soles of your feet, which strengthens them and increases their resilience to various terrains. As your technique improves, you’ll also notice your toes splaying naturally, allowing for better balance and stability.\n\nIn the end, practicing landing techniques barefoot can lead to more mindful movements and a stronger awareness of how your feet interact with the ground. This simple method not only enhances your landing skills but also strengthens your feet, ultimately making your physical activities safer and more enjoyable. So give barefoot traini