Id','Auth1'),(75632,55877,'searchId','Tutorials - Landings'),(75633,55877,'filterId','none'),(75634,55877,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75635,55877,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Landings'),(75636,55877,'_edit_last','1'),(75637,55877,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Jumping and landing are essential skills that can enhance your overall athletic ability, whether you\'re getting into sports or just enjoying a bit of fun outdoors. The goal here is to master the technique of taking off from two feet and landing safely. Practicing this will help you develop muscle memory, so when you\'re ready to tackle bigger jumps, you\'ll have a solid foundation to rely on.\n\nTo begin, find a safe, stable surface such as a box or a curb where you can practice your jumps. Start by standing with your feet about shoulder-width apart, and when you\'re ready to jump, push off with both feet simultaneously. Focus on landing softly on the balls of your feet, aiming to maintain balance and stability. Make sure your knees are slightly bent to absorb the impact, and remember, it’s not about the height or distance of the jump at this stage; it’s about perfecting your landing technique. Take your time with this; the more you practice, the more natural it will feel.\n\nIn conclusion, incorporating these jump and landing drills into your routine is a smart way to prepare for more challenging movements in the future. As you practice, be patient with yourself and keep refining your form. This foundational skill will set you up for success as you progress to bigger jumps and more advanced athletic activities. \n\n- Focus on both feet taking off and land on the balls of your feet for better balance.\n- Practice frequently to develop muscle memory; it’s all about repetition.\n- Prioritize technique over distance or height to ensure you land safely each time.'),(75638,55877,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75639,55877,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"