 landing positions every time. The key is to CHALLENGE yourself, not keep doing the think you can already do. If you want to progress, you need to keep finding situations you have to adapt to.nnDon\'t  forget that there are so many variables you can use to make landings more difficult.n- area (big / small ?)n- material (concrete / wood / metal ?)n- direction (angle from you; to it)n- angle (landing sloped or level)n- shape (flat / rounded / spiked / pointed )n- weather (wet / dry / slippery / icy )n- visibility (Can you see the landing?)n- distractions ( Other movement in eye sight)n- surroundings (What is around the landing? )n- height (Are you High / low off ground?)n- distance (Far / near?)n- trajectory (Are you Going up? down?)n- obstacles (Something partially in the way you have to avoid?)n- landing ( landing on 1 foot,  2 foot, 1 on top of other)n- structure ( Stable? Wobbly? Crumbling? )n- timing ( Restriction of time to do the jump? )n- lighting (Day / Night? )n- sound ( need for silence? )n- fear ( Scary jump? is it risky? dangerous? )nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud