aP\",\"position\":15,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"dM6IEaU6il0\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":15}'),(75702,55880,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Landings'),(75703,55880,'authId','Auth1'),(75704,55880,'searchId','Tutorials - Landings'),(75705,55880,'filterId','none'),(75706,55880,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75707,55880,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Landings'),(75708,55880,'_edit_last','1'),(75709,55880,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to improving your landing skills, it\'s essential to step outside the boundaries of traditional techniques. While most landings may feel familiar and straightforward, practicing \"weird landings\" can significantly enhance your adaptability and control. These unconventional landings involve angles, slopes, and various positions where you have to adjust your body to land effectively. The goal is to challenge yourself beyond the usual drills, allowing your muscles to respond dynamically to different situations.\n\nTo master these weird landings, start by experimenting with different angles and positions. For instance, you can try landing while moving sideways or from an inclined surface. Focus on maintaining a strong, controlled position as you land, ensuring your muscles are engaged and ready to absorb the impact. It\'s crucial to practice this adaptability by incorporating various obstacles and turning points into your training. This diversity will help you build stability and responsiveness, making you more versatile in any landing situation.\n\nIn summary, exploring unconventional landing techniques is key to becoming a more skilled and adaptable athlete. Embracing these challenges not only helps improve your physical capabilities but also boosts your confidence in tackling unexpected scenarios. Stay curious and keep pushing your limits; the more you practice, the more proficient you will become in landing, regardless of the circumstances.\n\n- Experiment with landing at various angles and positions to enhance adaptability.\n- Make sure to engage your muscles during landings for better control and stability.\n- Regularly introduce new challenges to your landing practice to prevent stagnation.'),(75710,55880,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75711,55880,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"carrying on with the landing series you\",\n        \"start\": 3.08,\n        \"duration\": 5.769\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"should also be looking at weird landings\",\n        \"start\": 6.029,\n        \"duration\": 5.61\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so things that are not normal they\'re\",\n        \"start\": 8.849,\n        \"duration\": 4.471\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"not straight on they\'re not\",\n        \"start\": 11.639,\n        \"duration\": 3.63\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"perpendicular they\'re not perfect\",\n        \"start\": 13.32,\n        \"duration\": 4.77\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"positions they are angles and stuff or\",\n        \"start\": 15.269,\n        \"duration\": 6.081\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"they\'re going down or they\'re coming up\",\n        \"start\": 18.09,\n        \"duration\": 6.029\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"slight angles maybe I want to land on\",\n        \"start\": 21.35,\n        \"duration\": 6.64\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the corner turning various things where\",\n        \"start\": 24.119,\n        \"duration\": 6.721\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"I have to go sideways and I have to keep\",\n        \"start\": 27.99,\n        \"duration\": 5.729\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"that landing position constantly I have\",\n        \"start\": 30.84,\n        \"duration\": 5.01\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"to be able to do the same thing landing\",\n        \"start\": 33.719,\n        \"duration\": 4.261