25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Vaulting #HandFirst #---nnWhen approaching the wall or obstacle, the hand wants to be placed down first. In fact, if you\'re not comfortable with pushing up with a single arm, use both. nnPlace both arms onto the box, push your torso off the ground and give yourself enough space to put one foot onto the wall.nnWe first learn to put hands on first because it gives us more time to control our movement and also limit the amount of impact coming onto the obstacle. You arms will act as speed breaks when coming in with a little momentum, so the amount of force coming in cannot be too much. By place hands first we will limit the amount of force we\'re comfortable bringing into the movement.nnRemember to place the hand far enough along the wall to give your foot space to be placed on too.nnOnce the hand is on, then place your foot on the wall, using the ball of the foot. Slow, soft and controlled. The equal distribution of body weight between your arm and foot will help you get over the wall easier.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Vaulting}}{{Series:Step Vault Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SEbtG6L6a5w/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SEbtG6L6a5w/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SEbtG6L6a5w/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SEbtG6L6a5w/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SEbtG6L6a5w/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMlXqDokEh3bNO1BW9LroT7\",\"position\":1,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"SEbtG6L6a5w\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":1}'),(75798,55884,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Quickstart Step Vaults'),(75799,55884,'authId','Auth1'),(75800,55884,'searchId','Tutorials - Quickstart Step Vaults'),(75801,55884,'filterId','none'),(75802,55884,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75803,55884,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Step Vault'),(75804,55884,'_edit_last','1'),(75805,55884,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you\'re looking to improve your ability to navigate obstacles like walls or boxes, learning the step vault technique can be incredibly beneficial. This movement is all about building confidence as you transition over obstacles, making it a great choice for beginners or anyone feeling a bit apprehensive. By understanding the basic mechanics, you can safely and effectively get over barriers.\n\nTo start with, focus on placing your hand down first, followed by your opposite foot. Begin by pushing your hand into the surface for support, which allows your hips to elevate. From this position, it\'s easier to lift your opposite foot and push through, landing safely on the other side. Practice this sequence—hand placement, hip elevation, foot lift, and landing—until you feel more comfortable. It’s a straightforward way to gain confidence and finesse as you tackle those walls or boxes ahead of you.\n\nIn summary, mastering the step vault not only enhances your agility but also supports your overall movement skills. As you practice, you\'ll find yourself more at ease when approaching obstacles, no matter how daunting they may seem. Embrace the steps, feel the movement, and watch how your confidence grows.\n\nHighlights:\n- Start with your hand, then place the opposite foot for balance.\n- Use your hands to push your hips up before lifting your foot over the obstacle.\n- Practice consistently to build confidence and ease with the technique.'),(75806,55884,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75807,55884,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay so the idea was last session we\",\n        \"start\": 0.29,\n        \"duration\": 6.85\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"were looking at just making our way over\",\n        \"start\": 4.62,\n        \"duration\": 5.25\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"during the step for safety vault it was\",\n        \"start\": 7.14,\n        \"duration\": 4.56\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"one hand and the opposite foot something\",\n        \"start\": 9.87,\n        \"duration\": 4.139\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"to clarify is the fact that to begin\",\n        \"start\": 11.7,\n        \"duration\": 4.919\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"with as you are starting just to\",\n        \"start\": 14.009,\n        \"duration\": 4.621\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"understand this movement you are going\",\n        \"start\": 16.619,\n        \"duration\": 4.711\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"to place your hand first and then your\",\n        \"start\": 18.63,\n        \"duration\": 4.83\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"foot okay so the hand goes down for us\",\n        \"start\": 21.33,\n        \"duration\": 5.279\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you can actually use both hands to push\",\n        \"start\": 23.46,\n        \"duration\": 5.22\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"your hips up high to then get the\",\n        \"start\": 26.609,\n        \"duration\": 4.281\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"opposite foot up so I\'m going to push up\",\n        \"start\": 28.68,\n        \"duration\": 6.539\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"foot push through and down and I can\",\n        \"start\": 30.89,\n        \"duration\": 6.31\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\"