rofessionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Vaulting}}{{Series:Step Vault Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uRnomTvLno8/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uRnomTvLno8/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uRnomTvLno8/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uRnomTvLno8/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uRnomTvLno8/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMlXqDokEh3bNO1BW9LroT7\",\"position\":6,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"uRnomTvLno8\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":6}'),(75918,55889,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Quickstart Step Vaults'),(75919,55889,'authId','Auth1'),(75920,55889,'searchId','Tutorials - Quickstart Step Vaults'),(75921,55889,'filterId','none'),(75922,55889,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75923,55889,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Step Vault'),(75924,55889,'_edit_last','1'),(75925,55889,'video_transcript_chatgpt','To master effective movement, particularly when navigating tight spaces or positions, understanding the role of your hips is essential. In many situations, attempting to get through with your legs at a low position can feel awkward and limiting. This tutorial focuses on elevating your hips to create more room, making it much easier to transition through movements while reducing unnecessary strain on your body. \n\nStart by practicing lifting your hips as high as possible before you make any leg movements. Instead of simply trying to maneuver your leg through a small space, focus on generating space by raising your hips. This elevation creates a comfortable gap underneath, allowing your leg to easily step through. As you become more comfortable with this technique, you can start to lessen the height of your hips, but initially, aim for a significant lift to feel the ease it brings to your movement. Adopting this method not only simplifies the process but also minimizes the need for extensive flexibility or mobility to achieve your goals.\n\nIn conclusion, the ability to elevate your hips can dramatically improve your movement efficiency. By prioritizing hip height, you create the necessary space to maneuver with confidence and ease. Embrace this technique, and you’ll likely find that not only is the movement smoother, but it also feels more natural and less physically demanding. \n\n- Focus on lifting your hips high to create space before leg movements.\n- Practice making the gap underneath bigger to ease transitions.\n- Once comfortable, you can gradually lower your hips for more advanced movements.'),(75926,55889,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75927,55889,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"all right so this session we\'re going to\",\n        \"start\": 0.56,\n        \"duration\": 4.39\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"have a quick look at the hips so the\",\n        \"start\": 3,\n        \"duration\": 5.309\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"point of this is going to be that you\",\n        \"start\": 4.95,\n        \"duration\": 5.46\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"want to try to get your hips nice and\",\n        \"start\": 8.309,\n        \"duration\": 5.401\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"high so if you try to get through using\",\n        \"start\": 10.41,\n        \"dura