 limbs extended allows for minor adjustments, making it easier to control your movements. Additionally, by balancing on one leg while extending both arms and the opposite leg out, you\'ll engage three points of contact—your arms and the grounded leg—providing a sturdy base for maintaining balance.nnIn conclusion, practice keeping your arms straight and extended to improve your overall stability. This method not only allows for more controlled movements but also helps you engage your core and maintain focus. As you continue to refine your balancing techniques, remember the importance of posture and limb positioning for achieving your goals.nnHighlights:n- Extend your arms to the sides and keep them straight for better balance.n- Make small adjustments with your limbs to control your center of gravity.n- Utilize multiple contact points for enhanced stability when balancing.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 350,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 286,\n            \"total_tokens\": 636,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"9aFUApae3v0Zrs6V0gWK8x3jm9mZGRc4e16WvrFdCB4-1730718105-1.0.1.1-oZOBSkTw3MKM9MgwQB9g3nCxidfvX4SigNKpAoNS77_fmczRddLPrPgcvTbUDqGBaOaGB2CIwr5nTEr01lxCzA\",\n            \"expires\": 1730719905,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"XYdILie8jb6hBqyRmOp.XPCreEk.KDAgJXYCvg2M5cE-1730718105502-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(75954,55890,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(75955,55890,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to balance training, maintaining a stable posture can make all the difference. A common challenge people face is keeping their center of gravity in check while performing various exercises, particularly when using equipment like a balance beam or a bar. This tutorial will guide you through some effective techniques for improving your balance by utilizing your limbs in a strategic way.\n\nTo start, extend your arms out to the sides and keep them straight. This position will help you distribute your weight more evenly and maintain a stable center of gravity. If you move your arms far from your body, remember that it will create larger shifts in your hips, which can disrupt your balance. Keeping your limbs extended allows for minor adjustments, making it easier to control your movements. Additionally, by balancing on one leg while extending both arms and the opposite leg out, you\'ll engage three points of contact—your arms and the grounded leg—providing a sturdy base for maintaining balance.\n\nIn conclusion, practice keeping your arms straight and extended to improve your overall stability. This method not only allows for more controlled movements but also helps you engage your core and maintain focus. As you continue to refine your balancing techniques, remember the importance of posture and limb positioning for achieving your goals.\n\nHighlights:\n- Extend your arms to the sides and keep them straight for better balance.\n- Make small adjustments with your limbs to control your center of gravity.\n- Utilize multiple contact points for enhanced stability when balancing.'),(75956,55890,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75957,55890,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(75958,55890,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(75959,55890,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(75960,55890,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(75961,55891,'_thumbnail_id','14256'),(75962,55891,'video_id','VurtJBj7zHM'),(75963,55891,'video_type','tutorial'),(75964,55891,'order_position','1'),(75965,55891,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"QmrPOrUTijMZC_SQB5OwFR57MJA\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUF9IbVZpVVFKdnJvZnFhZ1pVWXRlRC4zMDg5MkQ5MEVDMEM1NTg2\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-10-08T14:17:07Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Balance #02 - Foot Position Parkour Tutorial. [002]\",\"description\":\"\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Balance (Beginner) in Parkour - Foot Position.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Balance Series. Episode #02nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Balancing #FootPosition #---nnBar balance foot position.n nnWhen you\'re starting out, try to have the foot as straight along the bar as you can.n No twisting at all.n The other leg will try to stay parallel to it and *Not* in front or behind because this will lead to you trying to balance with a twisted body and hips.n nnLets start with everything being straight and perfect first.n nSorry for the twisted camera angle, was tricky balancing and holding the phone at the same time!nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM