--> 00:00:47,000\ngive it a go and let us know how it goes\n\n'),(75976,55891,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(75977,55891,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APp7tIM76A3RWbIuvWfbdWVcOlUbJ\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730718093,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"Balancing on a bar can be a fun and challenging skill to master, whether you\'re doing it for exercise, sports, or just for the thrill of it. It’s a common struggle to maintain stability, especially when you\'re trying to find the right positioning and posture. Many people may not realize how important it is to align your body properly to enhance balance and prevent unnecessary falls or slips. This tutorial will guide you through some steps to improve your bar-balancing technique.nnTo start, focus on your feet. Place the foot that will be on the bar as straight and aligned with it as possible. This means no twisting or angling your foot away from the bar – it should be directly above it. As for your other foot, keep it parallel to the foot on the bar, making sure it doesn’t slide in front of or behind it. This alignment helps keep your hips in line without unnecessary twisting. Remember, the key is to keep those hips facing straight down the bar so as to maintain balance and fluidity.nnIn summary, keeping your feet aligned is crucial for achieving harmony and balance on the bar. Remember to prevent your hips from twisting, as that can lead to instability and make it much harder to stay upright. With some practice and attention to your foot and hip positioning, you should see improvements in your balance. Don’t hesitate to give it a try and see how your technique evolves!nn- Align the foot on the bar straight in line with it for better balance.n- Keep the other foot parallel to the bar foot to avoid twisting your hips.n- Practice consistently to enhance your stability and control.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 307,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 322,\n            \"total_tokens\": 629,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"oF14O9otpuXSzNWb1bGiFQH9dZvDPY1eZmuqwzM6XYU-1730718098-1.0.1.1-ii06wS8Dx6qTkCCCBHiYGmMsKRtcSURJDVoRUQcS2zV9zQRpvVEUYjnheRp8ETu51xspaLCoBYYFtLGD466F.A\",\n            \"expires\": 1730719898,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"o9WgGJ2E_UaKgr6wls_djNRnFqJA0ltAtdANr2kMxsU-1730718098214-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(75978,55891,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(75979,55891,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Balancing on a bar can be a fun and challenging skill to master, whether you\'re doing it for exercise, sports, or just for the thrill of it. It’s a common struggle to maintain stability, especially when you\'re trying to find the right positioning and posture. Many people may not realize how important it is to align your body properly to enhance balance and prevent unnecessary falls or slips. This tutorial will guide you through some steps to improve your bar-balancing technique.\n\nTo start, focus on your feet. Place the foot that will be on the bar as straight and aligned with it as possible. This means no twisting or angling your foot away from the bar – it should be directly above it. As for your other foot, keep it parallel to the foot on the bar, making sure it doesn’t slide in front of or behind it. This alignment helps keep your hips in line without unnecessary twisting. Remember, the key is to keep those hips facing straight down the bar so as to maintain balance and fluidity.\n\nIn summary, keeping your feet aligned is crucial for achieving harmony and balance on the bar. Remember to prevent your hips from twisting, as that can lead to instability and make it much harder to stay upright. With some practice and attention to your foot and hip positioning, you should see improvements in your balance. Don’t hesitate to give it a try and see how your technique evolves!\n\n- Align the foot on the bar straight in line with it for better balance.\n- Keep the other foot parallel to the bar foot to avoid twisting your hips.\n- Practice consistently to enhance your stability and control.'),(75980,55891,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75981,55891,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(75982,55891,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(75983,55891,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(75984,55891,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(75985,55892,'_thumbnail_id','14258'),(75986,55892,'video_id','R807ZtMV1-s'),(75987,55892,'video_type','tutorial'),(75988,55892,'order_position','2'),(75989,55892,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"iW3jN5uR94PAI_uVMK-hoVQnw90\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUF9IbVZpVVFKdnJvZnFhZ1pVWXRlRC4yODlGNEE0NkRGMEEzMEQy\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T08:31:13Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Balance #03 - Walking Parkour Tutorial. [003]\",\"description\":\"\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Balance (Beginner) in Parkour - Walking.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Balance Series. Episode #03nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Balancing #Walking #---nnBalance walking on a bar.n n So back to the bar today! Let\'s look at the mechanics of walking along it.n Try to not just shift your weight onto the front foot straight away.n Make sure that it\'s in a good position first, then shift the bodyweight afterwards.n n### Things to think about.n Make sure the foot is straight when you position it down.n When things are rushed, it gets sloppy and the front foot becomes angled along the bar, get out of that habit.n n###Take it slow.n Also, it should be noted that this is for when you\'re just starting out or when you are in a difficult, uncomfortable position (maybe it\'s higher than usual).n As you become more comfortable this routine can become more instinctive and will be safer and controlled, but will look like you are just putting you weight straight over the foot.n We are trying to build control and stability, so going slow and managing every movement is important.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 http