s://i.ytimg.com/vi/R807ZtMV1-s/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/R807ZtMV1-s/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/R807ZtMV1-s/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/R807ZtMV1-s/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTP_HmViUQJvrofqagZUYteD\",\"position\":2,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"R807ZtMV1-s\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":2}'),(75990,55892,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Rail Balance'),(75991,55892,'authId','Auth1'),(75992,55892,'searchId','Tutorials - Rail Balance'),(75993,55892,'filterId','none'),(75994,55892,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(75995,55892,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Rail Balance'),(75996,55892,'_edit_last','1'),(75997,55892,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you\'re looking to improve your balance skills, focusing on using one foot for balance on a bar can be an effective technique. This approach helps you engage your core and develop better stability by utilizing three limbs—your two arms and one foot—while minimizing reliance on both feet. By practicing this method, you’ll gradually enhance your coordination and control, ultimately leading to improved performance in various activities.\n\nTo get started, find a sturdy bar that you can safely balance on. Begin by placing one foot on the bar, lifting the other foot off the surface. The key is to keep only one foot on the bar for as long as you can. As you become comfortable, you can begin shifting your weight from one foot to the other. When you do this, be careful not to hold your balance with both feet at the same time. The focus should be on landing one foot in front while quickly bringing the other foot off the bar. This way, you engage your arms and the foot you have on the bar to help maintain your balance more effectively.\n\nIn conclusion, practicing this technique will not only strengthen your balance but also enhance your overall stability. By focusing on one foot at a time, you\'re learning to rely more on your body’s natural balance mechanisms. Remember, it may take some practice, but with patience and persistence, you\'ll notice significant improvements in your coordination and balance abilities.\n\nHighlights:\n- Use one foot on the bar for balance to engage your core and improve stability.\n- Shift your weight from one foot to the other while minimizing contact with the bar.\n- Focus on landing your foot quickly while keeping your arms engaged for better control.'),(75998,55892,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(75999,55892,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"I want you to focus on trying to have\",\n        \"start\": 0.1,\n        \"duration\": 5.58\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"just one foot on the bar the most amount\",\n        \"start\": 2.649,\n        \"duration\": 5.7\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"of time you can okay so try not to have\",\n        \"start\": 5.68,\n        \"duration\": 5.31\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"both feet on the bar and you\'re just\",\n        \"start\": 8.349,\n        \"duration\": 4.65\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"shifting one foot in front of the other\",\n        \"start\": 10.99,\n        \"duration\": 4.2\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the idea is that you\'re on one foot as\",\n        \"start\": 12.999,\n        \"duration\": 3.661\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you feel comfortable you shift to the\",\n        \"start\": 15.19,\n        \"duration\": 3.089\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"next and the other leg comes off as\",\n        \"start\": 16.66,\n        \"duration\": 3.689\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"quick as possible this means that you\",\n      