: \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730718039,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"This tutorial is centered around maintaining balance while transitioning your weight between your feet, a skill that can enhance your stability and coordination. Whether you’re preparing for sports activities, dance, or simply trying to improve your physical confidence, mastering this foundational movement can be incredibly beneficial. It allows you to maneuver fluidly, promoting strength and stability in your movements.nnTo begin, find a comfortable standing position. Start practicing by balancing on one foot, ensuring you feel stable before introducing the other leg. Once you’re steady, focus on bringing the other foot behind you without shifting your weight onto it right away. Keep both feet close to the ground and only transfer your weight to the back foot when you feel secure. If at any point you start to wobble, simply lift your back foot back off the ground to regain your balance. It\'s all about finding that sweet spot where you feel confident before you fully commit to the transition.nnIn summary, this exercise emphasizes the importance of balance and controlled movements. By learning to shift your weight effectively between your feet without rushing, you can build a strong foundation for more complex movements later. Remember to practice at your own pace and focus on comfort; the key is to feel secure before you make any shifts.nnHighlights: n- Start by balancing on one foot before introducing the other foot into the movement. n- Only shift your weight onto the back foot when you feel secure and stable. n- If you feel wobbly, don’t hesitate to lift your foot back off the ground to regain balance.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 348,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 305,\n            \"total_tokens\": 653,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"FBf3CRKj2rfj4ZxiT3pInuBrxUa7Vym0sqSnPqq6aBU-1730718044-1.0.1.1-nH0ld97L5cHWLMt5ocAIjzQP39WD90bCGjrWTTsk4jDzdMoQhqQUnlRkhY1Pa1IDbG3la7nDQbp__Z5TcIDzZg\",\n            \"expires\": 1730719844,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"_NQ5CfuVnYcOzwsUqrFXTupbdD9c6mufg6C8077m3GE-1730718044246-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76026,55893,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76027,55893,'video_transcript_chatgpt','This tutorial is centered around maintaining balance while transitioning your weight between your feet, a skill that can enhance your stability and coordination. Whether you’re preparing for sports activities, dance, or simply trying to improve your physical confidence, mastering this foundational movement can be incredibly beneficial. It allows you to maneuver fluidly, promoting strength and stability in your movements.\n\nTo begin, find a comfortable standing position. Start practicing by balancing on one foot, ensuring you feel stable before introducing the other leg. Once you’re steady, focus on bringing the other foot behind you without shifting your weight onto it right away. Keep both feet close to the ground and only transfer your weight to the back foot when you feel secure. If at any point you start to wobble, simply lift your back foot back off the ground to regain your balance. It\'s all about finding that sweet spot where you feel confident before you fully commit to the transition.\n\nIn summary, this exercise emphasizes the importance of balance and controlled movements. By learning to shift your weight effectively between your feet without rushing, you can build a strong foundation for more complex movements later. Remember to practice at your own pace and focus on comfort; the key is to feel secure before you make any shifts.\n\nHighlights: \n- Start by balancing on one foot before introducing the other foot into the movement. \n- Only shift your weight onto the back foot when you feel secure and stable. \n- If you feel wobbly, don’t hesitate to lift your foot back off the ground to regain balance.'),(76028,55893,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76029,55893,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76030,55893,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76031,55893,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76032,55893,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76033,55894,'_thumbnail_id','14262'),(76034,55894,'video_id','JV-D4oIS2fQ'),(76035,55894,'video_type','tutorial'),(76036,55894,'order_position','4'),(76037,55894,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"MJkDXVy_7TLZ0d45gJO8vUtuBik\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUF9IbVZpVVFKdnJvZnFhZ1pVWXRlRC41MjE1MkI0OTQ2QzJGNzNG\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T08:31:16Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Balance #05 - Turning Parkour Tutorial. [005]\",\"description\":\"\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Balance (Beginner) in Parkour - Turning.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Balance Series. Episode #05nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Balancing #Turning #---nnTurning on the bar.n n Turning time! So, if you want to really hammer into your system a good turn, you have to do it slow, not missing any part of the turn at all.nnThings to consider: - Your arms are going to be doing a lot of the balancing work and should transition from your sides to the front, to the sides again.nn - Knees are bent and you should have maximum contraction in your quads, hamstrings and glutes. This will stabilise you.n - The BALLS of the foot (just behind the toes) are the pivot point. Imagine you are turning on a penny. You don\'t allow the bar to slip into the middle of the foot. This is because you will lack any ability to control the turn and balancing will much harder.n - Make sure both feet start facing the same direction, both feet turn simultaneously, and both feet finish facing the opposite direction at the same time. This will take a little while to master, but it will definitely enable you to move with more confidence and control.n nIf you feel that you\'re moving fast, skipping a foot placement or are just wobbly, it\'s a sign you\'re not in control.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJump