are doing the majority of the work. This way, you\'ll have the ability to adjust your movements quickly if necessary and maintain a smooth, controlled turn.nnIn conclusion, mastering your turning technique requires practice and awareness of your foot placement. Remember to focus on the balls of your feet, maintain a slow, controlled pace, and engage your muscles properly. With time and dedication, you\'ll be able to turn confidently and gracefully, enhancing your overall performance and enjoyment.nn- Use the balls of your feet for better pivoting and control when turning.n- Maintain a slow pace to focus on balance and muscle engagement.n- Practice regularly to build confidence and skill in your turning technique.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 342,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 274,\n            \"total_tokens\": 616,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"lAoIALalAIrHYwthm9zTAyn7hypAWE4Fibj8x3jT0YI-1730718138-1.0.1.1-iSKze6.7xWuFSOfCv4nzAPfutRy2pEJU996Zvtos.jlifVc6fpdaSPfaBcuz5MkbGfwan2_q0.3AUZ2AXfZjpg\",\n            \"expires\": 1730719938,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"HkLg2PoQQks8ZXCmsRUjDeha3ZTMC2mqu4eYVcgPlsA-1730718138371-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76050,55894,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76051,55894,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you\'ve ever struggled with turning while maintaining balance and control, you\'re not alone. Many people find that making smooth, precise turns can be challenging. This tutorial will guide you on the proper technique to help you master turning by focusing on how to use your feet effectively, giving you more control and confidence in your movements.\n\nThe key to successful turning begins with using the balls of your feet as your pivot point. It\'s essential to avoid slipping into the middle of your foot, as this can result in a loss of balance and control. Start your practice at a slow pace, which allows you to really feel what your body is doing and how it\'s positioned. As you turn, ensure that your muscles are engaged and your legs are doing the majority of the work. This way, you\'ll have the ability to adjust your movements quickly if necessary and maintain a smooth, controlled turn.\n\nIn conclusion, mastering your turning technique requires practice and awareness of your foot placement. Remember to focus on the balls of your feet, maintain a slow, controlled pace, and engage your muscles properly. With time and dedication, you\'ll be able to turn confidently and gracefully, enhancing your overall performance and enjoyment.\n\n- Use the balls of your feet for better pivoting and control when turning.\n- Maintain a slow pace to focus on balance and muscle engagement.\n- Practice regularly to build confidence and skill in your turning technique.'),(76052,55894,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76053,55894,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(