This initial stance is critical as it helps you gain balance before you begin to crouch. Gradually lower your body into a squat while simultaneously reaching your hands toward the bar. You are aiming to create four points of contact—two feet and two hands—which will give you better control over your center of gravity. Although it might feel challenging at first, don’t hesitate to keep practicing; as you become more accustomed to this position, you will feel safer and more stable.nnIn summary, practicing the crouch position on the bar with your hands in contact will help build your strength and improve your confidence in your movements. Remember, the key is to focus on finding your balance and maintaining comfort in your squat position. With patience and practice, you\'ll master this technique smoothly and effectively.nn- Position your feet firmly on the bar before attempting to crouch.n- Aim to make four points of contact: two feet and two hands.n- Practice regularly to build strength and confidence in your movements.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 356,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 288,\n            \"total_tokens\": 644,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"rvtlHeI3.CjxK6UwZHWmlOytZa.4HnqDplJtEygP9R0-1730718127-1.0.1.1-HhLY3lLCYp5WzOhfRvWrnxoS0JVoP.IQ22b3DpDljCuhqZhLN5TtzsMXWP8nYN3Jrh8e747YflbQiuXNseUSDA\",\n            \"expires\": 1730719927,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"4HA.GO_P5WsKhJkbRmDfSyezz1xlsvfsCXvY2Pj2Vro-1730718127707-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76146,55898,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76147,55898,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Crouching on a bar gives you a solid workout foundation and can help improve your overall strength and balance. Many people struggle with learning how to control their center of gravity while attempting this move, leading to frustration. This tutorial will guide you through the steps to properly crouch on a bar, placing your hands in the right position to create a sense of stability and security.\n\nTo get started, position yourself on the bar with both feet firmly planted on it. This initial stance is critical as it helps you gain balance before you begin to crouch. Gradually lower your body into a squat while simultaneously reaching your hands toward the bar. You are aiming to create four points of contact—two feet and two hands—which will give you better control over your center of gravity. Although it might feel challenging at first, don’t hesitate to keep practicing; as you become more accustomed to this position, you will feel safer and more stable.\n\nIn summary, practicing the crouch position on the bar with your hands in contact will help build your strength and improve your confidence in your movements. Remember, the key is to focus on finding your balance and maintaining comfort in your squat position. With patience and practice, you\'ll master this technique smoothly and effectively.\n\n- Position your feet firmly on the bar before attempting to crouch.\n- Aim to make four points of contact: two feet and two hands.\n- Practice regularly to build strength and confidence in your movements.'),(76148,55898,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76149,55898,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76150,55898,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76151,55898,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76152,55898,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76153,55899,'_thumbnail_id','14272'),(76154,55899,'video_id','z6iPwC_6z5M'),(76155,55899,'video_type','tutorial'),(76156,55899,'order_position','9'),(76157,55899,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"1up0nJFzhKkQPJuzX59kLZ48dRo\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUF9IbVZpVVFKdnJvZnFhZ1pVWXRlRC45NDk1REZENzhEMzU5MDQz\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T08:31:24Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Balance #10 - Without Using Arms Parkour Tutorial. [010]\",\"description\":\"\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Balance (Beginner) in Parkour - Without Using Arms.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Balance Series. Episode #10nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Balancing #WithoutUsingArms #---nnBalancing without using Arms.n n Trying to balance without the use of your arms will be particularly tricky and will take a while to get used to.n Keep persevering! - Go slowly! Spend 10seconds on the bar without arms and come off.n Then 15secs.n Work up until you feel comfortable for longer periods of time - The other leg will be doing most of the balancing for you, so make sure it is straight, as well as your hips.n Always do both legs! nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 http