1u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Balancing}}{{Series:Rail Balance Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/z6iPwC_6z5M/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/z6iPwC_6z5M/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/z6iPwC_6z5M/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/z6iPwC_6z5M/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/z6iPwC_6z5M/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTP_HmViUQJvrofqagZUYteD\",\"position\":9,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"z6iPwC_6z5M\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":9}'),(76158,55899,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Rail Balance'),(76159,55899,'authId','Auth1'),(76160,55899,'searchId','Tutorials - Rail Balance'),(76161,55899,'filterId','none'),(76162,55899,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(76163,55899,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Rail Balance'),(76164,55899,'_edit_last','1'),(76165,55899,'video_transcript_chatgpt','As you progress in your balance training, you\'ll find that your body begins to develop a natural sense of equilibrium. This tutorial will help you take the next step by focusing on reducing your reliance on your arms and refining your balance using your legs. This focused practice is great for enhancing your stability and confidence while on the balance bar, which can be particularly useful in various physical activities and sports.\n\nTo begin, it\'s important to establish a solid foundation. Stand on the balance bar with your legs straight and arms out to the sides for initial support. Once you feel comfortable, gradually transition to positioning your hands behind your back. This adjustment shifts the responsibility for balance primarily to your legs. As you do this, your primary balancing leg will engage more actively while your other leg will help in making subtle shifts to maintain your centered gravity. Remember to take your time and focus on how your body naturally finds its balance, as this will enhance your overall control.\n\nIn closing, practicing balance without using your arms can significantly strengthen your overall stability and body awareness. By challenging yourself in this way, you\'ll cultivate a greater understanding of how to manage your body and its movements, ultimately leading to improved performance in more complex physical tasks. Embrace the challenge, and enjoy the process of becoming more balanced and centered.\n\n- Transition your hands behind your back to focus solely on leg balance.\n- Use your primary balancing leg to help maintain equilibrium while shifting weight.\n- Practice consistently to build confidence and improve body awareness over time.'),(76166,55899,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76167,55899,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so as you start feeling more comfortable\",\n        \"start\": 2.6,\n        \"duration\": 5.009\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you\'re going to get a feeling for how to\",\n        \"start\": 4.84,\n        \"duration\": 6.579\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"control your balance and now with the\",\n        \"start\": 7.609,\n        \"duration\": 6.39\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"arms out and the legs straight and the\",\n        \"start\": 11.419,\n        \"duration\": 5.041\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"arms straight and all of that you\'re not\",\n        \"start\": 13.999,\n        \"duration\": 4.471\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"going to have to rely on that quite so\",\n        \"start\": 16.46,\n        \"duration\": 3.69\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\