ughout the squat for better results.\n- Keep your back straight and chest lifted to maintain proper form.\n- Practice consistently for improved strength and balance over time.'),(76196,55900,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76197,55900,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76198,55900,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76199,55900,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76200,55900,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76201,55901,'_thumbnail_id','14276'),(76202,55901,'video_id','S05RGvMCDEA'),(76203,55901,'video_type','tutorial'),(76204,55901,'order_position','11'),(76205,55901,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"YQrmw1mGgEeVslzcXEJAvOMVrvY\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUF9IbVZpVVFKdnJvZnFhZ1pVWXRlRC40NzZCMERDMjVEN0RFRThB\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T08:31:28Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Balance #12 - Pelvic Tilt Parkour Tutorial. [012]\",\"description\":\"\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Balance (Beginner) in Parkour - Pelvic Tilt.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Balance Series. Episode #12nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Balancing #PelvicTilt #---nnPelvic Tilt Position.n n Super important topic today. Pelvis position.n Every movement to do has something to do with the hips and where they sit will make a big impact.n - Day to Day sitting will cause a bad exposition on the pelvis. Correcting it and stacking your spine correctly will make you more stable.n - Squeeze your butt, engage the abs about 20% to keep the pelvis in the correct position.n - Film yourself for feedback and look at your spine position.n - Correcting this is a never-ending challenge! Good luck amigos! nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 http