und unpredictably, making it challenging to maintain stability. Conversely, by keeping your body contracted and your muscles engaged, you create a more stable environment for that marble, which allows for better control and coordination.nnTo achieve this balance, start by consciously engaging your muscles. Stand with your arms out to the side and focus on tightening your core, legs, and arms. When you contract your muscles in this way, you create a solid framework that helps you maintain your center of gravity. Imagine that marble sitting in your hips; when your muscles are engaged and aligned, it becomes much easier to guide and control your movements without unnecessary effort. This slight adjustment can make all the difference when you\'re on the bar or participating in other physical activities.nnIn summary, understanding and managing your center of gravity can significantly enhance your performance and control in any physical pursuit. By maintaining a contracted posture, you\'ll find that not only is it easier to stabilize your movements, but you\'ll also reduce the risk of injury. Remember, keeping your body engaged leads to better balance and a more enjoyable experience in any activity you choose to partake in.nnHighlights:n- Your center of gravity acts like a marble in your hips; keep it controlled for better balance.n- Engage and contract your muscles to stabilize your movements and maintain control.n- A tighter posture can improve performance and reduce injury risk during physical activities.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 384,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 334,\n            \"total_tokens\": 718,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"7MKl_LhFYylbkiEyNq_sv5.BZ5Of2MxeiGxiIYjtB1A-1730718086-1.0.1.1-LObU_WO0pbg7r5gJeZRc57PQauuJXgqPwAyoIKFbJw0YJXk.sgZp4psAXGdGT5TJa6Pho3omC_Cxs4wlZ7hhLg\",\n            \"expires\": 1730719886,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"j3ID.O6ct.sh9Rneu.m8rDZNddTNn6wcecnOxrJiaxk-1730718086830-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76242,55902,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76243,55902,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Understanding your center of gravity is essential for maintaining balance and control in your movements, whether you\'re on the dance floor, participating in a sport, or simply navigating through life. Think of your center of gravity as a marble located in the middle of your hips. When your body is loose and relaxed, that marble can roll around unpredictably, making it challenging to maintain stability. Conversely, by keeping your body contracted and your muscles engaged, you create a more stable environment for that marble, which allows for better control and coordination.\n\nTo achieve this balance, start by consciously engaging your muscles. Stand with your arms out to the side and focus on tightening your core, legs, and arms. When you contract your muscles in this way, you create a solid framework that helps you maintain your center of gravity. Imagine that marble sitting in your hips; when your muscles are engaged and aligned, it becomes much easier to guide and control your movements without unnecessary effort. This slight adjustment can make all the difference when you\'re on the bar or participating in other physical activities.\n\nIn summary, understanding and managing your center of gravity can significantly enhance your performance and control in any physical pursuit. By maintaining a contracted posture, you\'ll find that not only is it easier to stabilize your movements, but you\'ll also reduce the risk of injury. Remember, keeping your body engaged leads to better balance and a more enjoyable experience in any activity you choose to partake in.\n\nHighlights:\n- Your center of gravity acts like a marble in your hips; keep it controlled for better balance.\n- Engage and contract your muscles to stabilize your movements and maintain control.\n- A tighter posture can improve performance and reduce injury risk during physical activities.'),(76244,55902,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76245,55902,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76246,55902,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76247,55902,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76248,55902,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76249,55903,'_thumbnail_id','14280'),(76250,55903,'video_id','bdYJ4nd8D2k'),(76251,55903,'video_type','tutorial'),(76252,55903,'order_position','13'),(76253,55903,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"fbp2x0RkAU4PQv-XeMp52VCwg8A\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUUF9IbVZpVVFKdnJvZnFhZ1pVWXRlRC45ODRDNTg0QjA4NkFBNkQy\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T08:31:32Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Balance #14 - Shifting Your Weight Parkour Tutorial. [014]\",\"description\":\"\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Balance (Beginner) in Parkour - Shifting Your Weight.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Balance Series. Episode #14nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Balancing #ShiftingYourWeight #---nnBalance - Shifting your weight.nnSimple one today. Just the idea of moving forwards and stepping. Don\'t automatically shift your bodyweight at the same time. Get used to placing and the shifting.n - As you become more experienced this movement will automatically become natural and LOOK like you are shifting at the same time, but there is a split second before the commitment where you can stop. So let\'s get started on the process! n- Try not to linger too long with two feet on the bar either.nn Three free limbs are better for balance than two! nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u