tually we\'re going to put the\n\n164\n00:00:429,000 --> 00:01:374,000\nwarm up video at the end of the series\n\n165\n00:00:432,000 --> 00:01:377,000\nthe reason being that we need to be able\n\n166\n00:00:435,000 --> 00:01:380,000\nto understand all the variations of the\n\n167\n00:00:437,000 --> 00:01:382,000\npull-up that you can do and find out\n\n168\n00:00:440,000 --> 00:01:385,000\nwhich one is applicable to you once we\n\n169\n00:00:443,000 --> 00:01:388,000\nknow what that one is then we can\n\n170\n00:00:446,000 --> 00:01:393,000\nregress back to one or two before that\n\n171\n00:00:448,000 --> 00:01:393,000\nand use those to do a warm-up however we\n\n172\n00:00:453,000 --> 00:01:397,000\nneed to know what all those different\n\n173\n00:00:454,000 --> 00:01:400,000\nvariations are before we actually jump\n\n174\n00:00:457,000 --> 00:01:402,000\nonto the bar okay so let\'s get into the\n\n175\n00:00:460,000 --> 00:01:403,000\nseries and we\'re going to go into the\n\n176\n00:00:462,000 --> 00:01:405,000\nvery first one which is actually\n\n177\n00:00:464,000 --> 00:01:410,000\nunderstanding what we want to try to do\n\n178\n00:00:466,000 --> 00:01:409,000\nwhen we are doing a pull-up\n\n179\n00:00:477,000 --> 00:01:419,000\nyou\n\n'),(76315,55905,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(76316,55905,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APqEOnqVaOWGR7HoN66ezJmyZe76d\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730722340,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"If you\'re gearing up to tackle a pull-up training course, it\'s great to have a solid foundation before diving into it. Pull-ups can be a challenging yet rewarding exercise, and having the right equipment and preparing your body properly is crucial for success. In this tutorial, we\'ll walk you through the essential tools and warm-up routines you should know before starting your pull-up journey.nnFirst and foremost, you\'ll need a bar to pull up on. A sturdy scaffolding bar is ideal, but if that\'s not accessible, consider investing in a reliable pull-up bar that you can find online. While these tend to be thinner than scaffolding bars, they can still support your training effectively. You\'ll also want to grab some mobility bands, which will help facilitate different variations of pull-ups and assist in your training as you progress. Look for high-quality bands, as the rubber quality directly impacts safety and durability; reputable brands like Rogue Fitness are a good choice. In addition to these essentials, a weight belt might come in handy if you\'re looking to add resistance down the line. For now, focus on securing your bar and bands as these are the foundation of your training.nnBefore you jump into exercising, it\'s vital to warm up your joints. A proper warm-up will help prevent injuries and ensure you get the most out of your workout. Start with some wrist exercises, using figure-eight movements to enhance range of motion. Move on to elbow circles and bending exercises to keep your elbows nimble. Finally, spend some time loosening up your shoulders with circular movements, experimenting with different angles and directions. This joint mobility routine gets your body ready for the demands of pull-ups and primes your muscles for action. Once you\'ve warmed up, you can then explore the variations of pull-ups to find what suits your level best. nnTo sum up, preparing adequately for your pull-up training is crucial for both performance and safety. Make sure you have the proper equipment: a sturdy pull-up bar and mobility bands are your main tools. Don\'t forget to incorporate a thorough warm-up routine that focuses on your wrists, elbows, and shoulders to keep your joints healthy and primed for exercise. nn- Essential equipment: a sturdy pull-up bar and high-quality mobility bands are key to your training success.n- Focus on warming up your wrists, elbows, and shoulders to prevent injury and enhance your range of motion.n- Explore different variations of pull-ups to find what works best for your current fitness level.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1741,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 490,\n            \"total_tokens\": 2231,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"414KcGSsHoCu8hDTgN5LKVkMFw.bRIFjRoaE3bs4kJU-1730722348-1.0.1.1-7GKsWzEamciyhBaUG8pKsfJAS3sxYzI5LZnXr_doUQqCo4C09TCcxJoh6w3WdlwntqtuoqCTLLPek5Ij6mqM_g\",\n            \"expires\": 1730724148,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"11W2GPutxu1tZP_fcEB9yUqPcrl7pPjEY.m9QtYX24s-1730722348303-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76317,55905,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76318,55905,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76319,55905,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76320,55905,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76321,55905,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76322,55906,'_thumbnail_id','14182'),(76323,55906,'video_id','S3IgsFQazyQ'),(76324,55906,'video_type','tutorial'),(76325,55906,'order_position','2'),(76326,55906,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"BpYD2R0i7qthiFLtv30ndSD_-a0\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC45RjNFMDhGQ0Q2RkFCQTc1\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #03 - Fundamentals Parkour Tutorial. [078]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Beginner) in Parkour - Fundamentals.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #03nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnFROMAGE.nnLet\'s get started with the basics of how to do a pull-up and what the point of doing it is. We will cover the main pieces that you should always do when on the bar to make sure you\'re doing it correctly.nn### What are we trying to do?nThe whole idea is that we want to be strong enough to pull ourselves up, right? The pull-up is one of the best tools to make us stronger to achieve this (if done right). It also is the exact movement we would use if we needed to pull ourselves up too. This makes it very useful as an exercise.nn### DeadhangnWhen you hang on the bar in the starting position of the pull-up try to go to the lowest point you can with every attempt you do.nnThe reason for this is that this is usually one of the weakest sections of the pull-up for most people due to the fact that it\'s the bit that is missed the most.nnWhen you are in NEED of getting up onto something in a real situation then you want to make sure you can pull up from the absolute bottom, not from a staged ready position with your muscles already tense and contracted.nn### Hand PositionnThe easiest way to think of this is \'how would I hold a wall?\'. Since this is the method that will be used most often, it\'s the one you should get more comfortable doing.nnI used to have a hard time remembering the technical terms for the grip position until I was told this:nnHow would you hold a large bowl of SOUP in your hands? This is called SUPinated grip. (Pronounced \'soup-in-ate-ed\'). The other way around is the pronated grip.nn### FROMnThis is something that is so important for all movement it\'s crazy. This stands for FULL RANGE OF MOTION.nnThis basically means that the pull-up you should always go to the absolute bottom (the dead-hang as mentioned above) and the absolute top. Anything less and you\'re cheating, you cheating cheater.nnI have a funnier and more memorable acronym that will stick in your head more. F.R.O.M.A.G.E. (The French word for cheese.)nnFull. Range. Of. Motion. And. Good. Execution. So, if you\'re in any doubt, think of cheese...nn### Where To LooknA smaller detail, but when we do a pull-up, the spine should be in a normal \'neutral\' position. Basically, don\'t bend your neck and try to look forward, not up.nnI personally pick a spot in front of me and focus intently on that single small thing. It helps to keep my neck correct and also my mind focused on tuning out any distractions around me.nn### The Dish ShapenStaying on the idea of having a good body position, we want to create a subtle \'dish\' shape with our torso.nnTo accomplish this, our legs should be ahead of us, not behind us (unless our knees are bent). Getting into the nitty-gritty, we really are trying to make sure our butts are not sticking out and our hips are rotated back into a \'backward banana\' position.nnIf you think your lower back is getting squashed, you\'re in the wrong position. Use your belly (abs) to try to bring your legs in front of you.nn### Grip HardnThe more you grip as hard as you can, the more muscles get involved in the action. The more muscles you use, the easier the work will be. Simple, right?nnJust think you\'re hanging off a plane and your grip is all that\'s keeping you on. Crush that bar.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Strengthening}}{{Series:Pullups}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/S3IgsFQazyQ/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/S3IgsFQazyQ/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/S3IgsFQazyQ/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/S3IgsFQazyQ/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/S3IgsFQazyQ/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMmrCVs_bOotQLjVdq5zGhT\",\"position\":2,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"S3IgsFQazyQ\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":2}'),(76327,55906,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Pullups'),(76328,55906,'authId','Auth1'),(76329,55906,'searchId','Tutorials - Pullups'),(76330,55906,'filterId','none'),(76331,55906,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(76332,55906,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Pullups'),(76333,55906,'_edit_last','1'),(76334,55906,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Pull-ups are a fantastic exercise for building upper body strength, but they\'re not always easy for everyone. Whether you’re a beginner struggling to lift your body weight or someone looking to perfect your form, understanding the correct techniques and variations can significantly enhance your training. This tutorial will guide you through the essential steps to perform a pull-up effectively, ensuring you can engage the right muscle groups and work towards increasing your strength while enjoying the process.\n\nTo start, it’s important to understand the position of your body during a pull-up. Begin in what’s known as a \"dead hang\" position, where your muscles are relaxed and fully extended. This sets a solid foundation for the proper movement. Next, focus on your grip. An optimal grip involves holding the bar with your palms facing away from you, ensuring that your hands are positioned correctly to facilitate better pulling mechanics. Aim for a full range of motion; when you pull up, do so until your chin is above the bar, and keep your body in a slight forward arch to utilize your core effectively. During this entire movement, maintain a neutral head position by looking forward rather than upward. \n\nAs you get more comfortable with the pull-up, remember to engage your entire body. This involves squeezing your grip tightly on the bar to activate more muscle fibers up through your arms. It can help prevent injury and assist in efficient pulling. Lastly, wholeheartedly embrace the different variations of pull-ups, whether you’re using bands for assistance as a beginner or advancing to more difficult versions as you gain strength. This adaptability will ensure that everyone, regardless of experience or ability, can benefit from this effective exercise. \n\nHighlights:\n- Start with a \"dead hang\" position and maintain a proper grip for effective movement.\n- Achieve a full range of motion by pulling until your chin is above the bar.\n- Engage your entire body by squeezing the bar tight and explore different variations suitable for your level.'),(76335,55906,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76336,55906,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"welcome to the foundation video we\'re\",\n        \"start\": 0.06,\n        \"duration\": 4.56\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"going to have a look at a few examples\",\n        \"start\": 2.55,\n        \"duration\": 4.349\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"of doing the pull-up we\'re going to try\",\n        \"start\": 4.62,\n        \"duration\": 4.14\