nner\n\n198\n00:00:533,000 --> 00:01:475,000\nones and\n\n199\n00:00:534,000 --> 00:01:480,000\nhave a look at how we can use these\n\n200\n00:00:535,000 --> 00:01:480,000\nbands to enable us to an upper-body poll\n\n201\n00:00:547,000 --> 00:01:489,000\nyou\n\n'),(76339,55906,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(76340,55906,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APqCzRYsNlhf5pZATscF7Kp7pYamI\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730722253,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"Pull-ups are a fantastic exercise for building upper body strength, but they\'re not always easy for everyone. Whether you’re a beginner struggling to lift your body weight or someone looking to perfect your form, understanding the correct techniques and variations can significantly enhance your training. This tutorial will guide you through the essential steps to perform a pull-up effectively, ensuring you can engage the right muscle groups and work towards increasing your strength while enjoying the process.nnTo start, it’s important to understand the position of your body during a pull-up. Begin in what’s known as a \"dead hang\" position, where your muscles are relaxed and fully extended. This sets a solid foundation for the proper movement. Next, focus on your grip. An optimal grip involves holding the bar with your palms facing away from you, ensuring that your hands are positioned correctly to facilitate better pulling mechanics. Aim for a full range of motion; when you pull up, do so until your chin is above the bar, and keep your body in a slight forward arch to utilize your core effectively. During this entire movement, maintain a neutral head position by looking forward rather than upward. nnAs you get more comfortable with the pull-up, remember to engage your entire body. This involves squeezing your grip tightly on the bar to activate more muscle fibers up through your arms. It can help prevent injury and assist in efficient pulling. Lastly, wholeheartedly embrace the different variations of pull-ups, whether you’re using bands for assistance as a beginner or advancing to more difficult versions as you gain strength. This adaptability will ensure that everyone, regardless of experience or ability, can benefit from this effective exercise. nnHighlights:n- Start with a \"dead hang\" position and maintain a proper grip for effective movement.n- Achieve a full range of motion by pulling until your chin is above the bar.n- Engage your entire body by squeezing the bar tight and explore different variations suitable for your level.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 2008,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 384,\n            \"total_tokens\": 2392,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"EYkIIazuvISyG7q3M4zJCrIaRXp_NBfM7HIAye0mKek-1730722258-1.0.1.1-CI_ZrKotlxpfoRW3YbmyP7p.3q81Ggd5hYndgV9C0cRgY6GxeNBzi5kth3e73cyicXDVlk4hgqKS7jVDn.bC9A\",\n            \"expires\": 1730724058,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"8ufhmBXwboAFAC0wnh0oG_lzTEF_9Osu20LK2s.zX4M-1730722258884-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76341,55906,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76342,55906,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76343,55906,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76344,55906,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76345,55906,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76346,55907,'_thumbnail_id','14184'),(76347,55907,'video_id','r8luq1dWVaM'),(76348,55907,'video_type','tutorial'),(76349,55907,'order_position','3'),(76350,55907,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"nZQryin0Q19rx0fR4cyClQ4LeHc\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC42MTI4Njc2QjM1RjU1MjlG\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #04 - Beginner 1 Parkour Tutorial. [079]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Beginner) in Parkour - Beginner 1.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #04nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnLet\'s get started with our first beginner option, the banded pulldown. Pulling on, and stretching, a resistance band is one of the best and most scalable techniques for anyone to try.nnThe fact that this also enables you to do a nearly identical motion as the pull-up, for the entire range of motion, makes it one of the best options too.nnn### Pulling PositionnThe best position to do this exercise would be standing since it would closely replicate how you would be on a bar pullup. However, this would require the band to be tied up very high, so using your knees might be the only option.nnIf you are using your knees, try to still engage your abs and squeeze your glutes to align your hips correctly. Essentially, we want to be as close to the bodyweight pull-up position as we can possibly be.nnn### Scaling the difficulty up or downnThere are a few different ways (that I have used in the past) to adjust the difficulty of this exercise.nn- You can shorten or lengthen the band by wrapping it over the pull-up bar or the bar you are pulling on more or fewer times.n- Changing the thickness of the band by using a different one.n- Use multiple bands at the same time to increase the resistance.n- A combination of all of the above.nnn### Easier at the top and harder at the bottomnJust because the way the band works, you will always find the beginning part of the pull easier than at the end, with a gradual increase.nnThis is not the exact way that a bodyweight pull-up works since that will be usually harder at the start and end, with the middle section being a little easier. The reason for this is because the middle section is the part your arms would have had the most use and will be at their strongest.nnn### The accuracy of resistancenIf you wish to have a much more accurate reading of the amount of tension (and stress on your body) that the bands are giving you, then a simple hooked weighing scale can come in useful.nnYou can hook the scale onto the band and pull it down to the lowest point. Record the amount of weight that you are pulling as a way to gauge your progress.nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Strengthening}}{{Series:Pullups}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/r8luq1dWVaM/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/r8luq1dWVaM/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/r8luq1dWVaM/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/r8luq1dWVaM/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/r8luq1dWVaM/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMmrCVs_bOotQLjVdq5zGhT\",\"position\":3,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"r8luq1dWVaM\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":3}'),(76351,55907,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Pullups'),(76352,55907,'authId','Auth1'),(76353,55907,'searchId','Tutorials - Pullups'),(76354,55907,'filterId','none'),(76355,55907,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(76356,55907,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Pullups'),(76357,55907,'_edit_last','1'),(76358,55907,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you\'re looking to improve your pull-up game but find the traditional movement challenging, using resistance bands can be an excellent starting point. Bands not only assist with lifting your body weight but also allow you to practice the full range of motion, from a dead hang to the top position. This tutorial will guide you through using bands effectively, making pull-ups accessible for everyone, regardless of their strength level.\n\nTo get started, select a thin resistance band and loop it over a pull-up bar, adjusting its length by creating two loops. For added stability, insert a stick or bar through the bottom of the band and wrap it around twice. Kneel down to grip the bar overhead, starting in a dead hang position. From here, pull down, engaging your muscles through the full range, then release and repeat. If the movement feels too easy, shorten the band or switch to a thicker one to increase resistance. This scalable approach allows you to tailor the challenge according to your ability and ensures that you can work on your pull-up technique without the strain of lifting your entire body weight.\n\nWhile using resistance bands is a fantastic way to build strength, it\'s worth noting some of their limitations. Performing the exercise from a kneeling position can affect your core engagement and body alignment, so it\'s essential to be aware of your posture. Also, using bands requires some extra equipment, which may not always be accessible. Moreover, determining the exact amount of assistance from the bands can be tricky, as their elasticity affects the difficulty of the movement throughout its range. Nevertheless, this method remains one of the best ways for beginners to practice the pull-up and build strength progressively.\n\nTo recap: \n- Use a resistance band to assist with pull-ups, which allows for a full range of motion.\n- Adjust the band’s length or thickness to customize the difficulty level.\n- Be mindful of your posture and the need for extra equipment when incorporating bands into your workout.'),(76359,55907,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76360,55907,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"hey everyone welcome to the first\",\n        \"start\": 0.06,\n        \"duration\": 6.06\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"beginner variation of pull-up so what\",\n        \"start\": 2.52,\n        \"duration\": 6.539\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we\'re going to look at today is using\",\n        \"start\": 6.12,\n        \"duration\": 4.86\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"these bands so they\'re going to become\",\n        \"start\": 9.059,\n        \"duration\": 5.611\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"very very handy for us to do the full\",\n        \"start\": 10.98,\n        \"duration\": 4.949\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"range