8b7'),(76430,55908,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76431,55908,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76432,55909,'_thumbnail_id','14188'),(76433,55909,'video_id','2-20wwiLC-0'),(76434,55909,'video_type','tutorial'),(76435,55909,'order_position','5'),(76436,55909,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"dr5juqZm532izdZ2sCUmxSrtrlg\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC4zRDBDOEZDOUM0MDY5NEEz\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #06 - Beginner 3 Parkour Tutorial. [081]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Beginner) in Parkour - Beginner 3.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #06nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnThe negative is a method of reversing the movement to make the exercise easier. This allows you to practice the mechanics of the movement and start to get used to putting your body in the right positions.nnIt\'s a tool that does have it\'s downfalls, however. In this episode, we will cover the pros and cons of using the negative.nnn### Reversing the movementnRemember that as soon as you stop doing any pulling, then you will not become stronger in a pull. You will be resisting gravity and therefore will use different muscles to achieve this. (Namely your pecs and inner bicep)nnn### Using the BandsnDon\'t forget that you can also use the mobility bands to help with the negative too. This means that you will be able to make this technique more scalable with easier and harder versions.nnn### Do not JoltnAn important thing to remember with negatives is that you drop hard into the bottom hang you can do damage to your arms and chest.nnThe connective tissue (tendons) connects your muscles (at each end) to your skeleton. The hard jolt into the dead-hang will pull your muscles and tendons to their longest length. With a lot of force, this can strain the muscle or tendon. So be careful!n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Strengthening}}{{Series:Pullups}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2-20wwiLC-0/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2-20wwiLC-0/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2-20wwiLC-0/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2-20wwiLC-0/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2-20wwiLC-0/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMmrCVs_bOotQLjVdq5zGhT\",\"position\":5,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"2-20wwiLC-0\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":5}'),(76437,55909,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Pullups'),(76438,55909,'authId','Auth1'),(76439,55909,'searchId','Tutorials - Pullups'),(76440,55909,'filterId','none'),(76441,55909,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(76442,55909,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Pullups'),(76443,55909,'_edit_last','1'),(76444,55909,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Understanding the mechanics of motion in exercises like the pull-up can enhance your workout efficiency and effectiveness. It’s essential to grasp how your body should move through each phase of the exercise. In a pull-up, for instance, the movement starts from a dead hang position at the bottom and transitions to a full pull-up position. Focusing on these mechanics ensures that you\'re not only strong enough to pull yourself up, but also performing the movement correctly to avoid injury.\n\nOne effective way to practice the mechanics of a pull-up is through a technique called a \"negative.\" Instead of starting from the bottom, you begin at the top of the motion and slowly lower yourself down. This reverse action allows gravity to assist you, making it easier to work on the mechanics without the full strength required for a regular pull-up. To get started, you can use a wall to jump into the top position or a step ladder. Once there, take your time as you resist the fall, controlling your descent until you reach a dead hang. This method emphasizes the essential movement pattern without needing additional equipment, making it accessible to anyone.\n\nWhile negatives are a great way to get familiar with the body mechanics involved in a pull-up, they do have some limitations. They are not scalable, meaning once you’re accustomed to the negative, there are fewer options for adjusting difficulty. Furthermore, since you’re not actually pulling, the exercise alone may not build enough strength to progress to a full pull-up. To complement your training, consider using resistance bands when practicing negatives. This can help make the exercise scalable, allowing for different levels of support as you gain strength. In summary, mastering the mechanics of pull-ups through negatives and potentially incorporating bands can greatly benefit your fitness routine.\n\n- Practicing the motion of a pull-up through negatives allows for improved mechanics and reduces injury risk.\n- Starting from the top position during negatives helps control the descent and eases the strength demands.\n- Incorporating resistance bands can enhance the scalability and effectiveness of your negative practice.'),(76445,55909,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76446,55909,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so a term that i