\'re\n\n134\n00:00:386,000 --> 00:01:330,000\nstill not doing the pulling and it means\n\n135\n00:00:389,000 --> 00:01:333,000\nthat you\'re still only working the\n\n136\n00:00:391,000 --> 00:01:335,000\nmechanics\n\n137\n00:00:393,000 --> 00:01:336,000\nso let\'s use the band and we\'re going to\n\n138\n00:00:395,000 --> 00:01:341,000\nstart from the top again\n\n139\n00:00:396,000 --> 00:01:348,000\nfrom here and you can slowly lower\n\n140\n00:00:401,000 --> 00:01:351,000\nyourself to the dead hang position so\n\n141\n00:00:408,000 --> 00:01:355,000\nnow using the band and the negative\n\n142\n00:00:412,000 --> 00:01:358,000\ntogether it means that it is a very\n\n143\n00:00:415,000 --> 00:01:359,000\nscalable exercise we can change the\n\n144\n00:00:418,000 --> 00:01:363,000\nlength of the band the type of band and\n\n145\n00:00:420,000 --> 00:01:365,000\ngo in the negative position however\n\n146\n00:00:423,000 --> 00:01:369,000\nremember you are not going to be doing\n\n147\n00:00:426,000 --> 00:01:370,000\nany pulling with this exercise\n\n148\n00:00:437,000 --> 00:01:379,000\nyou\n\n'),(76449,55909,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(76450,55909,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APq3rwLtgfyH9qvXlvYLsAnCPf1iQ\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730721687,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"Understanding the mechanics of motion in exercises like the pull-up can enhance your workout efficiency and effectiveness. It’s essential to grasp how your body should move through each phase of the exercise. In a pull-up, for instance, the movement starts from a dead hang position at the bottom and transitions to a full pull-up position. Focusing on these mechanics ensures that you\'re not only strong enough to pull yourself up, but also performing the movement correctly to avoid injury.nnOne effective way to practice the mechanics of a pull-up is through a technique called a \"negative.\" Instead of starting from the bottom, you begin at the top of the motion and slowly lower yourself down. This reverse action allows gravity to assist you, making it easier to work on the mechanics without the full strength required for a regular pull-up. To get started, you can use a wall to jump into the top position or a step ladder. Once there, take your time as you resist the fall, controlling your descent until you reach a dead hang. This method emphasizes the essential movement pattern without needing additional equipment, making it accessible to anyone.nnWhile negatives are a great way to get familiar with the body mechanics involved in a pull-up, they do have some limitations. They are not scalable, meaning once you’re accustomed to the negative, there are fewer options for adjusting difficulty. Furthermore, since you’re not actually pulling, the exercise alone may not build enough strength to progress to a full pull-up. To complement your training, consider using resistance bands when practicing negatives. This can help make the exercise scalable, allowing for different levels of support as you gain strength. In summary, mastering the mechanics of pull-ups through negatives and potentially incorporating bands can greatly benefit your fitness routine.nn- Practicing the motion of a pull-up through negatives allows for improved mechanics and reduces injury risk.n- Starting from the top position during negatives helps control the descent and eases the strength demands.n- Incorporating resistance bands can enhance the scalability and effectiveness of your negative practice.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1472,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 401,\n            \"total_tokens\": 1873,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"srfFPZ_P1mNjVsQc1ORdu_613DokF4BDlPB4lssVne0-1730721693-1.0.1.1-tUSXAMhE1LjrNf0ZfPTmAFyJIf_hteMqgHUATLEweMvRk2sp2Z04VifxsaCO8d4v.2KWSi6k5hkEZ2vqodydQw\",\n            \"expires\": 1730723493,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"jFFm1DsCZ5Sc9u2spN1QEzSgQXxAo.ndHh2g5ryjW3A-1730721693930-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76451,55909,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76452,55909,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76453,55909,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76454,55909,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76455,55909,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76456,55910,'_thumbnail_id','14190'),(76457,55910,'video_id','MVueVEaxwVg'),(76458,55910,'video_type','tutorial'),(76459,55910,'order_position','6'),(76460,55910,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"fqSSuQyws1xhk-TTpjUHQSL7WIc\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC41QUZGQTY5OTE4QTREQUU4\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #07 - Beginner 4 Parkour Tutorial. [082]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Beginner) in Parkour - Beginner 4.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #07nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnChanging the angle of your body with your feet touching the floor is also an easy way to make the pulling action easier or harder.nnHaving some gymnastics rings available will make this exercise much easier, but can equally be performed outside, under a railing too.nnn### Body AnglenBy changing the angle of your body, with your feet on the floor, allows you to increase the amount of bodyweight you are placing onto your arms and rings.nnThe harder you want to make the exercise, the more you should be level with the floor.nnMathematically working out the exact load of the exercise is going to be difficult because of the angle of your body, the angle of the rings, bodyweight, etc... would have to be calculated to get an accurate measurement. This makes gauging progress a little more tricky.nnn### Body PositionnAs straight as an arrow.  No bending at the hips, spine, knees or anything else.nnYou\'ll find you will need to squeeze those glutes together, as well as your quads and abs. Actually, pretty much everything in your body will be contracted as hard as they can...nnn### Pulling AnglenOne of the parts of this exercise that is slightly different is that you will be pulling forward, not upwards.nnThis may seem like a minor detail, but it means that your major joints are in a different position and the muscles that are being used to pull are slightly different too.nnIt\'s still a great pulling-action training method, but I would suggest that the ring rows be used in conjunction with another exercise that works the correct technique and mechanics like the banded-pullup.nnn### InstabilitynGetting all of those little stabilising muscles to do some work by keeping the rings still will work wonders for you.nnYou are essentially getting more muscles involved and therefore they are are getting some training in and will become stronger over time.nnn### RingsnHead over to the prerequisite episode for a list of links to reputable sources of gymnastics rings.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588