3eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #08nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnIt sounds like a name for a mathematical shape, but isometrics simply means to train without moving your body.nnRemaining still in a physically hard position can also be used to work your muscles. In this episode, we will use this idea on the negative pull-up.nnn### Easy to HardnWe can make this exercise as easy or hard as we like by changing a few different things.nnFirst, the number of positions we repeat the hold. We can start with a single hold and increase it as much as we like.nnSecond, the length of time we spend in a hold. The longer the hold, the harder the exercise will be.nnn### ROM But not PullingnWith isometric training, we are not actually doing any pulling or working any mechanics again. We are using our stabilising muscles to hold onto the bar only.nnHowever, we can really work the Range of Motion a lot. We can spend more time in those positions we ourselves weakest in.nnn### Endurance over StrengthnWithout going into the details yet (we\'ll cover it in the programming episodes), we are not really doing much strength training with isometrics. We are doing more endurance work instead.nnThis is what you would call more of a conditioning exercise. Conditioning is a way of repeating the actual thing you want to get better at.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://