th\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1LuZAO-P714/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1LuZAO-P714/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1LuZAO-P714/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMmrCVs_bOotQLjVdq5zGhT\",\"position\":7,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"1LuZAO-P714\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":7}'),(76485,55911,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Pullups'),(76486,55911,'authId','Auth1'),(76487,55911,'searchId','Tutorials - Pullups'),(76488,55911,'filterId','none'),(76489,55911,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(76490,55911,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Pullups'),(76491,55911,'_edit_last','1'),(76492,55911,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Isometric training can be an effective way to enhance your pull-up performance, especially if you\'re looking to build endurance and stability. This tutorial dives into isometric exercises specifically focused on the pull-up, a popular upper body strength movement. By engaging in these holds, you can target specific positions along the pull-up path, helping you to develop muscle endurance and better manage lactic acid buildup during workouts. Whether you’re just starting or looking to reinforce your pull-up routine, this method is both adaptable and efficient.\n\nTo begin your isometric training, find a sturdy pull-up bar and decide on specific positions to hold. Start with the bottom of the pull-up in a dead hang—grip the bar tightly and hang there for as long as you can. After you\'ve gotten comfortable, move to the middle position; you can use a box or a step if needed. For these holds, focus on squeezing your muscles and maintaining stability. You can then progress to the top position of the pull-up, holding for set intervals. Aim to stay in each position for around 10 seconds initially, and feel free to mix in intervals from various spots along the pull-up\'s path to develop endurance over time. Remember, the duration and the position you choose can be adjusted based on your comfort level.\n\nIn summary, isometric training for pull-ups is a fantastic way to boost your muscular endurance without solely focusing on strength. By holding different positions, you can reinforce specific muscle fibers crucial for pull-ups while also acclimating your body to lactic acid buildup, which is particularly beneficial for activities like parkour. Although this technique might not significantly enhance your pulling strength on its own, it can serve as a valuable complement to your overall training regime, making it easier to tackle those challenging pull-ups in the long run.\n\nHighlights:\n- Start by practicing dead hangs to build foundational grip strength.\n- Vary your hold durations and positions to enhance muscular endurance.\n- Use isometric training as a supplement to your regular strength training for pull-ups.'),(76493,55911,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76494,55911,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"in this episode beginner option number\",\n        \"start\": 0.03,\n        \"duration\": 4.59\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"five we\'re gonna have a look at some\",\n        \"start\": 2.52,\n        \"duration\": 5.19\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"pull-up isometrics so the idea with the\",\n        \"start\": 4.62,\n        \"duration\": 5.729\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"isometric training is that we\'re going\",\n        \"start\": 7.71,\n        \"duration\": 6.509\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"to pick a spot down the path of the\",\n        \"start\": 10.349,\n        \"duration\": 6.421\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"pull-up so you can start at the top\",\n        \"start\": 14.219,\n      