me. Remember, the duration and the position you choose can be adjusted based on your comfort level.nnIn summary, isometric training for pull-ups is a fantastic way to boost your muscular endurance without solely focusing on strength. By holding different positions, you can reinforce specific muscle fibers crucial for pull-ups while also acclimating your body to lactic acid buildup, which is particularly beneficial for activities like parkour. Although this technique might not significantly enhance your pulling strength on its own, it can serve as a valuable complement to your overall training regime, making it easier to tackle those challenging pull-ups in the long run.nnHighlights:n- Start by practicing dead hangs to build foundational grip strength.n- Vary your hold durations and positions to enhance muscular endurance.n- Use isometric training as a supplement to your regular strength training for pull-ups.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1536,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 403,\n            \"total_tokens\": 1939,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"RjoFgi4RIv8Tga.eDxpDA9Db25gOFxTy8AKBLvQyFuk-1730721707-1.0.1.1-KDOCUaU6oF5wiNkzinropuHPomjdp1VuXUKjEu4heZYD_qfd7LO4BWd3YmxFL2m3Pg72O40YvSwaPF.1t4BhuA\",\n            \"expires\": 1730723507,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"k0LNpUfZs8gTAhFMXp8LzxNYxuaR26ZSpQXp66X9kq4-1730721707673-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76499,55911,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76500,55911,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76501,55911,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76502,55911,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76503,55911,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76504,55912,'_thumbnail_id','14194'),(76505,55912,'video_id','KLQeH9zx3UM'),(76506,55912,'video_type','tutorial'),(76507,55912,'order_position','8'),(76508,55912,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"MUf2WJirpd0GKGs8hoOOUH4F22I\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC44Mjc5REFBRUE2MTdFRDU0\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #09 - Intermediate 1 Parkour Tutorial. [084]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Beginner) in Parkour - Intermediate 1.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #09nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnSo, here we are with the humble body-weight pull-up! In this episode, we will add more detail to the things covered in the fundamentals video.nnn### Type of trainingnThe bodyweight pull-up is arguably one of the oldest and most used types of training in the world. What makes this so good is that it can be used in many, many different ways depending on the type of training you want to do.nnThe idea is that changing the volume & intensity of the training (number of repetitions or weight/stress of the repetitions) allows us to obtain different results.nnOn one end of the scale, doing low repetitions at a very high stress less (heavy) allows us to build strength much better. However, at the other end, doing very high repetitions at low stress (light) focuses much more on endurance.nnn### Not FunctionalnWhat does \'functional\' mean? Well, it means to be able to perform a function. In the loosest of terms, a pull-up DOES allow you to perform the function of a pull-up. However, how useful is that in the real world?nnI believe that when the term \'functional\' is being used, it actually means to be able to do a \'Real-world useful Function\'. Of which, the pull-up is not because it doesn\'t really allow you to get over/on to the thing you\'re pulling up on. Just up to your chest.nnThis is why the muscle-up or climb-up is considered a real functional movement since performing it allows you to get on or over the bar.  This is not to say that the pull-up is not useful, far from it, but in my opinion it shouldn\'t be considered \'functional\'.nnThe next time someone says they do \'Functional\' training, think about what the function is and how useful it is.nnn### Full Body TrainingnAll-body training is much more useful than isolated muscle-group training. The body is built to be used as a complete unit, so the more muscles you get involved, the better.nnMake sure you add other pull-motion training in that works your entire body too. For instance, swinging, climbing, bouldering, parkour, etc...nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:intermediate}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Strengthening}}{{Series:Pullups}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{