       \"created\": 1730722321,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"Pull-ups are a fundamental exercise for building upper body strength, but many people struggle to achieve the full range of motion required for optimal effectiveness. This tutorial addresses an advanced technique to help you master true full range pull-ups, emphasizing the importance of effectively engaging your muscles from the bottom of the movement to a higher point where your forearms become parallel to the ground. By making this transition, you’ll not only enhance your pulling strength but also prepare yourself for more complex movements like muscle-ups and climb-ups.nnTo start, focus on how to pull yourself higher by incorporating speed and a slight curve around the bar. Begin from a dead hang position and use a bit of momentum to propel your chest forward, rounding your back to lift yourself up. Instead of stopping your upward motion when your chin passes the bar, aim to lift your chest until your forearms reach parallel to the ground. This requires practicing the full range of motion, making sure that you’re not just relying on your sheer strength. Be cautious about kipping, as it can lead to poor habits by using elasticity instead of muscle strength. Keep your form clean and focus on engaging your muscles throughout the entire movement, from the dead hang to the top.nnRemember, mastering this technique is a journey and might feel challenging at first, especially if you\'re used to only doing partial pull-ups. However, the benefits of developing a true full range of motion will become evident as you progress, leading to greater power and speed in your pull-ups. Establishing a solid foundation now will pave the way for more advanced movements later on, solidifying your overall functional fitness. So, be patient and practice consistently, and you’ll see marked improvements in no time!nnHighlights:n- Focus on achieving a full range of motion by pulling up until your forearms are parallel to the ground.n- Incorporate slight momentum and a rounding motion to lift your chest higher rather than just relying on chin-ups.n- Practice consistently and avoid kipping to ensure you\'re building strength effectively for future more complex movements.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1329,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 404,\n            \"total_tokens\": 1733,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"ubnIQ3WJSHaK3RKKrp95OqptnOaKe18a_wZjmhOtRCU-1730722326-1.0.1.1-qXwIzd01zGrfYxjrb4RtR5lEfVMIGphyiyb_D5CSbemX3gTiSqnT3y8x0C0RbJCZhx2UQmkDgwaQmzotD_9NSg\",\n            \"expires\": 1730724126,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"6SxCZd.LZrZiv.K9jFr2X2QJtwQ1s80XFs3JnHHpBc4-1730722326728-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76595,55915,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76596,55915,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76597,55915,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76598,55915,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76599,55915,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76600,55916,'_thumbnail_id','14202'),(76601,55916,'video_id','KJYDAt3o5fY'),(76602,55916,'video_type','tutorial'),(76603,55916,'order_position','12'),(76604,55916,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"XH0kjcPhtnwmZowMm6X60KmT8kg\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC43MTI1NDIwOTMwQjIxMzNG\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #13 - Advanced 1 Parkour Tutorial. [088]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Intermediate) in Parkour - Advanced 1.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #13nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnAre bodyweight pull-ups getting a little too easy for you now? Time to start increasing the stress on your arms by adding additional weight.nnUsing a weight belt and weight plates are going to be the go-to method for keeping those strength increases going.nnn### What to use.nThe prerequisite video covered some options for the weight-belt and any standard weight plate should be able to have the chain threaded through the middle.nnTri-grip plates are handy for multiple holes in the plates, but kettlebells also work just as well.nnn### Scalability and type of training.nSince weight plates come in a very wide range of sizes and amounts, it allows you to have very fine control over how much weight you wish to add on.nnHaving control over this weight means that you can also change the type of training depending on the number of reps and sets that the weight allows you to do.nnn### Weight VestsnThe weight-vest is a good tool to use for certain types of training. Cardiovascular and endurance training benefit a lot from weight vests. Perhaps you also want to put pressure on the lungs a bit and make it harder to suck in oxygen. This makes the lungs work harder too.nnHowever, using weight vests for the pull-up isn\'t the best choice.nnIt\'s hard to change the amount of weight precisely since the vests only come in one or two sizes, and the other problem is that it adds bulk to your chest, which makes it more difficult and unnatural to try to go past the bar to complete that full-range-of-motion.nnThey do look cool though...nnn### For the Beginners toonThe weight belt and weight plates are NOT just for people who want to add more weight on to their current bodyweight.nnIf you were using the assistance bands, let\'s say you were using the blue band, and it was becoming too easy, but the thinner red band was too hard, you can use the weight belt to make a half-way step (or more) between the two.nnFor instance, you could use the blue band and then make it a little harder by going up in 1.5kg increments with the weight belt until you are doing roughly the same as if you had no weight and using the red band...nnYou\'ve got to love the versatility of those tools.nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:advanced}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Strengthening}}{{Series:Pullups}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KJYDAt3o5fY/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KJYDAt3o5fY/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KJYDAt3o5fY/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KJYDAt3o5fY/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KJYDAt3o5fY/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMmrCVs_bOotQLjVdq5zGhT\",\"position\":12,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"KJYDAt3o5fY\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":12}'),(76605,55916,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Pullups'),(76606,55916,'authId','Auth1'),(76607,55916,'searchId','Tutorials - Pullups'),(76608,55916,'filterId','none'),(76609,55916,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(76610,55916,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Pullups'),(76611,55916,'_edit_last','1'),(76612,55916,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Weighted pull-ups are an excellent way to enhance your strength training regimen by adding extra resistance to an exercise you may already be comfortable with. If you’ve mastered bodyweight pull-ups and are looking to challenge yourself further, incorporating a weight belt can significantly amplify the effectiveness of your workout. In this tutorial, we\'ll go through the step-by-step process of how to set up a weight belt for your pull-ups, encouraging you to adapt and grow stronger as you tackle increasing weight.\n\nTo get started, you will first need a weight belt designed for pull-ups. Begin by putting on the belt and threading the chain through the front hoop. Next, choose your desired weight. For instance, a 1.25 kg plate is a great starting point, and you can adjust accordingly based on your fitness level. Attach the weight to the chain, ensuring that the clip faces away from your body to avoid snagging on your clothing. Once secured, you are ready to perform your pull-ups! Remember to maintain proper form: hang from the bar in a dead position, pull up with as much control as possible, and return to the starting position before attempting the next repetition. You can gradually increase the weight as you get stronger, utilizing various plate sizes or even kettlebells for variety.\n\nIn conclusion, using a weight belt for pull-ups not only allows for scalable training but also enhances the versatility of your workouts—whether you’re focusing on strength, endurance, or hypertrophy. While there may be some challenges, like managing momentum when using larger weights, the benefits of adding weight are significant. You can start training with lighter weights and work your way up, making this method suitable for not only advanced athletes but also beginners looking to push their limits. The key takeaway is that, with the right equipment and approach, weighted pull-ups can be a phenomenal addition to your strength training routine.\n\nHighlights:\n- Start by securely attaching a weight belt and choosing your desired weight for pull-ups.\n- Maintain proper form by starting from a dead hang and pulling up with control.\n- Incrementally increase your weight as you gain strength, ensuring the workout remains challenging.'),(76613,55916,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76614,55916,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"this is going to be the first option for\",\n        \"start\": 0.03,\n        \"duration\": 4.499\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the advanced group and we\'re going to be\",\n        \"start\": 2.19,\n        \"duration\": 5.58\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"looking at weighted pull-ups today so\",\n        \"start\": 4.529,\n        \"duration\": 6.181\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"with this option we are now going to\",\n        \"start\": 7.77,\n        \"duration\": 5.4\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"have a look at weighting ourselves so\",\n        \"start\": 10.71,\n        \"duration\": 5.37\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"putting extra weight onto our body to\",\n        \"start\": 13.17,\n        \"duration\": 5.4\n    },\n    {\n 