ult.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMmrCVs_bOotQLjVdq5zGhT\",\"position\":19,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"Vgr0qZP5f0Y\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":19}'),(76773,55923,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Pullups'),(76774,55923,'authId','Auth1'),(76775,55923,'searchId','Tutorials - Pullups'),(76776,55923,'filterId','none'),(76777,55923,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(76778,55923,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Pullups'),(76779,55923,'_edit_last','1'),(76780,55923,'video_transcript_chatgpt',''),(76781,55923,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76782,55923,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76783,55923,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76784,55923,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76785,55923,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76786,55924,'_thumbnail_id','14218'),(76787,55924,'video_id','WWmz6Mzxan8'),(76788,55924,'video_type','tutorial'),(76789,55924,'order_position','20'),(76790,55924,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"8je59ZoTAY5BIzi_uqYKEs1fsec\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC4yMUQyQTQzMjRDNzMyQTMy\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #21 - Example 2 Parkour Tutorial. [096]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Beginner) in Parkour - Example 2.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #21nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnWe know that strength is still the goal of this program example, so we need to keep on the \'anaerobic\' (low rep / high weight) type training.nnRemember that \'Intermediate\' is just a word and not a rank of your ability or strength. I\'m just using it to order the strength-levels required in these examples.nnn### Joint MobilitynVery similar to the first example program. For the joint mobility, let\'s do all the important joints we will be using. Wrists, Elbows, Shoulder, Spine, Hips. We can follow this with 5 minutes with a foam roller.nnn### WarmupnSame as the beginner version, 10-minutes of QM (Quadrupedal movement).nnHowever, we will ALSO add in the Bicep and Tricep openers to help warm up the maximum range of motion for the pulling. It will also get us to use the correct muscle groups and torque (External Rotation) for the pull.nnSee the previous episode for videos and details on these warmup techniques and click on the link below for the StrongFit Youtube channel.nnn### Warmup Specificn2 sets of 2 reps of pull-ups with the Red band. Focus on perfect mechanics and pulling to the absolute top range of the motion.nnn### The Work SetsnDoing unassisted bodyweight pull-ups is the goal here. Let\'s do 3 sets of 5 reps.nnRemember, a full range of motion with no swinging.nnn### CooldownnAfter the work-sets, you can add some extra movement practice or train some assistance exercises to improve similar muscle groups or areas of weakness.nnFinally, make sure you stretch. This will be addressed to the \'Recovery\' videos .n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/