erformance in that anaerobic strength zone, where work is done at 80-100% of the practitioner’s maximum effort.nnIn conclusion, advanced strength training demands a systematic approach, balancing strength gains with precise technique. By emphasizing small adjustments and thoughtful progression, it’s possible to continue growing stronger while mastering the mechanics of each exercise. Remember, just because weight increases are subtler doesn’t mean workouts should become less challenging; rather, they should focus on perfecting every detail for long-lasting functional strength.nn- Focus on form and technique to maximize strength gains in advanced training.n- Include a comprehensive warm-up that targets joint mobility and specific muscle groups.n- Use lower rep ranges (e.g., 4 reps) with increased weights to optimize anaerobic strength without sacrificing form.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1066,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 365,\n            \"total_tokens\": 1431,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"Bq4RWBTfBPib_sH6vQbafIsfCKj1otrrr8_aR8mM764-1730722221-1.0.1.1-b2lf3V_e9yLGcQfS316l5TZPaJxxsvTzsZ1Ug3BZTjG1VU1cjcD.OOx..fildA6J4rBhVfncT5pr3CuRWWLIYQ\",\n            \"expires\": 1730724021,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"AUL1CwhVcwR8lXomX_OzKHdofny9vj30d8YMyMUFTZQ-1730722221697-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76829,55925,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76830,55925,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76831,55925,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76832,55925,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76833,55925,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76834,55926,'_thumbnail_id','14222'),(76835,55926,'video_id','Bwi-7-4ly_0'),(76836,55926,'video_type','tutorial'),(76837,55926,'order_position','22'),(76838,55926,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"aY6MgLhU-Z7CGImF44c7-FB_W7w\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC5EQUE1NTFDRjcwMDg0NEMz\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #23 - Example 4 Parkour Tutorial. [098]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Intermediate) in Parkour - Example 4.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #23nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnSo this one is a little different from the strength training we\'ve been doing. Instead, we\'re going to change our goal to some muscular endurance.nnWhat is muscular endurance? Well, it\'s more focused on the amount of time your muscles can keep going doing a particular thing.nnTo clarify, regular \'endurance\' is what most people think as \'cardiovascular endurance\'. Which is focused on your \'cardio\' systems of oxygen, blood, and organs.nnn### WarmupnAs always, make sure you do your joint mobility and general warmup. Using the bicep/tricep openers and route work would be a great way to start.nnThe specific warm-up will be:nn2 sets of 4 reps of an easy progression for you. You should know by now what that could be.nnn### Work sets with More reps and less weightnWe are going to up the amount of volume (sets * reps * weight), but lowering the intensity, you will be doing for this program.nn5 sets of 8-10 reps of a weight you can do 8-10 reps of.nnn### Limiting RestnBecause we are now focusing on how long the muscles can go one for more, we are going to stop them from recovering completely. Therefore the amount of rest you have between each set will be 3-4 minutes.nnn### Lactic AcidnThat heavy, thick feeling in your muscle that stops you from pulling any more is a buildup of lactate and the acidity of your muscle cells.nnFor more information, check out this short, but interesting article:nnn### The benefitsnSo why do this type of training? Muscular endurance is a fundamental training method to become more functional and more \'endurant\'.nnWhen you need to do parkour for one reason or another, muscular endurance training would have made that move second nature to your body. That\'s why we do rep, after rep, after rep. Build up that muscle memory and endurance.n n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:advanced}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Strengthening}}{{Series:Pullups}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Bwi-7-4ly_0/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Bwi-7-4ly_0/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Bwi-7-4ly_0/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Bwi-7-4ly_0/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Bwi-7-4ly_0/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMmrCVs_bOotQLjVdq5zGhT\",\"position\":22,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"Bwi-7-4ly_0\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":22}'),(76839,55926,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Pullups'),(76840,55926,'authId','Auth1'),(76841,55926,'searchId','Tutorials - Pullups'),(76842,55926,'filterId','none'),(76843,55926,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(76844,55926,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Pullups'),(76845,55926,'_edit_last','1'),(76846,55926,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Muscular endurance training focuses on increasing your ability to perform repeated movements over time, rather than solely increasing strength. This type of training is particularly useful for activities that require sustained physical exertion, like parkour or other dynamic sports. By emphasizing higher repetitions with lower weights, you build the stamina your muscles need to excel in prolonged activities. In this tutorial, we’ll break down how to effectively incorporate muscular endurance training into your routine, ensuring you get the most out of each workout.\n\nThe key to muscular endurance lies in adjusting your reps and sets. Start with a proper warm-up that includes two sets of four repetitions to prepare your muscles. For your main workout, aim for about five sets of eight to ten repetitions. This totals to around 50 repetitions for your work sets, so be sure to lower the weight to accommodate this higher volume. A critical aspect of this training is managing your rest periods. Instead of resting fully between sets like in strength training, limit your rest time to about three to four minutes. This keeps your heart rate elevated and enhances muscular endurance, making each set feel a bit more challenging. To further intensify your workout, consider adding an additional exercise targeting different muscle groups during your rest, such as bodyweight squats or lunges. \n\nIn summary, muscular endurance training is all about higher volumes and shared recovery. The fundamental takeaway is that by focusing on more repetitions with less weight and shorter rest periods, you condition your muscles to work harder for longer durations. This kind of training not only improves your performance in endurance-based activities but also reinforces proper movement techniques, making them second nature in applications like parkour. By consistently practicing these strategies, you will enhance your physical capabilities and make your activities feel easier and more natural.\n\nKey takeaways: \n- Focus on 8-10 reps for 5 sets with reduced weight to enhance muscular endurance.\n- Limit rest periods to 3-4 minutes to maintain intensity and challenge your muscles.\n- Incorporate different exercises during rest to elevate your training and build functional strength.'),(76847,55926,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(76848,55926,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"welcome to example number four we\'re\",\n        \"start\": 0.06,\n        \"duration\": 4.83\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"going to be looking at some muscular\",\n        \"start\": 2.429,\n        \"duration\": 5.1\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"endurance rather than strength training\",\n        \"start\": 4.89,\n        \"duration\": 4.47\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"and we\'re going to have a look at what\",\n        \"start\": 7.529,\n        \"duration\": 4.921\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"those sets and reps look like the\",\n        \"start\": 9.36,\n        \"duration\": 4.5\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"difference between muscular endurance\",\n        