e, typically one minute. After this minute of high-intensity work, you’ll rest for one minute before repeating. This cycle can be done for as long as you like—20 minutes, for instance—with the goal of maximizing the number of high-quality repetitions you can perform, while gradually increasing the overall volume in future sessions.nnBy consistently tracking the total number of repetitions you complete, you can set tangible goals for your endurance training. For instance, if you manage 200 repetitions in one session, aim for 201 the next time. This progressive approach not only helps you build your endurance but also allows you to see measurable improvements over time. Incorporating endurance training into your routine will facilitate better performance in activities like parkour, where being able to handle oxygen deprivation and lactic acid buildup is vital for success. Remember, the goal here is to enhance your ability to perform for longer periods, making endurance training an invaluable tool for any serious athlete.nn- Focus on light weights and high repetitions to build endurance.n- Use the AMRAP format for structured, timed endurance workouts.n- Track your repetitions to set progressive goals and improve stamina over time.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1270,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 426,\n            \"total_tokens\": 1696,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"cCCwlmFKSyOYm0_XpIqvZ76S.RFmbdDoTqGfru1VkmM-1730722237-1.0.1.1-4Y0siSb.AtP1EF3IwiRmxYTkGbpZWjwtpGopLRZ_5Cws2PXLSSyTz6.jMcOMsuHuTyG.RXycOaJngKks1gH_6w\",\n            \"expires\": 1730724037,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"C7goUJCnJsA3N7CH1Q0scWnVWsCO4ejTyGUoS7CGWWY-1730722237791-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76877,55927,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76878,55927,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76879,55927,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76880,55927,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76881,55927,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76882,55928,'_thumbnail_id','14226'),(76883,55928,'video_id','lqn7WgQlBWM'),(76884,55928,'video_type','tutorial'),(76885,55928,'order_position','24'),(76886,55928,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"mCcNAZT6vUTBPQJEmTmuAG131JY\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC4zMDg5MkQ5MEVDMEM1NTg2\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #25 - Example 6 Parkour Tutorial. [100]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Intermediate) in Parkour - Example 6.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #25nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nn\'Power\' is one of those words that gets abused a little bit... Let\'s clear up the confusion and talk about what it really means.nnOnce we understand what power is and how beneficial it is to have it, lets apply it to a training plan and get working towards having some!nnn### What is powernHere\'s the simple answer... Power is strength + speed. Fast strength. It\'s using all your strength at the absolute fastest speed you can.nnThink about your biggest long jump. You have to push as hard as you can (with all your strength), as fast as you can (speed) to go the furthest distance as you can. That\'s power.nnYou can develop power in three ways...nnGet stronger through strength training.nIncrease you speed with speed training.nBuild both strength and speed at the same time with power training.nnn### The double tapnThe double tap (and \'dyno\' - which uses the feet as well) is about being explosive as possible and using as much power as you can.nnThe idea is to hang on a lower bar/ledge/wall/edge and pull as hard as you can so you transition to a higher level hand hold.nnDouble-taps are very useful for reaching positions that are further than an arms-length away.nnn### WarmupnA warning here. Make sure you thoroughly warm-up properly. You will be doing very dynamic movements with your maximum strength, fast. This is the exact situation which gives the most injuries if not prepared.nnEnsure you do a lot of warm-up on the arms and upper body as well as a full-range-of-motion type of warm-up.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping 