nthey\'ve worked really really really hard\n\n202\n00:00:507,000 --> 00:01:452,000\nthat works you know 110 percent and but\n\n203\n00:00:511,000 --> 00:01:454,000\nthey still don\'t make it so they have to\n\n204\n00:00:512,000 --> 00:01:457,000\nget they have to do a consequence again\n\n205\n00:00:514,000 --> 00:01:458,000\ndepending on the person that can be that\n\n206\n00:00:518,000 --> 00:01:461,000\nthat can affect them as well so you have\n\n207\n00:00:519,000 --> 00:01:463,000\nto be a little bit careful with\n\n208\n00:00:521,000 --> 00:01:467,000\nconsequences and rewards but they can\n\n209\n00:00:523,000 --> 00:01:471,000\nstill be fun if perhaps something that I\n\n210\n00:00:527,000 --> 00:01:474,000\ndo is I\'ll say that if if you don\'t\n\n211\n00:00:532,000 --> 00:01:474,000\nmanage as a group perhaps if you don\'t\n\n212\n00:00:534,000 --> 00:01:477,000\nmanage to do\n\n213\n00:00:535,000 --> 00:01:480,000\nthe goal you\'re going to get extra work\n\n214\n00:00:537,000 --> 00:01:482,000\nbut so that this is going to motivate\n\n215\n00:00:540,000 --> 00:01:484,000\nthem to go towards the goal but when\n\n216\n00:00:543,000 --> 00:01:486,000\nthey get to their goal perhaps they\n\n217\n00:00:544,000 --> 00:01:489,000\ndon\'t do it and they have to do in\n\n218\n00:00:546,000 --> 00:01:491,000\nconsequence actually the consequence is\n\n219\n00:00:549,000 --> 00:01:494,000\nnothing it\'s like one other one pull-up\n\n220\n00:00:552,000 --> 00:01:495,000\nor something like that that it\'s very\n\n221\n00:00:555,000 --> 00:01:499,000\neasy for them so it\'s kind of like a\n\n222\n00:00:556,000 --> 00:01:502,000\nrelief that actually the consequence\n\n223\n00:00:559,000 --> 00:01:504,000\nisn\'t something that is horrible but\n\n224\n00:00:562,000 --> 00:01:507,000\nit\'s done its job to motivate them and\n\n225\n00:00:565,000 --> 00:01:511,000\nkeep them focused on that goal another\n\n226\n00:00:567,000 --> 00:01:515,000\nway is clear progression paths so if the\n\n227\n00:00:571,000 --> 00:01:516,000\nperson or students can see that where\n\n228\n00:00:575,000 --> 00:01:519,000\nthey are and they can see a clear\n\n229\n00:00:577,000 --> 00:01:523,000\nprogression of what stages they have to\n\n230\n00:00:580,000 --> 00:01:524,000\ngo through to get towards a target and a\n\n231\n00:00:583,000 --> 00:01:527,000\ngoal\n\n232\n00:00:584,000 --> 00:01:529,000\nif they can see that path then it\'s\n\n233\n00:00:588,000 --> 00:01:531,000\ngoing to motivate them more because\n\n234\n00:00:589,000 --> 00:01:534,000\nevery time they come back and see that\n\n235\n00:00:591,000 --> 00:01:537,000\npath and that progression then they know\n\n236\n00:00:594,000 --> 00:01:538,000\nokay I\'ve got it here\'s the next step\n\n237\n00:00:597,000 --> 00:01:539,000\nthat I\'ve got to take his the next step\n\n238\n00:00:599,000 --> 00:01:542,000\nthe next step and it\'s going to be a\n\n239\n00:00:600,000 --> 00:01:544,000\nlittle bit more motivating for them to\n\n240\n00:00:602,000 --> 00:01:547,000\nsee their progression bit by bit towards\n\n241\n00:00:605,000 --> 00:01:549,000\nthat end goal the last thing to touch on\n\n242\n00:00:607,000 --> 00:01:553,000\nis pact that with strength and\n\n243\n00:00:609,000 --> 00:01:556,000\nconditioning it actually takes quite a\n\n244\n00:00:613,000 --> 00:01:560,000\nlot of work and time to see differences\n\n245\n00:00:617,000 --> 00:01:563,000\nin strength and one session is not\n\n246\n00:00:621,000 --> 00:01:566,000\nreally going to see it much progression\n\n247\n00:00:623,000 --> 00:01:567,000\nat all unless you are doing you know\n\n248\n00:00:626,000 --> 00:01:570,000\nsome personal training and you see that\n\n249\n00:00:628,000 --> 00:01:572,000\nperson very often and you\'re with them\n\n250\n00:00:631,000 --> 00:01:574,000\nall the time and you can see their\n\n251\n00:00:632,000 --> 00:01:577,000\nprogram and you can see the little wins\n\n252\n00:00:634,000 --> 00:01:579,000\nand you can see the progression and it\n\n253\n00:00:637,000 --> 00:01:581,000\nyou know that way you can kind of see\n\n254\n00:00:639,000 --> 00:01:585,000\nand they can see okay you\'re getting\n\n255\n00:00:642,000 --> 00:01:587,000\nstronger but with big groups and when\n\n256\n00:00:646,000 --> 00:01:590,000\nyou see a lot of different people and\n\n257\n00:00:648,000 --> 00:01:595,000\nthey changes a lot it\'s going to be hard\n\n258\n00:00:650,000 --> 00:01:596,000\nto kind of keep track of any strength\n\n259\n00:00:655,000 --> 00:01:599,000\ngain and it\'s going to be down to the\n\n260\n00:00:657,000 --> 00:01:603,000\nperson but they need to be aware that it\n\n261\n00:00:660,000 --> 00:01:605,000\nis a long process and it\'s down to\n\n262\n00:00:663,000 --> 00:01:608,000\nmaking sure that they understand that\n\n263\n00:00:665,000 --> 00:01:610,000\nit\'s all about time and the amount\n\n264\n00:00:668,000 --> 00:01:612,000\ntime they put into it and the amount of\n\n265\n00:00:671,000 --> 00:01:616,000\ngood quality work that they put into it\n\n266\n00:00:673,000 --> 00:01:617,000\nso if they put a lot of time and a good\n\n267\n00:00:676,000 --> 00:01:621,000\nquality work into it then they\'re gonna\n\n268\n00:00:678,000 --> 00:01:624,000\nstart seeing changes but within one\n\n269\n00:00:681,000 --> 00:01:626,000\nsession one or two sessions there\'s not\n\n270\n00:00:684,000 --> 00:01:627,000\ngonna be a huge difference and there\'s\n\n271\n00:00:686,000 --> 00:01:630,000\nyou know gonna have to be something that\n\n272\n00:00:688,000 --> 00:01:633,000\nyou\'ve got to manage for them so as a\n\n273\n00:00:691,000 --> 00:01:636,000\nstudent you\'ve got to make sure that\n\n274\n00:00:694,000 --> 00:01:638,000\nthey\'re not disheartened by seeing no\n\n275\n00:00:696,000 --> 00:01:642,000\ndifference so a lot of things covered\n\n276\n00:00:698,000 --> 00:01:645,000\nthere make sure that out of all of it\n\n277\n00:00:702,000 --> 00:01:648,000\nyou focus on the first thing which was\n\n278\n00:00:706,000 --> 00:01:651,000\nmake sure your students do everything\n\n279\n00:00:709,000 --> 00:01:653,000\ncorrectly and make sure that the\n\n280\n00:00:711,000 --> 00:01:655,000\ntechnical aspects the mechanics are\n\n281\n00:00:713,000 --> 00:01:658,000\nabsolutely perfect before you start\n\n282\n00:00:716,000 --> 00:01:660,000\nadding weights or increasing any of the\n\n283\n00:00:719,000 --> 00:01:663,000\nstress you want to make sure they\'re\n\n284\n00:00:721,000 --> 00:01:663,000\ndoing it correctly\n\n285\n00:00:729,000 --> 00:01:671,000\nyou\n\n'),(76971,55931,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(76972,55931,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APq4Kjh1f1K4o55ofFBvsEOq1o9rb\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730721716,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"Incorporating effective training strategies into your coaching sessions is crucial for achieving the desired outcomes while keeping students safe and engaged. A key part of this process involves ensuring that students master basic techniques and mechanics before any additional loads or advanced skills are introduced. By solidifying their foundational skills, you not only decrease the risk of injury but also enhance their overall confidence and enjoyment during training sessions. The core principle here is that without proper technique, pushing students towards heavier loads or more complex moves can backfire, leading to frustration and injury.nnOnce the mechanics are in place, it’s essential to communicate clear goals so students understand their purpose in the training. Developing personalized objectives based on individual skill levels can keep students motivated and invested in their progression. No matter the size of the class, it\'s important to start from simpler tasks before scaling up to more challenging ones. If students see a clear pathway for growth—from beginner to advanced levels—they\'re likely to feel more accomplished and engaged. Incorporating fun elements into strength and conditioning, such as friendly competition or group challenges, can also enhance their experience by making the exercises more enjoyable, breaking the monotony that often comes with such training.nnAs you wrap up each session, remind students that strength training is a gradual process that requires time and consistent effort to yield visible results. Recognizing that significant improvements might not come immediately can help foster patience and perseverance among your students. By continuously revisiting their goals, celebrating small wins, and maintaining an engaging atmosphere, you create a supportive environment where students can thrive. Most importantly, they will leave each session reaffirmed in their abilities and eager to tackle new challenges in the future.nnKey takeaways include ensuring students master technique before adding difficulty, providing clear and personalized goals to maintain motivation, and creating a fun, engaging environment that encourages consistent effort and growth.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 2628,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 363,\n            \"total_tokens\": 2991,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"XDoeYzDc991Vr7nj7X4fjpJCqC_dYfuel4vrFfhVzhM-1730721722-1.0.1.1-FLsLqJxRIDjJJR.SR7ZdmTIZftpv3moH4fMEPPDBs_LD9DWSB6hiEGTG6NrkJDNj4vr3AaED5Yc6jWHkRfPbeg\",\n            \"expires\": 1730723522,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"R9G8NcaalYc0Wco2YgyupAgT8Fo3RMBJljMCrDL3rMU-1730721722612-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(76973,55931,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(76974,55931,'_edit_lock','1730721760:1'),(76975,55931,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(76976,55931,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(76977,55931,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(76978,55931,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(76979,55932,'_thumbnail_id','14234'),(76980,55932,'video_id','vdPLospgJw0'),(76981,55932,'video_type','tutorial'),(76982,55932,'order_position','28'),(76983,55932,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"Vup7XbMtx9XfrU22mI_PP5eM_no\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC5GNjNDRDREMDQxOThCMDQ2\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #29 - Coaching Collab Parkour Tutorial. [104]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Intermediate) in Parkour - Coaching Collab.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #29nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnA quick recap of some of the points from the last video, but also let\'s also focus on some bits that a lot of coaches fail to do.nnWe\'ll cover some ideas around planning, collaborative training rather than competitive training and other bits and pieces too.nnn### PLANnPlanning is just good. It\'s something that all good coaches do, regardless of how much time they\'ve been teaching. Planning will make you more confident and professional in your coaching. With the pull-ups training, there are a lot of things to think about too.nnSome potential things to consider:nnDo you have the equipment for your students? How many students? Can everyone, regardless of ability, do your session? Will everyone be moving, all of the time? If the students rest, how much? Where will they rest? How will they warm-up? Cool-down? Will there be space for everyone? Will everyone understand what they have to do? What if they don\'t? How will you make sure technique is perfect? How will you make sure the strong, long-time practitioners will improve? etc...nnLots to consider.nnn### Collaborative and Cooperative NOT CompetitivenI\'m just going to say it, competition in training can be bad. Whenever you introduce an aspect of competing against someone else, the focus becomes about beating that person, NOT the technique, improving your ability or any of the more important things.nnQuality of movement is usually the first thing to suffer and a lot of the time will actually end up in injury through poor work.nnWhat is more important, getting functionally more able and a better built human being or stroking your ego to say you beat Joe Bloggs at a particular exercise, under certain conditions at some point?nnThere are a lot of other sports and disciplines(most!) out there that allow you to compete, this shouldn\'t be one of them. This is about training smart and becoming the best ve