  \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APqEHvTVHJiY7lESDXkb0W1luxv4J\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730722333,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"Understanding the importance of recovery in fitness is essential for anyone looking to enhance their performance and overall well-being. One key aspect of recovery is myofascial release, which helps alleviate muscle tension and improve flexibility. Myofascial release techniques, using tools like lacrosse balls and foam rollers, can greatly reduce soreness and improve your range of motion, allowing you to train harder and more effectively without the risk of injury.nnTo start with myofascial release, you’ll need a lacrosse ball (or a sturdy spiky ball) and a foam roller. Begin by targeting your shoulders: lie on your back with the ball placed under your shoulder, then lean into it and make small, circular movements. If you find a tender spot, stay there for a little while to really feel the release. Next, place the ball on the floor and target your chest and the front of your shoulders the same way by rolling over those areas. To enhance shoulder mobility, grab a resistance band attached to a sturdy point, bending at your hips rather than your back; this will help lift your arms and improve motion. Finally, use the foam roller for your lats by lying on your side and adjusting your body position to find those tight areas, ensuring you’re addressing both major and minor muscle groups effectively.nnIn summary, incorporating myofascial release into your recovery routine is invaluable. Not only does it help you bounce back from workouts quicker, but it also reduces the risk of injury and enhances overall mobility and performance. By making a habit of these simple techniques, you can train harder, recover faster, and enjoy your fitness journey with minimal discomfort.nnHighlights:n- Use a lacrosse ball or foam roller to target tight muscles during recovery.n- Focus on the shoulders, chest, and lats for effective myofascial release.n- Incorporate resistance bands to enhance shoulder mobility and improve range of motion.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1437,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 381,\n            \"total_tokens\": 1818,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"o_KG1VLZ54CG8Ae93I4rowIkPfk6ABd8AEJoYwP82dk-1730722339-1.0.1.1-JXcrDEwjHSMq7tN6iV497_Ygk6j5v8QNGGPAPDDVJqvVMFA8Qh6Jahqn0lBzbabxEnMk6XZxnXu6_ij3VEy11Q\",\n            \"expires\": 1730724139,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"FBY87DcUAX09JVn.Z2W.vK6aR_0l9ki1lB.TFFVu1_4-1730722339469-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(77118,55937,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(77119,55937,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(77120,55937,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(77121,55937,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(77122,55937,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(77123,55938,'_thumbnail_id','14246'),(77124,55938,'video_id','Nh0JjnGvipM'),(77125,55938,'video_type','tutorial'),(77126,55938,'order_position','34'),(77127,55938,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"KQc9sKv8XRmpb8oj5RmAp8zbOrQ\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC41MjE1MkI0OTQ2QzJGNzNG\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #35 - Assistance Work Parkour Tutorial. [110]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Beginner) in Parkour - Assistance Work.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #35nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnAssistance exercises can be a few different things. In this episode, we\'ll have a look at what falls under the term and how to put them into your training.nnn### Being more specificnYou are probably doing upper-body strength work for a specific reason, and that is usually to help do something else. That \'something else\' is the more specific exercises and training you should add into your training for assistance work to the strength training.nnn### Supporting MusclesnThe other assistance exercises are those that develop secondary muscles that will greatly help the goal.nnFor instance, doing sled pulls, deadlifts, pushups, swinging, etc... Will indirectly help the pulling, and will also help develop those other muscle groups that aren\'t used so much in a pull-up...nnn### Adding more stressnYou may also want to put in \'finishers\' into the training session that adds more stress to the body.nnMake sure you do your strength work first, but afterwards, you may want to always finish with a \'finisher\' that works your cardio system, stamina, etc... that will help benefit you in other ways.nnMake sure that you can recover from all of the training, however. As long as you are fully rested within the 48-72 hours to do the next training session, then it\'s all good.nnn### IdeasnnHere is a list of a few ideas of assistance exercises you may want to try out:nn- Climb-ups. (Parkour method of climbing up on a wall)n- Chin-ups (Pull-up with hands facing the other way)n- Climbingn- Boulderingn- Builderingn- Rope Climbingn- Koala Climbs (Climbing poles or columns)n- Brachiation (Swinging on bars)n--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:intermediate}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Strengthening}}{{Series:Pullups}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Nh0JjnGvipM/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Nh0JjnGvipM/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Nh0JjnGvipM/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Nh0JjnGvipM/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Nh0JjnGvipM/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMmrCVs_bOotQLjVdq5zGhT\",\"position\":34,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"Nh0JjnGvipM\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":34}'),(77128,55938,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Pullups'),(77129,55938,'authId','Auth1'),(77130,55938,'searchId','Tutorials - Pullups'),(77131,55938,'filterId','none'),(77132,55938,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(77133,55938,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Pullups'),(77134,55938,'_edit_last','1'),(77135,55938,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Assistance work is a crucial component of any fitness routine, especially if you\'re looking to enhance your strength and performance in specific exercises like pull-ups. It’s not just about building muscle in isolation, but rather about improving functional strength that translates into real-world activities, such as parkour movements. By incorporating assistance exercises, you can develop other muscle groups, increase your overall strength, and prevent training monotony, making your workouts more enjoyable and effective.\n\nTo get started with assistance work, think about exercises that complement your main training goals. For instance, if pull-ups are your focus, swinging on bars can help build grip strength and acclimate your body to hanging movements. Climb-ups and variations like rope climbs or koala climbs target similar muscle groups and improve your functional strength. Bouldering and sled pulls are great additions too, as they engage your entire body and add variety to your workouts. Remember, the key is to supplement your strength training without replacing it; assistance work should enhance your primary goals, not become the sole focus of your sessions.\n\nUltimately, the main takeaway is that assistance work can significantly elevate your training experience and results. It\'s essential not only to train hard but also to rest effectively, allowing your body to recover and grow stronger. Don’t overlook the role of rest in your routine; without it, your body may struggle to perform at its best. Balancing strength training with well-chosen assistance exercises and adequate recovery will help you reach your fitness goals while keeping your sessions fresh and engaging.\n\n- Incorporate assistance exercises like swinging, climbing, and sled pulls to enhance your strength training.\n- Keep your main focus on specific exercises like pull-ups but use assistance work to target complementary muscle groups.\n- Prioritize rest and recovery to support your training efforts and prevent burnout.'),(77136,55938,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77137,55938,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"with this video we are going to be\",\n        \"start\": 0.06,\n        \"duration\": 4.14\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"talking about some assistance work and\",\n        \"start\": 1.949,\n        \"duration\": 5.64\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"what that means and what it is so the\",\n        \"start\": 4.2,\n        \"duration\": 6.09\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"idea with assistance work is it has a\",\n        \"start\": 7.589,\n        \"duration\": 5.401\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"few different reasons why we put this in\",\n        \"start\": 10.29,\n        \"duration\": 5.84\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"a few different things of what it can be\",\n        \"start\": 12.99,\n        \"duration\": 7.14\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"to be more specific is the goal so\",\n        \"start\": 16.13,\n        \"duration\": 6.909\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"potentially you\'re doing pull-ups and\",\n        \"start\": 20.13,\n        \"duration\": 5.909\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"trying to get stronger not for the sake\",\n        \"start\": 23.039,\n        \"duration\": 5.371\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"of just getting stronger with a pull-up\",\n        \"start\": 26.039,\n        \"duration\": 6.06\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"but for a functional reason you might be\",\n        \"start\": 28.41,\n        \"duration\": 6.96\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"wanting to do some swinging on the bars\",\n        \"start\": 32.099,\n        \"duration\": 6.751\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so what we call a Shay\'s in parkour you\",\n        \"start\": 35.37,\n        \"dura