l to the push that\'s the hardest part\n\n168\n00:00:463,000 --> 00:01:409,000\nnow the thing is about the muscle up is\n\n169\n00:00:465,000 --> 00:01:411,000\nis super functional it is something that\n\n170\n00:00:469,000 --> 00:01:414,000\nis very very handy because it allows you\n\n171\n00:00:472,000 --> 00:01:416,000\nto get up onto things where you only\n\n172\n00:00:474,000 --> 00:01:418,000\nneed your arms you don\'t need your legs\n\n173\n00:00:477,000 --> 00:01:421,000\non you don\'t need to use elbows or\n\n174\n00:00:479,000 --> 00:01:424,000\nanything else you can just pop up on top\n\n175\n00:00:481,000 --> 00:01:425,000\nof something just by using your arms now\n\n176\n00:00:484,000 --> 00:01:428,000\nthis is something you want to be\n\n177\n00:00:486,000 --> 00:01:432,000\nthinking of as a potential goal for\n\n178\n00:00:489,000 --> 00:01:434,000\nfuture stuff on top of the pulling but\n\n179\n00:00:492,000 --> 00:01:436,000\ngetting used to doing the strength\n\n180\n00:00:494,000 --> 00:01:439,000\ntraining of the pull is very very handy\n\n181\n00:00:496,000 --> 00:01:441,000\nbecause it\'s going to translate into the\n\n182\n00:00:499,000 --> 00:01:442,000\nmuscle up work later on so there you\n\n183\n00:00:502,000 --> 00:01:445,000\nhave it\n\n184\n00:00:502,000 --> 00:01:447,000\na load of variations things that you can\n\n185\n00:00:505,000 --> 00:01:450,000\nplay around with research into and maybe\n\n186\n00:00:507,000 --> 00:01:450,000\nadd into your training\n\n187\n00:00:516,000 --> 00:01:458,000\nyou\n\n'),(77164,55939,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(77165,55939,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APqF1aJKz0681Dq3LdwMQcg9fafjf\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730722379,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"If you\'re looking to enhance your upper body strength and functional movement, exploring different types of pull-ups can significantly boost your fitness routine. Traditional pull-ups and chin-ups are excellent for building back and arm muscles, but they can also be adapted to better suit activities like parkour where grip and climbing techniques are essential. In this tutorial, we will delve into various pull-up variations and their benefits, making your workouts much more versatile and engaging.nnTo get started, you want to familiarize yourself with the basic grip. The traditional pull-up grip involves your palms facing away, which helps in developing strength through the lats and back. However, switching to a chin-up grip, where your palms face towards you, allows your biceps and chest to take on more of the load. Once comfortable with these, you can experiment with alternative grips, such as placing your hands in different positions on the bar to mimic real-world climbing scenarios. Additionally, techniques like the swing-up and skin-the-cat provide a more dynamic approach to pull-ups, integrating a playful aspect while also working on your strength.nnIn conclusion, mastering a variety of pull-up styles will not only make your workouts more enjoyable but will also translate into improved performance in functional movements like climbing and parkour. Incorporating exercises like the muscle-up into your regimen can serve as an advanced goal, as it requires a strong transition from pulling to pushing. So, whether you\'re a beginner or looking to level up your training, exploring these different pull-up variations can really enhance your overall physical capabilities. nnHighlights:n- Experiment with traditional pull-ups and chin-ups to build strength effectively.n- Incorporate variations like the swing-up and skin-the-cat to add fun and challenges to your training.n- Aim for advanced exercises like the muscle-up to enhance your overall functional strength.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 1845,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 359,\n            \"total_tokens\": 2204,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"oAs1vNJygqpHAyWf48mZE4ttZBLCp5ldpT6yE38pcGI-1730722384-1.0.1.1-GDO28SsaZcSv9zGXdAoSTBajwt9u2blVKJucL8v4ti4VhZ7vTOBYrs_5sZHWIzRdVFVCpNhfKJdyDspOSE8zhQ\",\n            \"expires\": 1730724184,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"QMlKTs5llT9pnuTsFpFoURZmgJ6GK.K.VP4IwuN5SO0-1730722384240-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(77166,55939,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(77167,55939,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(77168,55939,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(77169,55939,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(77170,55939,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(77171,55940,'_thumbnail_id','14250'),(77172,55940,'video_id','55CIX1fDDd8'),(77173,55940,'video_type','tutorial'),(77174,55940,'order_position','36'),(77175,55940,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"NHnnrPTjg5UYSAZNHYKy1y8o0AQ\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTW1yQ1ZzX2JPb3RRTGpWZHE1ekdoVC4yODlGNEE0NkRGMEEzMEQy\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-08-19T07:32:10Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Pullup #37 - Challenges Parkour Tutorial. [112]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Pullup (Beginner) in Parkour - Challenges.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Pullup Series. Episode #37nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnI\'ve mentioned many times throughout the series that you should be challenging yourself all the time. Figuring out how to do that sometimes can be tricky without examples or ideas to start from.nnIn this episode, I will present a few ideas that you can potentially try or base your own challenges off.nnn### Mixed GripnThis one can be fun to do and easily scalable by using any of the techniques we\'ve discussed in the series. All we do is do a set of five pull-ups, all with different grips and without coming off the bar.nnThe order of each grip you should do is as follows:nn1. Normal grip pull-up.n2. Turn right hand so that it is supinated. Do 1 pull-up with this grip.n3 . Turn left hand so that both hands are supinated. Do 1 Chin-up.n4. Turn right hand so that only left hand is only supinated. Do 1 pull-up.n5. Turn left hand and finish with 1 normal pull-up.nnn### Add onnThis is a pretty simple challenge to do but requires a little imagination on what it involves. It can also be a little tricky for those that need bands or assistance. So this one is more for bodyweight pull-ups or above.nnAll you do is start at doing 1 pull-up. You then take a short rest and then you add a different second thing after the pull-up, so it becomes two exercises. Then three, four, etc...nnSo as an example, you could do:nn1 pull-up.n1 pull-up, 1 skin-the-cat.n1 pull-up, 1 skin-the-cat, 1 chin-up.n1 pull-up, 1 skin-the-cat, 1 chin-up, 360 hanging turn.n1 pull-up, 1 skin-the-cat, 1 chin-up, 360 hanging turn, 1 mixed-grip pull.nThis is good to do with a couple of other people, so you get significant rest between each set. This is a good endurance challenge.nnn### The laddernThe ladder is a very simple concept that can be applied to many different exercises and can be changed in many different ways.nnStart by picking a top number that you want to get to. Let\'s say 5. You now have to work up to that number and then back down again.nnStart doing by one pull-up. Then rest and then do two. Three, etc... Until you get to your goal number. Then you have to work back down again.nnSo, it\'ll be: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.nnA total of 25 pull-ups.nnn### GimmicksnEating a carrot at the top of a pull-up is a bit of a gimmick challenge, but it works. It can be fun and forces the student / you to focus on quality. These types of challenges are made to inject more enjoyment into the session and just requires imagination with the planning.nnnn### Big NumbersnI\'ve mentioned this earlier in the series but trying for very, very large numbers will test everything about you as a person. Physically, mentally, emotionally.nnNot to be done often because it can be very detrimental to your body and if care isn\'t taken, can be damaging to your tendons.nnn### Dice of DeathnThis can be a fun way to create challenges. Using dice in various ways to randomly assign exercises or reps or any other variable makes you work hard but never in the same way.nnOne example is by using a normal 6-sided dice to challenge a friend. Whoever rolls the highest number makes the other person do that number of pull-ups. Keep going until the both of you cannot continue.nnOther methods include assigning different exercises to different numbers and making everyone do the same exercise. This can be good for groups.n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000  uff2cuff2fuff2euff24uff2fuff2euff30uff21uff32uff2buff2fuff35uff32nnnnnThis video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Strengthening}}{{Series:Pullups}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/55CIX1fDDd8/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/55CIX1fDDd8/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/55CIX1fDDd8/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/55CIX1fDDd8/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/55CIX1fDDd8/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMmrCVs_bOotQLjVdq5zGhT\",\"position\":36,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"55CIX1fDDd8\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":36}'),(77176,55940,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Pullups'),(77177,55940,'authId','Auth1'),(77178,55940,'searchId','Tutorials - Pullups'),(77179,55940,'filterId','none'),(77180,55940,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(77181,55940,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Pullups'),(77182,55940,'_edit_last','1'),(77183,55940,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you\'re looking to spice up your workout routine, especially when it comes to pull-ups, this tutorial is for you! Engaging in varied challenges can not only enhance your strength but also keep your training sessions fun and exciting. Whether you’re working alone or with friends, these challenges will stimulate your muscles, boost your endurance, and add a touch of playful competition to your exercise regimen.\n\nStart with the mixed grip challenge, which involves performing various pull-up progressions while rotating your grip. Begin with a standard pull-up, then switch one hand at a time for chin-ups and back to pull-ups, creating a seamless flow of movements. Aim for five sets of this cycle, adjusting rest times to suit your fitness level. Next, try the add-on challenge where you stack different pull-up variations on top of each other, gradually increasing the number as you go along. This can be a fun way to explore your limits. Alternatively, the ladder challenge lets you build up reps in a structured way—start at one, add a rep each round up to five, and then make your way back down to one. \n\nTo add even more variety, consider using props like a carrot dangling above the bar to motivate you to complete full-range pull-ups, or grab a set of dice. With the dice game, you and a partner take turns rolling to see how many pull-ups each must complete, mixing up the challenge and keeping things light-hearted. Whether you’re engaging in high-volume endurance sessions or playful competition, these exercises will challenge you both physically and mentally, making your training experiences not only effective but also enjoyable.\n\nHighlights:\n- Try the mixed grip and add-on challenges to engage different muscle groups and push your limits.\n- Incorporate fun elements, like a dangling item for full-range motion or a dice game for a playful twist.\n- Mix up your routine to avoid monotony and keep your workouts engaging and challenging.'),(77184,55940,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77185,55940,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we\'re near the end of the series now and\",\n        \"start\": 0.149,\n        \"duration\": 3.931\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we\'re gonna have a look at some fun\",\n        \"start\": 2.25,\n        \"duration\": 3.6\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"challenges I\'m gonna give you some\",\n        \"start\": 4.08,\n        \"duration\": 3.33\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"examples of things that you could\",\n        \"start\": 5.85,\n        \"duration\": 4.68\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"potentially have a go at doing and try\",\n        \"start\": 7.41,\n        \"duration\": 5.79\n    },\n  