1u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Strengthening #Pullup #---nnCongratulations! You made it through. Hopefully, you\'ve learned something in this series to do with pull-ups and how to start getting stronger with your upper-body.nnLet\'s run through a quick summary and checklist of the highlights.nnn### The most important conceptsnIf there is anything that you should take away from this course, it is the following things in the following list.nn1. Technique trumps all.nTechnique and mechanics are the number one thing you should absolutely make sure you are doing right. If you\'re not, then fix it now.nn2. Current Ability.nYou need to know what you are able to do right now before you can make a plan or a goal. If you have no idea of your current ability, now is the time to find out.nn3. Plan.nIf you don\'t have a plan (even a simple one), you\'re just guessing. This will work for a short period of time and then that\'s it. Plans are what separates the amateurs from the professionals.nn4. Pre and Post.nJoint mobility, warming up, assistance work, cooling down, stretching and myofascial release are just as important, if not more than the training.nnTo be injury free and last for years to come, you can\'t neglect this stuff. You just can\'t. It\'s either this or injury, rehab and surgery.nn5. Enjoy.nOne of the most fundamental aspects that are missing from most people\'s training is fun. If you\'re not enjoying it then it\'s not sustainable and won\'t last. It needs to be something you look forward to doing every time.nnYou\'ll have up and down days, but overall, the experience should be one of pleasure.nnn### Going furthernThroughout the series, I\'ve linked to a few different external resources, but here are a few that I highly recommend you check out if you haven\'t already.nnAs an extra note, if you get the chance to go to one of Julien Pineau\'s seminars, do it. It\'s well worth the money and will teach you a great deal about his systems of training, how to decide exercises, torque and much more.nnFinally, have a read of Mark Rippetoe\'s \'Starting Strength\' and \'Practical Programming\'. Both have invaluable knowledge on strength training.nnn### DonenSo there you are. You should have everything you need to take on the beast of pull-ups and start getting stronger.nnSo the big question is what\'s the next thing you want to overcome?n nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25