,(77223,55942,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"ZaUkjzOonvizB3aOrZKsTFZ8B_k\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTWJaalBxdlg3NzJUd0xVZ2lFTEtJdC4wMTcyMDhGQUE4NTIzM0Y5\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T09:22:45Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Turn Vault #01 - Introduction Parkour Tutorial. [121]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Turn Vault (Beginner) in Parkour - Introduction.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Turn Vault Series. Episode #01nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Vaulting #Introduction #---nnTurn Vaults - Hand Position.n nBack to basics! Today we\'ll start working on the turn vault, an absolutely essential Parkour technique.nn1. The turn vault is usually used to get over a fence or barrier with a height drop in the other side. It enables us to get on to that other side while maintaining secure contact and not falling.nn2. Remember to try both hands and just make your way over the bar however you like, practicing the hand transition.nn3. Always do both sides! This is very important with the turn vault because you WILL come across environmental situations where you can only do the turn vault on one particular side, so get comfortable going both ways!nnI\'m a big fan of turn Vaults, so hopefully you\'ll all enjoy this series!nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Vaulting}}{{Series:Turn Vaults Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/oshG-RAQ-3Q/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/oshG-RAQ-3Q/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/oshG-RAQ-3Q/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/oshG-RAQ-3Q/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/oshG-RAQ-3Q/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMbZjPqvX772TwLUgiELKIt\",\"position\":0,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"oshG-RAQ-3Q\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":0}'),(77224,55942,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Turn Vaults'),(77225,55942,'authId','Auth1'),(77226,55942,'searchId','Tutorials - Turn Vaults'),(77227,55942,'filterId','none'),(77228,55942,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(77229,55942,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Turn Vaults'),(77230,55942,'_edit_last','1'),(77231,55942,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Learning how to transition smoothly over a rail or fence with the right hand position can enhance your skills and confidence in performing tricks. This tutorial will guide you through the basics of a maneuver commonly referred to as turn vaults. By focusing on the specific hand movements involved, you\'ll be equipped to make your transfers cleaner and more controlled.\r\n\r\nTo get started, position your hands on the bar with one palm facing down and the other facing up. As you approach the rail or fence, use your down-facing hand to grip the bar firmly. When you initiate your move, allow your palm-up hand to release the grip just as you\'re about to go over the bar. At the same time, your down-facing hand will rotate around, repositioning as you complete the transfer. This motion helps you maintain balance and prepares you for a smooth descent back to the ground on the other side.\r\n\r\nIn summary, mastering the hand positions and the timing of your movement is key to executing this trick successfully. As you practice, focus on the flow of your hands as they rotate around during the transition, which will help you gain better control. With time and perseverance, not only will you become more adept at exhilarating maneuvers, but you’ll also enjoy the process of learning and improving your technique.\r\n\r\n- Use a balanced hand position: one hand faces down and one faces up. \r\n- Practice the rotation of your hands for a smooth transition.\r\n- Patience is essential; with practice, your control and confidence will improve.'),(77232,55942,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77233,55942,'video_transcript_json','[\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"so today we\'re going to have a look at\",\r\n        \"start\": 2.95,\r\n        \"duration\": 3.96\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"doing some turn vaults alright so the idea\",\r\n        \"start\": 4.69,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.47\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"is that this is going to be where you\'re\",\r\n        \"start\": 6.91,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.94\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"on one side of a rail or a fence and\",\r\n        \"start\": 9.16,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.04\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"you\'re going to get on to the other side\",\r\n        \"start\": 11.85,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.2\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"of the fence by going up turning around\",\r\n        \"start\": 14.2,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.919\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"and coming back down we\'re going to look\",\r\n        \"start\": 17.05,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.199\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"at hand position today so essentially\",\r\n        \"start\": 19.119,\r\n        \"duration\": 4.47\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"what happens is you start with your\",\r\n        \"start\": 21.249,\r\n        \"duration\": 5.071\r\n    },\r\n    {\r\n        \"text\": \"hands with one facing down and one\",\r\n        \"start\": 23.589