(77439,55949,'video_transcript_chatgpt','In this tutorial, we\'re going to explore the exciting world of landing techniques, specifically focusing on landing with both feet facing the correct direction. This practice is particularly useful for activities like parkour or any sport that involves jumping and landing safely. The main goal today is to improve your stability and control when you land, which can prevent injuries and make your movements much smoother.\n\nTo get started, picture yourself jumping off a ledge or a bar, and as you come down, ensure that your legs are positioned correctly. The aim is to land with both feet slightly apart and facing in the direction opposite where you jumped from, essentially completing a rotation of around 180 degrees. While practicing this, concentrate on your legs without stressing too much about where your hands are; they will find their position as you get more comfortable. The key here is to find your balance and focus on a solid landing before worrying about additional movements.\n\nIn summary, mastering this landing technique will enhance your agility and coordination while minimizing the risk of injury during jumps. Remember that practice makes perfect; keep honing your skills by repeating these steps, and soon, landing with confidence will become second nature. Learning to properly land is not only beneficial for your performance but also adds a layer of safety to your athletic pursuits.\n\n- Focus on landing with both feet slightly apart and facing the opposite direction.\n- Prioritize your leg positioning first; don\'t worry about your hands during this stage.\n- Consistent practice will improve your technique and boost your confidence in jumping.'),(77440,55949,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77441,55949,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so today we\'re going to do it exactly\",\n        \"start\": 2.899,\n        \"duration\": 4.621\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the sam