, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Vaulting}}{{Series:Turn Vaults Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/0ZslE8x2WWk/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/0ZslE8x2WWk/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/0ZslE8x2WWk/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/0ZslE8x2WWk/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/0ZslE8x2WWk/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMbZjPqvX772TwLUgiELKIt\",\"position\":8,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"0ZslE8x2WWk\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":8}'),(77456,55950,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Turn Vaults'),(77457,55950,'authId','Auth1'),(77458,55950,'searchId','Tutorials - Turn Vaults'),(77459,55950,'filterId','none'),(77460,55950,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(77461,55950,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Turn Vaults'),(77462,55950,'_edit_last','1'),(77463,55950,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When you’re looking to master the vault in gymnastics or parkour, one of the key elements is understanding the importance of positioning your hips and hands. A common challenge athletes face is not generating enough space beneath them, making it difficult to get into the correct position for the vault. By focusing on elevating your hips and keeping your head low, you\'ll set the foundation for a successful vault and improve your overall technique.\n\nTo practice this, start by positioning your hands correctly on the ground. Rather than attempting to vault over an obstacle right away, your goal should be to elevate your hips high while maintaining a low head position. This technique creates the necessary space under you, enabling your knees to come through smoothly when you do attempt the vault. Spend some time getting comfortable with raising your hips without the pressure of actually going over an object, as this will help refine your body mechanics and set you up for success.\n\nIncorporating drills that emphasize these movements will not only enhance your confidence but also prepare your body for more challenging vaults in the future. Remember, the ultimate aim is to translate this practice into your vaulting technique, ensuring you feel at ease with getting your hips high and using your hands effectively when you’re ready to leap over those obstacles. \n\nKey takeaways include: \n- Focus on hip elevation to create space beneath you.\n- Practice hand positioning without the vault to refine your technique.\n- Incorporate drills that emphasize getting your hips high and head low for better vault performance.'),(77464,55950,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77465,55950,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we covered this on the comms cat part\",\n        \"start\": 3.5,\n        \"duration\": 8.61\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the idea about having your hips high\",\n        \"start\": 8.54,\n        \"duration\": 7.17\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"when you vault over something the key to\",\n        \"start\": 12.11,\n        \"duration\": 7.2\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"this is creating space underneath you so\",\n        \"start\": 15.71,\n        \"duration\": 6.389\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you can get your knees underneath and so\",\n        \"start\": 19.31,\n        \"duration\": 5.73\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you can do the vault alright so we\'re\",\n        \"start\": 22.099,\n        \"duration\": 4.441\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"going to do the same thing today but\",\n        \"start\": 25.04,\n        \"duration\": 3.39\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"with our hands in the correct position\",\n        \"start\": 26.54,\n        \"duration\": 3.6\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"and we\'re going to train get our hips\",\n        \"start\": 28.43,\n        \"duration\": 4.169\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"high and that\'s it we\'re not going over\",\n        \"start\": 30.14,\n        \"duration\": 3.81\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"and I\'m going around we\'re not doing\",\n        \"start\": 32.599,\n        \"duration\": 3.03\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"anything other than trying to get our\",\n        \"start\": 33.95,\n        \"duratio