changing your hand positions while maintaining good form. The side vault is not only a great way to improve your agility but also helps build strength and coordination. By the end of this tutorial, you\'ll be more confident in executing this move with greater finesse.\n\nTo get started, you\'ll want to approach the vault with a focus on your hand movements. Begin by placing one hand down on the surface with the palm facing down and the other hand facing up. As you initiate the jump and pass your body over, you\'ll switch these hand positions. This also means that as you land on the other side, you\'ll be switching the hand that was previously facing down to face up and vice versa. It\'s a continuous process of regripping the hands as you shift your body from one side to the other, which will help you develop a fluid motion and allows you to better adapt to different positions during your vault.\n\nIn summary, practicing this variation of the side vault will enhance your technique and make you more comfortable with the movement. Remember to focus on the regripping of your hands, maintaining a rhythm throughout your practice. The more you incorporate these changes into your technique, the easier the vault will become. So, keep at it and watch as your skills improve!\n\n- Focus on changing hand positions during the vault to enhance your control.\n- Start with one hand down and one hand up, then switch as you move across.\n- Maintain a fluid motion to build strength and improve your overall agility.'),(77608,55956,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77609,55956,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you\'re gonna have a go at doing the side\",\n        \"start\": 3.53,\n        \"duration\": 4.17\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"vault again but we\'re gonna keep\",\n        \"start\": 5.569,\n        \"duration\": 4.471\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"changing the hand position all right\",\n        \"start\": 7.7,\n        \"durat