fessionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Vaulting}}{{Series:Turn Vaults Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lrfyTA9tTYM/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lrfyTA9tTYM/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lrfyTA9tTYM/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lrfyTA9tTYM/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lrfyTA9tTYM/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMbZjPqvX772TwLUgiELKIt\",\"position\":21,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"lrfyTA9tTYM\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":21}'),(77744,55962,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Turn Vaults'),(77745,55962,'authId','Auth1'),(77746,55962,'searchId','Tutorials - Turn Vaults'),(77747,55962,'filterId','none'),(77748,55962,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(77749,55962,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Turn Vaults'),(77750,55962,'_edit_last','1'),(77751,55962,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Parkour is all about functional movement, enabling you to tackle physical challenges in various environments confidently and creatively. Whether you’re navigating urban landscapes or just looking to enhance your agility, learning essential techniques—like the turn vault—can significantly boost your skills. The beauty of parkour lies in its gradual progression; you start from a lower height and gradually work your way up, ensuring that you perfect your form along the way.\n\nTo get started with the turn vault, first, find a safe, low surface to practice on. It can be as simple as a sturdy bench or a low wall. Focus on your technique; approach the surface with speed and confidence, use your arms to propel yourself upward, and rotate your hips to guide your body over the obstacle. Once you feel comfortable executing the move with correct form and control, you can then begin to increase the height gradually. This ensures that your body adapts and strengthens with these new challenges while maintaining the correct technique.\n\nIn summary, the key to mastering parkour moves like the turn vault is to prioritize safety and technique over height. Start small, perfect your form, and build your confidence before moving on to more significant challenges. Remember, every expert was once a beginner, so keep practicing and don’t rush the process!\n\nHighlights:\n- Start practicing low to ensure you master your technique before increasing the height.\n- Focus on your form to build confidence and avoid injury.\n- Progress gradually, allowing your body to adapt to new challenges.'),(77752,55962,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77753,55962,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"with parkour the whole idea is that we\",\n        \"start\": 3.97,\n        \"duration\": 7.17\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"are functional and we can do the turn\",\n        \"start\": 7.63,\n        \"duration\": 5.7\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"ball or any other thing in any situation\",\n        \"start\": 11.14,\n        \"duration\": 5.85\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we take on that challenge and I should\",\n        \"start\": 13.33,\n        \"duration\": 6.209\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"be able to do this at fight all right\",\n        \"start\": 16.99,\n        \"duration\": 5.099\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the t