idth\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/aJw6UeI2EEQ/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMPPwg52msvrAueGiI8MoIk\",\"position\":1,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"aJw6UeI2EEQ\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":1}'),(77792,55964,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Cat Pass'),(77793,55964,'authId','Auth1'),(77794,55964,'searchId','Tutorials - Cat Pass'),(77795,55964,'filterId','none'),(77796,55964,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(77797,55964,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Cat Pass'),(77798,55964,'_edit_last','1'),(77799,55964,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to mastering a new skill in fitness, sometimes the smallest adjustments can create the biggest impact. Today, we\'re focusing on a key movement that combines getting your hips high while transitioning a foot onto a box. This technique is not only important for improving your overall strength and agility, but it also lays the groundwork for more advanced movements. Whether you\'re training for a specific sport or looking to enhance your workout routine, this simple adjustment can make all the difference.\n\nTo start, you’ll want to practice getting your hips up high as you prepare to place your foot on the box. It’s crucial to remember that you need to bring one foot underneath you at a time, which means alternating sides. This ensures that you’re not only working on both legs but also building balance and coordination. A key tip here is to focus on replacing your hand with your foot. In other words, when you place your foot on the box, make sure you lift your hands off the box, rather than keeping both your hands and foot on at the same time. This creates the necessary space and leverage to lift your foot without feeling cramped.\n\nIn conclusion, the transition from getting your hips high to placing your foot on the box is a valuable skill that can elevate your fitness game. By focusing on one foot at a time and ensuring that your hands come off the box as your foot takes their place, you’re setting yourself up for success. Remember, practice makes perfect, so take your time to master each step as you build your strength and agility.\n\nHighlights:\n- Aim to get your hips high while transferring weight to one foot at a time on the box.\n- Always lift hands off the box before placing the foot on to create ample space.\n- Practice on both the left and right sides to develop balance and coordination.'),(77800,55964,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77801,55964,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay so today we\'re going to move on\",\n        \"start\": 8.809,\n        \"duration\": 7.841\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"from getting the hips high on we\'re now\",\n        \"start\": 12.48,\n        \"duration\": 6.24\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"trying to get the foot on to the box as\",\n        \"start\": 16.65,\n        \"duration\": 2.46\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"well\",\n        \"start\": 18.72,\n        \"duration\": 2.19\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so you\'re still trying to get your hips\",\n        \"start\": 19.11,\n        \"duration\": 3.57\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"high but now you\'re trying to bring the\",\n        \"start\": 20.91,\n        \"duration\": 3.84\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"one foot underneath you onto the box\",\n        \"start\": 22.68,\n        \"duration\": 4.08\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"make sure you do both sides left and\",\n        \"start\": 24.75,\n        \"duration\": 4.65\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"right now what you don\'t want to do is\",\n        \"start\": 26.76,\n        \"duration\": 5.279\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"have both hands and your foot on at the\",\n        \"start\": 29.4,\n  