rmance. \n\nTo start, set yourself up so that your hands are comfortably placed on the box. As you prepare to make the move, think about creating enough space beneath you by raising your feet off the ground. The key to this step is to ensure that both feet land on the box without any hands for support. It’s essential to avoid having both your hands and feet on the box at the same time, as this could lead to a collision and may cause you to hit your chin. Rather, focus on lifting both feet together while keeping your hands elevated, allowing you to achieve a stable position on top of the box. Remember, practice makes perfect, so don’t hesitate to give it your best shot multiple times! \n\nIn conclusion, this exercise not only builds strength but also enhances your coordination and body awareness. By eliminating hand contact with the box and concentrating on your feet, you’ll develop a sense of balance and confidence in your movements. Keep working at it, and you’ll be able to execute this technique smoothly with time and practice. \n\n- Focus on creating enough space under you by lifting your feet.\n- Avoid having both hands and feet on the box simultaneously to prevent injury.\n- Practice regularly to build your confidence and improve coordination.'),(77824,55965,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77825,55965,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"all right so third stage is now trying\",\n        \"start\": 9.1,\n        \"duration\": 5.5\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"to get both feet up onto the box at the\",\n        \"start\": 12.95,\n        \"duration\": 4.14\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"same time again creating that space\",\n        \"start\": 14.6,\n        \"duration\": 5.13\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"underneath you let the hands come off of\",\n        \"start\": 17.09,\n        \"duration\": 5.46\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the box replacing with both feet okay\",\n        \"start\": 19.73,\n