s'),(77867,55967,'filterId','none'),(77868,55967,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(77869,55967,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Cat Pass'),(77870,55967,'_edit_last','1'),(77871,55967,'video_transcript_chatgpt','In this tutorial, we’re diving into a fun exercise that focuses on improving your movement skills, specifically in the context of the standing Kong technique. This skill is not just about agility; it also enhances your overall control and coordination. Whether you\'re looking to add some flair to your workouts or simply want to push your fitness routine to the next level, mastering the standing Kong can be a fantastic addition.\n\nTo begin, find a sturdy box or platform that you can jump over. The key to the standing Kong is to approach the box with focus. Start by positioning yourself a couple of steps back from the edge. As you gain momentum, drive your knees up while extending your arms forward. The goal here is to launch yourself in a way that helps you clear the box comfortably without losing balance. When you are in the air, think about tucking your knees close to your body as you pass over the edge. This tuck will make it easier to land safely on the other side, ensuring a smooth transition in your movement.\n\nAs you practice this technique, remember to keep a positive mindset and don’t be afraid to fall a few times—it\'s part of the learning process. With persistence and practice, you’ll find that your agility and confidence will improve. So get out there, have fun with it, and don’t forget that every attempt gets you closer to perfecting your technique.\n\nKey highlights to remember:\n- Position yourself a couple of steps back from the box before jumping.\n- Tuck your knees close to your body as you clear the box for a safe landing.\n- Persistence and practice are crucial for mastering this movement.'),(77872,55967,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77873,55967,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\"