xres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/gj5VmdOS4uo/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMPPwg52msvrAueGiI8MoIk\",\"position\":6,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"gj5VmdOS4uo\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":6}'),(77912,55969,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Cat Pass'),(77913,55969,'authId','Auth1'),(77914,55969,'searchId','Tutorials - Cat Pass'),(77915,55969,'filterId','none'),(77916,55969,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(77917,55969,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Cat Pass'),(77918,55969,'_edit_last','1'),(77919,55969,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you’re familiar with the concept of using a splitter in your training but want to advance your technique further, this tutorial will help you progress step-by-step. The aim here is to master the transition from running into the splitter position, which is essential for improving your overall performance. By breaking down the movements into manageable parts, you can build both your confidence and skill without feeling overwhelmed.\n\nTo start, find a comfortable position where you can slip into your initial stance. From there, take one deliberate step back, focusing on maintaining your balance. Once you feel secure, practice stepping forward into the correct position, ensuring your body is aligned and ready for the next movement. After getting comfortable with that step, the next task is to jump up onto a box, landing with both feet solidly on top. Just remember that practice is key, so make sure to repeat these movements on both sides to develop a balanced technique.\n\nIn summary, this training progression allows you to gradually enhance your skills without rushing through the process. By starting from a stable position and working your way up to more dynamic movements, you\'ll not only improve your technique but also increase your confidence in using the splitter effectively. So keep practicing and take it one step at a time, and you\'ll soon see great improvements in your performance.\n\n- Start with a comfortable stance before progressing to the step-back movement.\n- Focus on aligning your body properly when stepping forward into the splitter position.\n- Practice both sides to ensure balanced development and technique.'),(77920,55969,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77921,55969,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"[Music]\",\n        \"start\": 1.9,\n        \"duration\": 13.779\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay so we\'ve got used to the splitter\",\n        \"start\": 15.78,\n        \"duration\": 6.22\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"now what we\'re gonna try to do is\",\n        \"start\": 19.62,\n        \"duration\": 5.68\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"progress into it from running I\'m we\'re\",\n        \"start\": 22,\n        \"duration\": 4.38\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"only going to do this one step at a time\",\n        \"start\": 25.3,\n        \"duration\": 3.84\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so the idea is to start in the position\",\n        \"start\": 26.38,\n        \"duration\": 3.75\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"that you\'re comfortable with and your\",\n        \"start\": 29.14,\n        \"duration\": 4.079\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"feet slip up and now from there you take\",\n        \"start\": 30.13,\n        \"duration\": 5.1\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"one step back and you\'re going to get\",\n        \"start\": 33.219,\n        \"duration\": 3.87\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"used to taking that step forward into\",\n        \"start\": 35.23,\n        \"duration\": 4.5\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the correct position and then gonna come\",\n        \"start\": 37.089,\n        \"duration\": 4.441\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"up on top of the box ge