"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMPPwg52msvrAueGiI8MoIk\",\"position\":7,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"DuI8T9mHA-8\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":7}'),(77936,55970,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Cat Pass'),(77937,55970,'authId','Auth1'),(77938,55970,'searchId','Tutorials - Cat Pass'),(77939,55970,'filterId','none'),(77940,55970,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(77941,55970,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Cat Pass'),(77942,55970,'_edit_last','1'),(77943,55970,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you’re looking to improve your skills in a particular activity that requires both timing and coordination, adding a second step can be a game-changer. This tutorial will guide you through the process of building momentum by incorporating additional movements. It’s all about refining your technique so that you can take off confidently and land smoothly.\n\nTo get started, focus on executing a sequence of actions; first, you perform one movement, followed by a second one. Picture this as a one-two action: first, you take a step or a jump, and then you add another before making your landing. This combination helps you build momentum, which is particularly helpful if you\'re aiming to land on a specific target, like a box. As you practice, notice how this added step increases your speed and height, allowing you to push through and even leap over obstacles. Think of this as a dance between timing and control—each action should flow into the next seamlessly, leading you to the success of your landing.\n\nIn summary, incorporating an additional step not only enhances your momentum but also helps you achieve more accurate landings. As you continue to practice this technique, you’ll likely find yourself feeling more confident and capable, whether you\'re tackling a new sport or simply improving your balance. Remember, it\'s all about building a rhythm that works for you and allowing yourself to explore new heights with ease.\n\n- Start with a simple one-two movement sequence to build momentum.\n- Focus on timing and control to improve your landing accuracy.\n- Practice regularly to increase your confidence and skills in any activity.'),(77944,55970,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77945,55970,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"all right so now you can start feeling\",\n        \"start\": 18.77,\n        \"duration\": 3.929\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"that there is going to be quite a lot of\",\n        \"start\": 20.99,\n        \"duration\": 3.299\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"momentum now because what we\'re doing is\",\n        \"start\": 22.699,\n        \"duration\": 5.071\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"acting adding a second step in so it\'s\",\n        \"start\": 24.289,\n        \"duration\": 6.571\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"now one two and then take off and land\",\n        \"start\": 27.77,\n        \"duration\": 6.059\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"on the Box you can start feeling that\",\n        \"start\": 30.86,\n        \"duration\": 5.1\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you\'re gonna have enough momentum start\",\n        \"start\": 33.829,\n        \"duration\": 3.741\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"heading towards the back of the box and\",\n        \"start\": 35.96,\n        \"duration\": 5.4\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"then potentially over the top and on to\",\n        \"start\": 37.57,\n        \"duration\": 6.129\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the other side so see if we can do it so\",\n        \"start\": 41.36,\n        \"duration\": 6.979\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you go all the way over if you can\",\n        \"start\": 43.699,\n        \"duration\": 4.64\n    }\n]'),(77946,55970,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(77947,55970,'video_transcript_srt','1\n00:00:18