you can learn to dive deeper and gain a better trajectory towards your landing spot, making those jumps smoother and more efficient.\n\nTo get started, you\'ll want to position yourself further back before executing a split Kong. This means shuffling your feet behind your original starting point. By doing this, you\'re setting yourself up for a more powerful forward motion. As you leap over the obstacle, aim to really engage your core, keeping your body controlled as you dive past the box. This technique allows for better momentum and helps ensure that you land neatly after your jump. It\'s all about practice, so make sure to experiment with your foot placements and notice how it changes your jumps.\n\nIn summary, adjusting your starting position can significantly enhance your jumping technique and help you land more gracefully. Remember to keep shuffling your feet further back and engage your body correctly as you dive over obstacles. With some consistent practice, you should see noticeable improvements in both your ability to jump and your overall confidence in these movements.\n\n- Position yourself further back from the obstacle to improve your jumping range.\n- Focus on engaging your core and controlling your body as you leap.\n- Practice consistently to build confidence and refine your technique.'),(77992,55972,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(77993,55972,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"[Laughter]\",\n        \"start\": 5.47,\n        \"duration\": 6.81\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"all right so it\'s more different today\",\n        \"start\": 21.57,\n        \"duration\": 5.189\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the idea is that you can start in split\",\n        \"start\": 23.789,\n        \"duration\": 5.61\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"Kong again but we\'re gonna start\",\n        \"start\": 26.759,\n        \"duration\": 5.221\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"shuffling our feet further back okay\"