80,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Fl9zGhVhTJE/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Fl9zGhVhTJE/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMPPwg52msvrAueGiI8MoIk\",\"position\":11,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"Fl9zGhVhTJE\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":11}'),(78032,55974,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Cat Pass'),(78033,55974,'authId','Auth1'),(78034,55974,'searchId','Tutorials - Cat Pass'),(78035,55974,'filterId','none'),(78036,55974,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(78037,55974,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Cat Pass'),(78038,55974,'_edit_last','1'),(78039,55974,'video_transcript_chatgpt','In this tutorial, we will explore a slightly more advanced technique that focuses on improving your foundational skills while adding a bit of dynamism to your practice. Instead of counting steps, you\'ll learn to initiate the movement from a small run-up. This approach not only challenges you but also helps cultivate better timing and body positioning, which are crucial for mastering various athletic maneuvers.\n\nTo get started, find a suitable area where you can comfortably take two or three quick steps before executing the technique. As you begin your run-up, your goal is to transition into a split-foot position just before you land. This might feel a bit tricky at first, but with practice, you\'ll find your rhythm. While doing this, it’s important to focus on how your feet land and align correctly for the subsequent movements. Be sure to practice on both sides to develop balance and coordination, allowing you to switch direction fluidly.\n\nIn conclusion, this exercise not only helps you enhance your footwork but also emphasizes the importance of timing and body alignment in athletic performance. As you incorporate this technique into your training, remember to keep it fun and engaging by experimenting with different approaches. With dedication and practice, you\'ll improve your skills significantly, making your movements feel more natural and effortless.\n\nKey highlights: \n1. Focus on initiating movement from a small run-up instead of counting steps.\n2. Transition into a split-foot position for better alignment and timing.\n3. Practice on both sides to enhance balance and coordination.'),(78040,55974,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78041,55974,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"all right slightly trickier one today\",\n        \"start\": 18.539,\n        \"duration\": 6.011\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"now what we\'re gonna do is we\'re gonna\",\n        \"start\": 21.93,\n        \"duration\": 5.38\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"focus on not counting the steps and\",\n        \"start\": 24.55,\n        \"duration\": 4.559\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we\'re just going to put in a small run\",\n        \"start\": 27.31,\n        \"duration\": 5.429\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"up about two or three steps away but\",\n        \"start\": 29.109,\n        \"duration\": 5.671\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we\'re trying to get into that split foot\",\n        \"start\": 32.739,\n        \"duration\": 5.401\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"position with the slight dive and\",\n        \"start\": 34.78,\n        \"duration\": 5.55\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"essentially trying time it so you can\",\n        \"start\": 38.14,\n        \"duration\": 3.9\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"get up feet in the correct position so\",\n        \"start\": 40.33,\n        \"duration\": 3.72\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"you can get over doing exactly what\",\n        \"start\": 42.04,\n        \"duration\": 3.78\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we\'ve been doing again both sides\"