London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMPPwg52msvrAueGiI8MoIk\",\"position\":12,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"NvNzJJtMEYA\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":12}'),(78056,55975,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Cat Pass'),(78057,55975,'authId','Auth1'),(78058,55975,'searchId','Tutorials - Cat Pass'),(78059,55975,'filterId','none'),(78060,55975,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(78061,55975,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Cat Pass'),(78062,55975,'_edit_last','1'),(78063,55975,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When learning to take off with both feet in a parallel stance, it\'s important to start from the right position. Many beginners often make the mistake of jumping into their take-off, which can waste energy and limit the distance they achieve. This tutorial will guide you on how to set up your take-off properly for better results. The key here is to focus on ensuring you’re not expending unnecessary energy during your landing, which can hinder your overall performance.\n\nBegin by approaching the take-off area with a controlled run. Instead of jumping into a landing position before your take-off, aim to arrive in a balanced stance that allows for a smooth transition into the jump. Remember, a lot of people find it tempting to land heavily on their feet, but this ultimately drains your energy and decreases the distance you can achieve. Instead, concentrate on keeping your movements fluid and connected, allowing your body to naturally carry you into the take-off without a power-hungry jump.\n\nTo sum it up, mastering the technique of taking off with both feet from a parallel position can significantly enhance your performance while saving energy. Focus on maintaining balance and smoothness in your movements, eliminating the need for a heavy landing. With practice, you\'ll find yourself jumping further and with greater ease. Keep these tips in mind, and you’ll improve your technique in no time.\n\nHighlights:\n- Focus on a smooth transition into the jump, avoiding heavy landings.\n- Save energy by maintaining balance rather than jumping into position.\n- With practice, achieve better distance and performance in your take-off.'),(78064,55975,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78065,55975,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"all right so today we\'re going to have a\",\n        \"start\": 0.06,\n        \"duration\": 5.37\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"go at taking off parallel feet so one of\",\n        \"start\": 1.979,\n        \"duration\": 5.131\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the older videos that we\'ve been doing\",\n        \"start\": 5.43,\n        \"duration\": 4.05\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"of trying to take away both feet but\",\n        \"start\": 7.11,\n        \"duration\": 6.09\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"with a running and I want you to try not\",\n        \"start\": 9.48,\n        \"duration\": 7.89\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"to jump into the take off all right so\",\n        \"start\": 13.2,\n        \"duration\": 7.52\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"let me show you what to do\",\n        \"start\": 17.37,\n        \"duration\": 3.35\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"[Music]\",\n        \"start\": 22.16,\n        \"duration\": 3.14\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so you can see that I did not jump into\",\n        \"start\": 26.49,\n        \"duration\": 5.949\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the position and then take off so what a\",\n        \"start\": 30.25,\n        \"duration\": 4.32\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"lot of people do is they spend a lot of\",\n        \"start\": 32.439,\n        \"duration\": 4.171\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"energy landing into the position and\",\n        \"start\": 34.57,\n        \"duration\": 4.29\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"then taking off so this is 