n these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Vaulting}}{{Series:Cat Pass Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/D0zisMQVPzU/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/D0zisMQVPzU/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/D0zisMQVPzU/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/D0zisMQVPzU/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/D0zisMQVPzU/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTMPPwg52msvrAueGiI8MoIk\",\"position\":13,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"D0zisMQVPzU\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":13}'),(78080,55976,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Cat Pass'),(78081,55976,'authId','Auth1'),(78082,55976,'searchId','Tutorials - Cat Pass'),(78083,55976,'filterId','none'),(78084,55976,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(78085,55976,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Cat Pass'),(78086,55976,'_edit_last','1'),(78087,55976,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to mastering the cat pass technique, one common issue that many encounter is noise during the movement. This noise typically arises from a forceful landing that creates a slapping sound as you make contact with the box. This not only signals an ineffective execution of the move but can also lead to unnecessary strain or injury. Our goal is to minimize this noise by focusing on the proper trajectory, making your cat pass smoother and more efficient.\n\nTo eliminate the unwanted sounds, start by evaluating your approach. Rather than thinking about hopping up to clear the box, aim to move horizontally across it. Picture yourself gliding along the surface instead of dropping straight down. This subtle shift in perspective can drastically reduce the noise generated during your landing. You’ll want to practice the motion to ensure that when you make contact, it feels controlled and gentle, resulting in significantly quieter landings. If you hear a big slam, it’s a cue to adjust your technique.\n\nUltimately, the takeaway is that a successful cat pass should not produce a loud sound—quiet landings indicate a correct technique. By focusing on a horizontal trajectory and adjusting your approach, you can achieve a smoother execution that feels more graceful and ends up being kinder to both your body and the equipment. Remember, the quieter the landing, the better your technique!\n\n- Focus on a horizontal trajectory rather than a vertical drop for smoother landings.\n- If you hear a loud noise, adjust your technique to promote quieter executions.\n- Smooth, controlled movements lead to better performance and less strain.'),(78088,55976,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78089,55976,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so today we\'re going to have a look at\",\n        \"start\": 1.77,\n        \"duration\": 6.36\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"trying to get rid of noise eliminate any\",\n        \"start\": 3.75,\n        \"duration\": 8.28\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"sounds from doing the cat Pass what I\",\n        \"start\": 8.13,\n        \"duration\": 7.079\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"hear a lot is slapping down onto the\",\n        \"start\": 12.03,\n        \"duration\": 5.7\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"wall of the box and this is kind of\",\n        \"start\": 15.209,\n        \"duration\": 4.261\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"telling me that you\'re doing the wrong\",\n        \"start\": 17.73,\n        \"duration\": 3.389\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"traje