l explore a simple yet effective technique for improving your form and efficiency in the water. Many who engage in water sports or swimming often struggle with how to position their hands and wrists correctly. This guidance here focuses on adjusting your wrist position, which can make a significant difference in your overall technique and ability to maneuver in the water.nnTo start, aim to keep your hands flat and focused around the pivot point when you\'re entering the water. This means that your wrists should initially be below the water surface, making it challenging to lift your arms. The key is to raise your wrists above the water to transition into a more powerful position. Once in this correct stance, you will find it much easier to lift your body up out of the water effectively. A great way to practice this is by gradually working from your initial wrist position to achieving that optimal height, which is essential for maintaining balance and propulsion.nnIn summary, adjusting the position of your wrists while in the water is crucial for enhancing your technique. By getting your wrists above the water and pivoting accordingly, you’ll find it easier to control your movements and maintain a smooth flow. This small adjustment can lead to better performance and a more enjoyable experience on the water, whether you\'re swimming, kayaking, or engaging in any water-based activity.nn- Keep your hands flat and focused around the pivot point when entering the water.n- Raise your wrists above the water for better control and positioning.n- Practice transitioning smoothly from your initial wrist position to enhance your technique.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 308,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 303,\n            \"total_tokens\": 611,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\"