\",\n        \"start\": 17.58,\n        \"duration\": 5.279\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"lot of energy trying to keep it up it\",\n        \"start\": 20.67,\n        \"duration\": 5.13\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"means that you put the foot too low you\",\n        \"start\": 22.859,\n        \"duration\": 4.92\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"want to bring that foot high enough so\",\n        \"start\": 25.8,\n        \"duration\": 4.2\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"essentially it\'s just sticking into the\",\n        \"start\": 27.779,\n        \"duration\": 4.32\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"wall when we do the climb up it\'s going\",\n        \"start\": 30,\n        \"duration\": 4.14\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"to be used as a pivot so we can leave\",\n        \"start\": 32.099,\n        \"duration\": 4.081\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"her ourselves up and if you\'re really\",\n        \"start\": 34.14,\n        \"duration\": 3.599\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"trying to fight hard to stop it from\",\n        \"start\": 36.18,\n        \"duration\": 3.66\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"slipping down then there\'s a lot of work\",\n        \"start\": 37.739,\n        \"duration\": 5.691\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"going on there that we don\'t need to do\",\n        \"start\": 39.84,\n        \"duration\": 3.59\n    }\n]'),(78161,55979,'_video_transcript_json','field_67221da62655b'),(78162,55979,'video_transcript_srt','1\n00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:07,000\nback to the climb ups today we\'re going\n\n2\n00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000\nto have a look at just placing our feet\n\n3\n00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000\non the wall and essentially the best\n\n4\n00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,000\nplace for them the foot that is gonna be\n\n5\n00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000\nhigher you want to place it in a high\n\n6\n00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000\nenough so you don\'t have to worry about\n\n7\n00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000\nit slipping down if you\'re expending a\n\n8\n00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000\nlot of energy trying to keep it up it\n\n9\n00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000\nmeans that you put the foot too low you\n\n10\n00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000\nwant to bring that foot high enough so\n\n11\n00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000\nessentially it\'s just sticking into the\n\n12\n00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000\nwall when we do the climb up it\'s going\n\n13\n00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000\nto be used as a pivot so we can leave\n\n14\n00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000\nher ourselves up and if you\'re really\n\n15\n00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000\ntrying to fight hard to stop it from\n\n16\n00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:42,000\nslipping down then there\'s a lot of work\n\n17\n00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000\ngoing on there that we don\'t need to do\n\n'),(78163,55979,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(78164,55979,'_edit_lock','1730717503:1'),(78165,55979,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APpyIlAEP1VveftP0j7jyTbAcu5xr\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730721342,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"When it comes to climbing, especially during those demanding climb-ups, foot placement can make a significant difference in your efficiency and overall upper body strength. One common challenge many climbers face is ensuring their feet are positioned correctly on the wall. A solid foot placement will allow you to conserve energy while maximizing your ability to ascend smoothly. Getting it right is crucial, as improper placement can lead to unnecessary strain as you climb.nnTo achieve optimal foot placement, focus on positioning your higher foot on the wall. It’s essential to set this foot at a height that feels comfortable, yet high enough so that you don\'t have to exert extra effort to keep it in place. If you find yourself struggling to prevent your foot from slipping down, chances are it’s resting too low. Aim to plant that foot so it essentially feels \'stuck\' to the wall, as this will help it serve as a strong pivot point. This way, you’ll rely on your foot to support your weight and help propel you upwards, allowing your upper body to work more efficiently rather than fighting against gravity.nnIn conclusion, mastering foot placement during climb-ups is a key component of successful climbing. By ensuring your foot is positioned high and secure on the wall, you’ll not only relieve unnecessary tension on your arms and back but also enhance your overall climbing technique. Remember, a good foothold is the foundation of a good climb, so take a moment to assess your foot placement before you begin your ascent. This small adjustment can lead to a much more enjoyable climbing experience.nnHighlights:n- Position your higher foot on the wall at a comfortable, secure height.n- Ensure your foot feels \'stuck\' to avoid unnecessary energy expenditure.n- Mastering foot placement improves efficiency and enhances your climbing technique.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 353,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 351,\n            \"total_tokens\": 704,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"DKMI3_AK85kycHcdu.WF2z3XlVbOKCPrxBl759ChLSo-1730721347-1.0.1.1-i09oUBYJZc0ObTg5Ck1tUGQAFFlDrnAZ4Hzmhn_1D0PWQRLTss2tgYfGg06ivUGQtr9Yazrj7_Qomezec8t1yg\",\n            \"expires\": 1730723147,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"uNmGHSCjL6PiBJdbifmE84.cf1TeQ.bxGuIGP3hVoOU-1730721347119-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(78166,55979,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(78167,55979,'video_transcript_chatgpt','When it comes to climbing, especially during those demanding climb-ups, foot placement can make a significant difference in your efficiency and overall upper body strength. One common challenge many climbers face is ensuring their feet are positioned correctly on the wall. A solid foot placement will allow you to conserve energy while maximizing your ability to ascend smoothly. Getting it right is crucial, as improper placement can lead to unnecessary strain as you climb.\n\nTo achieve optimal foot placement, focus on positioning your higher foot on the wall. It’s essential to set this foot at a height that feels comfortable, yet high enough so that you don\'t have to exert extra effort to keep it in place. If you find yourself struggling to prevent your foot from slipping down, chances are it’s resting too low. Aim to plant that foot so it essentially feels \'stuck\' to the wall, as this will help it serve as a strong pivot point. This way, you’ll rely on your foot to support your weight and help propel you upwards, allowing your upper body to work more efficiently rather than fighting against gravity.\n\nIn conclusion, mastering foot placement during climb-ups is a key component of successful climbing. By ensuring your foot is positioned high and secure on the wall, you’ll not only relieve unnecessary tension on your arms and back but also enhance your overall climbing technique. Remember, a good foothold is the foundation of a good climb, so take a moment to assess your foot placement before you begin your ascent. This small adjustment can lead to a much more enjoyable climbing experience.\n\nHighlights:\n- Position your higher foot on the wall at a comfortable, secure height.\n- Ensure your foot feels \'stuck\' to avoid unnecessary energy expenditure.\n- Mastering foot placement improves efficiency and enhances your climbing technique.'),(78168,55979,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78169,55979,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(78170,55979,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(78171,55979,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(78172,55979,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(78173,55980,'_thumbnail_id','13998'),(78174,55980,'video_id','0U8tpMvst8I'),(78175,55980,'video_type','tutorial'),(78176,55980,'order_position','2'),(78177,55980,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"4yWO5DSKz9Y7YaU634fF6yYdh7w\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTktJVUhMckdzRTkwTXU5VXJZaERxTC41QTY1Q0UxMTVCODczNThE\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T09:08:34Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Climbup #03 - Stepping Up Parkour Tutorial. [042]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Climbup (Beginner) in Parkour - Stepping Up.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Climbup Series. Episode #03nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Climbing #SteppingUp #---nnClimbups - Stepping Up.nnThe next part to work on is trying to step the bottom foot up higher than it currently is. This will give us momentum and traction when the actual climbup happens.nn1. Make sure you have a good grip on the wall so you don\'t slip.nn2. Make sure you practice both sides.nn3. Keep practicing until you can get that bottom foot level or higher than the top foot. This foot will really help the next stages of getting on top of the wall.nn4. Even though we\'re not doing cat-to-cats yet, this movement is absolutely necessary to be able to do them, so get the practice in now!nnFind your favourite wall and start practicing!nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2