 skills. Incorporating these techniques into your training routine can significantly contribute to your overall success and enjoyment in climbing.nn- Utilize an over grip for better control and biomechanics when climbing.n- Practice negative movements by starting from the top and lowering slowly to build strength.n- Focus on maintaining control and engaging your core during negative climbs for improved technique.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 328,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 305,\n            \"total_tokens\": 633,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"uQHhWt1VhjJVOkbEXYlQ07MK1gpudVAxQGYak2hNkTM-1730721393-1.0.1.1-kr_ZJ_xpks4qAz4DIvML_oY2ycqC8qLS68l5eIjeF3p8Ku5MsBwMIzVRgnFtei1NFnEuzVfs7TxXAaEyXX3Raw\",\n            \"expires\": 1730723193,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"xYyyFoqIQ.Sp6SUQe4Nnf8fD88kX1ydCCSo04Lt0ANQ-1730721393910-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(78215,55981,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(78216,55981,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you\'ve been looking to improve your climbing technique, focusing on your hand position is a great place to start. In this tutorial, we\'ll explore how to use the over grip effectively and practice a negative climb—an excellent way to build strength and refine your movements without putting too much strain on your body. This approach is ideal whether you\'re a seasoned climber or just starting out, and it helps to reinforce good biomechanics while minimizing injury risk.\n\nTo begin, find a comfortable starting position using the over grip. This grip involves wrapping your fingers around the hold, allowing for better control and better weight distribution. Once you\'re in position, the goal is to execute a negative movement, which essentially means starting from the top of the hold and slowly lowering your body towards the ground. This technique focuses on the descent, allowing you to build strength while honing your climbing form. Remember to engage your core and maintain a steady pace during the negative—control is key here!\n\nIn summary, practicing a negative climb while utilizing an over grip is a fantastic way to enhance your climbing efficiency and technique. By starting from the top and focusing on your descent, you’ll not only strengthen your muscles but also gain confidence in your climbing skills. Incorporating these techniques into your training routine can significantly contribute to your overall success and enjoyment in climbing.\n\n- Utilize an over grip for better control and biomechanics when climbing.\n- Practice negative movements by starting from the top and lowering slowly to build strength.\n- Focus on maintaining control and engaging your core during negative climbs for improved technique.'),(78217,55981,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78218,55981,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(78219,55981,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(78220,55981,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(78221,55981,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(78222,55982,'_thumbnail_id','14002'),(78223,55982,'video_id','O7eoEknVicY'),(78224,55982,'video_type','tutorial'),(78225,55982,'order_position','4'),(78226,55982,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"4htAj83zS2sls9r1IQirQhrV9cQ\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTktJVUhMckdzRTkwTXU5VXJZaERxTC4zMDg5MkQ5MEVDMEM1NTg2\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T09:08:34Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Climbup #05 - Overgrip To Front Parkour Tutorial. [044]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Climbup (Beginner) in Parkour - Overgrip To Front.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Climbup Series. Episode #05nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Climbing #OvergripToFront #---nnOvergrip to Front Grip.nnThis is a simple extension of yesterday\'s progression and it\'s used for one simple purpose... To get us used to taking our bodyweight on the hands at the front edge of the wall.nn1. Go slowly and make sure you have a firm grip on the wall as you transition.nn2. The fingers should fully be over the top of the wall and your grip strength will come into play heavily.nn3. Make sure that foot is in the high position (see the foot placement video ) and you are not struggling to keep it up!nnRinse and repeat!nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly