ion\n\n12\n00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000\nokay make your way up however you need\n\n13\n00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:48,000\nto get into the top position and then\n\n14\n00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:50,000\ncome down slowly okay okay so we\'re just\n\n15\n00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000\ngetting used to changing from the back\n\n16\n00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000\nof the wall to the\n\n'),(78237,55982,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(78238,55982,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APpzELFH5eUidTQkqvHRw6KJLpCvN\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730721400,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"Climbing can be challenging, especially when it comes to mastering hand positions. Today, we’re going to focus on a technique that helps you transition smoothly from an over grip to a normal grip while climbing. This skill is important because it prepares you to better navigate different holds and maintain control as you change positions on the wall.nnTo get started, find a climbing wall and practice getting your body into the top position using whatever method feels comfortable for you. Once you’re at the top, take a moment to orient yourself before making your way down. As you descend, concentrate on gradually switching from your over grip to the normal grip. This transition is key, as it trains your muscles to adapt to different hand placements and positions on the wall, which is essential for effective climbing.nnRemember, climbing is as much about technique as it is about strength. By practicing this grip transition, you’ll be setting yourself up for success on the wall. Not only will this improve your climbing ability, but it will also make you feel more confident with your hand placements as you tackle various routes in the future.nnHighlights:n- Practice transitioning from an over grip to a normal grip while descending.n- Focus on getting into the top position using your preferred climbing method.n- Mastering grip changes enhances control and confidence on the climbing wall.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 328,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 262,\n            \"total_tokens\": 590,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"BIv6SU_oFuKgPRSlEpbYWeHJaRzR3gwAVvqhlYSaoUA-1730721405-1.0.1.1-QEvk2EL_6Rrutd6BqVkM0NvbBvNvO3Qbg_q0VNQuZtUJVaR_MtsH9IhtDr3iwDwLzxltzIHXRxHdKZ_jxJ2DwA\",\n            \"expires\": 1730723205,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \"_wBIaTw2YfIFlCuJKlSBXTCaxStgYOZAanfa0f1pd7M-1730721405082-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(78239,55982,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(78240,55982,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Climbing can be challenging, especially when it comes to mastering hand positions. Today, we’re going to focus on a technique that helps you transition smoothly from an over grip to a normal grip while climbing. This skill is important because it prepares you to better navigate different holds and maintain control as you change positions on the wall.\n\nTo get started, find a climbing wall and practice getting your body into the top position using whatever method feels comfortable for you. Once you’re at the top, take a moment to orient yourself before making your way down. As you descend, concentrate on gradually switching from your over grip to the normal grip. This transition is key, as it trains your muscles to adapt to different hand placements and positions on the wall, which is essential for effective climbing.\n\nRemember, climbing is as much about technique as it is about strength. By practicing this grip transition, you’ll be setting yourself up for success on the wall. Not only will this improve your climbing ability, but it will also make you feel more confident with your hand placements as you tackle various routes in the future.\n\nHighlights:\n- Practice transitioning from an over grip to a normal grip while descending.\n- Focus on getting into the top position using your preferred climbing method.\n- Mastering grip changes enhances control and confidence on the climbing wall.'),(78241,55982,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78242,55982,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(78243,55982,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(78244,55982,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(78245,55982,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(78246,55983,'_thumbnail_id','14004'),(78247,55983,'video_id','icmKI-QkFwk'),(78248,55983,'video_type','tutorial'),(78249,55983,'order_position','5'),(78250,55983,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"4kbzqJYyx3z3DwHggqwTyZmXFz4\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTktJVUhMckdzRTkwTXU5VXJZaERxTC5DQUNERDQ2NkIzRUQxNTY1\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T09:08:34Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Climbup #06 - Slow Transitions Parkour Tutorial. [045]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Climbup (Beginner) in Parkour - Slow Transitions.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Climbup Series. Episode #06nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Climbing #SlowTransitions #---nnClimbups - Slow TransitionsnnToday we\'ll look at trying to tackle the super tricky part of the climbup where we transition the pulling action into the pushing action.nn1. Make sure you go slllllllllllow. This indicates control of the movement and will highlight any weaker parts of the range of motion.nn2. The weaker parts of the range of motion are the bits that go faster because you can\'t slow them down. This is where strength training is going to start to play a part. Repetition and conditioning of this drill alone will help to improve the strength and control of it.nn3. The nature of this movement will put strain and tension on your tendons (especially at the elbow). Be careful about this and monitor if they are continually sore afterwards. If they are,then stop the training and focus on strength training first. It means the tendons are becoming inflamed from too much damage and pulling.nn4. Repetition of this drill will also help \'grease the groove\'s for other movements in Parkour like the \'Muscle Up\'. nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.l