7221da62655b'),(78356,55987,'video_transcript_srt','1\n00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,000\nso today we are going to have a look at\n\n2\n00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,000\ntrying to incorporate a pole now so the\n\n3\n00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000\nidea is we\'re going to still go back to\n\n4\n00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000\nthe overgrip we\'re still doing a\n\n5\n00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000\nnegative but when we get to the bottom\n\n6\n00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000\nposition with our arms completely\n\n7\n00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,000\nstraight\n\n8\n00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000\nwe\'re going to try and pull it up as\n\n9\n00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000\nhigh as we can don\'t forget to step up\n\n10\n00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:43,000\nwith that other leg and to let it help\n\n11\n00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:44,000\nyou alright okay so don\'t worry if you\n\n12\n00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000\ncan\'t get all the way up on top but the\n\n13\n00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000\nidea is we\'re starting to get used to\n\n14\n00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:52,000\nthe biomechanics of pulling and\n\n15\n00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,000\nessentially used to just trying to get\n\n16\n00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000\nfrom the bottom position and pulling\n\n17\n00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000\nokay so just keep repeating\n\n'),(78357,55987,'_video_transcript_srt','field_67224b69b74d7'),(78358,55987,'video_transcript_chatgpt_json','{\n    \"headers\": {},\n    \"body\": {\n        \"id\": \"chatcmpl-APpynnEYyMDTl5uhwE4KtM91pzsFV\",\n        \"object\": \"chat.completion\",\n        \"created\": 1730721373,\n        \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18\",\n        \"choices\": [\n            {\n                \"index\": 0,\n                \"message\": {\n                    \"role\": \"assistant\",\n                    \"content\": \"Incorporating pole exercises into your routine can be a fantastic way to enhance your strength and improve your biomechanics. Whether you’re a beginner or looking to refine your skills, focusing on the right techniques can make a significant difference. This tutorial will guide you through the steps to effectively use a pole in your workouts, particularly emphasizing the importance of posture and technique while performing negative pulls.nnFirst, start by positioning yourself for the exercise, ensuring you have a firm grip on the pole. Begin by executing a negative pull, which involves lowering yourself slowly from the top position. When you reach the bottom, with your arms straight, the goal is to pull yourself back up as high as you can. It’s important not to rush this process—focus on using your other leg to assist as you pull yourself upward. This not only helps in easing the movement but also allows your muscles to adapt gradually to the pulling mechanics. Remember, if you can’t pull yourself all the way up at first, that\'s perfectly okay! Consistency is key, so keep practicing and repeating the motion.nnIn conclusion, regularly practicing this pole exercise can significantly improve your strength and technique over time. The combination of using your arms and legs will enhance your pulling ability, making the overall movement feel more natural and effective. Keep working at it and don’t be discouraged by initial challenges—progress will come with persistence and practice!nn- Focus on proper grip and posture for effective pole exercises.n- Utilize your legs to assist with the pull, especially from the bottom position.n- Practice consistently to build strength and improve your pulling mechanics.\",\n                    \"refusal\": null\n                },\n                \"logprobs\": null,\n                \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"\n            }\n        ],\n        \"usage\": {\n            \"prompt_tokens\": 336,\n            \"completion_tokens\": 316,\n            \"total_tokens\": 652,\n            \"prompt_tokens_details\": {\n                \"cached_tokens\": 0\n            },\n            \"completion_tokens_details\": {\n                \"reasoning_tokens\": 0\n            }\n        },\n        \"system_fingerprint\": \"fp_0ba0d124f1\"\n    },\n    \"response\": {\n        \"code\": 200,\n        \"message\": \"OK\"\n    },\n    \"cookies\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"__cf_bm\",\n            \"value\": \"KJLYaxxPpXQ30wy7aX_DUcOaXsWpMFq2.NoK0roOapU-1730721377-1.0.1.1-Is4ItFPe2w1o6d10Ndp.q2lDHQ85hnclzLVfu20NzfOjUMYv4.mPW8OoI5b1r4BuXGg4etv2LuFZpmIBFp.Ufg\",\n            \"expires\": 1730723177,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"_cfuvid\",\n            \"value\": \".sXZhWg7RR8RUuw6y.MQs6AHb3E8dkEgFGRwj.399rk-1730721377416-0.0.1.1-604800000\",\n            \"expires\": null,\n            \"path\": \"/\",\n            \"domain\": \"api.openai.com\",\n            \"port\": null,\n            \"host_only\": false\n        }\n    ],\n    \"filename\": null,\n    \"http_response\": {\n        \"data\": null,\n        \"headers\": null,\n        \"status\": null\n    }\n}'),(78359,55987,'_video_transcript_chatgpt_json','field_67224645b19c3'),(78360,55987,'video_transcript_chatgpt','Incorporating pole exercises into your routine can be a fantastic way to enhance your strength and improve your biomechanics. Whether you’re a beginner or looking to refine your skills, focusing on the right techniques can make a significant difference. This tutorial will guide you through the steps to effectively use a pole in your workouts, particularly emphasizing the importance of posture and technique while performing negative pulls.\n\nFirst, start by positioning yourself for the exercise, ensuring you have a firm grip on the pole. Begin by executing a negative pull, which involves lowering yourself slowly from the top position. When you reach the bottom, with your arms straight, the goal is to pull yourself back up as high as you can. It’s important not to rush this process—focus on using your other leg to assist as you pull yourself upward. This not only helps in easing the movement but also allows your muscles to adapt gradually to the pulling mechanics. Remember, if you can’t pull yourself all the way up at first, that\'s perfectly okay! Consistency is key, so keep practicing and repeating the motion.\n\nIn conclusion, regularly practicing this pole exercise can significantly improve your strength and technique over time. The combination of using your arms and legs will enhance your pulling ability, making the overall movement feel more natural and effective. Keep working at it and don’t be discouraged by initial challenges—progress will come with persistence and practice!\n\n- Focus on proper grip and posture for effective pole exercises.\n- Utilize your legs to assist with the pull, especially from the bottom position.\n- Practice consistently to build strength and improve your pulling mechanics.'),(78361,55987,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78362,55987,'portrait_thumnbail_filename',''),(78363,55987,'_portrait_thumnbail_filename','field_682053ef408b7'),(78364,55987,'landscape_thumnbail_filename',''),(78365,55987,'_landscape_thumnbail_filename','field_68205408408b8'),(78366,55988,'_thumbnail_id','14014'),(78367,55988,'video_id','hTZ7RBSt1HY'),(78368,55988,'video_type','tutorial'),(78369,55988,'order_position','10'),(78370,55988,'originalJSON','{\"kind\":\"youtube#playlistItem\",\"etag\":\"Zqn7oFpDo1XS3WUlKfRDrZ0teT8\",\"id\":\"UExsSWQ4SDdOa3hUTktJVUhMckdzRTkwTXU5VXJZaERxTC45NDk1REZENzhEMzU5MDQz\",\"snippet\":{\"publishedAt\":\"2019-06-25T09:08:34Z\",\"channelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Climbup #11 - Front Grip + Pulling Parkour Tutorial. [050]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Climbup (Beginner) in Parkour - Front Grip + Pulling.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Climbup Series. Episode #11nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2