nelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\",\"title\":\"How to Climbup #13 - Full Parkour Tutorial. [052]\",\"description\":\"ud83cudf93 A Tutorial on how to Climbup (Beginner) in Parkour - Full.nud83eudd77 The Parkour Climbup Series. Episode #13nu25e3u25e5 https://LONDONPARKOUR.comnnu2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2571u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572u2572nu2003u2003#Climbing #Full #---nnCLIMBUPS!!! u2b06ud83dudc46ud83dudc4dud83dudc12ud83dudd3cu23ebu23cfud83dudd3au26f0ud83dudeebud83dude80 nnSo the previous dozen or so videos have all been leading up to this... A proper climbup!nnMy aim of all these videos was to show you how this technique can be scaled to any ability level and allow anyone to start structuring their training to overcome this movement.nnIt\'s a particularly tricky movement to master and getting the correct mechanics and strength levels to do it will take time... But is achievable for ANYONE. Yes, that means YOU!nnSide note... I always chuckle at movies that have the hero dangling from one arm of a building/cliff, holding someone else in the other and they manage to do a climbup with that other person on them... Pffff... Do they KNOW how hard that would be?!? Anyway, make sure that you maintain the strict technique.. no one elbow and then the other... You\'re just fooling yourself, no one else.nnHave fun and enjoy the climbups! nn--- Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fX1d8knStep Vault Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3wV3ckvnBalancing Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cdWrlTnPullups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3g3cX9hnTurn Vaults Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3yUnM6cnCat Pass Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fG9qyEnClimbups Tutorial u25b6 https://bit.ly/2Rcs8VenCat Leaps Tutorial u25b6 https://bit. Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/2S1yBTinUnderbar Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/34FM7yInSwinging Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3cbcAbKnRolling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIuogAnJumping Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3fIfbMjnCrawling Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vIT7qpnClimbing Demo u25b6 https://bit.ly/3vNB6YinBalancing Demo u25b6 https://bit. to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COMnnud83dudd39 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.nnu26a1ufe0f https://pulse.localhost:8443nnud83euddea https://labs.localhost:8443nnud83dudd38 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkournnud83dudd38 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkournnud83dudd38 contact@localhost:8443nnu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nu2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u25e3 u25e5u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588u2588nnu3000u3000   video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.nnu2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Climbing}}{{Series:Climbups Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/pMSvVRQ27OU/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/pMSvVRQ27OU/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/pMSvVRQ27OU/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/pMSvVRQ27OU/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/pMSvVRQ27OU/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTNKIUHLrGsE90Mu9UrYhDqL\",\"position\":12,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"pMSvVRQ27OU\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":12}'),(78419,55990,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Climbups'),(78420,55990,'authId','Auth1'),(78421,55990,'searchId','Tutorials - Climbups'),(78422,55990,'filterId','none'),(78423,55990,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(78424,55990,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Climbups'),(78425,55990,'_edit_last','1'),(78426,55990,'video_transcript_chatgpt','In this tutorial, we\'re diving into a climbing exercise that focuses on building strength and technique through a series of movements. If you’ve been training and honing your skills, this is the perfect opportunity to put all that hard work into practice. We’ll be exploring the combination of pull-ups and dips to help you master the climbing motion while engaging your upper body effectively.\n\nTo get started, find a sturdy pull-up bar or similar structure. Begin with a normal grip on the bar, ensuring your hands are shoulder-width apart. Engage your core, pull your body upward, and aim to get your chin above the bar while keeping your belly tight. This initial pull-up is crucial—focus on exerting maximum effort and control. Once you\'ve reached the top of the pull-up position, transition smoothly into a dip by lowering your body further down, leaning slightly forward. From here, push upward with all your strength until your arms are fully extended. This combination not only builds strength but also develops fluidity in movement, which is essential for serious climbing.\n\nRemember, the key takeaways from this exercise are to maintain control and focus on engaging your core throughout the process. With consistent training, you\'ll find that mastering these movements will significantly improve your climbing prowess. Take note of your form and progress, and before long, you\'ll notice greater strength and stability in your climbing activities.\n\n- Start with a solid grip on the pull-up bar and engage your core for better control.\n- Transition smoothly from the pull-up to the dip position for an effective workout.\n- Consistent practice will enhance your climbing strength and overall performance.'),(78427,55990,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78428,55990,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"today\'s the day we are now going to do a\",\n        \"start\": 2.02,\n        \"duration\": 4.71\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"proper climb up so we\'re going to do a\",\n        \"start\": 4.33,\n        \"duration\": 5.219\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"normal grip pull and we\'re trying to get\",\n        \"start\": 6.73,\n        \"duration\": 5.73\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"up on top and then do the dip position\",\n        \"start\": 9.549,\n        \"duration\": 6.541\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"and push ok so all of the training all\",\n        \"start\": 12.46,\n        \"duration\": 5.76\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"of the slopes and everything is working\",\n        \"start\": 16.09,\n        \"duration\": 5.52\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"up to this where we\'re just trying to\",\n        \"start\": 18.22,\n        \"duration\": 4.59\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"pull as hard as we can\",\n        \"start\": 21.61,\n        \"duration\": 3.45\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"y\'all belly up and then do the dip and\",\n        \"start\": 22.81,\n        \"duration\": 29.429\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"push ok and then pushing with as much as\",\n        \"sta