to focus on other aspects of your training. Let\'s dive into a simple yet effective method that you can easily incorporate into your routine.\n\nTo start, find a flat wall that is smooth and even. The goal here is to create an environment where overgripping isn’t a possibility, so choose a surface where your hands can comfortably rest. Once you have your wall in place, position yourself as if you were about to start a practice routine. Focus on maintaining a relaxed grip and let your hands rest naturally against the wall. By doing this, you’ll train yourself to engage with the wall while centering your thoughts on technique rather than how tightly you may be holding on.\n\nIn conclusion, practicing against a flat wall can prove to be a game-changer in your training sessions. By ensuring that overgripping is not an option, you\'ll be able to concentrate on improving your overall form and technique. Remember, a relaxed grip allows you to perform better and feel more comfortable during your practice. Embrace this exercise, and watch how it enhances your performance over time.\n\nHighlights:\n- Choose a flat, smooth wall to eliminate the possibility of overgripping.\n- Focus on maintaining a relaxed grip to enhance your technique.\n- Practice against the wall to improve form without the distraction of tight gripping.'),(78451,55991,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78452,55991,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"this is a very quick one that is exactly\",\n        \"start\": 2.629,\n        \"duration\": 5.341\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the same about yesterday\",\n        \"start\": 6.47,\n        \"duration\": 3.72\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"however we\'re going to try and do this\",\n        \"start\": 7.97,\n        \"duration\": 4.709\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"so you don\'t even have the possibility\",\n        \"start\": 10.19,\n        \"duration\": 4.349\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"to overg