utorial}}{{Tax:Climbing}}{{Series:Climbups Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uAhAHX3A3fc/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uAhAHX3A3fc/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uAhAHX3A3fc/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uAhAHX3A3fc/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/uAhAHX3A3fc/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTNKIUHLrGsE90Mu9UrYhDqL\",\"position\":14,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"uAhAHX3A3fc\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":14}'),(78467,55992,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Climbups'),(78468,55992,'authId','Auth1'),(78469,55992,'searchId','Tutorials - Climbups'),(78470,55992,'filterId','none'),(78471,55992,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(78472,55992,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Climbups'),(78473,55992,'_edit_last','1'),(78474,55992,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you\'re looking to improve your climbing skills, mastering the explosive climb is an essential technique. This exercise not only enhances your overall mobility but also builds strength as you lift yourself up during the climb. In this tutorial, we\'ll focus on the key steps to effectively execute the climb while maintaining good form and control, allowing you to reach higher with ease.\n\nTo get started, position yourself in front of a sturdy wall. Begin with one foot firmly placed on the wall at a comfortable height. Your goal is to use that foot to push off explosively while simultaneously bringing your other foot up to the wall. As you elevate yourself, aim to bring one knee in tightly towards your chest; this will help in creating a swift lift. Once you’ve pushed off, your bottom foot should rise up to rest atop the wall. This position is called the crane position — practice this fluid motion repeatedly until you can transition smoothly and efficiently.\n\nIn summary, focusing on explosive strength and controlled mobility is key to mastering the climb up. By practicing the steps outlined, you will enhance your climbing prowess and feel more confident in your techniques. Keep challenging yourself, and remember that with persistence, you\'ll see improvement in your climbing abilities.\n\n- Begin by placing one foot on the wall for a stable push-off.\n- Bring your knee in close to enhance explosiveness and control.\n- Aim for the crane position, where your bottom foot rests on the wall for balance.'),(78475,55992,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78476,55992,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"today we are going to have a look at\",\n        \"start\": 2.909,\n        \"duration\": 5.64\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"trying to explosively do the climb up\",\n        \"start\": 5.519,\n        \"duration\": 4.471\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"we\'re going to try it up as high as we\",\n        \"start\": 8.549,\n        \"duration\": 5.82\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"can with good mobility and being able to\",\n        \"start\": 9.99,\n        \"duration\": 7.32\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"bring one knee in nice and close to you\",\n        \"start\": 14.369,\n        \"duration\": 5.161\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"the idea is we\'re going to put one foot\",\n        \"start\": 17.31,\n        \"duration\": 4.41\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"on the wall we\'re going to step up and\",\n        \"start\": 19.53,\n        \"duration\": 4.32\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"then the bottom foot is going to come\",\n        \"start\": 21.72,\n        \"duration\": 4.56\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"straight up on top of the wall i