1u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501u2501n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Climbing}}{{Series:Climbups Tips}}\"\",\"thumbnails\":{\"default\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/O7UwW4uCNCg/default.jpg\",\"width\":120,\"height\":90},\"medium\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/O7UwW4uCNCg/mqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":320,\"height\":180},\"high\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/O7UwW4uCNCg/hqdefault.jpg\",\"width\":480,\"height\":360},\"standard\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/O7UwW4uCNCg/sddefault.jpg\",\"width\":640,\"height\":480},\"maxres\":{\"url\":\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/O7UwW4uCNCg/maxresdefault.jpg\",\"width\":1280,\"height\":720}},\"channelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"playlistId\":\"PLlId8H7NkxTNKIUHLrGsE90Mu9UrYhDqL\",\"position\":16,\"resourceId\":{\"kind\":\"youtube#video\",\"videoId\":\"O7UwW4uCNCg\"},\"videoOwnerChannelTitle\":\"London Parkour\",\"videoOwnerChannelId\":\"UCufdBIaXEIQwIX0CMGbXdAw\"},\"index\":16}'),(78515,55994,'scrapeId','Tutorial - Climbups'),(78516,55994,'authId','Auth1'),(78517,55994,'searchId','Tutorials - Climbups'),(78518,55994,'filterId','none'),(78519,55994,'mapperId','YouTube - Playlist Items - Tutorial Videos'),(78520,55994,'importId','Tutorial Videos - Climbups'),(78521,55994,'_edit_last','1'),(78522,55994,'video_transcript_chatgpt','If you\'re looking to level up your workout routine, focusing on single-leg exercises can be a game changer. This tutorial will guide you through the process of strengthening your body, improving balance, and increasing your overall fitness by isolating one leg at a time. By embracing these advanced exercises, you\'ll challenge your muscles in new ways and enhance your stability, while also keeping your upper body engaged.\n\nTo get started, pick an exercise that fits your level of comfort, such as a single-leg squat or lunge. When you perform these movements, make sure that one leg is doing the work while the other remains steady. Your arms can assist you for balance or pulling purposes, but the essence lies in empowering that one leg to carry the load. After you\'ve mastered one side, don\'t forget to switch and work the other leg as well—this will ensure balanced strength and coordination. If you\'re feeling particularly ambitious, you can even transition into more challenging positions, like moving to the front, to really test your limits.\n\nIn summary, incorporating single-leg exercises into your routine can tremendously benefit your fitness journey. You\'ll not only develop greater strength and control but also improve your overall balance and prevent potential injuries. Remember to focus on form, alternate legs, and consider advancing to more difficult variations as you progress. Embrace the challenge and enjoy the strides you’ll make in your fitness journey!\n\n- Start with basic single-leg exercises like squats or lunges to build strength.\n- Ensure that each leg gets equal attention by alternating sides.\n- Consider more advanced variations as you gain confidence and stability.'),(78523,55994,'_video_transcript_chatgpt','field_67221db82655c'),(78524,55994,'video_transcript_json','[\n    {\n        \"text\": \"today we\'re gonna have a bit of a\",\n        \"start\": 2.62,\n        \"duration\": 5.849\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"advanced version and that is essentially\",\n        \"start\": 5.399,\n        \"duration\": 5.021\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"trying to do the same thing but with one\",\n        \"start\": 8.469,\n        \"duration\": 4.59\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"leg only so like I said yesterday let\'s\",\n        \"start\": 10.42,\n        \"duration\": 4.35\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"do a little work but now you\'re just\",\n        \"start\": 13.059,\n        \"duration\": 4.081\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"gonna have one leg doing all the work\",\n        \"start\": 14.77,\n        \"duration\": 4.259\n    },\n    {\n        \"text\": \"okay yes your arms are still gonna