is essential training! Learning how to recover from missing something is critical training.\n\n---\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃ ＴＵＴＯＲＩＡＬ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ  ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nLanding Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fX1d8k\nStep Vault Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3wV3ckv\nBalancing Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3cdWrlT\nPullups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3g3cX9h\nTurn Vaults Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3yUnM6c\nCat Pass Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fG9qyE\nClimbups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/2Rcs8Ve\nCat Leaps Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fY2EmW\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃   ＤＥＭＯ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ    ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nVaulting Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/2S1yBTi\nUnderbar Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/34FM7yI\nSwinging Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3cbcAbK\nRolling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIuogA\nJumping Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIfbMj\nCrawling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vIT7qp\nClimbing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vNB6Yi\nBalancing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fFoQmX\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃    ＳＵＢＳＣＲＩＢＥ     ┃┃  🔔  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nSubscribe to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_confirmation=1\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ   ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\n🔹  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COM\n\n🔹 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.\n\n⚡️ https://pulse.localhost:8443\n\n🧪 https://labs.localhost:8443\n\n🔸 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour\n\n🔸 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour\n\n🔸 contact@localhost:8443\n\n████████◣ ◥██████████████\n█████████◣ ◥█████████████\n██████████◣ ◥████████████\n███████████◣ ◥███████████\n████████████◣ ◥██████████\n█████████████◣ ◥█████████\n\n　　  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ\n\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃    ＤＩＳＣＬＡＩＭＥＲ    ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\nThis video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Climbing}}{{Series:Cat Leaps Tips}}\" Arm Jump','How to Cat Leap #10 - Splat Cats Parkour Tutorial. [024] image','','inherit','open','closed','','how-to-cat-leap-10-splat-cats-parkour-tutorial-024-image','','','2024-10-21 16:27:57','2024-10-21 16:27:57','',0,'http://localhost:8102/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/4eCeYbYTVwc.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(14106,1,'2024-10-21 16:32:56','2024-10-21 16:32:56','🎓 A Tutorial on how to Cat Pass (Beginner) in Parkour - Introduction.\n🥷 The Parkour Cat Pass Series. Episode #01\n◣◥ https://LONDONPARKOUR.com\n\n╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲\n  #Vaulting #Introduction #Parkour\n╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱\n\n\n┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓\n┃   ＤＥＳＣＲＩＰＴＩＯＮ    ┃\n┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛\n\n\n---\n\nCat-pass / kong hip drill.\n\nWhen doing the 🐈-pass you need to be able to support your weight on your arms while vaulting, be able to get your hips up high enough so that you create enough space underneath you for your legs to pass through and also get comfortable with leaning your head over your arms and be slightly leaning forwards.\n\nThis drill is usually the first one I start beginners off with so that they can start getting used to having their hips higher than the wall. I\'ll explain the next progressions in another video, but this is always a good starting drill.\n\n---\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃ ＴＵＴＯＲＩＡＬ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ  ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nLanding Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fX1d8k\nStep Vault Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3wV3ckv\nBalancing Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3cdWrlT\nPullups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3g3cX9h\nTurn Vaults Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3yUnM6c\nCat Pass Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fG9qyE\nClimbups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/2Rcs8Ve\nCat Leaps Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fY2EmW\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃   ＤＥＭＯ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ    ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\