 Vault (Beginner) in Parkour - Foot Trajectory.\n🥷 The Parkour Step Vault Series. Episode #6\n◣◥ https://LONDONPARKOUR.com\n\n╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲\n  #Vaulting #FootTrajectory #Parkour\n╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱\n\n\n┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓\n┃   ＤＥＳＣＲＩＰＴＩＯＮ    ┃\n┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛\n\n\n---\n\nTo minimise clipping the foot on the front edge of the wall, we over-compensate the trajectory and make sure we come DOWN onto the foot position.\n\nWhen students start they tend to drive the foot up towards the foot placement, barely missing the front edge by millimeters. With lower motor-control ability, the risk of clipping the foot is higher, so to mitigate this, the foot needs to raise over and above the wall, then return down to it.\n\nThis also allows us more time to control the positioning of the foot and ensure we\'re secure before vaulting.\n \n\n---\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃ ＴＵＴＯＲＩＡＬ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ  ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nLanding Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fX1d8k\nStep Vault Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3wV3ckv\nBalancing Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3cdWrlT\nPullups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3g3cX9h\nTurn Vaults Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3yUnM6c\nCat Pass Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fG9qyE\nClimbups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/2Rcs8Ve\nCat Leaps Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fY2EmW\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃   ＤＥＭＯ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ    ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nVaulting Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/2S1yBTi\nUnderbar Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/34FM7yI\nSwinging Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3cbcAbK\nRolling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIuogA\nJumping Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIfbMj\nCrawling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vIT7qp\nClimbing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vNB6Yi\nBalancing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fFoQmX\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃    ＳＵＢＳＣＲＩＢＥ     ┃┃  🔔  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nSubscribe to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_confirmation=1\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ   ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\n🔹  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COM\n\n🔹 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.\n\n⚡️ https://pulse.localhost:8443\n\n🧪 https://labs.localhost:8443\n\n🔸 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour\n\n🔸 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour\n\n🔸 contact@localhost:8443\n\n████████◣ ◥██████████████\n█████████◣ ◥█████████████\n██████████◣ ◥████████████\n███████████◣ ◥███████████\n████████████◣ ◥██████████\n█████████████◣ ◥█████████\n\n　　  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ\n\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃    ＤＩＳＣＬＡＩＭＥＲ    ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\nThis video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Vaulting}}{{Series:Step Vault Tips}}\" Step Vaults','How to Step Vault #6 - Foot Trajectory Parkour Tutorial. [119] image','','inherit','open','closed','','how-to-step-vault-6-foot-trajectory-parkour-tutorial-119-image','','','2024-10-21 16:35:44','2024-10-21 16:35:44','',0,'http://localhost:8102/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/bUw-cYzKaHk.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(14294,1,'2024-10-21 16:35:44','2024-10-21 16:35:44','🎓 A Tutorial on how to Step Vault (Beginner) in Parkour - Foot First.\n🥷 The Parkour Step Vault Series. Episode #7\n◣◥ https://LONDONPARKOUR.com\n\n╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲\n  #Vaulting #FootFirst #Parkour\n╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱\n\n\n┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓\n┃   ＤＥＳＣＲＩＰＴＩＯＮ    ┃\n┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛\n\n\n---\n\nOnce the step vault is feeling comfortable and you are happy overcoming any wall or obstacle with it, we actually change the technique completely.\n\nWhen bringing in a much higher entry force (from a jump, downwards trajectory or running speeds) we actually need the bigger muscle groups to take the impact first.\n\nThis means the FOOT needs to land on the wall and allow the leg muscles (Hip flexors, Quads, Calves, Hamstrings and Glutes) to absorb the impact first, then slow your speed enough for you to place your hand on the wall to control your body position into the step vault.\n\nThis takes a lot more practice and is a more advanced vaulting technique since it\'s rare that this amount of force is directed into a step vault.\n\nHowever, it\'s a useful tool and you should make sure you\'re comfortable leading with your feet first, since many other vaults  and techniques rely on this.\n\n \n\n---\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃ ＴＵＴＯＲＩＡＬ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ  ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nLanding Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fX1d8k\nStep Vault Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3wV3ckv\nBalancing Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3cdWrlT\nPullups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3g3cX9h\nTurn Vaults Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3yUnM6c\nCat Pass Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fG9qyE\nClimbups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/2Rcs8Ve\nCat Leaps Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fY2EmW\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃   ＤＥＭＯ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ    ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nVaulting Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/2S1yBTi\nUnderbar Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/34FM7yI\nSwinging Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3cbcAbK\nRolling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIuogA\nJumping Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIfbMj\nCrawling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vIT7qp\nClimbing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vNB6Yi\nBalancing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fFoQmX\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃    ＳＵＢＳＣＲＩＢＥ     ┃┃  🔔  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nSubscribe to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_confirmation=1\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ   ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\n🔹  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COM\n\n🔹 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.\n\n⚡️ https://pulse.localhost:8443\n\n🧪 https://labs.localhost:8443\n\n🔸 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour\n\n🔸 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour\n\n🔸 contact@localhost:8443\n\n████████◣ ◥██████████████\n█████████◣ ◥█████████████\n██████████◣ ◥████████████\n███████████◣ ◥███████████\n████████████◣ ◥██████████\n█████████████◣ ◥█████████\n\n　　  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ\n\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃    ＤＩＳＣＬＡＩＭＥＲ    ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\nThis video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Vaulting}}{{Series:Step Vault Tips}}\" Step Vaults','How to Step Vault #7 - Foot First Parkour Tutorial. [120] image','','inherit','open','closed','','how-to-step-vault-7-foot-first-parkour-tutorial-120-image','','','2024-10-21 16:35:44','2024-10-21 16:35:44','',0,'http://localhost:8102/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/uRnomTvLno8.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(14296,1,'2024-10-21 16:35:52','2024-10-21 16:35:52','🎓 A Tutorial on how to Land (Beginner) in Parkour - Intro.\n🥷 The Parkour Land Series. Episode #01\n◣◥ https://LONDONPARKOUR.com\n\n╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲\n  #Jumping #Intro #Parkour\n╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱\n\n\n┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓\n┃   ＤＥＳＣＲＩＰＴＩＯＮ    ┃\n┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛\n\n\n---\n\nThe Landings Tip Series\n\nSo I\'ve decided to hit the 20s with new Parkour Tutorials.\nEvery Monday, Wednesday & Friday at 11am.\n\n1. First up, Landing Properly.\n\nUsing the balls of your feet. ( Or the largest \"metatarsaophalangeal joint\" ). This will enable you to engage your muscles and muscular system rather than the skeletal system and joints. \n\nUse your toes to grip the wall, curb or rail. This will help you to contract tighter.\n\nAs you contract your muscles, try to keep your heels up, above the toes. Dropping the heel (which will put your foot into a \'dorsiflexion\' position) can injure your ligaments in the ankle and cause issues with:\n- Achilles Heel.\n- Anterior Talofibular ligament (top of the foot, on top of the ankle)\n- Calcaneofibular ligament (outside of the foot, behind the ankle)\n\n---\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃ ＴＵＴＯＲＩＡＬ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ  ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nLanding Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fX1d8k\nStep Vault Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3wV3ckv\nBalancing Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3cdWrlT\nPullups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3g3cX9h\nTurn Vaults Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3yUnM6c\nCat Pass Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fG9qyE\nClimbups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/2Rcs8Ve\nCat Leaps Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fY2EmW\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃   ＤＥＭＯ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ    ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nVaulting Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/2S1yBTi\nUnderbar Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/34FM7yI\nSwinging Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3cbcAbK\nRolling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIuogA\nJumping Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIfbMj\nCrawling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vIT7qp\nClimbing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vNB6Yi\nBalancing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fFoQmX\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃    ＳＵＢＳＣＲＩＢＥ     ┃┃  🔔  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nSubscribe to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_confirmation=1\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ   ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\n🔹  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COM\n\n🔹 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.\n\n⚡️ https://pulse.localhost:8443\n\n🧪 https://labs.localhost:8443\n\n🔸 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour\n\n🔸 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour\n\n🔸 contact@localhost:8443\n\n████████◣ ◥██████████████\n█████████◣ ◥█████████████\n██████████◣ ◥████████████\n███████████◣ ◥███████████\n████████████◣ ◥██████████\n█████████████◣ ◥█████████\n\n　　  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ\n\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃    ＤＩＳＣＬＡＩＭＥＲ    ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\nThis video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Jumping}}{{Series:Landing Tips}}\" Precisions','How to Land #01 - Intro Parkour Tutorial. [058] image','','inherit','open','closed','','how-to-land-01-intro-parkour-tutorial-058-image','','','2024-10-21 16:35:52','2024-10-21 16:35:52','',0,'http://localhost:8102/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/FXMj3tUcifs.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(14298,1,'2024-10-21 16:35:52','2024-10-21 16:35:52','🎓 A Tutorial on how to Land (Beginner) in Parkour - Focus.\n🥷 The Parkour Land Series. Episode #02\n◣◥ https://LONDONPARKOUR.com\n\n╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲\n  #Jumping #Focus #Parkour\n╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱\n\n\n┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓\n┃   ＤＥＳＣＲＩＰＴＩＯＮ    ┃\n┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛\n\n\n---\n\nFocal Points\n\nKeep your eye on a specific point of the landing. This will help to eliminate outside distractions and the peripheral vision from pulling your attention away.\nPractice the basics as if they\'re advanced. Maintain visual contact with your mark for the entire jump.\n\n When performing maximum-ability fear-based jumps, our attention will want to move from \'fight\' mode to \'flight\' mode. The flight mode will use any excuse to stop you from doing the jump. By using a focal point, you\'re reducing the amount of excuses your sympathetic nervous system can use.\n\nThere are occasions when you also jump and \'blackout\' for a fraction of a second as the fear goes to maximum. By having a focus point, you can negate this effect. \n\n---\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃ ＴＵＴＯＲＩＡＬ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ  ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nLanding Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fX1d8k\nStep Vault Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3wV3ckv\nBalancing Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3cdWrlT\nPullups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3g3cX9h\nTurn Vaults Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3yUnM6c\nCat Pass Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fG9qyE\nClimbups Tutorial ▶ h