 gravity to be pushed forward over that contact point, which then requires the right tension and throughout the body.\n\nTo stabilise the center of gravity, you need to push you head and . arms a little further forward and the hips backwards.\n \n\n---\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃ ＴＵＴＯＲＩＡＬ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ  ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nLanding Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fX1d8k\nStep Vault Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3wV3ckv\nBalancing Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3cdWrlT\nPullups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3g3cX9h\nTurn Vaults Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3yUnM6c\nCat Pass Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fG9qyE\nClimbups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/2Rcs8Ve\nCat Leaps Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fY2EmW\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃   ＤＥＭＯ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ    ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nVaulting Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/2S1yBTi\nUnderbar Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/34FM7yI\nSwinging Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3cbcAbK\nRolling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIuogA\nJumping Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIfbMj\nCrawling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vIT7qp\nClimbing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vNB6Yi\nBalancing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fFoQmX\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃    ＳＵＢＳＣＲＩＢＥ     ┃┃  🔔  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nSubscribe to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_confirmation=1\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ   ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\n🔹  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COM\n\n🔹 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.\n\n⚡️ https://pulse.localhost:8443\n\n🧪 https://labs.localhost:8443\n\n🔸 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour\n\n🔸 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour\n\n🔸 contact@localhost:8443\n\n████████◣ ◥██████████████\n█████████◣ ◥█████████████\n██████████◣ ◥████████████\n███████████◣ ◥███████████\n████████████◣ ◥██████████\n█████████████◣ ◥█████████\n\n　　  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ\n\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃    ＤＩＳＣＬＡＩＭＥＲ    ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\nThis video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Jumping}}{{Series:Landing Tips}}\" Precisions','How to Land #12 - Center Of Gravity Parkour Tutorial. [069] image','','inherit','open','closed','','how-to-land-12-center-of-gravity-parkour-tutorial-069-image','','','2024-10-21 16:35:55','2024-10-21 16:35:55','',0,'http://localhost:8102/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Zc0xqXaUw0Y.jpg',0,'attachment','image/jpeg',0),(14320,1,'2024-10-21 16:35:56','2024-10-21 16:35:56','🎓 A Tutorial on how to Land (Beginner) in Parkour - A Jump Into It.\n🥷 The Parkour Land Series. Episode #13\n◣◥ https://LONDONPARKOUR.com\n\n╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲\n  #Jumping #AJumpIntoIt #Parkour\n╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╲╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱╱\n\n\n┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓\n┃   ＤＥＳＣＲＩＰＴＩＯＮ    ┃\n┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛\n\n\n---\n\nJumping\n\nLets start increasing the difficulty by incorporating a small jump into the landing. The MAIN idea is to replicate the exact same landing position as before. We\'re slowly increasing the stress onto the structure of the body, so don\'t go crazy. If the structure doesn\'t do exactly as it was doing before the jumping, then it\'s too much of a jump. Reduce it and try again.\n\nThe main fault I see with landings is that the landing or force is too great because the person has tried to do too big of a jump. If you can\'t maintain the good stable structure, then you\'re going to damage your body over longer periods of time. Don\'t let ego get in the way, slow down, reduce the size of the jump and repeat with quality.\n\n---\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃ ＴＵＴＯＲＩＡＬ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ  ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nLanding Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fX1d8k\nStep Vault Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3wV3ckv\nBalancing Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3cdWrlT\nPullups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3g3cX9h\nTurn Vaults Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3yUnM6c\nCat Pass Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fG9qyE\nClimbups Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/2Rcs8Ve\nCat Leaps Tutorial ▶ https://bit.ly/3fY2EmW\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃   ＤＥＭＯ　ＳＥＲＩＥＳ    ┃┃  ▶  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nVaulting Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/2S1yBTi\nUnderbar Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/34FM7yI\nSwinging Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3cbcAbK\nRolling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIuogA\nJumping Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fIfbMj\nCrawling Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vIT7qp\nClimbing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3vNB6Yi\nBalancing Demo ▶ https://bit.ly/3fFoQmX\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮╭━━━━━╮\n┃    ＳＵＢＳＣＲＩＢＥ     ┃┃  🔔  ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯╰━━━━━╯\n\nSubscribe to channel: https://youtube.com/londonparkour?sub_confirmation=1\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ   ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\n🔹  https://LONDONPARKOUR.COM\n\n🔹 Practical movement that will transform the way you think, move and feel.\n\n⚡️ https://pulse.localhost:8443\n\n🧪 https://labs.localhost:8443\n\n🔸 https://www.Instagram.com/london_parkour\n\n🔸 https://www.youtube.com/londonparkour\n\n🔸 contact@localhost:8443\n\n████████◣ ◥██████████████\n█████████◣ ◥█████████████\n██████████◣ ◥████████████\n███████████◣ ◥███████████\n████████████◣ ◥██████████\n█████████████◣ ◥█████████\n\n　　  ＬＯＮＤＯＮＰＡＲＫＯＵＲ\n\n\n\n\n╭━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╮\n┃    ＤＩＳＣＬＡＩＭＥＲ    ┃\n╰━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╯\n\nThis video features Parkour performed either by professionals or under the supervision of professionals. All members of LondonParkour have been training since 2005 and insist that no one attempt to re-create or re-enact any ROOFTOP activities or movement AT HEIGHT performed in these videos. Do not use private property.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n{{Tag:beginner}}{{PostType:Tutorial}}{{Tax:Jumping}}{{Series:Landing Tips}}\" Precisions','How to Land #13 - A Jump Into It Parkour Tutorial. [070] image','','inherit','open','closed','','how-to-land-13-a-jump-into-it-parkour-tutori